-dev/commit/c520871da93570b926274cbf041c1b665e91f7f8","sha":"c520871da93570b926274cbf041c1b665e91f7f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/c520871da93570b926274cbf041c1b665e91f7f8"}],"sha":"f5f1a5fb48718b15f6a4101dd19817d506a30483","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/f5f1a5fb48718b15f6a4101dd19817d506a30483"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/c520871da93570b926274cbf041c1b665e91f7f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:06:26Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T20:06:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: recover genuine work from mixed tree (i18n, publish pin gate, session recovery, rate-limit health, sonner, hardening) (#308)\n\n* chore: recover genuine work from mixed tree\n\nThe working tree contained an accidental wholesale revert of the\nlate-V2 line (#296-#306: workspace train, bos.app.ts canonical config,\ncore-ui stubs, manifest v2, node/pnpm cutover, MF fix series,\ntwo-database contract, builtAt byte-stability) layered together with\ngenuine new work. This commit re-applies only the genuine work on top\nof main and drops the revert entirely.\n\nKept:\n- i18n deepening: locale negotiation (cookie + Accept-Language with\n  q-values), Vary header, request-scoped SSR locale in router context,\n  shared locale across bundle runtimes, degraded-compose toast,\n  localized RouterError copy; framework-level plumbing the ui surface\n  can adopt\n- publish pin-verification gate: block publishes whose pinned slots''\n  bytes fail SRI verification against their production URLs\n- session recovery: a failing getSession errors instead of caching\n  null as signed-out\n- rate limiter /health exemption + integration test (bind-probe guard\n  for 127/8 aliases absent on macOS)\n- sonner as an optional UI shared dependency\n- defensive error formatting across host, every-plugin,\n  better-near-auth\n- staging config parsing through BosConfigInputSchema\n- hygiene: typed server bootstrap await, proxiedFetch env forwarding,\n  CSP/e2e test type fixes, Effect.sync/void hardening\n\nDropped (accidental revert): workspace.ts/workspace-catalog.ts\ndeletions, bos.config.json precedence flip, core-ui stubs + manifest\nv1 downgrade, node->bun re-migration (every-plugin and child\nscaffolding), MF fix-series rollback, builtAt re-introduction,\ntwo-database fallback removal, better-near-auth citynode.app URL\nrevert and @tanstack/intent downgrade, skills version downgrades.\n\n8 changesets added for the user-facing work.\n\n* fix: address review — revert session.ts, defer sonner sharing\n\n- Revert resolution/session.ts to main: drops the this: void\n  annotations flagged in review, and a slipped-in dispatchEntry hunk\n  that hardcoded bos.config.json over findConfigPath — a real\n  regression for bos.app.ts-authored repos.\n- Defer the sonner optional-shared-dep feature (spec flag,\n  dependencies option, rsbuild pass-through, tests) — the\n  dependencies map was a caller-coupled presence check; redesign in\n  its own PR. The hydrate degraded-toast''s runtime sonner import\n  stays (resolvable in the ui workspace).\n\n* feat(host,everything-dev): practical rate limiting — two tiers, HTML 429, client retry\n\nThe 300/15min edge budget was too strict for shared egress (NAT/VPN)\nand rate-limited clients saw the site crash: raw JSON as the page\ndocument, silently failing queries, and the session check erroring.\n\nHost:\n- general tier 300 → 2000 / 15min (RATE_LIMIT_MAX)\n- new mutation tier (60/15min, RATE_LIMIT_MUTATION_MAX) for non-GET\n  requests outside the transports that own their throttling (oRPC,\n  Better-Auth, MCP) — direct REST writes get brute-force protection\n  without touching sessions, procedures, or agents\n- x-forwarded-for keying trusts only the LAST hop (proxy-appended);\n  rotating a spoofed first hop no longer mints unlimited keys\n- rate-limited document navigations (Accept: text/html) get a styled\n  HTML retry page honoring Retry-After semantics instead of raw JSON;\n  API requests keep the JSON body\n- GET/HEAD /health stays exempt from both tiers\n\nClient (everything-dev ui/api):\n- the oRPC fetch retries 429s up to three times honoring Retry-After\n  (capped 2s) — transient saturation self-heals in queries and the\n  session check instead of surfacing errors\n\nTests:\n- rewrite the Go regression burst: /health burst asserts the probe\n  exemption (zero 429s); the 429 contract moved to /api/ping\n- host integration: HTML-vs-JSON 429, mutation-tier boundaries\n  (exemptions + disjoint buckets), last-hop xff semantics\n- ui unit: retry-until-success and give-up-after-budget","tree":{"sha":"e02da52e47fbbc7a440f5cdf8bd3e753de517bba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/e02da52e47fbbc7a440f5cdf8bd3e753de517bba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/c520871da93570b926274cbf041c1b665e91f7f8","verification":{"payload":"tree e02da52e47fbbc7a440f5cdf8bd3e753de517bba\nparent 86e31a4314ae5d8c3bcea14cdd4fffb3e72ff770\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1791317186 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791317186 -0500\n\nchore: recover genuine work from mixed tree (i18n, publish pin gate, session recovery, rate-limit health, sonner, hardening) (#308)\n\n* chore: recover genuine work from mixed tree\n\nThe working tree contained an accidental wholesale revert of the\nlate-V2 line (#296-#306: workspace train, bos.app.ts canonical config,\ncore-ui stubs, manifest v2, node/pnpm cutover, MF fix series,\ntwo-database contract, builtAt byte-stability) layered together with\ngenuine new work. This commit re-applies only the genuine work on top\nof main and drops the revert entirely.\n\nKept:\n- i18n deepening: locale negotiation (cookie + Accept-Language with\n  q-values), Vary header, request-scoped SSR locale in router context,\n  shared locale across bundle runtimes, degraded-compose toast,\n  localized RouterError copy; framework-level plumbing the ui surface\n  can adopt\n- publish pin-verification gate: block publishes whose pinned slots''\n  bytes fail SRI verification against their production URLs\n- session recovery: a failing getSession errors instead of caching\n  null as signed-out\n- rate limiter /health exemption + integration test (bind-probe guard\n  for 127/8 aliases absent on macOS)\n- sonner as an optional UI shared dependency\n- defensive error formatting across host, every-plugin,\n  better-near-auth\n- staging config parsing through BosConfigInputSchema\n- hygiene: typed server bootstrap await, proxiedFetch env forwarding,\n  CSP/e2e test type fixes, Effect.sync/void hardening\n\nDropped (accidental revert): workspace.ts/workspace-catalog.ts\ndeletions, bos.config.json precedence flip, core-ui stubs + manifest\nv1 downgrade, node->bun re-migration (every-plugin and child\nscaffolding), MF fix-series rollback, builtAt re-introduction,\ntwo-database fallback removal, better-near-auth citynode.app URL\nrevert and @tanstack/intent downgrade, skills version downgrades.\n\n8 changesets added for the user-facing work.\n\n* fix: address review — revert session.ts, defer sonner sharing\n\n- Revert resolution/session.ts to main: drops the this: void\n  annotations flagged in review, and a slipped-in dispatchEntry hunk\n  that hardcoded bos.config.json over findConfigPath — a real\n  regression for bos.app.ts-authored repos.\n- Defer the sonner optional-shared-dep feature (spec flag,\n  dependencies option, rsbuild pass-through, tests) — the\n  dependencies map was a caller-coupled presence check; redesign in\n  its own PR. The hydrate degraded-toast''s runtime sonner import\n  stays (resolvable in the ui workspace).\n\n* feat(host,everything-dev): practical rate limiting — two tiers, HTML 429, client retry\n\nThe 300/15min edge budget was too strict for shared egress (NAT/VPN)\nand rate-limited clients saw the site crash: raw JSON as the page\ndocument, silently failing queries, and the session check erroring.\n\nHost:\n- general tier 300 → 2000 / 15min (RATE_LIMIT_MAX)\n- new mutation tier (60/15min, RATE_LIMIT_MUTATION_MAX) for non-GET\n  requests outside the transports that own their throttling (oRPC,\n  Better-Auth, MCP) — direct REST writes get brute-force protection\n  without touching sessions, procedures, or agents\n- x-forwarded-for keying trusts only the LAST hop (proxy-appended);\n  rotating a spoofed first hop no longer mints unlimited keys\n- rate-limited document navigations (Accept: text/html) get a styled\n  HTML retry page honoring Retry-After semantics instead of raw JSON;\n  API requests keep the JSON body\n- GET/HEAD /health stays exempt from both tiers\n\nClient (everything-dev ui/api):\n- the oRPC fetch retries 429s up to three times honoring Retry-After\n  (capped 2s) — transient saturation self-heals in queries and the\n  session check instead of surfacing errors\n\nTests:\n- rewrite the Go regression burst: /health burst asserts the probe\n  exemption (zero 429s); the 429 contract moved to /api/ping\n- host integration: HTML-vs-JSON 429, mutation-tier boundaries\n  (exemptions + disjoint buckets), last-hop xff semantics\n- ui unit: retry-until-success and give-up-after-budget","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxVTCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoO4QAFB0TQ2dmLSN/lJtwmdUogeO\nItw9q2gXasLzVpO6Uhm3g9a+AH3oz3VsdZb5kYjMcwHjlKjSWdYsSZsVQPfV7Ce/\n9xm5fh8ASUjra8Y5Q8sCOn+TZfelSo/FQT6C4MoZMoOKK7bqDEGOoIxTGWAneGa6\na6UK+0KqcEG9vupjbyAXbQatiKbpPlg2XAQo9exW7dLkRqeCvk4Al7xTLS9INcX9\niziMIDvRzVBkYRslzwbnHp5jSe/6dtjXcV5iLvCSe7hqx71hDQhEFhYjbPNYm1lg\nJqpPAuk+bgMmq2P/jycb5CTtvPD5l0gpQjhodq4s4W0QWA7S+gACut5PUkQ57UhQ\nGI74dpUPhukrHP2uZgZjcYwCqC9hIQW664xd1XwYi+Kv4pNNSnoVxI/VqIYOhAb/\nMGRi4E04QjMmZ1nBtVoo3UZAjMV5WdfyGxWfxZXymBlLkoyY1W5SL8oUR2/qq20K\n3Uh7xZTd6vjSn/o5RFYXxz2IzHk1yKBq9KuWvXLcYlXwHUtR8WkIHy+XUoIS0zkh\nwckSwJsGlmj54sT3mZl+OeJ4HpQkaTAzPty8HMBbMRjuei0LfHaOliCe6/5+xuG9\nIhP+7yDg31IjGc4jhubQh2CpSQYZeYi02enkCRLak0eky/ImQ8pZdRF94wBww5HJ\n4SLriG40GTVa3YYknuLG\n=tbJm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T20:06:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_ur