-published copy under the same content-derived version id, and the\nstaged-first bundle resolver served bytes whose SRI did not match the\nconfig''s pin.","tree":{"sha":"ebafe8316d6d372f1737d5da66e93642c8ec8234","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/ebafe8316d6d372f1737d5da66e93642c8ec8234"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/88d8ef53f4f8adb2f1ee62a0b055073b61e1d729","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/88d8ef53f4f8adb2f1ee62a0b055073b61e1d729","node_id":"C_kwDORq8oVtoAKDg4ZDhlZjUzZjRmOGFkYjJmMWVlNjJhMGIwNTUwNzNiNjFlMWQ3Mjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/cb2c1f188c39feab7ca990745708f93e71e18328","sha":"cb2c1f188c39feab7ca990745708f93e71e18328","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/cb2c1f188c39feab7ca990745708f93e71e18328"}],"sha":"88d8ef53f4f8adb2f1ee62a0b055073b61e1d729","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/88d8ef53f4f8adb2f1ee62a0b055073b61e1d729"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/cb2c1f188c39feab7ca990745708f93e71e18328/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T02:04:20Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T02:04:20Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"message":"fix(everything-dev): drop builtAt from version manifests — same version id must map to identical bytes\n\nThe version id is derived from the artifact coordinates with builtAt\nexcluded (republishing unchanged content is a pointer no-op), but the\nmanifest bytes embedded a per-build timestamp — the same version id then\nmapped to different bytes per build machine. The image''s staged copy of a\nworkspace''s version manifest carried the dist-builder stage''s timestamp\nwhile the config''s pin carried the train''s, so the staged-first bundle\nresolver served bytes whose SRI did not match the pin (SRI version\nmanifest integrity mismatch) and the boot died before loading anything.\nbuiltAt is now optional in the schema and omitted at compose time.","tree":{"sha":"59c784d00d73d67a805670363f182cb740d5bf8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/59c784d00d73d67a805670363f182cb740d5bf8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/cb2c1f188c39feab7ca990745708f93e71e18328","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/cb2c1f188c39feab7ca990745708f93e71e18328","node_id":"C_kwDORq8oVtoAKGNiMmMxZjE4OGMzOWZlYWI3Y2E5OTA3NDU3MDhmOTNlNzFlMTgzMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/7d8e54e8baa4ddf5a6c672e4e6dba5ee2617061a","sha":"7d8e54e8baa4ddf5a6c672e4e6dba5ee2617061a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/7d8e54e8baa4ddf5a6c672e4e6dba5ee2617061a"}],"sha":"cb2c1f188c39feab7ca990745708f93e71e18328","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/cb2c1f188c39feab7ca990745708f93e71e18328"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/7d8e54e8baa4ddf5a6c672e4e6dba5ee2617061a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:52:45Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T01:52:45Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"message":"fix(every-plugin): machine-independent module ids — named ids + data-URI path normalization\n\nrspack''s default deterministic module ids hash module identifiers that\nembed machine-absolute resource paths, so the same source built different\nid spaces on the host deploy train and inside the image''s dist-builder\nstage. A mixed-generation load — the CDN-pinned entry served the image''s\nstaged chunks (stable chunk filenames) — then spliced two incompatible id\nspaces and failed with __webpack_modules__[r] is not a function.\n\nModule ids are now named (context-relative requests), making the two\nbuilds semantically identical: verified per-workspace that the docker and\nhost builds agree on expose targets, consume-module id sets, and\nexpose-chunk module key sets, with expose chunks byte-identical.\nFixMfDataUriPlugin rewrites the data-URI runtime module''s machine-absolute\nnode_modules imports to bare specifiers (the composition aliases them back\nto on-disk copies for resolution, including the unexported\n@module-federation/node runtimePlugin subpath), and the ui rsbuild\nenvironments get the same aliases.","tree":{"sha":"ed0e68e5611387eac549e262e1b0d06bcfc324db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/ed0e68e5611387eac549e262e1b0d06bcfc324db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/7d8e54e8baa4ddf5a6c672e4e6dba5ee2617061a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/7d8e54e8baa4ddf5a6c672e4e6dba5ee2617061a","node_id":"C_kwDORq8oVtoAKDdkOGU1NGU4YmFhNGRkZjVhNmM2NzJlNGU2ZGJhNWVlMjYxNzA2MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/fd9be146f1a1e12a4f0219159d414b262ced45cc","sha":"fd9be146f1a1e12a4f0219159d414b262ced45cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/fd9be146f1a1e12a4f0219159d414b262ced45cc"}],"sha":"7d8e54e8baa4ddf5a6c672e4e6dba5ee2617061a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/7d8e54e8baa4ddf5a6c672e4e6dba5ee2617061a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/fd9be146f1a1e12a4f0219159d414b262ced45cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T00:48:17Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T00:48:17Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"message":"fix(every-plugin): register remotes under the container''s self name — node chunk loader entry-URL fallback\n\nThe node runtime''s chunk loading falls back to resolving chunk URLs from\nthe remote''s entry URL, keyed by the container''s own name\n(mf-manifest.json metaData.name). The service registered remotes under\nthe plugin id instead, so the fallback missed, resolveUrl returned null,\nand loadChunk handed back an empty chunk as if it had loaded — the\nexposed module then required ids nothing had registered\n(__webpack_modules__[r] is not a function). Registering and loading\nunder the container''s self name keeps that lookup a hit. An integration\ntest pins the fix via a mismatched host-side alias key.","tree":{"sha":"c9d1718939a744e0e7edfd1a117bb45a6269f35a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/c9d1718939a744e0e7edfd1a117bb45a6269f35a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/fd9be146f1a1e12a4f0219159d414b262ced45cc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/fd9be146f1a1e12a4f0219159d414b262ced45cc","node_id":"C_kwDORq8oVtoAKGZkOWJlMTQ2ZjFhMWUxMmE0ZjAyMTkxNTlkNDE0YjI2MmNlZDQ1Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/c23dfb6e5055c2af7279cfdf040f08e908e874fe","sha":"c23dfb6e5055c2af7279cfdf040f08e908e874fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/c23dfb6e5055c2af7279cfdf040f08e908e874fe"}],"sha":"fd9be146f1a1e12a4f0219159d414b262ced45cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/fd9be146f1a1e12a4f0219159d414b262ced45cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/c23dfb6e5055c2af7279cfdf040f08e908e874fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:57:55Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:57:55Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"message":"fix(every-plugin): disable splitChunks — rspack 2.x re-ids chunks behind MF get-factory codegen\n\nrspack 2.2.8''s default splitChunks re-ids the final chunk graph while the\nfederation get-factory codegen keeps pre-split ids: emitted container\nentries eagerly load chunks that were never emitted (554/842/920-class\nphantoms in every workspace), and the load-time failure surfaces as\n__webpack_modules__[r] is not a function. Splitting off keeps the emitted\nbundle self-consistent; ChunkCompletenessPlugin now fails the build loudly\nif any entry references an unemitted chunk.","tree":{"sha":"27462b678101cb6ddde83f358f26d7f2aaee9a18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/27462b678101cb6ddde83f358f26d7f2aaee9a18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/c23dfb6e5055c2af7279cfdf040f08e908e874fe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/c23dfb6e5055c2af7279cfdf040f08e908e874fe","node_id":"C_kwDORq8oVtoAKGMyM2RmYjZlNTA1NWMyYWY3Mjc5Y2ZkZjA0MGYwOGU5MDhlODc0ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/0a07bf26578d4f91baf8db0ba0c123fe1f59305d","sha":"0a07bf26578d4f91baf8db0ba0c123fe1f59305d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/0a07bf26578d4f91baf8db0ba0c123fe1f59305d"}],"sha":"c23dfb6e5055c2af7279cfdf040f08e908e874fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/c23dfb6e5055c2af7279cfdf040f08e908e874fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/0a07bf26578d4f91baf8db0ba0c123fe1f59305d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:07:38Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T23:07:38Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"message":"fix(every-plugin): log the deepest cause''s stack for plugin-load failures\n\nThe previous stack fix logged the PluginRuntimeError wrapper''s own frames —\nthe wrapping site, not the throw site. Walk the cause chain (mirroring\nclassifyPluginFailure''s walk) and log the deepest Error''s stack: the\noriginal failure inside the evaluated remote entry.","tree":{"sha":"95b15ba6ccc458b2cd80fe79d6a999ef1667936f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/95b15ba6ccc458b2cd80fe79d6a999ef1667936f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/0a07bf26578d4f91baf8db0ba0c123fe1f59305d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/0a07bf26578d4f91baf8db0ba0c123fe1f59305d","node_id":"C_kwDORq8oVtoAKDBhMDdiZjI2NTc4ZDRmOTFiYWY4ZGIwYmEwYzEyM2ZlMWY1OTMwNWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/784fcad104267fe7f570110dbcaf54d10abed872","sha":"784fcad104267fe7f570110dbcaf54d10abed872","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/784fcad104267fe7f570110dbcaf54d10abed872"}],"sha":"0a07bf26578d4f91baf8db0ba0c123fe1f59305d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/0a07bf26578d4f91baf8db0ba0c123fe1f59305d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/784fcad104267fe7f570110dbcaf54d10abed872/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T22:04:43Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T22:04:43Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"message":"fix(every-plugin): restore the v1-proven core sharing set; log plugin-load stacks\n\nThe v2 fleet-spec pass added @orpc/openapi, @orpc/experimental-effect, and\n@orpc/publisher to CORE_SHARED_DEPS and the runtime''s core module loaders —\nand the first-ever runtime load of the resulting bundle generation failed on\nsix of seven plugin bundles with \"__webpack_modules__[r] is not a function\"\n(image-smoke). The correlation is exact: every failing workspace imports\n@orpc/openapi; template — the only loader — does not (its failure is the\nsmoke env''s missing TEMPLATE_DATABASE_URL). The runtime''s import()-based\nshare provides hand the rspack consumer an ESM namespace object where a\nmodule factory is expected; consuming @orpc/openapi through the share scope\ncrashes the consumer''s module registry.\n\nThe v1 production bundle generation shared six core deps and loaded fine;\nthe three additions are the delta. They now leave CORE_SHARED_DEPS and the\ncoreModuleLoaders — declared in each workspace''s package.json (the\nphantom-dep fix stays) and bundled per workspace, matching v1''s proven\nshape. Bundle bytes are deterministic across build environments (identical\nremoteEntry hashes in the npm-children and pnpm-children CI runs), so this\nwas never a build-env issue — the bundles had simply never been\nruntime-tested: everything.dev still serves the old site.\n\nAlso: the plugin-load retry reporter now logs the failing error''s stack\nalongside the classified message — the message alone turned this diagnosis\ninto hours. The shared-identity gate compares only effect-critical names,\nso manifests from the 9-entry generation keep passing until the next\ndeploy publishes the shrunk set.","tree":{"sha":"028abcec78eec7787186aa1add5a53b9a0accacd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/028abcec78eec7787186aa1add5a53b9a0accacd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/784fcad104267fe7f570110dbcaf54d10abed872","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/784fcad104267fe7f570110dbcaf54d10abed872","node_id":"C_kwDORq8oVtoAKDc4NGZjYWQxMDQyNjdmZTdmNTcwMTEwZGJjYWY1NGQxMGFiZWQ4NzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/9191ab32bef072d070cde3efa8aecd5390f15a82","sha":"9191ab32bef072d070cde3efa8aecd5390f15a82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/9191ab32bef072d070cde3efa8aecd5390f15a82"}],"sha":"784fcad104267fe7f570110dbcaf54d10abed872","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/784fcad104267fe7f570110dbcaf54d10abed872"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/9191ab32bef072d070cde3efa8aecd5390f15a82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:24:15Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T19:24:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"v2-rc: pnpm workspace + node runtime cutover (ADR 0026), universal image thinning, de-brand sweep (#304)\n\n* feat(cli): authored bos.app.ts as canonical config form\n\nPrefer bos.app.ts over a legacy bos.config.json when both coexist\n(findConfigPath flip), so a generated write-back can no longer shadow\nthe authored descriptor.\n\nPublish (packages/everything-dev):\n- config-only publish on TS-form projects no longer crashes (ENOENT);\n  it merges authored hand-edits over the published FastKV config via\n  mergeAuthoredOverPublished — hand-edits win, live pipeline state\n  (bundle URLs, integrity) carries over. Aborts when the registry is\n  unreachable instead of publishing a URL-less payload.\n- deploy write-back is form-aware: pipeline state stays in FastKV for\n  TS-form; legacy JSON-form children keep their bos.config.json\n  write-back. FastKV key name unchanged.\n\nConfig-mutating commands (plugin add/remove, upgrade, registry use)\npersist to the authored form via the descriptor serializer (authored\nleaf + delta, no inherited values baked in); JSON-form children keep\ntheir file, with a null sentinel for removing parent-inherited plugins.\n\nSweep: hardcoded bos.config.json paths (status, mf check, shared-deps,\nbundle-fetch identity) moved to form-aware helpers; error wording\nneutralized behind a shared MISSING_CONFIG_MESSAGE; AGENTS.md,\nCONTRIBUTING.md, and skill docs updated to the canonical-form model.\n\n* feat(ui): durable cleanup — trim exposes, core-only fallback without compose payload, honest headers\n\n- drop the unconsumed ./providers and ./hooks web exposes (declare tables as exported constants)\n- core hydrate: construct the core-only tree from the app''s manifest when the\n  runtime config carries no (or a malformed) compose payload — plugin-free\n  CSR deployments no longer crash with ''no route tree''\n- trim ui globals ambient file to the rsbuild types reference\n- fix stale ownership/role headers (compose.ts, app.ts file-roles block)\n\n* feat(ui): invert router control — the authored router factory is load-bearing\n\n- coreHydrate gains createRouter/createQueryClient options (framework\n  factories stay the fallback for pre-migration stubs)\n- createServerRouterModule mints each request''s router through the same\n  authored factory (SSR parity); framework factory remains the fallback\n- app stubs pass the authored factory; router.tsx header reflects its\n  real role\n- unit seams: hydrate factory injection, SSR factory injection + fallback\n\n* feat(ui): bootstrap stubs are generated, not authored (ADR 0023)\n\n- every-plugin emits the five mechanical stubs (entry, hydrate, SSR router\n  module, compose expose, globals) as gitignored .gen files from the\n  installed package version, via the code-artifact generation pass\n- build surface retargets entries/exposes to the generated paths; core-ui\n  detection no longer requires an entry stub (it is generated)\n- sync drops the retired stub files from ownership and tolerates templates\n  that no longer ship a file (old-CLI + new-template transitional combo)\n- root .gitignore gains **/*.gen.tsx; parent ui switches to the generated\n  shape (authored router.tsx + app.ts remain)\n- unit seams: stub emitter (content contract + idempotence), expose/entry\n  retarget, detection marker; web+ssr build smoke green\n\n* refactor(ui): review fixes — shared AppRouterFactory, query-client parity, honest SSR fallback\n\n- extract AppRouterFactory into the shared types module (client hydrator\n  and SSR module mint through one declared factory shape)\n- wire the app''s createQueryClient seam end to end: authored router.tsx\n  exports it, generated hydrate + SSR stubs pass it, the SSR module mints\n  per-request clients through it\n- SSR renderToStream falls back to the request-local query client when the\n  injected factory returns none (queryClientRef no longer lies)\n- composeCoreOnly takes a plain PluginManifest list; app.ts file-roles text\n  reflects the load-bearing factory\n\n* feat(cli): sync stops managing ui source files — app ownership flip + stub retirement (ADR 0023)\n\n- FRAMEWORK_OWNED_SYNC_FILES drops every ui/src entry; config-level ui\n  files (package.json, tsconfig, postcss) stay framework-owned\n- RETIRED_SYNC_FILES migration: unmodified old stubs deleted silently,\n  hand-modified copies backed up then deleted; reported via the sync\n  result (retired / retiredConflicted) and the CLI output\n- tests rewritten for the new contract: ownership structure, retirement\n  unit seam, sync integration (config delivered, app sources never\n  re-added, stale stubs retired), prune (app-owned fallbacks prunable)\n\n* test(regression): pin plugin route chunk laziness in composed apps (ADR 0024)\n\n- start:ssr regression: boot the landing, client-navigate to the auth\n  plugin''s /login, assert new chunks from the auth remote''s origin load\n  on demand — closes ADR 0008''s flagged coupling for the composed client path\n- ADR 0024 corrected: laziness comes from the build''s code-splitter\n  (loader/component/pending/error/notFound split per match), not a\n  constructTree rewrite; deferring the eager policy modules requires\n  nav-as-manifest-data — deferred with the vocabulary work\n\n* fix(cli): sync/upgrade report retirement reliably — distinct backup dir, gate fixes\n\n- derive hasRetirement once; the report gate, the ''Already up to date''\n  check, and the upgrade renderer all include retiredConflicted\n- retired hand-modified backups report their own dir (retiredBackupDir)\n  instead of being overwritten by the main conflict backup\n- drop a duplicated ownership note in app.ts; name the remote-directory\n  derivation in the laziness spec\n\n* feat(manifest): contract v2 — virtual-file-routes vocabulary, enforced version, one identity (ADR 0024)\n\n- RouteRecord.type: ''route'' | ''layout'' | ''index'' replaces isLayout/isIndex\n  booleans; manifest version 2; mount registry 5 (digest invalidation)\n- parsePluginManifest guards every host manifest load; the compose payload\n  schema rejects a skewed major (client degrades to core-only instead of\n  silently mis-constructing)\n- folder-form composition key derives only from the plugins/<key> layout —\n  non-derivable keys fail the build loudly; the container-name fallback that\n  mis-keyed the ai manifest is gone (ai emits ''ai'', verified by rebuild)\n- fixtures/tests migrated: generator golden, construct, host compose suites\n\n* fix(ai): make the plugin workspace typecheck self-sufficient\n\nThe rebuilt gen files invalidated the typecheck cache and surfaced a latent\nbreak: the root program pulls the folder-form ui in through the contract\ngraph, so it needs the ui''s @/* fallback path, DOM lib, and the rsbuild\nambient declarations (styles.css side-effect imports).\n\n* docs(ui): the ui-integration skill describes the authored/generated split\n\n- the skill''s SSR architecture section now covers the app-owned router.tsx\n  (the policy seam: notFound/pending/error + query timings), the generated\n  .gen bootstrap set, and SSR parity through the same factory\n- stale source-list metadata dropped; ticket tracker closed for 01-04, 06, 07\n  with recorded outcomes; 05 stays open with its scope finding\n\n* fix(compose): close the identity loop + review fixes\n\n- the host compose fails loudly when a ui manifest names itself something\n  other than its config key (ADR 0008 §2''s invariant, now enforced) —\n  fixtures migrated off the container-name drift they modeled\n- one shared version-skew diagnostic formatter (parsePluginManifest +\n  the payload schema check)\n- nav-items'' manifest consumer migrates to the v2 type field (was a v1\n  consumer that only worked by accident)\n- trim the generated-config comment block; AGENTS.md gains the UI\n  ownership statement (authored surface vs generated stubs)\n\n* feat(compose): per-remote failure isolation — a broken plugin drops itself, not the app (ADR 0024 §5)\n\n- resolveComposableSources: manifest-level drops (fetch failure with no\n  last-good snapshot, unparsable content, identity mismatch) warn and\n  exclude the source; the core failing stays loud\n- composeUi digests the healthy set AFTER route-config isolation, in\n  canonical sorted order — the engine''s parity check and the client\n  payload agree by construction; server-side drops hydrate cleanly\n- the client hydrator pre-flights each remote''s routeConfig: a failed\n  remote drops only its routes (degraded compose -> client-render, since\n  the SSR''d tree included it); full parity still guards no-drop composes\n- known limitation (documented): a dropped mount-declaring source that\n  other sources'' routes parent onto still fails construction loudly\n\n* refactor(host): rememberVariant''s second param is the variant key, not the digest\n\n* fix(start): emit core ui bootstrap stubs in the container dist build\n\nThe container-build train (Dockerfile dist-builder — the regression fixture\nAND the deploy runtime image) ran bun run build:client in ui without the\ncode-artifact generation pass bos build performs first. On a clean checkout\nthe gitignored src/*.gen.* stubs (entry.gen.ts, hydrate.gen.tsx, …) are\nabsent from the build context and rspack fails with Module not found.\nEmit them via emitCoreUiStubs before the core ui builds (ADR 0023).\n\n* refactor: introduce typed Effect errors across host, CLI, and plugin runtimes\n\nPort of NEARBuilders/citynode.app#317 (host + packages only). Tagged\nerrors replace hand-rolled Error subclasses; every-plugin''s initialize\ncontract narrows to PluginRuntimeError; orchestrator schema-encodes\nBOS_RUNTIME_CONFIG (omitting undefined fields).\n\n* chore(release): enter changesets pre mode (rc) for the v2 release candidate\n\n- .changeset/pre.json: pre mode with tag rc; next `changeset version` run\n  versions the pending changesets as 2.0.0-rc.0 (everything-dev, host, ui,\n  auth-plugin, better-near-auth) and 3.0.0-rc.0 (every-plugin)\n- release.yml npm publish step: when pre mode is active, publish under the\n  prerelease dist-tag instead of the default `latest` (bare npm publish\n  would otherwise hijack latest with the RC)\n- release.yml GitHub Releases step: mark hyphenated versions as prereleases\n\n* chore: universal image thinning + de-brand sweep\n\n- DEPLOY=true at both deploy build sites: dist-first, map-free, shared identity stable (ADR 0018/0021)\n- runtime-image smoke gate (plain-node harness + CI job) with bounded-retry health/SSR/API + in-image mf check\n- pin enforcement no longer fires on configs without a production form (NODE_ENV=production boot crash)\n- unified bundle resolution: staged disk -> network, own-namespace miss never 404s, cache scoped to foreign namespaces; template dist out of the image (ADR 0021 amendment)\n- derived dev-only-deletion node_modules prune + platform filter (image 1268 -> 515 MB in verification builds)\n- de-brand: generic login copy in 4 locales, app_locale cookie, neutral regression artifact names, better-near-auth repo URLs\n- ADR 0025 (auth identity value classes)\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 01 — parent install cutover to pnpm (ADR 0026)\n\n- pnpm-workspace.yaml: workspace globs + verbatim catalog mirror; root package.json drops the workspaces block, packageManager -> pnpm@10.20.0\n- bunfig.toml + bun.lock deleted; .npmrc keeps the npm-ecosystem posture, pnpm settings live in pnpm-workspace.yaml\n- @effect/oxc becomes a link: dependency on the vendored repos/effect package; prepare script loses the symlink hack\n- nodeLinker: hoisted (ADR 0026 §4 escape hatch) — isolated layout splits better-auth peer-context identities across the plugin fleet; deferred as its own workstream\n- framework deps use workspace: protocol (pnpm does not link catalog-indirect specs); pnpm publish converts to ranges at release (ticket 05)\n- overrides align transitive singletons bun''s hoisting had masked: @better-fetch/fetch, better-auth, react/react-dom, @rspack/core\n- phantom deps declared: @orpc/openapi side-effect import (api + all plugins), react/react-dom (@types) for everything-dev + every-plugin tests\n- shared-deps sync + init catalog seeding + sync-catalog script read/write the yaml catalog (workspace-catalog module, unit-tested; package.json fallback for pre-v2 runtimes)\n- scaffold synthesizes the child workspaces list from the init sections (parent no longer carries workspaces)\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 02 — parent script surface on pnpm/node/tsx\n\n- CLI-from-source: node --import tsx --conditions=development (NODE_OPTIONS conditions replace bun flag chaining at the orchestrator level in ticket 06)\n- workspace-targeted scripts via pnpm filters (test:ui/api/e2e/framework, db:*)\n- bunx -> pnpm exec/dlx; regression helpers spawn node\n- verified: pnpm run typecheck/lint/sync-catalog/db:migrate/test:framework/test:regression:unit green; pnpm run dev boots the full stack\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 03 — CI workflows on pnpm + stray-bun guard\n\n- all five workflows: setup-bun -> pnpm/action-setup + node 24; installs use pnpm --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts with the explicit prepare step kept\n- bun audit -> pnpm audit --json with the same AUDIT_STRICT gating\n- stray-bun guard fails CI/deploy when bun.lock appears (ADR 0026 silent-revert footgun)\n- path filters track pnpm-lock.yaml/pnpm-workspace.yaml\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): api suite pass-with-no-tests (suite deleted upstream in V2 #293); host e2e helper skips gracefully without a generated bos.config.json\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 04 — universal image on node + pnpm (ADR 0026)\n\n- all five Dockerfile stages on node:24-alpine with pinned pnpm@10.20.0; no oven/bun base remains\n- runtime CMD boots bos start on node (in-process MF host loading — no child spawns on the start path)\n- dist-builder + deploy train workspace builds spawn npm run build; shared-deps catalog changes run pnpm install (build.ts, workspace.ts, dev-program.ts)\n- every-plugin bins: node + tsx re-exec (dev carries the development condition); non-dev commands run dist/cli.cjs when present, tsx + src fallback for the fresh-checkout bootstrap build\n- prune script reads workspace globs from pnpm-workspace.yaml\n- verified: runtime image boots through tier detection -> FastKV fetch -> pin gate (expected red until first pinned deploy); regression fixture image boots (health 200)\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): finish ticket 03 — CI job steps off bun\n\n- ci.yml: biome via pnpm exec, typecheck/test via pnpm filters, lockfile\n  cache key, playwright via pnpm exec (bun is no longer installed on runners)\n- release.yml: build via pnpm filter, stage-release-packages.ts via\n  node --import tsx (shebang corrected)\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 06 — orchestrator spawns node, conditions via env\n\n- dev services spawn through pnpm; the bun-flag chaining is deleted\n- workspace-root discovery reads pnpm-workspace.yaml first (package.json\n  workspaces stays the pre-v2 fallback) — fixes the prerequisite train\n  silently no-oping after the catalog moved, which is what failed CI''s\n  build-template jobs (every-plugin dist never built, generated rspack\n  config resolved a missing dist/identity.mjs)\n- upgrade typecheck + db-repair hints on pnpm; test fixtures on node/tsx\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): every-plugin bootstrap — tsx fallback keeps the development condition\n\n- the non-dev tsx fallback (fresh checkout, no dist) passes\n  --conditions=development like the dev path, so the config chain''s\n  self-imports resolve source over a missing dist\n- the rspack config chain''s identity import is relative (a package\n  self-import fell through to the default condition under node)\n- emitted bin shebangs are node\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 07 — scaffolds emit pnpm children\n\n- init writes pnpm-workspace.yaml (synthesized child globs + merged\n  catalog) and a packageManager field; the workspaces block leaves the\n  copied root manifest; the child root carries exactly the framework deps\n  (parent monorepo deps — workspace members, vendored links — never exist\n  in the child)\n- non-framework workspace: deps (better-near-auth) normalize to catalog:\n  in children — pnpm does not link catalog-indirect workspace members\n- installs run pnpm (--ignore-scripts on init, --force on upgrade); stray\n  lockfiles are removed so installs re-resolve; the copied prepare script\n  is stripped\n- a TS-form parent''s authored config is regenerated from the loaded\n  parent config — the copied bos.app.ts imports everything-dev and cannot\n  load before the child''s install; convertChildConfigToAppForm still\n  leaves the child on the authored TS form only\n- all generated scripts/prose reference pnpm; child CI templates on\n  pnpm/action-setup + node 24 + pnpm audit + stray-bun guard\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 08 — stray-bun sweep, regression harness on node, v2 changesets\n\n- regression harness spawns node --import tsx / pnpm (framework stack.go,\n  http regtest + seed_test, regression-env/start-stack/start-container,\n  playwright webServer); shebangs corrected\n- stray deps dropped: @types/bun + bun-types (root + every-plugin),\n  @effect/platform-bun, infra/bun.lock; ui generate-metadata script\n  (vestigial, target file gone); every-plugin scripts on node/tsx/pnpm;\n  host tsconfig drops the bun types entry\n- mf-config reads the package version via node:fs — createRequire came up\n  empty under tsx in spawned serves, reading 0.0.0 and tripping the\n  shared-identity check (un-breaks the dev-serve integration test)\n- AGENTS.md + workflows README on pnpm; intent-skills block runs\n  pnpm dlx; skill reference links converted to direct markdown links\n  (fixes the Check Skills CI validation)\n- changesets cut the v2 majors (rc pre mode) — the next publish also\n  ships the corrected every-plugin dist (published 2.10.1 carries a\n  broken @orpc/contract import that the source has since fixed)\n- ADRs left as history (review decision)\n\n* test(pnpm-v2): pin the init final form — authored bos.app.ts only, no bos.config.json left behind\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): link the plugin-client api-keys reference — the intent validation was hidden behind the everything-dev failures\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): test harness + dev-config loader off bun\n\n- dev-serve spawns the bin via process.execPath; the other suites spawn\n  pnpm run — bun is not installed on CI runners\n- loadDevConfig binds require via createRequire: a bare require only\n  exists under bun''s ESM, so node silently dropped the plugin.dev.ts dev\n  config (validate-config then failed on missing variables)\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): regression dev stacks run the CLI via node --import tsx\n\nThe stack spec fed cli.ts straight to spawn(process.execPath) — under bun\nthat ran TS natively; node needs the tsx loader hooks, and the development\ncondition keeps framework src resolution (ADR 0018). Also fix a leftover\nrunBunInstall spy name in the full-init test.\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): child workspace manifests carry the fleet pnpm posture\n\n- pnpm-workspace.yaml synthesis adds nodeLinker: hoisted (isolated splits\n  better-auth peer-context identities across the plugin fleet — ticket 05\n  deviation), linkWorkspacePackages, ignoreScripts, and the transitive\n  singleton overrides derived from the catalog\n- release staging resolves non-framework workspace: deps to their catalog\n  range (npm publish has no pnpm''s workspace:-rewriting); the test fixture\n  packer handles workspace:^ too\n- child types:gen runs the bos bin directly — node cannot execute pnpm''s\n  sh shim\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): start-mode readiness budgets to 5m — the pnpm image build + container boot outgrew the bun-era 2m windows\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): start-mode readiness budgets to 5m — the pnpm image build + container boot outgrew the bun-era 2m windows\n\n* fix(v2-rc): restore the storage upload route; smoke gate reads green until the first pinned deploy\n\nThe v2 re-scaffold (13119ad1) dropped the old api surface wholesale, taking\nPOST /api/storage/bundles with it — the endpoint the whole deploy train\nuploads through (CLI client, host body-limit/timeout scoping, and the\npending child-bundle-storage changeset all survived, but the handler was\ngone). Without it no `bos deploy` can complete, so no config ever gains\nversion-manifest pins and the image-smoke gate can never boot the registry\nconfig (\"pins no version manifest — redeploy required\").\n\n- api: restore the storage service (S3-compatible aws4fetch client with\n  transient retry, memory fallback, sha384 SRI, namespace/path validation)\n  and the uploadStorageBundle route: session/API-key auth, NEAR-principal\n  account pinning, path allowlist + traversal rejection, 64 MB ceiling,\n  4-way concurrent PUTs, server-computed integrity map; StorageLive joins\n  the initialize layer. Ported from the pre-v2 tree (13119ad1^).\n- catalog/api deps: re-add aws4fetch (^1.0.20, catalog-pinned)\n- bos.app.ts: declare BOS_STORAGE_* in the api plugin''s secrets;\n  .env.example gains the storage section (unset → memory; publish aborts)\n- ci.yml: move the transitional continue-on-error from the image-smoke job\n  to the smoke step (job-level still yields a failing check-run) and gate\n  artifact upload on failure() || steps.smoke.outcome == ''failure''\n- tests/smoke/runtime-image.mjs: in-image `bos mf check` runs node, not\n  bun — the pnpm-cutover image ships no bun, so the gate would fail at the\n  compat step even after a pinned deploy\n- tests: ported storage unit tests + new route-level integration tests\n  (auth pinning, traversal, happy path with SRI + backend disclosure)\n\n* fix(deploy): prerequisite builds run in the deploy build mode; build-train children run pnpm\n\nTwo deploy-train fixes landed after the first successful bootstrap deploy:\n\n1. Build-mode contract at one seam (ADR 0018). The deploy''s prerequisite\n   train (ensureFreshDeps, force=true on deploy) spawned its build children\n   with the invoking shell''s ambient env — no DEPLOY=true, no\n   NODE_ENV=production — while the target builds they precede get both\n   (build.ts). A bundler-config workspace in the prerequisite closure\n   (host, force-rebuilt via plugins/registry''s devDependency edge) loaded\n   its rsbuild config in source-first mode and died in jiti at config load\n   before any output — killing every deploy at the first attempt.\n   buildWorkspaceTargets now builds the mode env once and threads it\n   through both the prerequisite loop and the target loops;\n   ensureFreshDeps accepts an optional env (dev-time staleness rebuilds\n   keep the ambient env). \"DEPLOY=true at both deploy build sites\" is now\n   enforced structurally instead of duplicated.\n\n2. Build-train children run pnpm (ADR 0026 completion). The deploy CLI is\n   itself a pnpm run-script, so pnpm exported its workspace settings\n   (node-linker, catalog, link-workspace-packages, overrides, …) as\n   npm_config_* env vars — and every npm child warned `Unknown env\n   config`, one wall per workspace (npm''s next major drops unknown env\n   configs). buildCommands, the ensureFreshDeps spawn default, and the\n   container dist builder now spawn `pnpm run build`; pnpm children read\n   those settings natively.\n\nAlso drops the vestigial \"host\": \"workspace:*\" devDependency from\nplugins/registry — nothing imports host (verified across src, tests,\ntsconfig paths); it only dragged host into every deploy''s prerequisite\nclosure for a doomed duplicate build before the target phase rebuilt it\ncorrectly. The dep was a migration umbilical from the plugin-as-bosconfig\ncarve-out (d1a56cbd), carried through V2 (#293) and #309.\n\n.env.example regains the canonical generated form for the BOS_STORAGE_*\nsecrets (bos dev regenerates it from the declared secrets; bare values,\nno hand comments — prevents perpetual churn).","tree":{"sha":"938e354f7092c32f82fe1748d0dfd63bf1b2c14d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/938e354f7092c32f82fe1748d0dfd63bf1b2c14d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/9191ab32bef072d070cde3efa8aecd5390f15a82","verification":{"payload":"tree 938e354f7092c32f82fe1748d0dfd63bf1b2c14d\nparent 097b52e7a41354ce69ad8c3737ae73015b449524\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1791228255 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791228255 -0500\n\nv2-rc: pnpm workspace + node runtime cutover (ADR 0026), universal image thinning, de-brand sweep (#304)\n\n* feat(cli): authored bos.app.ts as canonical config form\n\nPrefer bos.app.ts over a legacy bos.config.json when both coexist\n(findConfigPath flip), so a generated write-back can no longer shadow\nthe authored descriptor.\n\nPublish (packages/everything-dev):\n- config-only publish on TS-form projects no longer crashes (ENOENT);\n  it merges authored hand-edits over the published FastKV config via\n  mergeAuthoredOverPublished — hand-edits win, live pipeline state\n  (bundle URLs, integrity) carries over. Aborts when the registry is\n  unreachable instead of publishing a URL-less payload.\n- deploy write-back is form-aware: pipeline state stays in FastKV for\n  TS-form; legacy JSON-form children keep their bos.config.json\n  write-back. FastKV key name unchanged.\n\nConfig-mutating commands (plugin add/remove, upgrade, registry use)\npersist to the authored form via the descriptor serializer (authored\nleaf + delta, no inherited values baked in); JSON-form children keep\ntheir file, with a null sentinel for removing parent-inherited plugins.\n\nSweep: hardcoded bos.config.json paths (status, mf check, shared-deps,\nbundle-fetch identity) moved to form-aware helpers; error wording\nneutralized behind a shared MISSING_CONFIG_MESSAGE; AGENTS.md,\nCONTRIBUTING.md, and skill docs updated to the canonical-form model.\n\n* feat(ui): durable cleanup — trim exposes, core-only fallback without compose payload, honest headers\n\n- drop the unconsumed ./providers and ./hooks web exposes (declare tables as exported constants)\n- core hydrate: construct the core-only tree from the app''s manifest when the\n  runtime config carries no (or a malformed) compose payload — plugin-free\n  CSR deployments no longer crash with ''no route tree''\n- trim ui globals ambient file to the rsbuild types reference\n- fix stale ownership/role headers (compose.ts, app.ts file-roles block)\n\n* feat(ui): invert router control — the authored router factory is load-bearing\n\n- coreHydrate gains createRouter/createQueryClient options (framework\n  factories stay the fallback for pre-migration stubs)\n- createServerRouterModule mints each request''s router through the same\n  authored factory (SSR parity); framework factory remains the fallback\n- app stubs pass the authored factory; router.tsx header reflects its\n  real role\n- unit seams: hydrate factory injection, SSR factory injection + fallback\n\n* feat(ui): bootstrap stubs are generated, not authored (ADR 0023)\n\n- every-plugin emits the five mechanical stubs (entry, hydrate, SSR router\n  module, compose expose, globals) as gitignored .gen files from the\n  installed package version, via the code-artifact generation pass\n- build surface retargets entries/exposes to the generated paths; core-ui\n  detection no longer requires an entry stub (it is generated)\n- sync drops the retired stub files from ownership and tolerates templates\n  that no longer ship a file (old-CLI + new-template transitional combo)\n- root .gitignore gains **/*.gen.tsx; parent ui switches to the generated\n  shape (authored router.tsx + app.ts remain)\n- unit seams: stub emitter (content contract + idempotence), expose/entry\n  retarget, detection marker; web+ssr build smoke green\n\n* refactor(ui): review fixes — shared AppRouterFactory, query-client parity, honest SSR fallback\n\n- extract AppRouterFactory into the shared types module (client hydrator\n  and SSR module mint through one declared factory shape)\n- wire the app''s createQueryClient seam end to end: authored router.tsx\n  exports it, generated hydrate + SSR stubs pass it, the SSR module mints\n  per-request clients through it\n- SSR renderToStream falls back to the request-local query client when the\n  injected factory returns none (queryClientRef no longer lies)\n- composeCoreOnly takes a plain PluginManifest list; app.ts file-roles text\n  reflects the load-bearing factory\n\n* feat(cli): sync stops managing ui source files — app ownership flip + stub retirement (ADR 0023)\n\n- FRAMEWORK_OWNED_SYNC_FILES drops every ui/src entry; config-level ui\n  files (package.json, tsconfig, postcss) stay framework-owned\n- RETIRED_SYNC_FILES migration: unmodified old stubs deleted silently,\n  hand-modified copies backed up then deleted; reported via the sync\n  result (retired / retiredConflicted) and the CLI output\n- tests rewritten for the new contract: ownership structure, retirement\n  unit seam, sync integration (config delivered, app sources never\n  re-added, stale stubs retired), prune (app-owned fallbacks prunable)\n\n* test(regression): pin plugin route chunk laziness in composed apps (ADR 0024)\n\n- start:ssr regression: boot the landing, client-navigate to the auth\n  plugin''s /login, assert new chunks from the auth remote''s origin load\n  on demand — closes ADR 0008''s flagged coupling for the composed client path\n- ADR 0024 corrected: laziness comes from the build''s code-splitter\n  (loader/component/pending/error/notFound split per match), not a\n  constructTree rewrite; deferring the eager policy modules requires\n  nav-as-manifest-data — deferred with the vocabulary work\n\n* fix(cli): sync/upgrade report retirement reliably — distinct backup dir, gate fixes\n\n- derive hasRetirement once; the report gate, the ''Already up to date''\n  check, and the upgrade renderer all include retiredConflicted\n- retired hand-modified backups report their own dir (retiredBackupDir)\n  instead of being overwritten by the main conflict backup\n- drop a duplicated ownership note in app.ts; name the remote-directory\n  derivation in the laziness spec\n\n* feat(manifest): contract v2 — virtual-file-routes vocabulary, enforced version, one identity (ADR 0024)\n\n- RouteRecord.type: ''route'' | ''layout'' | ''index'' replaces isLayout/isIndex\n  booleans; manifest version 2; mount registry 5 (digest invalidation)\n- parsePluginManifest guards every host manifest load; the compose payload\n  schema rejects a skewed major (client degrades to core-only instead of\n  silently mis-constructing)\n- folder-form composition key derives only from the plugins/<key> layout —\n  non-derivable keys fail the build loudly; the container-name fallback that\n  mis-keyed the ai manifest is gone (ai emits ''ai'', verified by rebuild)\n- fixtures/tests migrated: generator golden, construct, host compose suites\n\n* fix(ai): make the plugin workspace typecheck self-sufficient\n\nThe rebuilt gen files invalidated the typecheck cache and surfaced a latent\nbreak: the root program pulls the folder-form ui in through the contract\ngraph, so it needs the ui''s @/* fallback path, DOM lib, and the rsbuild\nambient declarations (styles.css side-effect imports).\n\n* docs(ui): the ui-integration skill describes the authored/generated split\n\n- the skill''s SSR architecture section now covers the app-owned router.tsx\n  (the policy seam: notFound/pending/error + query timings), the generated\n  .gen bootstrap set, and SSR parity through the same factory\n- stale source-list metadata dropped; ticket tracker closed for 01-04, 06, 07\n  with recorded outcomes; 05 stays open with its scope finding\n\n* fix(compose): close the identity loop + review fixes\n\n- the host compose fails loudly when a ui manifest names itself something\n  other than its config key (ADR 0008 §2''s invariant, now enforced) —\n  fixtures migrated off the container-name drift they modeled\n- one shared version-skew diagnostic formatter (parsePluginManifest +\n  the payload schema check)\n- nav-items'' manifest consumer migrates to the v2 type field (was a v1\n  consumer that only worked by accident)\n- trim the generated-config comment block; AGENTS.md gains the UI\n  ownership statement (authored surface vs generated stubs)\n\n* feat(compose): per-remote failure isolation — a broken plugin drops itself, not the app (ADR 0024 §5)\n\n- resolveComposableSources: manifest-level drops (fetch failure with no\n  last-good snapshot, unparsable content, identity mismatch) warn and\n  exclude the source; the core failing stays loud\n- composeUi digests the healthy set AFTER route-config isolation, in\n  canonical sorted order — the engine''s parity check and the client\n  payload agree by construction; server-side drops hydrate cleanly\n- the client hydrator pre-flights each remote''s routeConfig: a failed\n  remote drops only its routes (degraded compose -> client-render, since\n  the SSR''d tree included it); full parity still guards no-drop composes\n- known limitation (documented): a dropped mount-declaring source that\n  other sources'' routes parent onto still fails construction loudly\n\n* refactor(host): rememberVariant''s second param is the variant key, not the digest\n\n* fix(start): emit core ui bootstrap stubs in the container dist build\n\nThe container-build train (Dockerfile dist-builder — the regression fixture\nAND the deploy runtime image) ran bun run build:client in ui without the\ncode-artifact generation pass bos build performs first. On a clean checkout\nthe gitignored src/*.gen.* stubs (entry.gen.ts, hydrate.gen.tsx, …) are\nabsent from the build context and rspack fails with Module not found.\nEmit them via emitCoreUiStubs before the core ui builds (ADR 0023).\n\n* refactor: introduce typed Effect errors across host, CLI, and plugin runtimes\n\nPort of NEARBuilders/citynode.app#317 (host + packages only). Tagged\nerrors replace hand-rolled Error subclasses; every-plugin''s initialize\ncontract narrows to PluginRuntimeError; orchestrator schema-encodes\nBOS_RUNTIME_CONFIG (omitting undefined fields).\n\n* chore(release): enter changesets pre mode (rc) for the v2 release candidate\n\n- .changeset/pre.json: pre mode with tag rc; next `changeset version` run\n  versions the pending changesets as 2.0.0-rc.0 (everything-dev, host, ui,\n  auth-plugin, better-near-auth) and 3.0.0-rc.0 (every-plugin)\n- release.yml npm publish step: when pre mode is active, publish under the\n  prerelease dist-tag instead of the default `latest` (bare npm publish\n  would otherwise hijack latest with the RC)\n- release.yml GitHub Releases step: mark hyphenated versions as prereleases\n\n* chore: universal image thinning + de-brand sweep\n\n- DEPLOY=true at both deploy build sites: dist-first, map-free, shared identity stable (ADR 0018/0021)\n- runtime-image smoke gate (plain-node harness + CI job) with bounded-retry health/SSR/API + in-image mf check\n- pin enforcement no longer fires on configs without a production form (NODE_ENV=production boot crash)\n- unified bundle resolution: staged disk -> network, own-namespace miss never 404s, cache scoped to foreign namespaces; template dist out of the image (ADR 0021 amendment)\n- derived dev-only-deletion node_modules prune + platform filter (image 1268 -> 515 MB in verification builds)\n- de-brand: generic login copy in 4 locales, app_locale cookie, neutral regression artifact names, better-near-auth repo URLs\n- ADR 0025 (auth identity value classes)\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 01 — parent install cutover to pnpm (ADR 0026)\n\n- pnpm-workspace.yaml: workspace globs + verbatim catalog mirror; root package.json drops the workspaces block, packageManager -> pnpm@10.20.0\n- bunfig.toml + bun.lock deleted; .npmrc keeps the npm-ecosystem posture, pnpm settings live in pnpm-workspace.yaml\n- @effect/oxc becomes a link: dependency on the vendored repos/effect package; prepare script loses the symlink hack\n- nodeLinker: hoisted (ADR 0026 §4 escape hatch) — isolated layout splits better-auth peer-context identities across the plugin fleet; deferred as its own workstream\n- framework deps use workspace: protocol (pnpm does not link catalog-indirect specs); pnpm publish converts to ranges at release (ticket 05)\n- overrides align transitive singletons bun''s hoisting had masked: @better-fetch/fetch, better-auth, react/react-dom, @rspack/core\n- phantom deps declared: @orpc/openapi side-effect import (api + all plugins), react/react-dom (@types) for everything-dev + every-plugin tests\n- shared-deps sync + init catalog seeding + sync-catalog script read/write the yaml catalog (workspace-catalog module, unit-tested; package.json fallback for pre-v2 runtimes)\n- scaffold synthesizes the child workspaces list from the init sections (parent no longer carries workspaces)\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 02 — parent script surface on pnpm/node/tsx\n\n- CLI-from-source: node --import tsx --conditions=development (NODE_OPTIONS conditions replace bun flag chaining at the orchestrator level in ticket 06)\n- workspace-targeted scripts via pnpm filters (test:ui/api/e2e/framework, db:*)\n- bunx -> pnpm exec/dlx; regression helpers spawn node\n- verified: pnpm run typecheck/lint/sync-catalog/db:migrate/test:framework/test:regression:unit green; pnpm run dev boots the full stack\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 03 — CI workflows on pnpm + stray-bun guard\n\n- all five workflows: setup-bun -> pnpm/action-setup + node 24; installs use pnpm --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts with the explicit prepare step kept\n- bun audit -> pnpm audit --json with the same AUDIT_STRICT gating\n- stray-bun guard fails CI/deploy when bun.lock appears (ADR 0026 silent-revert footgun)\n- path filters track pnpm-lock.yaml/pnpm-workspace.yaml\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): api suite pass-with-no-tests (suite deleted upstream in V2 #293); host e2e helper skips gracefully without a generated bos.config.json\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 04 — universal image on node + pnpm (ADR 0026)\n\n- all five Dockerfile stages on node:24-alpine with pinned pnpm@10.20.0; no oven/bun base remains\n- runtime CMD boots bos start on node (in-process MF host loading — no child spawns on the start path)\n- dist-builder + deploy train workspace builds spawn npm run build; shared-deps catalog changes run pnpm install (build.ts, workspace.ts, dev-program.ts)\n- every-plugin bins: node + tsx re-exec (dev carries the development condition); non-dev commands run dist/cli.cjs when present, tsx + src fallback for the fresh-checkout bootstrap build\n- prune script reads workspace globs from pnpm-workspace.yaml\n- verified: runtime image boots through tier detection -> FastKV fetch -> pin gate (expected red until first pinned deploy); regression fixture image boots (health 200)\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): finish ticket 03 — CI job steps off bun\n\n- ci.yml: biome via pnpm exec, typecheck/test via pnpm filters, lockfile\n  cache key, playwright via pnpm exec (bun is no longer installed on runners)\n- release.yml: build via pnpm filter, stage-release-packages.ts via\n  node --import tsx (shebang corrected)\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 06 — orchestrator spawns node, conditions via env\n\n- dev services spawn through pnpm; the bun-flag chaining is deleted\n- workspace-root discovery reads pnpm-workspace.yaml first (package.json\n  workspaces stays the pre-v2 fallback) — fixes the prerequisite train\n  silently no-oping after the catalog moved, which is what failed CI''s\n  build-template jobs (every-plugin dist never built, generated rspack\n  config resolved a missing dist/identity.mjs)\n- upgrade typecheck + db-repair hints on pnpm; test fixtures on node/tsx\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): every-plugin bootstrap — tsx fallback keeps the development condition\n\n- the non-dev tsx fallback (fresh checkout, no dist) passes\n  --conditions=development like the dev path, so the config chain''s\n  self-imports resolve source over a missing dist\n- the rspack config chain''s identity import is relative (a package\n  self-import fell through to the default condition under node)\n- emitted bin shebangs are node\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 07 — scaffolds emit pnpm children\n\n- init writes pnpm-workspace.yaml (synthesized child globs + merged\n  catalog) and a packageManager field; the workspaces block leaves the\n  copied root manifest; the child root carries exactly the framework deps\n  (parent monorepo deps — workspace members, vendored links — never exist\n  in the child)\n- non-framework workspace: deps (better-near-auth) normalize to catalog:\n  in children — pnpm does not link catalog-indirect workspace members\n- installs run pnpm (--ignore-scripts on init, --force on upgrade); stray\n  lockfiles are removed so installs re-resolve; the copied prepare script\n  is stripped\n- a TS-form parent''s authored config is regenerated from the loaded\n  parent config — the copied bos.app.ts imports everything-dev and cannot\n  load before the child''s install; convertChildConfigToAppForm still\n  leaves the child on the authored TS form only\n- all generated scripts/prose reference pnpm; child CI templates on\n  pnpm/action-setup + node 24 + pnpm audit + stray-bun guard\n\n* feat(pnpm-v2): ticket 08 — stray-bun sweep, regression harness on node, v2 changesets\n\n- regression harness spawns node --import tsx / pnpm (framework stack.go,\n  http regtest + seed_test, regression-env/start-stack/start-container,\n  playwright webServer); shebangs corrected\n- stray deps dropped: @types/bun + bun-types (root + every-plugin),\n  @effect/platform-bun, infra/bun.lock; ui generate-metadata script\n  (vestigial, target file gone); every-plugin scripts on node/tsx/pnpm;\n  host tsconfig drops the bun types entry\n- mf-config reads the package version via node:fs — createRequire came up\n  empty under tsx in spawned serves, reading 0.0.0 and tripping the\n  shared-identity check (un-breaks the dev-serve integration test)\n- AGENTS.md + workflows README on pnpm; intent-skills block runs\n  pnpm dlx; skill reference links converted to direct markdown links\n  (fixes the Check Skills CI validation)\n- changesets cut the v2 majors (rc pre mode) — the next publish also\n  ships the corrected every-plugin dist (published 2.10.1 carries a\n  broken @orpc/contract import that the source has since fixed)\n- ADRs left as history (review decision)\n\n* test(pnpm-v2): pin the init final form — authored bos.app.ts only, no bos.config.json left behind\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): link the plugin-client api-keys reference — the intent validation was hidden behind the everything-dev failures\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): test harness + dev-config loader off bun\n\n- dev-serve spawns the bin via process.execPath; the other suites spawn\n  pnpm run — bun is not installed on CI runners\n- loadDevConfig binds require via createRequire: a bare require only\n  exists under bun''s ESM, so node silently dropped the plugin.dev.ts dev\n  config (validate-config then failed on missing variables)\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): regression dev stacks run the CLI via node --import tsx\n\nThe stack spec fed cli.ts straight to spawn(process.execPath) — under bun\nthat ran TS natively; node needs the tsx loader hooks, and the development\ncondition keeps framework src resolution (ADR 0018). Also fix a leftover\nrunBunInstall spy name in the full-init test.\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): child workspace manifests carry the fleet pnpm posture\n\n- pnpm-workspace.yaml synthesis adds nodeLinker: hoisted (isolated splits\n  better-auth peer-context identities across the plugin fleet — ticket 05\n  deviation), linkWorkspacePackages, ignoreScripts, and the transitive\n  singleton overrides derived from the catalog\n- release staging resolves non-framework workspace: deps to their catalog\n  range (npm publish has no pnpm''s workspace:-rewriting); the test fixture\n  packer handles workspace:^ too\n- child types:gen runs the bos bin directly — node cannot execute pnpm''s\n  sh shim\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): start-mode readiness budgets to 5m — the pnpm image build + container boot outgrew the bun-era 2m windows\n\n* fix(pnpm-v2): start-mode readiness budgets to 5m — the pnpm image build + container boot outgrew the bun-era 2m windows\n\n* fix(v2-rc): restore the storage upload route; smoke gate reads green until the first pinned deploy\n\nThe v2 re-scaffold (13119ad1) dropped the old api surface wholesale, taking\nPOST /api/storage/bundles with it — the endpoint the whole deploy train\nuploads through (CLI client, host body-limit/timeout scoping, and the\npending child-bundle-storage changeset all survived, but the handler was\ngone). Without it no `bos deploy` can complete, so no config ever gains\nversion-manifest pins and the image-smoke gate can never boot the registry\nconfig (\"pins no version manifest — redeploy required\").\n\n- api: restore the storage service (S3-compatible aws4fetch client with\n  transient retry, memory fallback, sha384 SRI, namespace/path validation)\n  and the uploadStorageBundle route: session/API-key auth, NEAR-principal\n  account pinning, path allowlist + traversal rejection, 64 MB ceiling,\n  4-way concurrent PUTs, server-computed integrity map; StorageLive joins\n  the initialize layer. Ported from the pre-v2 tree (13119ad1^).\n- catalog/api deps: re-add aws4fetch (^1.0.20, catalog-pinned)\n- bos.app.ts: declare BOS_STORAGE_* in the api plugin''s secrets;\n  .env.example gains the storage section (unset → memory; publish aborts)\n- ci.yml: move the transitional continue-on-error from the image-smoke job\n  to the smoke step (job-level still yields a failing check-run) and gate\n  artifact upload on failure() || steps.smoke.outcome == ''failure''\n- tests/smoke/runtime-image.mjs: in-image `bos mf check` runs node, not\n  bun — the pnpm-cutover image ships no bun, so the gate would fail at the\n  compat step even after a pinned deploy\n- tests: ported storage unit tests + new route-level integration tests\n  (auth pinning, traversal, happy path with SRI + backend disclosure)\n\n* fix(deploy): prerequisite builds run in the deploy build mode; build-train children run pnpm\n\nTwo deploy-train fixes landed after the first successful bootstrap deploy:\n\n1. Build-mode contract at one seam (ADR 0018). The deploy''s prerequisite\n   train (ensureFreshDeps, force=true on deploy) spawned its build children\n   with the invoking shell''s ambient env — no DEPLOY=true, no\n   NODE_ENV=production — while the target builds they precede get both\n   (build.ts). A bundler-config workspace in the prerequisite closure\n   (host, force-rebuilt via plugins/registry''s devDependency edge) loaded\n   its rsbuild config in source-first mode and died in jiti at config load\n   before any output — killing every deploy at the first attempt.\n   buildWorkspaceTargets now builds the mode env once and threads it\n   through both the prerequisite loop and the target loops;\n   ensureFreshDeps accepts an optional env (dev-time staleness rebuilds\n   keep the ambient env). \"DEPLOY=true at both deploy build sites\" is now\n   enforced structurally instead of duplicated.\n\n2. Build-train children run pnpm (ADR 0026 completion). The deploy CLI is\n   itself a pnpm run-script, so pnpm exported its workspace settings\n   (node-linker, catalog, link-workspace-packages, overrides, …) as\n   npm_config_* env vars — and every npm child warned `Unknown env\n   config`, one wall per workspace (npm''s next major drops unknown env\n   configs). buildCommands, the ensureFreshDeps spawn default, and the\n   container dist builder now spawn `pnpm run build`; pnpm children read\n   those settings natively.\n\nAlso drops the vestigial \"host\": \"workspace:*\" devDependency from\nplugins/registry — nothing imports host (verified across src, tests,\ntsconfig paths); it only dragged host into every deploy''s prerequisite\nclosure for a doomed duplicate build before the target phase rebuilt it\ncorrectly. The dep was a migration umbilical from the plugin-as-bosconfig\ncarve-out (d1a56cbd), carried through V2 (#293) and #309.\n\n.env.example regains the canonical generated form for the BOS_STORAGE_*\nsecrets (bos dev regenerates it from the declared secrets; bare values,\nno hand comments — prevents perpetual churn).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw/lfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeXAQAFbreVJK9V5skXUuEWXjOWIn\nMDy7Sx0SDDLhfd0C8aZud5HMiSxowo+TiRPuXnpx1Z9opHzzzyEgC+nnMxqK1g8x\n1SV7KqhwoSW+jIMltAu9KSAwtk445bT4dctSLxIiWFz8dawo56VI+nru5vFwREzn\nGm/jvXPLHQEDaRADsa9/tvkblHroDG39mOWYnbdA3gliLzCKnXWeSAixlDHpSJdw\njxAFX17a7jOfkjnqbwALmoD5pxx3fSFR6ksHUa6TWOs28Db4VV6FxbTmi1ioPMwG\nLIZPv/kVso8ClfVClQDHfrFSeWyY8127fuNSvjCGnuLbugyU03IfUNfuHqivPkgv\nY1l1JB6m8meLLSZnUS+ZiTZdSSegGCTP04xS2DN+Kl3JAr9ZVIRCNBzJQWFb5omB\nNU7bOokwBow1tt8ETSSE4G81S7OfmhOzXR3VQ+8k++iEN0VBdg+ju0guJx5z3j4Q\nzBWPtSuok1j8nECvH9QL+rlf9kY1zlnUuidpeBXw2FpRNmSvBBjE4btLhQX8pXJA\ngpMgsdTH+eM9JuWnG333/HT60vKXdJPKFkavcF4ejcH0ftgW657RRmXMUi38srGI\npEOoHiZmNeIMPkzwaJ+hVO85ATLIbHpLjgXB3UAHAUtfBw1gKI9/7fdsYDXl2vjK\n7wdNCaeuNcrvrC9ntiqt\n=TMl8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T19:24:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/9191ab32bef072d070cde3efa8aecd5390f15a82","node_id":"C_kwDORq8oVtoAKDkxOTFhYjMyYmVmMDcyZDA3MGNkZTNlZmE4YWVjZDUzOTBmMTVhODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/097b52e7a41354ce69ad8c3737ae73015b449524","sha":"097b52e7a41354ce69ad8c3737ae73015b449524","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/097b52e7a41354ce69ad8c3737ae73015b449524"}],"sha":"9191ab32bef072d070cde3efa8aecd5390f15a82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/9191ab32bef072d070cde3efa8aecd5390f15a82"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/097b52e7a41354ce69ad8c3737ae73015b449524/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T01:04:36Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T01:04:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(release): enter changesets pre mode (rc) for the v2 release candidate (#303)\n\n- .changeset/pre.json: pre mode with tag rc; next `changeset version` run\n  versions the pending changesets as 2.0.0-rc.0 (everything-dev, host, ui,\n  auth-plugin, better-near-auth) and 3.0.0-rc.0 (every-plugin)\n- release.yml npm publish step: when pre mode is active, publish under the\n  prerelease dist-tag instead of the default `latest` (bare npm publish\n  would otherwise hijack latest with the RC)\n- release.yml GitHub Releases step: mark hyphenated versions as prereleases","tree":{"sha":"0d11345ead6332535e10f73d120144fa7d2f0597","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/0d11345ead6332535e10f73d120144fa7d2f0597"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/097b52e7a41354ce69ad8c3737ae73015b449524","verification":{"payload":"tree 0d11345ead6332535e10f73d120144fa7d2f0597\nparent 8a06f6b7884bbf755347550688815d983b416ffc\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbrae