528d0b08599936c982c52cd0ee9c00"}],"sha":"8a06f6b7884bbf755347550688815d983b416ffc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/8a06f6b7884bbf755347550688815d983b416ffc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/f9d2dce029528d0b08599936c982c52cd0ee9c00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T01:04:35Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T01:04:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(ui): authored router + generated bootstrap stubs — the framework owns zero ui source files (ADR 0023/0024) (#300)\n\n* feat(ui): durable cleanup — trim exposes, core-only fallback without compose payload, honest headers\n\n- drop the unconsumed ./providers and ./hooks web exposes (declare tables as exported constants)\n- core hydrate: construct the core-only tree from the app''s manifest when the\n  runtime config carries no (or a malformed) compose payload — plugin-free\n  CSR deployments no longer crash with ''no route tree''\n- trim ui globals ambient file to the rsbuild types reference\n- fix stale ownership/role headers (compose.ts, app.ts file-roles block)\n\n* feat(ui): invert router control — the authored router factory is load-bearing\n\n- coreHydrate gains createRouter/createQueryClient options (framework\n  factories stay the fallback for pre-migration stubs)\n- createServerRouterModule mints each request''s router through the same\n  authored factory (SSR parity); framework factory remains the fallback\n- app stubs pass the authored factory; router.tsx header reflects its\n  real role\n- unit seams: hydrate factory injection, SSR factory injection + fallback\n\n* feat(ui): bootstrap stubs are generated, not authored (ADR 0023)\n\n- every-plugin emits the five mechanical stubs (entry, hydrate, SSR router\n  module, compose expose, globals) as gitignored .gen files from the\n  installed package version, via the code-artifact generation pass\n- build surface retargets entries/exposes to the generated paths; core-ui\n  detection no longer requires an entry stub (it is generated)\n- sync drops the retired stub files from ownership and tolerates templates\n  that no longer ship a file (old-CLI + new-template transitional combo)\n- root .gitignore gains **/*.gen.tsx; parent ui switches to the generated\n  shape (authored router.tsx + app.ts remain)\n- unit seams: stub emitter (content contract + idempotence), expose/entry\n  retarget, detection marker; web+ssr build smoke green\n\n* refactor(ui): review fixes — shared AppRouterFactory, query-client parity, honest SSR fallback\n\n- extract AppRouterFactory into the shared types module (client hydrator\n  and SSR module mint through one declared factory shape)\n- wire the app''s createQueryClient seam end to end: authored router.tsx\n  exports it, generated hydrate + SSR stubs pass it, the SSR module mints\n  per-request clients through it\n- SSR renderToStream falls back to the request-local query client when the\n  injected factory returns none (queryClientRef no longer lies)\n- composeCoreOnly takes a plain PluginManifest list; app.ts file-roles text\n  reflects the load-bearing factory\n\n* feat(cli): sync stops managing ui source files — app ownership flip + stub retirement (ADR 0023)\n\n- FRAMEWORK_OWNED_SYNC_FILES drops every ui/src entry; config-level ui\n  files (package.json, tsconfig, postcss) stay framework-owned\n- RETIRED_SYNC_FILES migration: unmodified old stubs deleted silently,\n  hand-modified copies backed up then deleted; reported via the sync\n  result (retired / retiredConflicted) and the CLI output\n- tests rewritten for the new contract: ownership structure, retirement\n  unit seam, sync integration (config delivered, app sources never\n  re-added, stale stubs retired), prune (app-owned fallbacks prunable)\n\n* test(regression): pin plugin route chunk laziness in composed apps (ADR 0024)\n\n- start:ssr regression: boot the landing, client-navigate to the auth\n  plugin''s /login, assert new chunks from the auth remote''s origin load\n  on demand — closes ADR 0008''s flagged coupling for the composed client path\n- ADR 0024 corrected: laziness comes from the build''s code-splitter\n  (loader/component/pending/error/notFound split per match), not a\n  constructTree rewrite; deferring the eager policy modules requires\n  nav-as-manifest-data — deferred with the vocabulary work\n\n* fix(cli): sync/upgrade report retirement reliably — distinct backup dir, gate fixes\n\n- derive hasRetirement once; the report gate, the ''Already up to date''\n  check, and the upgrade renderer all include retiredConflicted\n- retired hand-modified backups report their own dir (retiredBackupDir)\n  instead of being overwritten by the main conflict backup\n- drop a duplicated ownership note in app.ts; name the remote-directory\n  derivation in the laziness spec\n\n* feat(manifest): contract v2 — virtual-file-routes vocabulary, enforced version, one identity (ADR 0024)\n\n- RouteRecord.type: ''route'' | ''layout'' | ''index'' replaces isLayout/isIndex\n  booleans; manifest version 2; mount registry 5 (digest invalidation)\n- parsePluginManifest guards every host manifest load; the compose payload\n  schema rejects a skewed major (client degrades to core-only instead of\n  silently mis-constructing)\n- folder-form composition key derives only from the plugins/<key> layout —\n  non-derivable keys fail the build loudly; the container-name fallback that\n  mis-keyed the ai manifest is gone (ai emits ''ai'', verified by rebuild)\n- fixtures/tests migrated: generator golden, construct, host compose suites\n\n* fix(ai): make the plugin workspace typecheck self-sufficient\n\nThe rebuilt gen files invalidated the typecheck cache and surfaced a latent\nbreak: the root program pulls the folder-form ui in through the contract\ngraph, so it needs the ui''s @/* fallback path, DOM lib, and the rsbuild\nambient declarations (styles.css side-effect imports).\n\n* docs(ui): the ui-integration skill describes the authored/generated split\n\n- the skill''s SSR architecture section now covers the app-owned router.tsx\n  (the policy seam: notFound/pending/error + query timings), the generated\n  .gen bootstrap set, and SSR parity through the same factory\n- stale source-list metadata dropped; ticket tracker closed for 01-04, 06, 07\n  with recorded outcomes; 05 stays open with its scope finding\n\n* fix(compose): close the identity loop + review fixes\n\n- the host compose fails loudly when a ui manifest names itself something\n  other than its config key (ADR 0008 §2''s invariant, now enforced) —\n  fixtures migrated off the container-name drift they modeled\n- one shared version-skew diagnostic formatter (parsePluginManifest +\n  the payload schema check)\n- nav-items'' manifest consumer migrates to the v2 type field (was a v1\n  consumer that only worked by accident)\n- trim the generated-config comment block; AGENTS.md gains the UI\n  ownership statement (authored surface vs generated stubs)\n\n* feat(compose): per-remote failure isolation — a broken plugin drops itself, not the app (ADR 0024 §5)\n\n- resolveComposableSources: manifest-level drops (fetch failure with no\n  last-good snapshot, unparsable content, identity mismatch) warn and\n  exclude the source; the core failing stays loud\n- composeUi digests the healthy set AFTER route-config isolation, in\n  canonical sorted order — the engine''s parity check and the client\n  payload agree by construction; server-side drops hydrate cleanly\n- the client hydrator pre-flights each remote''s routeConfig: a failed\n  remote drops only its routes (degraded compose -> client-render, since\n  the SSR''d tree included it); full parity still guards no-drop composes\n- known limitation (documented): a dropped mount-declaring source that\n  other sources'' routes parent onto still fails construction loudly\n\n* refactor(host): rememberVariant''s second param is the variant key, not the digest\n\n* fix(start): emit core ui bootstrap stubs in the container dist build\n\nThe container-build train (Dockerfile dist-builder — the regression fixture\nAND the deploy runtime image) ran bun run build:client in ui without the\ncode-artifact generation pass bos build performs first. On a clean checkout\nthe gitignored src/*.gen.* stubs (entry.gen.ts, hydrate.gen.tsx, …) are\nabsent from the build context and rspack fails with Module not found.\nEmit them via emitCoreUiStubs before the core ui builds (ADR 0023).","tree":{"sha":"b056f9c91637b3c8127600d5a5a8d7468e5b78b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/b056f9c91637b3c8127600d5a5a8d7468e5b78b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/f9d2dce029528d0b08599936c982c52cd0ee9c00","verification":{"payload":"tree b056f9c91637b3c8127600d5a5a8d7468e5b78b0\nparent 1d0bfff87bd0f5b5e17e14bfbe9d3e1e6056c87e\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1791162275 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791162275 -0500\n\nfeat(ui): authored router + generated bootstrap stubs — the framework owns zero ui source files (ADR 0023/0024) (#300)\n\n* feat(ui): durable cleanup — trim exposes, core-only fallback without compose payload, honest headers\n\n- drop the unconsumed ./providers and ./hooks web exposes (declare tables as exported constants)\n- core hydrate: construct the core-only tree from the app''s manifest when the\n  runtime config carries no (or a malformed) compose payload — plugin-free\n  CSR deployments no longer crash with ''no route tree''\n- trim ui globals ambient file to the rsbuild types reference\n- fix stale ownership/role headers (compose.ts, app.ts file-roles block)\n\n* feat(ui): invert router control — the authored router factory is load-bearing\n\n- coreHydrate gains createRouter/createQueryClient options (framework\n  factories stay the fallback for pre-migration stubs)\n- createServerRouterModule mints each request''s router through the same\n  authored factory (SSR parity); framework factory remains the fallback\n- app stubs pass the authored factory; router.tsx header reflects its\n  real role\n- unit seams: hydrate factory injection, SSR factory injection + fallback\n\n* feat(ui): bootstrap stubs are generated, not authored (ADR 0023)\n\n- every-plugin emits the five mechanical stubs (entry, hydrate, SSR router\n  module, compose expose, globals) as gitignored .gen files from the\n  installed package version, via the code-artifact generation pass\n- build surface retargets entries/exposes to the generated paths; core-ui\n  detection no longer requires an entry stub (it is generated)\n- sync drops the retired stub files from ownership and tolerates templates\n  that no longer ship a file (old-CLI + new-template transitional combo)\n- root .gitignore gains **/*.gen.tsx; parent ui switches to the generated\n  shape (authored router.tsx + app.ts remain)\n- unit seams: stub emitter (content contract + idempotence), expose/entry\n  retarget, detection marker; web+ssr build smoke green\n\n* refactor(ui): review fixes — shared AppRouterFactory, query-client parity, honest SSR fallback\n\n- extract AppRouterFactory into the shared types module (client hydrator\n  and SSR module mint through one declared factory shape)\n- wire the app''s createQueryClient seam end to end: authored router.tsx\n  exports it, generated hydrate + SSR stubs pass it, the SSR module mints\n  per-request clients through it\n- SSR renderToStream falls back to the request-local query client when the\n  injected factory returns none (queryClientRef no longer lies)\n- composeCoreOnly takes a plain PluginManifest list; app.ts file-roles text\n  reflects the load-bearing factory\n\n* feat(cli): sync stops managing ui source files — app ownership flip + stub retirement (ADR 0023)\n\n- FRAMEWORK_OWNED_SYNC_FILES drops every ui/src entry; config-level ui\n  files (package.json, tsconfig, postcss) stay framework-owned\n- RETIRED_SYNC_FILES migration: unmodified old stubs deleted silently,\n  hand-modified copies backed up then deleted; reported via the sync\n  result (retired / retiredConflicted) and the CLI output\n- tests rewritten for the new contract: ownership structure, retirement\n  unit seam, sync integration (config delivered, app sources never\n  re-added, stale stubs retired), prune (app-owned fallbacks prunable)\n\n* test(regression): pin plugin route chunk laziness in composed apps (ADR 0024)\n\n- start:ssr regression: boot the landing, client-navigate to the auth\n  plugin''s /login, assert new chunks from the auth remote''s origin load\n  on demand — closes ADR 0008''s flagged coupling for the composed client path\n- ADR 0024 corrected: laziness comes from the build''s code-splitter\n  (loader/component/pending/error/notFound split per match), not a\n  constructTree rewrite; deferring the eager policy modules requires\n  nav-as-manifest-data — deferred with the vocabulary work\n\n* fix(cli): sync/upgrade report retirement reliably — distinct backup dir, gate fixes\n\n- derive hasRetirement once; the report gate, the ''Already up to date''\n  check, and the upgrade renderer all include retiredConflicted\n- retired hand-modified backups report their own dir (retiredBackupDir)\n  instead of being overwritten by the main conflict backup\n- drop a duplicated ownership note in app.ts; name the remote-directory\n  derivation in the laziness spec\n\n* feat(manifest): contract v2 — virtual-file-routes vocabulary, enforced version, one identity (ADR 0024)\n\n- RouteRecord.type: ''route'' | ''layout'' | ''index'' replaces isLayout/isIndex\n  booleans; manifest version 2; mount registry 5 (digest invalidation)\n- parsePluginManifest guards every host manifest load; the compose payload\n  schema rejects a skewed major (client degrades to core-only instead of\n  silently mis-constructing)\n- folder-form composition key derives only from the plugins/<key> layout —\n  non-derivable keys fail the build loudly; the container-name fallback that\n  mis-keyed the ai manifest is gone (ai emits ''ai'', verified by rebuild)\n- fixtures/tests migrated: generator golden, construct, host compose suites\n\n* fix(ai): make the plugin workspace typecheck self-sufficient\n\nThe rebuilt gen files invalidated the typecheck cache and surfaced a latent\nbreak: the root program pulls the folder-form ui in through the contract\ngraph, so it needs the ui''s @/* fallback path, DOM lib, and the rsbuild\nambient declarations (styles.css side-effect imports).\n\n* docs(ui): the ui-integration skill describes the authored/generated split\n\n- the skill''s SSR architecture section now covers the app-owned router.tsx\n  (the policy seam: notFound/pending/error + query timings), the generated\n  .gen bootstrap set, and SSR parity through the same factory\n- stale source-list metadata dropped; ticket tracker closed for 01-04, 06, 07\n  with recorded outcomes; 05 stays open with its scope finding\n\n* fix(compose): close the identity loop + review fixes\n\n- the host compose fails loudly when a ui manifest names itself something\n  other than its config key (ADR 0008 §2''s invariant, now enforced) —\n  fixtures migrated off the container-name drift they modeled\n- one shared version-skew diagnostic formatter (parsePluginManifest +\n  the payload schema check)\n- nav-items'' manifest consumer migrates to the v2 type field (was a v1\n  consumer that only worked by accident)\n- trim the generated-config comment block; AGENTS.md gains the UI\n  ownership statement (authored surface vs generated stubs)\n\n* feat(compose): per-remote failure isolation — a broken plugin drops itself, not the app (ADR 0024 §5)\n\n- resolveComposableSources: manifest-level drops (fetch failure with no\n  last-good snapshot, unparsable content, identity mismatch) warn and\n  exclude the source; the core failing stays loud\n- composeUi digests the healthy set AFTER route-config isolation, in\n  canonical sorted order — the engine''s parity check and the client\n  payload agree by construction; server-side drops hydrate cleanly\n- the client hydrator pre-flights each remote''s routeConfig: a failed\n  remote drops only its routes (degraded compose -> client-render, since\n  the SSR''d tree included it); full parity still guards no-drop composes\n- known limitation (documented): a dropped mount-declaring source that\n  other sources'' routes parent onto still fails construction loudly\n\n* refactor(host): rememberVariant''s second param is the variant key, not the digest\n\n* fix(start): emit core ui bootstrap stubs in the container dist build\n\nThe container-build train (Dockerfile dist-builder — the regression fixture\nAND the deploy runtime image) ran bun run build:client in ui without the\ncode-artifact generation pass bos build performs first. On a clean checkout\nthe gitignored src/*.gen.* stubs (entry.gen.ts, hydrate.gen.tsx, …) are\nabsent from the build context and rspack fails with Module not found.\nEmit them via emitCoreUiStubs before the core ui builds (ADR 0023).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwvejCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyEAQALDRD5RHW0YVewecfbGCMBQe\nVH5rZDjjQd6OJ2gU5w7D8XwHE8cy+b4M3Y4frGA5RtvWrj4P2sXcfAqZ5ze7Y1vd\nQu9RQdVNDR4usl3b+oFLYVx9o+D6e9Hw2TjyRnMNGxWWSW+6P0kGy49sto0ecxtZ\nA9CJmfQ47oX0FyT1OTGmIa6wDfJwCDm+us/xl67PjrawCPs7XpKcCIuFqYRqjjsL\nUqivUZSRwMeyCg5wSRcpazKS3JQ7LCZ7s7qjJgy9AKb7HHBkju/B72vSrEXOgIU+\n0zcWwcH+2dKI7R8dskAAtBpyYsv9sS674jlHv3SNk1DJIXbepaYBquYr97WAz5A3\ndSpv6qs37GCUNAhXZ18kKSpGjwsVlUF5sczhBsUNEC+JWQKYdv/L5zoYCv+bXe+M\n7dnITg0uGkTh/UH246S40lOnogPj2qdlcMLR8wSPdVCchxZ5EEjDas/4b53C1RoJ\n4I7ww/Abv+ps335xpnYva0nmb1hKuBvln6M+CzfbwEjsY65sc/iWEgVgCnHB7GeK\nrTzDd1bhV6Ht6Kj77X2iVv+rCNbAiQVBJFX/5mRUp2ctEhv+6yYlX/7jKEt121s+\nWvO0GTsdTjJbbmTJaO2kJPRPkWatCJeA1iINyvHSjH2ZC5hUFS31at+FkJMjCSYD\n7HjM8DgSRSpqUJYuaX+m\n=4IAk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T01:04:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/f9d2dce029528d0b08599936c982c52cd0ee9c00","node_id":"C_kwDORq8oVtoAKGY5ZDJkY2UwMjk1MjhkMGIwODU5OTkzNmM5ODJjNTJjZDBlZTljMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/1d0bfff87bd0f5b5e17e14bfbe9d3e1e6056c87e","sha":"1d0bfff87bd0f5b5e17e14bfbe9d3e1e6056c87e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/1d0bfff87bd0f5b5e17e14bfbe9d3e1e6056c87e"}],"sha":"f9d2dce029528d0b08599936c982c52cd0ee9c00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/f9d2dce029528d0b08599936c982c52cd0ee9c00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/1d0bfff87bd0f5b5e17e14bfbe9d3e1e6056c87e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T01:04:35Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T01:04:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(cli): authored bos.app.ts as canonical config form (#299)\n\nPrefer bos.app.ts over a legacy bos.config.json when both coexist\n(findConfigPath flip), so a generated write-back can no longer shadow\nthe authored descriptor.\n\nPublish (packages/everything-dev):\n- config-only publish on TS-form projects no longer crashes (ENOENT);\n  it merges authored hand-edits over the published FastKV config via\n  mergeAuthoredOverPublished — hand-edits win, live pipeline state\n  (bundle URLs, integrity) carries over. Aborts when the registry is\n  unreachable instead of publishing a URL-less payload.\n- deploy write-back is form-aware: pipeline state stays in FastKV for\n  TS-form; legacy JSON-form children keep their bos.config.json\n  write-back. FastKV key name unchanged.\n\nConfig-mutating commands (plugin add/remove, upgrade, registry use)\npersist to the authored form via the descriptor serializer (authored\nleaf + delta, no inherited values baked in); JSON-form children keep\ntheir file, with a null sentinel for removing parent-inherited plugins.\n\nSweep: hardcoded bos.config.json paths (status, mf check, shared-deps,\nbundle-fetch identity) moved to form-aware helpers; error wording\nneutralized behind a shared MISSING_CONFIG_MESSAGE; AGENTS.md,\nCONTRIBUTING.md, and skill docs updated to the canonical-form model.","tree":{"sha":"111c42227554efebeba4d67a7a4cfed5e4ea534e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/111c42227554efebeba4d67a7a4cfed5e4ea534e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/1d0bfff87bd0f5b5e17e14bfbe9d3e1e6056c87e","verification":{"payload":"tree 111c42227554efebeba4d67a7a4cfed5e4ea534e\nparent 4d8efd1f70ce29b0cc9d305b7c69a6904b2e1c5f\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1791162275 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791162275 -0500\n\nfeat(cli): authored bos.app.ts as canonical config form (#299)\n\nPrefer bos.app.ts over a legacy bos.config.json when both coexist\n(findConfigPath flip), so a generated write-back can no longer shadow\nthe authored descriptor.\n\nPublish (packages/everything-dev):\n- config-only publish on TS-form projects no longer crashes (ENOENT);\n  it merges authored hand-edits over the published FastKV config via\n  mergeAuthoredOverPublished — hand-edits win, live pipeline state\n  (bundle URLs, integrity) carries over. Aborts when the registry is\n  unreachable instead of publishing a URL-less payload.\n- deploy write-back is form-aware: pipeline state stays in FastKV for\n  TS-form; legacy JSON-form children keep their bos.config.json\n  write-back. FastKV key name unchanged.\n\nConfig-mutating commands (plugin add/remove, upgrade, registry use)\npersist to the authored form via the descriptor serializer (authored\nleaf + delta, no inherited values baked in); JSON-form children keep\ntheir file, with a null sentinel for removing parent-inherited plugins.\n\nSweep: hardcoded bos.config.json paths (status, mf check, shared-deps,\nbundle-fetch identity) moved to form-aware helpers; error wording\nneutralized behind a shared MISSING_CONFIG_MESSAGE; AGENTS.md,\nCONTRIBUTING.md, and skill docs updated to the canonical-form model.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwvejCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWGsQAE7xy3ukbZnfo/zT5uutCp7R\nBzD15ugoK7+2t3jBQ5V3lKYoCgPKoQeLdafnHkTLXWz4VtymCxxzzagug7ZjeF5k\n813qCo48xDogB5zuieScw42gQVeRLpSvd8+Fs99XXUvksYaOG8A7soO379AOr3gi\n0vQUsP4Jw7aqTLVXKPyOduQxr0ujFKNXn8GVLv1dCAuVCQUFZ3LaIJTKiPkyiA0z\n+2pIusBye5m7gXKTcdtcBrtYk5tNuernhB35dxUYg7bUctq/rdTLEh+qSQCh1tgq\nufztKASCh+0vw8iVaaNY7qvELpXfLkzQTuqZHelFYhqx8y4zCQDtupUUxFTxAPWD\nqE8Q3r8LQSJhzTBWq2zM6FqDUc+y5TWyznRbDyQ00MYY4UGuInZnDULW0joMethN\nc2uH/uQH+NOEo7QxlsDI44xtYjZAw7mP8XF3Aqe+FKHd4vYxk6WXno3GmLpDceaY\nfLvfqBo+zV5Y7J+wOUA0jATVct+vynmlgOR8Thbz2ISn2mBF3BC9IvqTY8lo+T/H\n3LdXYaVZVsA2KOOXEuqvni7+J1V7NkS5+1yFt3T6MmmmZWRF2fRm24Th9xl+2kgp\ndSuJKVCDkAoaJ4+avhKM0SQEOAJk42GM/KV6b8+hBgXFopAbCJhTqGXCQDTvQrd3\nNQEf5Bt+2Cb6qwiLYjTs\n=6Fp/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T01:04:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/1d0bfff87bd0f5b5e17e14bfbe9d3e1e6056c87e","node_id":"C_kwDORq8oVtoAKDFkMGJmZmY4N2JkMGY1YjVlMTdlMTRiZmJlOWQzZTFlNjA1NmM4N2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/4d8efd1f70ce29b0cc9d305b7c69a6904b2e1c5f","sha":"4d8efd1f70ce29b0cc9d305b7c69a6904b2e1c5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/4d8efd1f70ce29b0cc9d305b7c69a6904b2e1c5f"}],"sha":"1d0bfff87bd0f5b5e17e14bfbe9d3e1e6056c87e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/1d0bfff87bd0f5b5e17e14bfbe9d3e1e6056c87e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/4d8efd1f70ce29b0cc9d305b7c69a6904b2e1c5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:41:26Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T14:41:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(docs): consolidate plan tree under docs/plans, rename glossary to GLOSSARY.md (#297)\n\n* derive the prerequisite train from workspace edges — two-roots split (ADR 0022)\n\nThe CLI conflated the app root (bos.app.ts dir) with the bun workspace\nroot; correct only while they coincide. New module\npackages/everything-dev/src/workspace.ts owns the workspace frame:\n\n- findWorkspaceRoot: memoized walk-up to the nearest package.json\n  declaring workspaces\n- ensureFreshDeps: replaces buildPackageQuietly + the hardcoded\n  quietBuildPackages list — the prerequisite graph is derived from\n  declared dependencies/devDependencies resolved against workspace\n  members; staleness per member via its own export oracle; failures\n  aggregate into DepsBuildFailure (no more silent skip)\n- localDepsOf: pure closure over plain data — the test surface\n\nWorkspace-frame reads (catalog, node_modules, installs, member\nenumeration) now resolve the workspace root; app-frame anchors are\nuntouched. BOS_CONFIG_PATH retired: host scripts, server.ts, and\nrsbuild.config.ts rely on their own fallback chains; the container\nfixture drops its redundant explicit pass. Children get empty closures\nand identical behavior.\n\n* chore(docs): consolidate plan tree under docs/plans, rename glossary to GLOSSARY.md\n\n- merge advisor-plans/ + plans/ into docs/plans/: advisor audit queue flat,\n  thematic subdirs (beta-v2, wayfinder, prototypes, deploy-agents-rebuild,\n  extensions, infra, offline, v1-current), done/ archive; both READMEs\n  merged into one indexed docs/plans/README.md (dead links and phantom\n  files fixed, with a note on the gitignore data loss and its fix)\n- make docs/plans markdown first-class tracked; the old plans/ gitignore\n  regime silently dropped new .md files (lost the v1-current plan docs)\n- rename CONTEXT.md -> GLOSSARY.md to match the refreshed upstream skill\n  ecosystem (domain-modeling now ships GLOSSARY-FORMAT.md); GLOSSARY.md\n  un-ignored, GLOSSARY-MAP.md stays local-only\n- refresh all 35 upstream skills via skills update (writing-shape now\n  installed; setup-matt-pocock-skills/domain-modeling GLOSSARY renames)\n- rewrite the /improve skill to write docs/plans/NNN-slug.md; the\n  advisor-plans fallback rule is gone (collision resolved)\n- fix 9 dead metadata.sources in the package skills (auth middleware,\n  migrate, build/rspack, _authenticated routes, runtime entry); unify\n  better-near-auth''s @tanstack/intent on the catalog (was ^0.0.40);\n  bump auth-plugin/subaccount skill version anchors to 1.10.2\n- delete CityNode product docs (docs/discovery/, i18n.md,\n  teams-and-workspaces-walkthrough.md) per the v2-shell fork split;\n  recoverable from git history\n- delete :memory: PGlite artifacts (x3), test-results/, and prune six\n  stale .scratch sprint dirs\n- add scripts: skills:check (lock-vs-disk drift), skills:update,\n  intents:refresh\n- refresh CONTRIBUTING.md: dead LLM.txt/api/README.md links, pre-V2\n  plugin list, i18n doc pointer\n\n* chore(skills): bump mattpocock skills to v1.3.1\n\n- remove resolving-merge-conflicts (dropped upstream in v1.3.0; nothing\n  replaces it — the agent works through merge/rebase conflicts without\n  a dedicated skill; nothing in this repo referenced it)\n- add the newly graduated engineering skills: implement-spec (whole-spec\n  implementation via task graph + parallel implementer worktrees), pr\n  (PR-body shape: summary visuals, before/after evidence, merge-danger\n  call), retro (post-session environment review) — ask-matt already\n  routed to all three from the previous update\n- pull v1.3.1 content for the existing set (ask-matt retro routing fix;\n  em-dash sweep, ''Call the Skill tool'' invocation convention, and YAML\n  quoting fixes were already in the prior update''s pre-release pull)\n- re-apply the docs/plans path customization to the improve skill after\n  the update overwrote it (verified byte-identical to the committed\n  state)\n- skills-lock.json now carries 38 entries; skills:check in sync\n\n* chore(ci): retro follow-ups — docs link checker, skills CI wiring, AGENTS.md slimming\n\nRetro on the cleanup session surfaced four environment fixes (adopted),\nplus one deeper discovery (#298):\n\n- scripts/docs-link-check.mjs + ''bun run docs:check'': verifies the live\n  navigation surface (root docs, docs/agents, adr + plans indexes,\n  package SKILL.md incl. metadata.sources, repo-authored/improve agent\n  skills) — markdown links, backticked paths, and frontmatter sources\n  all resolve to real files. Caught and fixed 7 real rots this pass:\n  stale _layout route paths (x3), the removed admin.spec.ts example,\n  api/src/lib/auth.ts in the api-and-auth skill body, the absorbed\n  api/src/team-access-policy.ts citation, and stale ui/README route\n  list. Historical records (ADR/plan bodies, CHANGELOGs) are\n  deliberately out of scope — they are dated records with their own\n  drift mechanism (commit stamps).\n- check-skills.yml: widen PR path triggers to the source trees the\n  package skills'' metadata.sources point into (moves in non-skills PRs\n  are what silently rots the sources); add a ''Check skill drift'' step\n  (intent stale --json needsReview for all three packages).\n- ci.yml: run skills:check + docs:check in lint-and-typecheck.\n- AGENTS.md: extract the self-deployed production walkthrough (near-cli\n  install, publish keys, bos deploy, universal image, near-cli-rs\n  reference) to docs/self-deploy.md behind a pointer (818 -> 753\n  lines); make skills-lock.json the source of truth for the workflow\n  skill set instead of a stale ~35 count.\n- better-near-auth: re-export readSessionNearAccountId from client.ts —\n  the SIWN client skill teaches importing it there; it was previously\n  internal to store.js (real API drift caught by the new validate run).\n\nDiscovery: ''intent validate'' is red for ALL three packages (~123\npre-existing snippet findings, mixed excerpt pedantry and possible real\ndrift) — the CI validate step has been red-if-run for a while. Triage\nticket: #298.\n\n* fix(ci): docs:check passes a clean checkout\n\nCI''s first run of the new docs link check failed with 16 findings —\ntwo classes, both checkout-environment gaps rather than doc rot:\n\n- docs/self-deploy.md was never committed: the global *.md ignore rule\n  swallowed top-level docs/*.md (our negations covered adr/, agents/,\n  plans/ only). Collapse them into !docs/**/*.md — the same class of\n  silent gitignore data loss that ate the v1-current plans, this time\n  caught on first CI run by the checker itself.\n- 15 references pointed at gitignored generated files (*.gen.ts type\n  files, routeTree.gen.ts) that exist on dev machines but never in a\n  clean checkout. When a target does not exist, the checker now asks\n  ''git check-ignore'' (cached) and skips ignored paths as generated/\n  runtime artifacts — one rule for any future generated pattern, and\n  local vs CI behavior is now identical.\n\nVerified by hiding a generated file locally to force the skip path.","tree":{"sha":"bbe8542861051f71fa021b542bd5e8d0b9a4b132","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/bbe8542861051f71fa021b542bd5e8d0b9a4b132"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/4d8efd1f70ce29b0cc9d305b7c69a6904b2e1c5f","verification":{"payload":"tree bbe8542861051f71fa021b542bd5e8d0b9a4b132\nparent 8da5dbe579bbf09e9592c723fe02c25d09f5ba55\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1791124886 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791124886 -0500\n\nchore(docs): consolidate plan tree under docs/plans, rename glossary to GLOSSARY.md (#297)\n\n* derive the prerequisite train from workspace edges — two-roots split (ADR 0022)\n\nThe CLI conflated the app root (bos.app.ts dir) with the bun workspace\nroot; correct only while they coincide. New module\npackages/everything-dev/src/workspace.ts owns the workspace frame:\n\n- findWorkspaceRoot: memoized walk-up to the nearest package.json\n  declaring workspaces\n- ensureFreshDeps: replaces buildPackageQuietly + the hardcoded\n  quietBuildPackages list — the prerequisite graph is derived from\n  declared dependencies/devDependencies resolved against workspace\n  members; staleness per member via its own export oracle; failures\n  aggregate into DepsBuildFailure (no more silent skip)\n- localDepsOf: pure closure over plain data — the test surface\n\nWorkspace-frame reads (catalog, node_modules, installs, member\nenumeration) now resolve the workspace root; app-frame anchors are\nuntouched. BOS_CONFIG_PATH retired: host scripts, server.ts, and\nrsbuild.config.ts rely on their own fallback chains; the container\nfixture drops its redundant explicit pass. Children get empty closures\nand identical behavior.\n\n* chore(docs): consolidate plan tree under docs/plans, rename glossary to GLOSSARY.md\n\n- merge advisor-plans/ + plans/ into docs/plans/: advisor audit queue flat,\n  thematic subdirs (beta