ies/devDependencies resolved against workspace\n  members; staleness per member via its own export oracle; failures\n  aggregate into DepsBuildFailure (no more silent skip)\n- localDepsOf: pure closure over plain data — the test surface\n\nWorkspace-frame reads (catalog, node_modules, installs, member\nenumeration) now resolve the workspace root; app-frame anchors are\nuntouched. BOS_CONFIG_PATH retired: host scripts, server.ts, and\nrsbuild.config.ts rely on their own fallback chains; the container\nfixture drops its redundant explicit pass. Children get empty closures\nand identical behavior.","tree":{"sha":"d3f4d5cbb20026029afa8036ae57f6786d2878d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/d3f4d5cbb20026029afa8036ae57f6786d2878d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/8da5dbe579bbf09e9592c723fe02c25d09f5ba55","verification":{"payload":"tree d3f4d5cbb20026029afa8036ae57f6786d2878d4\nparent d57b8f4ee77094e939c2242b616869bd8054b514\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1791124019 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791124019 -0500\n\nderive the prerequisite train from workspace edges — two-roots split (ADR 0022) (#296)\n\nThe CLI conflated the app root (bos.app.ts dir) with the bun workspace\nroot; correct only while they coincide. New module\npackages/everything-dev/src/workspace.ts owns the workspace frame:\n\n- findWorkspaceRoot: memoized walk-up to the nearest package.json\n  declaring workspaces\n- ensureFreshDeps: replaces buildPackageQuietly + the hardcoded\n  quietBuildPackages list — the prerequisite graph is derived from\n  declared dependencies/devDependencies resolved against workspace\n  members; staleness per member via its own export oracle; failures\n  aggregate into DepsBuildFailure (no more silent skip)\n- localDepsOf: pure closure over plain data — the test surface\n\nWorkspace-frame reads (catalog, node_modules, installs, member\nenumeration) now resolve the workspace root; app-frame anchors are\nuntouched. BOS_CONFIG_PATH retired: host scripts, server.ts, and\nrsbuild.config.ts rely on their own fallback chains; the container\nfixture drops its redundant explicit pass. Children get empty closures\nand identical behavior.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwmIzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZsIQAHKoxhJoqv6XSIAPd9qzumVj\nYFGRi8aJJSofhMBdWbT7f7ZBdCYhypFQ4H4j/kBkfoMXubeyRDB5U/MdZRXH4JW1\nvkYHiS2p6ae4Gj2pA+k9s2wPm6N4N1yr49UNlPSbc0WWZ414KjH4jFQdS148++Za\nQKD/VhPBbV8d+XTWH39Za8YZervAzC7x4aD9PeupkYdUbPOg3lbC6olGPNraPHH8\nByVOWU5PquzjXzxl6Pw6p+n580qwAn8t9Yg8us+bWJWQkZZ0xlWmQ7HG/qq29CGI\njCKNCVgDu/Sd3KX2ik+oxDHlQEPOo6E5K7uVKbVPwwKS0/zADkKjj7ZcXmR6upmc\nEymXeJIJCJVyaS/zq4cakTxdJSz7FmAeNjJbSNU5aaqKXQBuNrxUxHTE6z9mFhLl\nIGR/ga6nV4LrnJA93sFZEuT0bIZBbKJsknAsjS8B4d+zJD1bxyO00uewwyfkiuZh\nUSBYPpkQvWiiYSpYAZOqPsCtzWwLaLwPi9Z190ZzxHzvhnDtKalvyp4AMQ1cAb74\nVnvow9BjWwSDfyk3kFlqAt4YOi4VHIDO+HFVmcM//2tuIUS0NEl+eNda1aw/AQu/\nYBaaaMg9ZhTi7rNqKQ5zZEQx0odg4aP82hMFQ9Iah40ZcfcRdyeH05EEYWvNeryg\n4AQIvk52h0K69ASHKd82\n=EAig\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T14:26:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/8da5dbe579bbf09e9592c723fe02c25d09f5ba55","node_id":"C_kwDORq8oVtoAKDhkYTVkYmU1NzliYmYwOWU5NTkyYzcyM2ZlMDJjMjVkMDlmNWJhNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/d57b8f4ee77094e939c2242b616869bd8054b514","sha":"d57b8f4ee77094e939c2242b616869bd8054b514","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/d57b8f4ee77094e939c2242b616869bd8054b514"}],"sha":"8da5dbe579bbf09e9592c723fe02c25d09f5ba55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/8da5dbe579bbf09e9592c723fe02c25d09f5ba55"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/d57b8f4ee77094e939c2242b616869bd8054b514/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T19:56:18Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T19:56:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"V2 (#293)\n\n* Upgrade v2 (#292)\n\n* wip\n\n* upgrade bindings\n\n* add branding\n\n* working\n\n* refactor(ui): reorganize routes into mount-point layouts, rename home to dashboard\n\n- add _admin pathless layout gating on admin role; tenant admin dashboard and system pages render as children via Outlet\n- rename authenticated /home route to /dashboard; update sidebar, mobile tabs, user nav, and login redirect fallbacks\n- move apps and things routes under the public layout\n- changeset: ui-layout-mounts\n\n* test(regression): update /home references to /dashboard after route rename\n\n* refactor(ui): add _anon mount for login, rename organizations to orgs, remove nostr\n\n- move login from public layout into new _anon pathless layout that redirects authed users to /dashboard and provides theme toggle header\n- rename organization route group from /organizations to /orgs; move invitation acceptance to /orgs/invites/$id\n- remove stale nostr entry from authenticated sidebar\n- changeset: ui-anon-orgs\n\n* organization\n\n* test(regression): add backcompat mode, run http + browser suites together\n\n* feat: add bos typecheck command\n\n* fix: stop bos sync from leaking parent-only scripts to children\n\n* fix: align apps plugin routes with _public layout paths\n\n* progress\n\n* relayer\n\n* feat(cli): lock deploys in FastKV, expose infra export, resolve plugin origin\n\n- Add per-account/gateway FastKV deploy lock (apps/<account>/<gateway>/lock/deploy.json)\n  acquired before publish and released in a finally block. Stale or concurrent\n  dispatches fail fast with status \"locked\" and a conflict payload listing owner,\n  nonce, expires, and txHash. opt out with --no-deploy-lock.\n- bos publish holds the lock for 10 minutes by default; bos deploy holds it for\n  25 minutes to cover publish + Railway redeploy. Override with\n  BOS_DEPLOY_LOCK_TTL_MS.\n- Add bos deploy lock inspect|release for ops visibility and stuck-lock recovery.\n- Add bos infra export that emits the resolved CI infra plan (env + services +\n  account/gateway/project/generatedAt) so CI consumers stop duplicating port and\n  DATABASE_URL knowledge from cli/infra.ts.\n- Update .github/workflows/deploy.yml to consume the export and drop the\n  hardcoded API_DATABASE_URL / AUTH_DATABASE_URL / CORS_ORIGIN env block.\n- buildOriginMap now reads runtimeConfig.plugins[id].extendsRef and\n  runtimeConfig.auth?.extendsRef instead of re-parsing raw bos.config.json.\n- Tests for the lock helpers, the CI plan builder, the resolved-config origin\n  lookup, and the per-command TTL resolution.\n\nCo-authored-by: opencode <opencode@local>\n\n* feat: remove deploy lock, keep infra export\n\nRemove FastKV-backed deploy lock feature:\n- Delete bos deploy lock acquire/release/inspect commands\n- Remove lock logic from publishToFastKv\n- Remove lockConflict from PublishResult and DeployResult schemas\n- Concurrent deploys now follow last-write-wins semantics (harmless for Railway redeploy)\n\nKeep bos infra export command:\n- Emits {env, services, account, gateway, project, generatedAt} JSON\n- buildOriginMap reads runtimeConfig.*.extendsRef (no raw JSON re-parse)\n\nTests: 263 pass, failures are pre-existing (auth types, template property)\n\n* wip\n\n* skills\n\n* pre\n\n* feat(geo): introduce nodes, validators, and domain bindings API\n\nReplace the legacy citynode model with three orthogonal services and a\nmatching UI surface.\n\nAPI\n- New NodesService: hierarchical node management with a recursive CTE\n  for subtree lookup, parent-cycle prevention on create/update, and\n  per-node validator scoping.\n- New ValidatorsService (replaces CityNodesService): multi-validator per\n  node, exact-one default enforcement via db.transaction, and\n  resolveForStaking which descends the subtree first and walks\n  ancestors as a fallback. resolveByAccountId looks up a single\n  validator by its NEAR account id.\n- Rewritten TenantsService: createBinding, verifyCustomDomain via HTTP\n  HEAD, and setPrimaryBinding wrapped in db.transaction. authorizedTenant\n  helper centralizes personal vs org tenant checks.\n\nRobustness\n- Shared toOrpcError extracted into api/src/lib/errors.ts so route\n  handlers stop hand-typing error maps.\n- isUniqueViolation(error) detects Postgres code 23505 instead of\n  string-sniffing the message.\n- HOSTNAME_REGEX validates DNS hostnames independently of NEAR\n  account ids in createBinding and the binding preflight.\n\nSchema\n- Drop node_tags (orphaned by the citynode removal) and regenerate\n  migrations as a single clean snapshot (4 tables: tenants, nodes,\n  validators, domain_bindings). The self-referencing nodes.parent_id\n  FK uses AnyPgColumn for the typed reference.\n\nHost\n- BindingResolver''s TenantBinding interface gained tenantId so resolve\n  flows can tie a hostname back to a tenant record. Mock updated to\n  keep the integration test green.\n\nUI\n- Public landing directory reads listValidators instead of\n  listLegacyCityNodes.\n- Stake page: CityNodeCard -> ValidatorCard, query keys -> validators,\n  resolver hooks -> resolveValidatorByAccountId.\n- Admin tenants wizard rebuilt around nodes / validators / bindings,\n  and tenant header affordances reference tenant.id instead of the\n  now-defunct subdomain field.\n\n* chore(changeset): rename to nodes-validators-bindings and trim the optional opener\n\n* feat(geo): landing directory, country aggregator, and stake selector UI\n\n- Landing page queries listRootNodes, renders root-node directory cards\n  (name, kind badge, slug) with subdomain links + skeleton/empty states\n- New public country page at /n/$slug aggregates children via\n  listChildren and shows stake guidance from resolveStakingValidators\n  (own validator CTA, or stake-to-city links for children with validators)\n- Stake page rewritten around resolveStakingValidators: selectable\n  validator list with isDefault pre-selected, role/protocol badges,\n  community secondary styling, inherited-validator banner, no-validator\n  fallback with child links. Node resolved from ?node= param or hostname.\n  Stake transaction + onramp flows unchanged; broken admin CRUD removed.\n\n* feat(geo): tenant + node + binding creation wizard\n\n- Rewrite admin tenant creation page from placeholder into full wizard:\n  inline org creation (if no active org), node details (kind, cascading\n  parent dropdown via listRootNodes + listChildren, slug, name), tenant +\n  binding form with auto-generated hostname and live bindingPreflight\n- On submit: createTenant → createNode → createBinding (blocking, with\n  rollback via deleteNode + deleteTenant on failure), then non-blocking\n  deploy steps for NEAR subaccount and registry config publish\n- Export StepList + useStepper from @/components barrel\n- Extend api/tests/setup.ts: optional plugins map param on getPluginClient,\n  role param on orgContext (enables requireOrgRole in integration tests)\n- Add api/tests/integration/wizard.test.ts: 5 tests covering full chain,\n  rollback on duplicate hostname, nested hierarchy, preflight availability\n\n* feat(ui): reset & simplification — strip platform cruft, surface CityNodes product\n\n- Landing: ''What are CityNodes?'' hero + root-node directory + Apply button\n- New /apply route (external redirect to citynode.app/apply)\n- Remove apps browser cruft (4 routes deleted, apps tab stripped from profile)\n- Things index → typed DataTable demo\n- Mobile responsive fixes (auth-shell double-padding, simple-header overflow)\n- README + skill.md rewritten for CityNodes product surface\n\n* chore: finalize citynode.app repo identity and platform docs\n\nUpdate bos.config.json repository to point to NEARBuilders/citynode.app.\nAlign docs (AGENTS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, LLM.txt, host/README.md) with the\nremote auth plugin architecture and PostgreSQL migration. Clean up CI\npostgres-template service and .env.example for new plugin databases.\nRemove docker-compose.yml in favor of the Railway-backed deploy flow.\n\n* chore: reorganize plans/ — consolidate prototypes, group by domain, fix contradictions\n\n- Move 5 beta-v2 docs into plans/beta-v2/ (overview, composable, ui, tenants, native)\n- Move extension plans into plans/extensions/ (ui-extends-ui-federation, client-runtime-plugins)\n- Move infra plans into plans/infra/ (toml-infra-alchemy, orpc-v2-effect-migration)\n- Move offline plans into plans/offline/ (shell-sw-caching, data-sync-queue)\n- Move v1 plan into plans/v1-current/ (tenant-feature-completeness)\n- Fetch full prototype source (85 files) from prototype/route-merging branch\n- Consolidate prototypes under plans/prototypes/beta-v2/ and beta-v2-override/\n- Fold react-native-migration.md into beta-v2/native.md, delete original\n- Fix TOML/JSON publishing contradiction in composable.md\n- Mark wayfinder tickets 01, 02 as RESOLVED; 06 as PARTIALLY RESOLVED\n- Rewrite plans/README.md with new directory structure and ticket status table\n- Update ~45 cross-references across all plan docs\n- Add .gitignore exceptions for prototype source files (*.css, *.gen.ts)\n\n* docs(contributing): add community onboarding and Telegram group\n\n* fix(dev): fix fresh-clone dev flow — commit docker-compose, boot CLI from source, drop postinstall\n\n- Commit docker-compose.yml (was gitignored and generated after preflight,\n  creating a chicken-and-egg where bun run dev exited before the file was\n  written). Provisions postgres-api (5432/api_db) and postgres-auth\n  (5433/auth_db); plugins isolate via plugin_<pluginId> schemas.\n- Add paths to packages/everything-dev/tsconfig.json mapping every-plugin\n  and subpath exports to source so bun''s runtime resolver finds them\n  without pre-built dist.\n- Remove postinstall: bun run types:gen (dead code under ignore-scripts).\n- Update AGENTS.md Quick Reference with docker compose step and plugin\n  schema isolation docs.\n\n* feat(ci): convert to downstream app-only deploy with testnet staging\n\n- Add optional  to BosStagingSchema, use staging.account in\n  publishToFastKv when --env staging (enables testnet account switching)\n- Add staging block to bos.config.json: v1.citynode.testnet on\n  testnet.citynode.app\n- Deploy workflow: trigger from ci-main-success (not release-completed),\n  exclude host via --packages, remove Postgres services and infra plan\n- Staging workflow: use NEAR_TESTNET_PRIVATE_KEY, exclude host\n- Release workflow: manual-only (remove ci-main-success trigger, remove\n  docker and notify-deploy jobs)\n- Docker workflow: remove push triggers on main/staging\n- Update workflow README to document downstream flow\n\n* docs: add Railway deploy button and conceptual env var descriptions\n\n- Root README: Deploy section with Railway button and BOS_ACCOUNT,\n  BOS_GATEWAY, BETTER_AUTH_SECRET table\n- host/README: add BOS_ACCOUNT/BOS_GATEWAY to env var table with\n  conceptual descriptions, refine tenant-mode example\n- init.ts: generated AGENTS.md now includes Railway deploy hint with\n  env var table\n\n* readme\n\n* docs: add self-deployed development workflow to AGENTS.md and child scaffold (#21)\n\n* fix(dev): stop showing UI-SSR running when SSR is off (#22)\n\nGate ui-ssr service descriptor on runtimeConfig.ui.ssrUrl so the\nplanner path matches service-descriptor.ts. Without this, the\norchestrator marked the missing descriptor as a ready Remote\nservice, printing ''UI-SSR running'' despite no dev:ssr process.\n\n* Clean up  (#23)\n\n* wip\n\n* wip\n\n* feat(ui): unify shells, public header, and page widths\n\n- Landing: left-aligned \"What are City Nodes\" + NodeDirectory table (shared\n  pathless n/-node-directory.tsx), healthy top spacing; /n/$slug adopts the\n  same directory + stake rows\n- Chrome: PublicShell for _public/_anon (showConnect hides connect on login),\n  AppShell (AppSidebar/AppHeader/MobileTabBar/NAV_ITEMS) for _authenticated/_admin,\n  BetaBanner extracted into _layout; auth-shell.tsx and stale root-level\n  user-nav/near-branding/theme-toggle/org-switcher deleted\n- Login: no brand element or anonymous option; single \"connect with NEAR\" CTA\n- Widths: public children default, app children wide; dashboard.tsx becomes a\n  layout route (content moved to dashboard/index.tsx, URLs unchanged); nested\n  container removed from admin/tenants/new\n- Buttons: hand-rolled inline-class links replaced with Button variants across\n  dashboard, admin, orgs, tenant, things, apply; hardcoded rgb border swapped\n  for semantic token\n- Changesets: directory-design-alignment, shell-consolidation\n\n* Fix/merge UI normalization (#24)\n\n* wip\n\n* wip\n\n* fix(deploy): retry Zephyr exit-code-1 crashes and fix xpack SSR misdetection (#25)\n\n- Move Zephyr error detection (ZE regex) before the exitCode !== 0 guard\n  in runBuildAttempt so Zephyr-caused build crashes (exit code 1) are\n  classified as retriable instead of failing immediately\n- Replace single retry with up to 3 retries using exponential backoff\n  (2s, 5s, 10s) for Zephyr edge provider errors\n- Add snapshotType: ''csr'' to UI server and host withZephyr calls to\n  prevent xpack coordinator from inferring ''ssr'' (triggered by\n  target: ''async-node'') and failing to find a server entrypoint or\n  hiding remoteEntry.js behind a 404\n\n* Update  (#26)\n\n* fix(deploy): retry Zephyr exit-code-1 crashes and fix xpack SSR misdetection\n\n- Move Zephyr error detection (ZE regex) before the exitCode !== 0 guard\n  in runBuildAttempt so Zephyr-caused build crashes (exit code 1) are\n  classified as retriable instead of failing immediately\n- Replace single retry with up to 3 retries using exponential backoff\n  (2s, 5s, 10s) for Zephyr edge provider errors\n- Add snapshotType: ''csr'' to UI server and host withZephyr calls to\n  prevent xpack coordinator from inferring ''ssr'' (triggered by\n  target: ''async-node'') and failing to find a server entrypoint or\n  hiding remoteEntry.js behind a 404\n\n* feat(ui): strip public header to user-nav only, default light theme, move Apply button to directory heading\n\n- Remove logo, border, and background from public shell header, keeping only UserNav\n- Change default theme from ''system'' to ''light'' in ThemeProvider and no-flash init script\n- Move Apply button from bottom section to top-right of Directory section heading\n\n* Clean up ui/public placeholder icons and stale docs\n\n- Renamed near.svg → icon.svg and logo.png → icon-512.png (placeholder\n  dot icons, named for replacement); updated site.webmanifest icon srcs\n- Removed dead public files: README.md (about route fetches from GitHub\n  raw), near_rev.svg (unreferenced), bos.png (orphan)\n- Rewrote llms.txt to follow standard llms.txt format\n- Removed /README.md from skill.md public entry points\n- Updated host integration test /near.svg → /icon.svg\n\n* organize\n\n* feat: audit and fix agent information flow for first-load discovery\n\n- Rewrite skill.md with two agent modes (MCP/REST + clone & modify)\n- Expand llms.txt with API, MCP, auth, and source sections\n- Add /.well-known/mcp.json host route for MCP discovery\n- Delete stale LLM.txt (superseded by AGENTS.md)\n- Create docs/agents/ files (issue-tracker, triage-labels, domain)\n- Add agent communication surface and .agents/skills/ sections to AGENTS.md\n- Add /settings/api-keys route with create/list/delete UI\n- Expose auth and plugin router routes as MCP tools\n- Update init.ts child AGENTS.md with MCP/API-key sections\n- Add child llms.txt and skill.md template generation in init.ts\n- Add MCP, agent surface, and settings API keys regression tests\n\n* fix(mcp): remove pluginRouters and authHealth, rely on base API''s composed spec\n\nThe base API router already composes all plugin routes (auth, registry,\nproposals, votes) via pluginsClient, so its OpenAPI spec already includes\nevery operation. Passing pluginRouters separately caused every auth tool\nto register as a duplicate.\n\n- Removed pluginRouters parameter from mountMcpRoute\n- Removed authHealth from base API contract and router (was a passthrough\n  to the auth plugin''s own health endpoint, now redundant)\n- Kept duplicate-skip safety net for future collisions\n- Simplified mcp.ts back to single-router registration\n\n* fix(ui): rebuild dashboard shell on shadcn Sidebar, fix double-header bug\n\nReplaces hand-rolled AppShell/AppSidebar/AppHeader/MobileTabBar with\nshadcn''s Sidebar/SidebarProvider/SidebarInset composition. Fixes a\ndouble-header render bug on dashboard routes from an interim\n\"global header\" experiment (sidebar wasn''t spanning full height,\nbreadcrumb bar visually disconnected from the identity nav above it).\n\n- Sidebar defaults expanded with icon+label, collapsible via trigger/cmd+b\n- Mobile nav is now the sidebar''s built-in off-canvas sheet, replacing\n  the persistent bottom tab bar\n- Split OrgSwitcher/UserNav into shell-appropriate variants sharing\n  session/org/profile/sign-out logic via a new useIdentity hook\n- UserNav moved back into PublicShell''s own header for non-sidebar\n  routes (/, /things/*, /login, /things/new)\n- Added Breadcrumb primitive to AppHeader, replacing plain text\n- Rebuilt NetworkToggle on ToggleGroup, moved to components/layout/\n- Added toggle.tsx, toggle-group.tsx, breadcrumb.tsx, sidebar.tsx\n  shadcn primitives (Radix flavor, adapted to project conventions)\n\nNo URL changes; the auth-guard vs dashboard-layout route separation\nis unaffected.\n\n* fix(db): eliminate pg-pool search_path race that crashed the host\n\n- Set search_path via pool connection options instead of an unawaited\n  async on(\"connect\") listener, so it''s applied atomically before any\n  query can run on a fresh connection.\n- Move one-time CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS to driver init instead of\n  re-running it racily on every reconnect.\n- Add uncaughtException/unhandledRejection handlers in\n  host/src/program.ts so a dropped DB connection logs an error instead\n  of killing the host process and cascading SIGTERM to every service.\n\nImplements the fix described in .changeset/db-search-path-race-fix.md\n(previously committed as docs-only, without the code changes).\n\n* fix(ui): update sidebar to Tailwind v4 arbitrary-property syntax\n\nsidebar.tsx, sidebar-org-switcher.tsx, and sidebar-user-nav.tsx used\nTailwind v3''s bracket syntax for CSS variable references\n(e.g. w-[--sidebar-width]), which Tailwind v4 no longer recognizes as\na variable reference — it fell back to no explicit width. Switch to\nv4''s arbitrary-property shorthand (w-(--sidebar-width)), including the\ncalc() variants that referenced the removed theme(spacing.4) helper,\nnow --spacing(4).\n\nAlso drops a stray trailing blank line in cli/init.ts and applies\nformatting cleanup to api-keys.tsx (no behavior change).\n\n* feat: add --env staging to bos key generate, extract shared UI menu components\n\nCLI:\n- Add --env staging flag to bos key generate; resolves staging account\n  from bos.config.json staging.account (falls back to top-level account)\n- Suggest NEAR_TESTNET_PRIVATE_KEY for staging, NEAR_PRIVATE_KEY for production\n- Remove unused account param from buildChildSkillMd in init scaffold\n- Remove unused packages:write permission from staging.yml workflow\n\nUI:\n- Extract OrgSwitcherMenuContent and UserNavMenuContent into shared components\n- Add useSwitchOrganization hook (replaces inline handleOrgSwitch in 3 places)\n- Add PublicHeader component; pass runtimeConfig to PublicShell\n- Remove handleOrgSwitch from useIdentity (query invalidation now in hook)\n- Remove mobile home link from AppHeader\n\nConfig:\n- Update deployment URLs and integrity hashes\n- Switch top-level account to v1.citynode.testnet (pre-mainnet)\n\n* hardcode testnet\n\n* fix: testnet FastKV registry namespace defaulted to mainnet account\n\nTestnet namespace was hardcoded to dev.everything.near (a mainnet account)\ninstead of dev.allthethings.testnet. Remove REGISTRY_FASTKV_* env var\noverrides, add --registry flag to publish/deploy/key generate for CLI override.\n\n* fix: add --registry to bos start, remove dead postinstall from Dockerfile\n\n- Thread --registry override through resolveRemoteConfigChain and\n  fetchPublishedConfig so bos start fetches from the correct FastKV\n  registry contract.\n- Remove RUN bun run postinstall from Dockerfile — the script was\n  removed from package.json in a prior commit but the Dockerfile was\n  never updated, causing Docker builds to fail.\n\n* deploy\n\n* fix railway\n\n* dockerfile\n\n* fix: respect process.env.PORT in production runtime config\n\nbuildRuntimeConfig hardcoded host.url and host.port to localhost:3000\nin production, ignoring PORT. The HTTP server listened on the correct\nport (from process.env.PORT) but config.host.url pointed at 3000,\ncausing the binding resolver to fetch /api/tenants/bindings from the\nwrong port and get 503.\n\n* add node aggregation api routes (#27)\n\n* feat: add node-scoped admin dashboard (#28)\n\n* feat: add node-scoped admin dashboard\n\n* fix: pass testnet parent key to auth\n\n* Revert \"fix: pass testnet parent key to auth\"\n\nThis reverts commit 14b645d6ec8fbf19c4715a4bb5ac3881e5816643.\n\n* fix: make tenant deployment network-aware\n\n* fix: align node proposal review permissions\n\n* Revert \"fix: make tenant deployment network-aware\"\n\nThis reverts commit 788d9fe9f83a69a3b3e6ceffcd0b50ecaf24aa96.\n\n* fix: make tenant deployment network-aware\n\n* feat: add platform admin structure reporting (#31)\n\n* feat: add admin structure reporting\n\n* fix: generate fallback remote auth types\n\n* test: align infra fixtures with shared database\n\n* fix: report visible data table rows\n\n* feat: add admin node management (#32)\n\n* fix(ci): workflow_run deploys, drop commit-back, remove dead postinstall\n\n- Deploy/staging trigger via workflow_run + head_sha checkout; notify/repository_dispatch removed\n- Commit-back of bos.config.json removed — runtime reads FastKV via BOS_ACCOUNT/BOS_GATEWAY (#33, everything-dev#243)\n- postinstall steps removed from all workflows and child scaffolding (dead under ignore-scripts)\n- release.yml permission cleanup; docker.yml dead workflow_call dropped; @railway/cli pinned\n\n* feat(cli): nostr-signed publish transport for FastKV registry writes\n\n- bos publish signs a NIP-78 kind-30078 event (d = registry key, content = config JSON)\n  and POSTs it to the apps plugin nostrRelayKvWrite route (#34)\n- Effect-based transport with typed errors: NostrKeyMissing, PayloadTooLarge, RelayRejected\n- no-op skip when FastKV already holds the identical config\n- NEAR signing path removed from publish.ts; near-signer dropped; near-kit dep\n  replaced by nostr-tools (key management trio stays for bos relay key in T2b)\n\n* feat(config): register remote nostr plugin; apps plugin composes it via pluginsClient\n\n- plugins.nostr remote-only entry (production URL + integrity) with dependsOn auth\n- apps dependsOn nostr so Phase-1 loading injects a typed client factory\n- siwn relayer whitelistedContracts += contextual.near (mainnet; no testnet contract exists)\n- apps switched to createPlugin.withPlugins<PluginsClient>() (#36)\n\n* Revert \"feat(config): register remote nostr plugin; apps plugin composes it via pluginsClient\"\n\nThis reverts commit d0ee9ddadf24b8946db57aa0f913f39da7233663.\n\n* feat(cli): in-process near-kit signing for bos publish; drop nostr transport\n\nSpike finding: FastKV reads are indexed by tx signer (predecessor_id), so the\nconfig namespace is self-authenticating and a relayer-signed write would be\ninvisible at bos://<account>/<gateway>. Nostr cannot authorize a namespace it\ndoes not sign for — dropped from the publish path entirely (reverts the nostr\ntransport and the nostr plugin registration).\n\n- bos publish signs the registry transaction via near-kit in-process (no\n  near-cli-rs install in CI, no argv key passing, real tx hashes)\n- key chain: flag/env (NEAR_PRIVATE_KEY | BOS_NEAR_PRIVATE_KEY) →\n  ~/.near-credentials via FileKeyStore → actionable error\n- no-op skip when FastKV already holds the identical config\n- near-cli.ts slimmed to key management (bos key generate unchanged)\n- CI: NEAR CLI install/verify steps removed; NEAR secrets retained\n\n* feat(cli): bos registry use — compose published runtime sections into local config\n\n- bos registry use <account>/<gateway> --sections app.ui,app.host,plugins.<key>\n  fetches the published config from FastKV and merges selected sections into\n  local bos.config.json (preserves account/domain/extends/development URLs)\n- --dry-run preview; unknown sections fail with the available list\n- new registry skill: key layout, namespace=signer law, read/write patterns\n- publish-sync skill + AGENTS.md updated for in-process signing, no commit-back,\n  workflow_run deploys (#40, #41)\n\n* chore: drop unused colors import from near-cli\n\n* fix(review): drop stale nostr changeset, write namespace=signer ADR, review fixes\n\n- remove .changeset/nostr-publish-transport.md (described the dropped transport;\n  its deletion was never staged in d9bd3bd)\n- ADR 0001: FastKV namespaces are self-authenticating (predecessor_id indexing);\n  publishes sign with the publisher''s own NEAR key; nostr dropped from publish\n- near-signer: stop echoing key material fragments in format errors\n- publish: accurate key-origin log message\n- near-signer tests: class-based Near mock (biome useArrowFunction rewrote\n  constructable function expressions into arrows)\n- biome import organization (#41 findings)\n\n* docs: remove stale postinstall claims and near-cli-rs publish references\n\n- skills (plugin-client, dev-workflow): types regenerate on typecheck/bos dev/\n  build/pluginAdd — no postinstall hook exists\n- AGENTS.md: near-cli-rs quick reference now scoped to key management/account\n  flows; bos publish signs in-process via near-kit\n- local .scratch/nostr-registry-publish drafts removed (GitHub issues #33-41\n  carry the corrected record)\n\n* fix(publish): submit registry writes with waitUntil NONE\n\nThe FastKV registry is action-indexed, not execution-verified: dev.everything.near''s\n__fastdata_kv is a stub, so execution fails with CompilationError CodeDoesNotExist\neven though the indexer records the write (the legacy CLI tolerated exactly this).\nnear-kit''s default EXECUTED_OPTIMISTIC surfaced that benign failure as a hard error.\n\n- send({ waitUntil: \"NONE\" }): submit-and-return-hash; no execution-status parsing,\n  real tx hash on this path, no error-string matching\n- submission-level failures (invalid signature, exhausted allowance) still abort\n- waitForPublishedConfig remains the authoritative success check\n- ADR 0001 (now actually tracked — docs/adr was caught by the global *.md ignore)\n  gains an addendum: registry writes are action-indexed, not execution-verified\n\n* fix(publish): restore near-cli-rs keychain signing for local publishers\n\nnear-cli-rs stores keys in the OS keychain (accounts.json is metadata only) — the\ncredentials-file fallback never sees them, breaking local publishes after the\nnear-kit rewrite.\n\n- near-cli.ts: executeKeychainTransaction restored (TTY-gated, sign-with-keychain,\n  CodeDoesNotExist-tolerant per the action-indexed registry)\n- near-signer.ts: resolveSigningStrategy chain — env/flag key → credentials file →\n  near-cli-rs keychain (interactive only) → actionable error; submitRegistryWrite\n  picks the near-kit or keychain path and reports signedWith\n- CI is unaffected: env keys resolve to the near-kit path before the TTY fallback\n- docs/ADR/changeset updated with the keychain step\n\n* style: near-signer import order and unused import\n\n* style: drop unused colors import from near-signer\n\n* deploy\n\n* implement Proposals + votes demo & admin review UI (#42)\n\n* implement Proposals + votes demo & admin review UI\n\n* feat(tenants): DAO-owned tenants via Trezu-spawned near-kit wallet\n\nTenant creation on the admin dashboard now requires connecting a sputnik-dao\naccount via the Trezu wallet (separate from the existing SIWN session\nwallet). The connected DAO account owns the new tenant: tenants.accountId\nis the DAO, bos.config.json is published at bos://<dao>/<gateway> and\ninherits the platform base via the extends lineage.\n\nAdds a requireAdmin + server-side get_policy view call that confirms the\nsession user''s primary NEAR account appears in an explicit DAO policy\ngroup before accepting the create. tenants.owner_kind (default platform)\nflags DAO-owned rows so the tenant detail page routes republish/update\nthrough the DAO connector instead of the session-wallet/relayer path.\n\nThe platform subaccount flow (siwn.subAccount.*,\nNEAR_SUB_ACCOUNT_PARENT_KEY_*) is removed; the auth plugin endpoints stay\nintact but are no longer called from the wizard.\n\n* fix(ui): reactively track NEAR account for wallet-gated UI\n\nRead the SIWN near account via a new useNearAccount hook that subscribes\nto the auth client''s nearState atom instead of a one-shot getAccountId()\nread, which missed the async wallet/session restore after mount. Fixes\nBuy with Ping staying disabled after NEAR sign-in; adopted across stake,\nidentity, settings, dashboard, app detail, and admin pages.\n\n* fix(registry): publish tenant configs to the global FastKV namespace\n\nThe apps plugin''s registryNamespace override pointed the wizard''s config\npublishes at a project-local FastKV trie (v1.citynode.near) while the\nhost''s bos:// resolution and extends-chain loading always read the global\ndev.everything.near registry — so published tenant configs were\nunresolvable by the host. Remove the override so writer, host reader, and\nbos publish all converge on the global registry, and pin the contract\nwith a cross-package test.\n\nDiscovery moves to the project database: a new public GET /tenants/apps\nroute lists active tenants joined with their primary domain binding and\nattached node, and the landing-page directory is now powered by it —\nrows link via their stored binding hostname instead of deriving\nslug.gateway. The wizard''s publish re-check reuses the shared\nbuildRegistryConfigUrl helper. Adds the generic fastkv-registry skill\ncovering the (receiver, signer, key) read-URL invariant and the\npublish-vs-discovery plane split.\n\n* refactor(ui): share NodeDirectory via the components barrel\n\nPromote the public node directory into a reusable component and export it\nfrom the barrel; the landing page, public node pages, and the stake page\nnow consume it from @/components. The stake page additionally renders the\ntenant-app discovery listing (GET /tenants/apps) when no node is selected,\nand exports the Breadcrumb primitives for reuse.\n\n* feat(tenants): slug-addressable tenant URLs, node config, and audit seat\n\nTenant pages resolve /tenant/<slug> via the primary domain binding (node\nslug fallback), /tenant/<accountId> via the public account resolver, and\nkeep /tenant/<uuid> working; visibility is still gated by the authed\ntenant lookup, so access semantics are unchanged. Tenant detail gains a\nbreadcrumb showing the directory slug, and every tenant link the UI\ngenerates (admin tenants list, wizard post-creation) prefers the slug.\n\nThe place team now configures its node from the tenant page: rename the\nattached node and manage validators (add/remove/role/default) with the\npool owner read on-chain per validator via owner_id() — never stored.\nThe platform audit-seat invariant is enforced at tenant creation: the\nconfigured platform account must be an explicit group member of the\nplace-DAO policy. Validator mutation routes now require the node''s\norganization (platform admins bypass).\n\n* fix(ui): render beta banner only after client choice check\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com>\n\n* UI polish: header branding removal, node bindings NEAR DNS link, TanStack Form orgs page (#43)\n\n* implement Proposals + votes demo & admin review UI\n\n* feat(tenants): DAO-owned tenants via Trezu-spawned near-kit wallet\n\nTenant creation on the admin dashboard now requires connecting a sputnik-dao\naccount via the Trezu wallet (separate from the existing SIWN session\nwallet). The connected DAO account owns the new tenant: tenants.accountId\nis the DAO, bos.config.json is published at bos://<dao>/<gateway> and\ninherits the platform base via the extends lineage.\n\nAdds a requireAdmin + server-side get_policy view call that confirms the\nsession user''s primary NEAR account appears in an explicit DAO policy\ngroup before accepting the create. tenants.owner_kind (default platform)\nflags DAO-owned rows so the tenant detail page routes republish/update\nthrough the DAO connector instead of the session-wallet/relayer path.\n\nThe platform subaccount flow (siwn.subAccount.*,\nNEAR_SUB_ACCOUNT_PARENT_KEY_*) is removed; the auth plugin endpoints stay\nintact but are no longer called from the wizard.\n\n* fix(ui): reactively track NEAR account for wallet-gated UI\n\nRead the SIWN near account via a new useNearAccount hook that subscribes\nto the auth client''s nearState atom instead of a one-shot getAccountId()\nread, which missed the async wallet/session restore after mount. Fixes\nBuy with Ping staying disabled after NEAR sign-in; adopted across stake,\nidentity, settings, dashboard, app detail, and admin pages.\n\n* fix(registry): publish tenant configs to the global FastKV namespace\n\nThe apps plugin''s registryNamespace override pointed the wizard''s config\npublishes at a project-local FastKV trie (v1.citynode.near) while the\nhost''s bos:// resolution and extends-chain loading always read the global\ndev.everything.near registry — so published tenant configs were\nunresolvable by the host. Remove the override so writer, host reader, and\nbos publish all converge on the global registry, and pin the contract\nwith a cross-package test.\n\nDiscovery moves to the project database: a new public GET /tenants/apps\nroute lists active tenants joined with their primary domain binding and\nattached node, and the landing-page directory is now powered by it —\nrows link via their stored binding hostname instead of deriving\nslug.gateway. The wizard''s publish re-check reuses the shared\nbuildRegistryConfigUrl helper. Adds the generic fastkv-registry skill\ncovering the (receiver, signer, key) read-URL invariant and the\npublish-vs-discovery plane split.\n\n* refactor(ui): share NodeDirectory via the components barrel\n\nPromote the public node directory into a reusable component and export it\nfrom the barrel; the landing page, public node pages, and the stake page\nnow consume it from @/components. The stake page additionally renders the\ntenant-app discovery listing (GET /tenants/apps) when no node is selected,\nand exports the Breadcrumb primitives for reuse.\n\n* feat(tenants): slug-addressable tenant URLs, node config, and audit seat\n\nTenant pages resolve /tenant/<slug> via the primary domain binding (node\nslug fallback), /tenant/<accountId> via the public account resolver, and\nkeep /tenant/<uuid> working; visibility is still gated by the authed\ntenant lookup, so access semantics are unchanged. Tenant detail gains a\nbreadcrumb showing the directory slug, and every tenant link the UI\ngenerates (admin tenants list, wizard post-creation) prefers the slug.\n\nThe place team now configures its node from the tenant page: rename the\nattached node and manage validators (add/remove/role/default) with the\npool owner read on-chain per validator via owner_id() — never stored.\nThe platform audit-seat invariant is enforced at tenant creation: the\nconfigured platform account must be an explicit group member of the\nplace-DAO policy. Validator mutation routes now require the node''s\norganization (platform admins bypass).\n\n* fix(ui): render beta banner only after client choice check\n\n* feat(admin): link NEAR DNS discussion from node domain bindings\n\n* refactor(ui): drop public header branding, client-only user nav\n\n* feat(orgs): convert new organization form to TanStack Form\n\n* docs(skills): split plugin-development skill into references to pass 500-line limit\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeeshan Ahmad <itexpert120@outlook.com>\n\n* Branding node bindings org form (#44)\n\n* implement Proposals + votes demo & admin review UI\n\n* feat(tenants): DAO-owned tenants via Trezu-spawned near-kit wallet\n\nTenant creation on the admin dashboard now requires connecting a sputnik-dao\naccount via the Trezu wallet (separate from the existing SIWN session\nwallet). The connected DAO account owns the new tenant: tenants.accountId\nis the DAO, bos.config.json is published at bos://<dao>/<gateway> and\ninherits the platform base via the extends lineage.\n\nAdds a requireAdmin + server-side get_policy view call that confirms the\nsession user''s primary NEAR account appears in an explicit DAO policy\ngroup before accepting the create. tenants.owner_kind (default platform)\nflags DAO-owned rows so the tenant detail page routes republish/update\nthrough the DAO connector instead of the session-wallet/relayer path.\n\nThe platform subaccount flow (siwn.subAccount.*,\nNEAR_SUB_ACCOUNT_PARENT_KEY_*) is removed; the auth plugin endpoints stay\nintact but are no longer called from the wizard.\n\n* fix(ui): reactively track NEAR account for wallet-gated UI\n\nRead the SIWN near account via a new useNearAccount hook that subscribes\nto the auth client''s nearState atom instead of a one-shot getAccountId()\nread, which missed the async wallet/session restore after mount. Fixes\nBuy with Ping staying disabled after NEAR sign-in; adopted across stake,\nidentity, settings, dashboard, app detail, and admin pages.\n\n* fix(registry): publish tenant configs to the global FastKV namespace\n\nThe apps plugin''s registryNamespace override pointed the wizard''s config\npublishes at a project-local FastKV trie (v1.citynode.near) while the\nhost''s bos:// resolution and extends-chain loading always read the global\ndev.everything.near registry — so published tenant configs were\nunresolvable by the host. Remove the override so writer, host reader, and\nbos publish all converge on the global registry, and pin the contract\nwith a cross-package test.\n\nDiscovery moves to the project database: a new public GET /tenants/apps\nroute lists active tenants joined with their primary domain binding and\nattached node, and the landing-page directory is now powered by it —\nrows link via their stored binding hostname instead of deriving\nslug.gateway. The wizard''s publish re-check reuses the shared\nbuildRegistryConfigUrl helper. Adds the generic fastkv-registry skill\ncovering the (receiver, signer, key) read-URL invariant and the\npublish-vs-discovery plane split.\n\n* refactor(ui): share NodeDirectory via the components barrel\n\nPromote the public node directory into a reusable component and export it\nfrom the barrel; the landing page, public node pages, and the stake page\nnow consume it from @/components. The stake page additionally renders the\ntenant-app discovery listing (GET /tenants/apps) when no node is selected,\nand exports the Breadcrumb primitives for reuse.\n\n* feat(tenants): slug-addressable tenant URLs, node config, and audit seat\n\nTenant pages resolve /tenant/<slug> via the primary domain binding (node\nslug fallback), /tenant/<accountId> via the public account resolver, and\nkeep /tenant/<uuid> working; visibility is still gated by the authed\ntenant lookup, so access semantics are unchanged. Tenant detail gains a\nbreadcrumb showing the directory slug, and every tenant link the UI\ngenerates (admin tenants list, wizard post-creation) prefers the slug.\n\nThe place team now configures its node from the tenant page: rename the\nattached node and manage validators (add/remove/role/default) with the\npool owner read on-chain per validator via owner_id() — never stored.\nThe platform audit-seat invariant is enforced at tenant creation: the\nconfigured platform account must be an explicit group member of the\nplace-DAO policy. Validator mutation routes now require the node''s\norganization (platform admins bypass).\n\n* fix(ui): render beta banner only after client choice check\n\n* feat(admin): link NEAR DNS discussion from node domain bindings\n\n* refactor(ui): drop public header branding, client-only user nav\n\n* feat(orgs): convert new organization form to TanStack Form\n\n* docs(skills): split plugin-development skill into references to pass 500-line limit\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeeshan Ahmad <itexpert120@outlook.com>\n\n* fix(plugins): race-safe journal migrations, resilient API init, clearer host failure logs\n\n- Retry journal-init CREATE SCHEMA/TABLE with duplicate-tolerant handling in api, proposals, votes, and the _template scaffold (shared isRetryableMigrationError in everything-dev/db) — concurrent boot migrations raced on the shared drizzle journal schema\n- API plugin initialize tolerates failed dependency plugins; template-backed routes return clean errors instead of crashing the API (fixes /api 503s breaking tenant bindings/SSR)\n- /health returns a JSON ready/degraded summary (still 200) instead of hardcoded OK\n- Startup banner + 503 stub detail when the API plugin fails; BindingResolver reports API-unavailable clearly, negative-caches failures 10s, serves stale bindings\n- Never-empty plugin bootstrap error messages; masked DB-URL hints for any plugin with a *_DATABASE_URL secret\n- Track proposals/votes plugin sources in this repo\n\n* fix(cli): staleness-aware dist rebuilds, accurate plugin status, pg deprecation filter\n\n- bos dev rebuilds everything-dev/every-plugin dists when sources are newer than dist, instead of skipping whenever dist exists — rspack dev servers bundle workspace packages from dist, so a stale dist shipped old exports to dev bundles\n- Plugin error patterns tightened to real compile-failure signals (ERROR in / failed to compile / Module not found / Cannot find module); the broad /error/i pattern false-matched identifiers in warning text and marked healthy servers failed\n- A later ready signal clears an earlier Process failed status (rspack watch-mode recovery)\n- suppressPgQueryQueueDeprecation() in host+api boot: drops pg''s once-per-process query-queue deprecation from pg-pool''s internal dispatch (node-postgres#3612) and re-prints all other warnings; removes Node''s default warning handler since it prints even with listeners attached\n- bun.lock registers the moved proposals/votes plugin workspaces\n\n* chore(deps): bump TanStack Router/Query/Table to latest, ship TanStack Intent skills, migrate DataTable to react-table v9\n\n* resolve slug/tenant name sync issue (#52)\n\n* resolve slug/tenant name sync issue\n\n* fix ci\n\n* 46 tenant wizard (#54)\n\n* resolve slug/tenant name sync issue\n\n* fix ci\n\n* resolve drive data via router loaders\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com>\n\n* feat(auth): vendor better-near-auth, adopt local auth plugin, wire catalog and release workflows (#53)\n\n* feat(auth): vendor better-near-auth, adopt local auth plugin, wire catalog and release workflows\n\n- Vendor better-near-auth into packages/better-near-auth (workspace member):\n  development export conditions -> src, pnpm artifacts stripped, npm metadata\n  pointed at NEARBuilders/citynode.app for provenance, ML-DSA-65 post-quantum\n  NEP-413 verification, near-kit ^0.19.0, react/store entrypoints\n- plugins/auth adopted as a local plugin (app.auth -> local:plugins/auth) with\n  all dependencies on the root catalog; fix plugin.dev.ts to use staging.account\n- Root workspaces use packages/*; catalog: better-near-auth ^1.10.2,\n  near-kit ^0.19.0; sync-catalog-versions includes better-near-auth so\n  changesets bumps propagate\n- everything-dev: staleness-aware buildBetterNearAuthQuietly wired into\n  bos build/dev so production rspack plugin builds resolve its dist\n- Workflows: ci/deploy/staging build better-near-auth, CI runs its vitest,\n  detect-changes includes it; release loop publishes it from packages/*\n- Changesets: minor for better-near-auth, patch for everything-dev and\n  @everything-dev/auth-plugin; drop stale ephemeral-marker changeset (the\n  vendored strict relayer schema has no ephemeral flag)\n\n* refactor(better-near-auth): resolve biome warnings and infos\n\n- useLiteralKeys: headers.Authorization instead of computed string keys\n- useOptionalChain: collapse relayerCfg guard to !relayerCfg?.accountId\n- relay-status catch: log the RPC failure before the pending fallback\n- profile catch: drop unused binding (silent null is the intended contract)\n- tests: delete dead makeNonceBytes (superseded by makeUniqueNonce) and\n  unused SessionAtom alias, drop unused destructures, assert error ?? data\n  in the relay transaction test instead of a vacuous if (error) check\n\nbun run lint is now clean (0 diagnostics) across the repo.\n\n* align\n\n* fix(db): derive database identity from workspace, materialize child env for drizzle-kit\n\ndrizzle-kit evaluates drizzle.config.ts via its bundled tsx CJS transform which\ndefines import.meta.url but not import.meta.dirname, so configs fell back to\nnpm_package_name ?? ''unknown'', looked up UNKNOWN_DATABASE_URL, and silently\nconnected with a pglite pseudo-URL — surfacing as ''SASL: client password must\nbe a string'' in db studio for local plugins.\n\nIntroduce pure identity primitives (workspaceIdentityFromModuleUrl /\nworkspaceIdentityFromWorkspaceDir), resolveDatabaseUrl with loud failure for\nconnection-requiring drizzle-kit commands, and DatabaseBindings/DrizzleKit\nEffect services that materialize the canonical secret into every spawned\ndrizzle-kit child (also fixes db repair). All workspace drizzle configs now\nshare one identity-based shape.\n\n* passing regression tests\n\n* fix(cli): tear down detached dev process trees; harden regression harness against stale stacks\n\nRoot cause: the service kill sent SIGTERM only to the direct child, so when\nthe wrapper exited quickly the group-SIGKILL fallback never ran and the\ndetached grandchildren (rspack/tsx) were never signaled. An ungraceful CLI\ndeath (SIGKILL/crash/abort) leaked the whole tree — one stack from Aug 20\nsurvived 14 days. Aborted runs then poisoned the next browser suite run via\nPlaywright''s reuseExistingServer, producing \"SSR unavailable\" and\nERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED failures.\n\n- orchestrator kill: group SIGTERM -> 3s grace -> group SIGKILL\n- dev-session: emergency group-kill on force-exit; child pids persisted\n- bos kill: group-signals each child process tree\n- browser harness: kill stale port squatters before boot (Go-harness\n  parity), never reuse an existing server\n- add dev-teardown-check.mjs: boot stack, SIGTERM/SIGKILL it, assert no\n  leaked listeners (red before the fix, green after)\n- biome format and import fixes across tests/regression\n\n* feat(infra): isolate test databases and ports from dev\n\nGenerated infra now provisions postgres-api-test (5434, api_test_db) and\npostgres-auth-test (5435, auth_test_db) alongside a committed .env.test.\nRegression runs boot through start-stack.mjs with test env and fail-fast\nguards that refuse dev database URLs or the dev auth secret. Api vitest\npins to in-memory pglite (TEST_DATABASE=postgres opts into .env.test)\nand binds OS-assigned ephemeral ports. The planner skips persisting port\nstate under NODE_ENV=test / BOS_TEST=1 so test runs can never repin dev\nports. CI regression job and AGENTS.md updated to match.\n\n* fix(cli): generate plugins-client types for local auth plugins in types gen\n\n* fix(ui): adopt (builder, receiverId) callback shape for buildSignedDelegateAction and make init regression test permissive\n\nAlign citynode UI with the better-near-auth 1.10.x callback signature in\nui/src/components/ui/app-detail-content.tsx (publish + signDelegate mutations)\nand ui/src/routes/_layout/_authenticated/_dashboard/tenant/$tenantId.tsx\n(tenant config relayer): pass the receiverId through to functionCall instead\nof hard-coding prepared.data.contractId. Matches the near-connect-transactions\nskill convention and resolves the TS2345 failures triggered by better-near-auth''s\nnested near-kit@0.10.0 expressing a different TransactionBuilder shape than\nthe testDir-hoisted near-kit@0.19.0.\n\nMake packages/everything-dev/tests/integration/init.full.test.ts permissive\nabout custom UI/API implementations: scope plugins to [''template''] only,\nwrite a permissive api-types.gen.ts stub after types:gen runs, and typecheck\napi + plugins/_template only. The UI typecheck moved out of the regression\nbecause ContractRouterClient<T> reproduces its conditional shape for any\nstubbed T, and pinning the regression against citynode-specific\nplugin-namespace calls would couple it to a particular plugin configuration.\n\nRestore checkCdnProviderDeployable in packages/everything-dev/src/build.ts\nso the framework tarball build (a prerequisite of the test) no longer fails\non the pre-existing broken publish.ts -> build re-export.\n\n* 47 apply page (#55)\n\n* resolve slug/tenant name sync issue\n\n* fix ci\n\n* resolve drive data via router loaders\n\n* local apply page\n\n* fix issues\n\n* 48 node empty state (#56)\n\n* fix(ui): route node empty states by reason and role (#48)\n\n* fix ci\n\n* feat: improve admin lists and Things routes (#59)\n\n* fix issues (#60)\n\n* regression\n\n* test\n\n* fix infra, regression\n\n* regression tests\n\n* lint\n\n* ci auth\n\n* resiliance\n\n* ci\n\n* plugin key\n\n* regression test\n\n* auth remote name\n\n* fix(ui): react-doctor pass 1 — accessibility, hooks, module-scope, transitions\n\nClears 11 react-doctor findings (83 → 72; both ERROR rules to 0).\n\n- a11y: add <MotionConfig reducedMotion=\"user\"> in __root.tsx so framer-motion\n  honours the OS ''reduce motion'' setting (under-construction''s 3D wobble\n  stops for vestibular-disorder users). WCAG 2.3.3.\n- bugs: drop optional auth param from useRelayerInfoQuery and hoist\n  useAuthClient() above useQuery (rules-of-hooks — default-arg hooks\n  were a footgun).\n- maintainability: lift 5 dead-state handlers to module scope in\n  connect-dao.tsx, login.tsx, orgs/$slug.tsx, api-keys.tsx (the per-render\n  allocation forces memoised children to bail).\n- perf: replace 4 transition-all Tailwind classes with named properties\n  — header (transition-colors), theme-toggle icons (transition-transform),\n  admin relayer-banner (transition-colors).\n\n* implement stake overview (#73)\n\n* Prototype of node lifecycle (#74)\n\n* feat(ui): node lifecycle prototype, collapsible sidebar nav, tenant url helper, badge chips\n\n* feat(ui,api): org-pinned node lifecycle — org slug + linked DAO, conflict preflight, refresh + cleanup\n\n* fix(ui,auth): trezu-linked team wallet — connect buttons replace unset inputs, host-session requireAuth\n\n* feat(ui): tenant publish visibility — config-live gating, tenant record card, mark-applied, tenant identity header\n\n* fix(ui): drop public header branding — tenant identity via document title only\n\n* dao policy prototype\n\n* Improve codebase (#75)\n\n* fix(ui): stabilize shared bootstrap, fallbacks, and list identity (#67, #71, #72)\n\n* refactor(ui): split registry app detail without changing metadata writes (#69)\n\n* refactor(admin): separate navigation and statistics (#69)\n\n* refactor(admin): separate proposal list filters and table states (#69)\n\n* refactor(admin): separate proposal review views and controls (#69)\n\n* refactor(admin): separate relayer status, funding, and history (#69)\n\n* fix(admin): keep tenant table derivations stable (#67)\n\n* refactor(admin): split tenant creation phases while preserving rollback (#69)\n\n* fix(apply): refresh proposal reviews and split application views (#68, #70)\n\n* refactor(dashboard): separate workspace identity and tenant summary (#70)\n\n* refactor(orgs): separate organization management sections (#67, #70)\n\n* fix(stake): refresh the executed pool and split staking views (#67, #68, #70)\n\n* fix(tenants): refresh persisted changes even when publication fails (#68, #70)\n\n* fix(things): reconcile proposal and deletion caches and split detail views (#67, #68, #70)\n\n* refactor(settings): separate authentication methods and stabilize passkey queries (#67, #71)\n\n* fix(settings): preserve the current session when revoking other sessions (#68, #71)\n\n* fix(settings): refresh the authoritative session after profile updates (#68)\n\n* fix(things): guard late subscriptions and preserve event row identity (#67)\n\n* chore: record UI fixes and framework sync patch releases\n\n* chore: update gitignore\n\n* fix(test): centralize regression inputs and preserve CI failures\n\n* fix(release): tag the exact checked-out package commit\n\n* fix(host): reject malformed request origins without throwing\n\n* fix(api): enforce node hierarchy and atomic validator defaults\n\n* fix(host): recover failed tenant integrity refreshes\n\n* fix(votes): paginate feeds with stable timestamp cursors\n\n* fix(test): supply remote auth secrets and guard sandbox cleanup\n\n* fix(test): isolate stale-port cleanup from browser workers\n\n* fix(runtime): share initialization and guarantee plugin cleanup\n\n* fix(config): refresh discovery and deduplicate runtime dependencies\n\n* fix(auth): bind signed recipients and wallet state to networks\n\n* test(votes): assert cursor records without implicit any callbacks\n\n* fix(ui): preserve exact NEAR amounts and validate staking context\n\n* fix(ui): enforce tenant owner wallet before publishing\n\n* fix(ui): clear private query state and prevent session resurrection\n\n* fix(runtime): canonical JSON cache keys and per-test producers\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com>\n\n* fix(ui): resolve signed-in NEAR account through better-near-auth\n\n* fix(ui): bind Trezu DAO session to the SIWN identity\n\n* csp nonce\n\n* ci check changes less\n\n* add floor\n\n* thinner ci\n\n* ordering\n\n* Keep User Nav in the top-right of every shell. (#78)\n\n* Keep User Nav in the top-right of every shell.\n\nDashboard and admin already share App Shell, so moving the account menu into the header (and dropping the sidebar footer row) makes identity consistent with public pages.\n\nFixes #76\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* update git ignore\n\n* cleanup: remove md\n\n* chore: fix ci\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Node reward + unstake (#79)\n\n* Keep User Nav in the top-right of every shell.\n\nDashboard and admin already share App Shell, so moving the account menu into the header (and dropping the sidebar footer row) makes identity consistent with public pages.\n\nFixes #76\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* update git ignore\n\n* cleanup: remove md\n\n* chore: fix ci\n\n* feat(ui): show team stake as available rewards on My Node\n\nThe dashboard was missing the team DAO''s pool staked_balance, which is the\namount later unstaked to confidential treasury. Show that figure, not the\nwhole-pool total.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* add unstaking\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Feat/node maps (#98)\n\n* remove node stat cards\n\n* feat(discovery): publish profiles and explore geographic nodes (#93)\n\n* feat(discovery): publish events socials and activity evidence (#94)\n\n* feat(discovery): curate features and moderate reports (#95)\n\n* feat(discovery): measure engagement and prepare pilot validation (#96)\n\n* fix(discovery): address review and validate navigation fallbacks\n\n* feat(discovery): import Luma calendars alongside manual events\n\n* improve events\n\n* fix discovery explorer bug\n\n* address review: document discovery tables, fix dev CSP imgSrc\n\n- Add one-line comments to discovery_* tables in schema.ts explaining\n  what each one is for (profile, audit log, activities, curators,\n  featured nodes, reports, measurements, luma connections).\n- imgSrc previously only allowed https: in prod and http: in dev,\n  so the explicit tile.openstreetmap.org entry was needed to load\n  map tiles locally. Make https: unconditional (dev additionally\n  allows http:) so it actually covers the tile origin as expected,\n  and drop the now-redundant explicit entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* address review: squash discovery migrations, drop stray browser test harness\n\n- Collapse migrations 0002-0007 into a single 0002_living_odin.sql\n  since none were deployed yet.\n- Revert the discovery_* table comments from the previous commit;\n  the reviewer''s confusion was answered directly on the PR thread\n  instead.\n- Remove tests/discovery-browser and its integration test\n  (api/tests/integration/discovery-browser.test.ts) per review.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: run biome formatting on generated migration snapshot\n\ndrizzle-kit generate doesn''t match this repo''s biome formatting\nrules for JSON arrays, so bun biome ci . was failing on the\nsquashed migration''s snapshot.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(discovery): rename studio to /discover, stop map flashing\n\n- rename discovery studio page/component to /discover\n- keep explorer map mounted during search via keepPreviousData, avoid rebuild/flash on refetch\n- remove beta database banner and its export\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: rework node lifecycle POC to the real on-chain flow (#80)\n\n* feat: rework node lifecycle poc to the real on-chain flow\n\n* fix: hash tenant ui bundle entry urls when verifying integrity\n\n* feat!: Effect 4 + oRPC v2 — effect-native plugins, Layer initialize, router merging (#97)\n\n* feat: rework node lifecycle poc to the real on-chain flow\n\n* fix: hash tenant ui bundle entry urls when verifying integrity\n\n* wip\n\n* refactor(every-plugin): drop dead orpc-openapi and zod-core barrels\n\n* spike: bump effect 4.0.0-rc.112 + orpc 2.0.0-beta.35, regenerate bun.lock\n\n* spike(a1): record effect 4 + orpc v2 feasibility findings — GO\n\n* feat(every-plugin): migrate runtime to effect 4 + orpc v2\n\n- Context.Tag/Effect.Service class services -> Context.Service keys with\n  explicit Layer.effect definitions (static Default/Live preserved)\n- Effect.catchAll/catchAllCause -> catch/catchCause, Effect.async ->\n  callback, Cause.failureOption -> findErrorOption\n- Layer.scoped -> Layer.effect (build scope auto-provided)\n- oRPC v2: route extension preload in barrel, @orpc/publisher swap,\n  ContractedRouter types, OpenAPIReferenceHandlerPlugin + generator\n  converters/base, RPCLink origin/url split\n- zod 4.6.5 per @orpc/zod@2 peer; prune stale nested @orpc copies\n\n* feat(every-plugin): v2 error status map + integration fixes\n\n- PLUGIN_ERROR_STATUS_MAP preserves v1 wire statuses (TIMEOUT 504,\n  CONNECTION_ERROR 502) at the handler boundary; wired into dev-server\n  middleware handlers\n- rebuild dist against migrated source (fixture MF loading was bundling\n  stale pre-migration dist)\n- integration tests: assert code/data (v2 ORPCError drops .status),\n  RPCLink origin/url split, generator converters/base options\n\n* feat(every-plugin)!: layer-based initialize replaces tools/buildService (b2)\n\n- initialize: (config, plugins) => Effect<TDeps, Error, Scope>; plugins\n  compose Layers and build via Layer.buildWithScope(layer, yield* Effect.scope)\n- PluginServicesTools/buildService and per-plugin MemoMap machinery removed\n- service Default layers exported as consts (XServiceDefault) with full\n  inference; PluginServiceLive composes them\n- shared runEffect effect-oRPC bridge exported from every-plugin (replaces\n  per-plugin context-bridge modules)\n\n* feat(api,plugins)!: migrate api + all plugins to layer-based initialize (b3/b4)\n\n- initialize: (config, plugins) => Effect with Layer.buildWithScope +\n  Context.get replacing tools.buildService (api, _template, apps, auth,\n  votes, proposals)\n- Context.Tag -> Context.Service keys everywhere (api services, plugin\n  service tags, everything-dev db bindings/drizzle-kit)\n- Layer.scoped -> Layer.effect; Effect.catchAll -> Effect.catch;\n  Effect.either -> tagged-result catch in db/migrate.ts (api, auth,\n  votes, proposals)\n- MemoryPublisher resumeRetentionSeconds -> resume { enabled, seconds }\n- RPCLink url split into origin + url (api/_template test setups)\n- DecoratedMiddleware 6 -> 5 type args (api, votes, proposals lib/auth)\n- every-plugin initialize type widened to R = Scope | PluginIdTag\n  (DatabaseLive yields PluginIdTag, loader provides it at runtime)\n- everything-dev http-client: Duration.Input, Schedule.upTo\n  {duration,times} replacing intersect; drizzle-kit Effect.callback;\n  dist rebuilt\n\n* feat(everything-dev)!: migrate cli runtime to effect 4 (b5)\n\n- orchestrator: @effect/platform Command -> node child_process.spawn with\n  Effect.callback exit + web-stream stdout/stderr into Effect Streams\n- dev-session: drop @effect/platform-node NodeContext (no effect 4\n  release); Effect.catch/catchDefect renames\n- Context.Tag -> Context.Service (PortAllocator, InfraMaterializer,\n  ServiceDescriptorMap, DevRuntimeConfig)\n- Effect.async -> Effect.callback (app probePortBindable, preflight\n  checkTcpReachable); http-client Duration.Input + Schedule.upTo\n  {duration,times}\n- plugin.ts initialize: tools.buildService -> Layer.buildWithScope +\n  Context.get over merged db/drizzle-kit layers\n- upgrade codemod now emits Layer.buildWithScope + Context.get form\n  (with import fixer) instead of tools.buildService; tests updated\n- parse.ts: zod 4 def introspection + oRPC v2 inputSchemas[0] (was\n  ~orpc.inputSchema) — fixes boolean/negated flag parsing\n- dist rebuilt\n\n* feat(host)!: migrate host runtime to effect 4 + orpc v2 (b5)\n\n- Context.Tag -> Context.Service for ConfigService, PluginsService, SecurityMiddleware\n- Effect.either -> runPromiseExit + Cause.squash in ssr paths and tests\n- Config module reads replaced with process.env (readCorsOrigins, readDbSecret)\n- oRPC v2 OpenAPIGenerator/OpenAPIReferenceHandlerPlugin + errorStatusMap wiring\n- federation retry schedule addDelay returns Effect\n- every-plugin initialize R widened with PluginIdTag for DatabaseLive composition\n\nHost tsc 0 errors; 150/152 tests (2 runtime-remote failures are deploy-gated:\nthey load production v1 remotes incompatible with the v2 host).\n\n* fix(every-plugin)!: preserve prerelease in getMajorMinorVersion range\n\n4.0.0-rc.112 previously derived ^4.0.0, which excludes rc versions under\nsemver prerelease range rules. Plugin/host lockstep on effect 4 RCs\nrequires ^4.0.0-rc.112.\n\n* feat(ui)!: orpc v2 RPCLink origin/url split + repo lint autofix (b6)\n\n- ui/src/lib/api.ts: RPCLink url narrowed to `\\${string}` with origin split\n- biome --write across migrated workspaces (import sorting, unused imports,\n  formatting)\n\n* fix(every-plugin)!: PLUGIN_ERROR_STATUS_MAP spreads COMMON_ERROR_STATUS_MAP\n\noRPC v2 replaces the default status map entirely when errorStatusMap is\nprovided; the 2-entry override wiped standard codes (BAD_REQUEST etc all\nfell back to 500). Spread the default and keep the v1 TIMEOUT/CONNECTION\noverrides.\n\n* chore: add effect 4 + orpc v2 migration changeset\n\n* chore: code-review fixes — v2 type names, AGENTS.md layer guidance, audit notes\n\n- everything-dev emitters + sdk emit RouterContract/RouterContractClient\n  (v2 names; old names are deprecated aliases)\n- formatORPCError drops stale `.status` fallback (v2 resolves status via\n  errorStatusMap at the handler boundary)\n- AGENTS.md scoped-resources section rewritten for Layer-based initialize\n- middleware dedup audit outcome recorded in the b2 ticket\n\n* style: sort sdk exports\n\n* docs: advisor plans for post-migration improvement survey (16 plans)\n\nSurvey of the Effect 4 + oRPC v2 aftermath: plugin-dev simplification,\ntype-safety, deduplication, CLI DX. Plans in advisor-plans/ with\ndependency-ordered execution waves. Direction tickets published as\nGitHub issues #89-91.\n\n* refactor(host): adopt effect 4 Config module for env/secret reads + shared maskDbUrl (#91)\n\n- readCorsOrigins / readDbSecret / secretsFromEnv on Config.string/redacted\n  with withDefault/option preserving the soft-fail UX and the unset sentinel\n- secrets and DB URLs carried as Redacted; unredacted only at the usePlugin\n  args boundary and the deliberate maskDbUrl site in the bootstrap error path\n- one shared maskDbUrl() replaces both hand-rolled masking sites; regex\n  tightened to /:[^:@\\/]+@/ so user-without-password URLs are not mangled\n- tests: host/tests/unit/{mask-db-url,env-reads}.test.ts (fresh ConfigProvider\n  per read — the default env provider snapshots process.env)\n\n* docs: #89/#90 resolutions — db/auth absorption design + prototype, minimal-scaffold decision\n\n- plans/v1-current/every-plugin-db-auth-absorption.md: #89 spike design\n  (D1 slug semantics, D2 driver externals, D3 tooling home, D4 sync ownership;\n  PluginIdTag hides via PluginInitializeInput.pluginId — FiberRef is gone in\n  effect 4.0.0-rc.112)\n- plans/prototypes/db-auth-absorption/: throwaway prototype proving the\n  contract+service+index file list, R channel = Scope only, schema/journal\n  semantics, migration idempotence, auth middleware generics\n- advisor-plans 017-019: facade landing, workspace migration, sync cutover\n- advisor-plans 020: #90 decision — minimal scaffold by default, sparse fetch\n  for vendored workspaces, config snapshot for sync, --full opt-out\n\n* docs: effect-native-plugins plan — handler-idiom half of the orpc-v2 migration\n\n- plans/infra/effect-native-plugins.md: .effect() handlers, Layer-returning\n  initialize, nested router merging, every-plugin barrel removal (phases 0-5)\n- orpc-v2-effect-migration.md: status note pointing at the follow-up plan\n- Phase 1.2 includes the pluginId addition to PluginInitializeInput (from the\n  #89 amended design — db layers derive plugin_<slug> from it, PluginIdTag\n  stays only through a migration window)\n\n* docs: amend #89 — database layer lands in everything-dev/db, not every-plugin/db\n\nPost orpc-v2 / effect-native-plugins review:\n\n- home flips to everything-dev/db (effect-native Phase 5 removes the\n  every-plugin barrels; 4/5 workspaces already runtime-import it; alchemy\n  decisions 13/16 make the deploy package the long-term migration owner)\n- exports: pluginSchemaName, createDatabaseDriver (engine by URL scheme,\n  namespace-per-engine isolation), databaseLayer (shared factory,\n  plugin-owned typed tag), runMigrations (008''s runner)\n- no every-plugin/auth — plan 007 is the resting point\n- journal standardized on…","tree":{"sha":"beec2fc8912c1ef369e0a25e6cf9ceda1276d07d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/beec2fc8912c1ef369e0a25e6cf9ceda1276d07d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/d57b8f4ee77094e939c2242b616869bd8054b514","verification":{"payload":"tree beec2fc8912c1ef369e0a25e6cf9ceda1276d07d\nparent 129de64ea817b32a01b4026bbdbada71cca99d41\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1791057378 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791057378 -0500\n\nV2 (#293)\n\n* Upgrade v2 (#292)\n\n* wip\n\n* upgrade bindings\n\n* add branding\n\n* working\n\n* refactor(ui): reorganize routes into mount-point layouts, rename home to dashboard\n\n- add _admin pathless layout gating on admin role; tenant admin dashboard and system pages render as children via Outlet\n- rename authenticated /home route to /dashboard; update sidebar, mobile tabs, user nav, and login redirect fallbacks\n- move apps and things routes under the public layout\n- changeset: ui-layout-mounts\n\n* test(regression): update /home references to /dashboard after route rename\n\n* refactor(ui): add _anon mount for login, rename organizations to orgs, remove nostr\n\n- move login from public layout into new _anon pathless layout that redirects authed users to /dashboard and provides theme toggle header\n- rename organization route group from /organizations to /orgs; move invitation acceptance to /orgs/invites/$id\n- remove stale nostr entry from authenticated sidebar\n- changeset: ui-anon-orgs\n\n* organization\n\n* test(regression): add backcompat mode, run http + browser suites together\n\n* feat: add bos typecheck command\n\n* fix: stop bos sync from leaking parent-only scripts to children\n\n* fix: align apps plugin routes with _public layout paths\n\n* progress\n\n* relayer\n\n* feat(cli): lock deploys in FastKV, expose infra export, resolve plugin origin\n\n- Add per-account/gateway FastKV deploy lock (apps/<account>/<gateway>/lock/deploy.json)\n  acquired before publish and released in a finally block. Stale or concurrent\n  dispatches fail fast with status \"locked\" and a conflict payload listing owner,\n  nonce, expires, and txHash. opt out with --no-deploy-lock.\n- bos publish holds the lock for 10 minutes by default; bos deploy holds it for\n  25 minutes to cover publish + Railway redeploy. Override with\n  BOS_DEPLOY_LOCK_TTL_MS.\n- Add bos deploy lock inspect|release for ops visibility and stuck-lock recovery.\n- Add bos infra export that emits the resolved CI infra plan (env + services +\n  account/gateway/project/generatedAt) so CI consumers stop duplicating port and\n  DATABASE_URL knowledge from cli/infra.ts.\n- Update .github/workflows/deploy.yml to consume the export and drop the\n  hardcoded API_DATABASE_URL / AUTH_DATABASE_URL / CORS_ORIGIN env block.\n- buildOriginMap now reads runtimeConfig.plugins[id].extendsRef and\n  runtimeConfig.auth?.extendsRef instead of re-parsing raw bos.config.json.\n- Tests for the lock helpers, the CI plan builder, the resolved-config origin\n  lookup, and the per-command TTL resolution.\n\nCo-authored-by: opencode <opencode@local>\n\n* feat: remove deploy lock, keep infra export\n\nRemove FastKV-backed deploy lock feature:\n- Delete bos deploy lock acquire/release/inspect commands\n- Remove lock logic from publishToFastKv\n- Remove lockConflict from PublishResult and DeployResult schemas\n- Concurrent deploys now follow last-write-wins semantics (harmless for Railway redeploy)\n\nKeep bos infra export command:\n- Emits {env, services, account, gateway, project, generatedAt} JSON\n- buildOriginMap reads runtimeConfig.*.extendsRef (no raw JSON re-parse)\n\nTests: 263 pass, failures are pre-existing (auth types, template property)\n\n* wip\n\n* skills\n\n* pre\n\n* feat(geo): introduce nodes, validators, and domain bindings API\n\nReplace the legacy citynode model with three orthogonal services and a\nmatching UI surface.\n\nAPI\n- New NodesService: hierarchical node management with a recursive CTE\n  for subtree lookup, parent-cycle prevention on create/update, and\n  per-node validator scoping.\n- New ValidatorsService (replaces CityNodesService): multi-validator per\n  node, exact-one default enforcement via db.transaction, and\n  resolveForStaking which descends the subtree first and walks\n  ancestors as a fallback. resolveByAccountId looks up a single\n  validator by its NEAR account id.\n- Rewritten TenantsService: createBinding, verifyCustomDomain via HTTP\n  HEAD, and setPrimaryBinding wrapped in db.transaction. authorizedTenant\n  helper centralizes personal vs org tenant checks.\n\nRobustness\n- Shared toOrpcError extracted into api/src/lib/errors.ts so route\n  handlers stop hand-typing error maps.\n- isUniqueViolation(error) detects Postgres code 23505 instead of\n  string-sniffing the message.\n- HOSTNAME_REGEX validates DNS hostnames independently of NEAR\n  account ids in createBinding and the binding preflight.\n\nSchema\n- Drop node_tags (orphaned by the citynode removal) and regenerate\n  migrations as a single clean snapshot (4 tables: tenants, nodes,\n  validators, domain_bindings). The self-referencing nodes.parent_id\n  FK uses AnyPgColumn for the typed reference.\n\nHost\n- BindingResolver''s TenantBinding interface gained tenantId so resolve\n  flows can tie a hostname back to a tenant record. Mock updated to\n  keep the integration test green.\n\nUI\n- Public landing directory reads listValidators instead of\n  listLegacyCityNodes.\n- Stake page: CityNodeCard -> ValidatorCard, query keys -> validators,\n  resolver hooks -> resolveValidatorByAccountId.\n- Admin tenants wizard rebuilt around nodes / validators / bindings,\n  and tenant header affordances reference tenant.id instead of the\n  now-defunct subdomain field.\n\n* chore(changeset): rename to nodes-validators-bindings and trim the optional opener\n\n* feat(geo): landing directory, country aggregator, and stake selector UI\n\n- Landing page queries listRootNodes, renders root-node directory cards\n  (name, kind badge, slug) with subdomain links + skeleton/empty states\n- New public country page at /n/$slug aggregates children via\n  listChildren and shows stake guidance from resolveStakingValidators\n  (own validator CTA, or stake-to-city links for children with validators)\n- Stake page rewritten around resolveStakingValidators: selectable\n  validator list with isDefault pre-selected, role/protocol badges,\n  community secondary styling, inherited-validator banner, no-validator\n  fallback with child links. Node resolved from ?node= param or hostname.\n  Stake transaction + onramp flows unchanged; broken admin CRUD removed.\n\n* feat(geo): tenant + node + binding creation wizard\n\n- Rewrite admin tenant creation page from placeholder into full wizard:\n  inline org creation (if no active org), node details (kind, cascading\n  parent dropdown via listRootNodes + listChildren, slug, name), tenant +\n  binding form with auto-generated hostname and live bindingPreflight\n- On submit: createTenant → createNode → createBinding (blocking, with\n  rollback via deleteNode + deleteTenant on failure), then non-blocking\n  deploy steps for NEAR subaccount and registry config publish\n- Export StepList + useStepper from @/components barrel\n- Extend api/tests/setup.ts: optional plugins map param on getPluginClient,\n  role param on orgContext (enables requireOrgRole in integration tests)\n- Add api/tests/integration/wizard.test.ts: 5 tests covering full chain,\n  rollback on duplicate hostname, nested hierarchy, preflight availability\n\n* feat(ui): reset & simplification — strip platform cruft, surface CityNodes product\n\n- Landing: ''What are CityNodes?'' hero + root-node directory + Apply button\n- New /apply route (external redirect to citynode.app/apply)\n- Remove apps browser cruft (4 routes deleted, apps tab stripped from profile)\n- Things index → typed DataTable demo\n- Mobile responsive fixes (auth-shell double-padding, simple-header overflow)\n- README + skill.md rewritten for CityNodes product surface\n\n* chore: finalize citynode.app repo identity and platform docs\n\nUpdate bos.config.json repository to point to NEARBuilders/citynode.app.\nAlign docs (AGENTS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, LLM.txt, host/README.md) with the\nremote auth plugin architecture and PostgreSQL migration. Clean up CI\npostgres-template service and .env.example for new plugin databases.\nRemove docker-compose.yml in favor of the Railway-backed deploy flow.\n\n* chore: reorganize plans/ — consolidate prototypes, group by domain, fix contradictions\n\n- Move 5 beta-v2 docs into plans/beta-v2/ (overview, composable, ui, tenants, native)\n- Move extension plans into plans/extensions/ (ui-extends-ui-federation, client-runtime-plugins)\n- Move infra plans into plans/infra/ (toml-infra-alchemy, orpc-v2-effect-migration)\n- Move offline plans into plans/offline/ (shell-sw-caching, data-sync-queue)\n- Move v1 plan into plans/v1-current/ (tenant-feature-completeness)\n- Fetch full prototype source (85 files) from prototype/route-merging branch\n- Consolidate prototypes under plans/prototypes/beta-v2/ and beta-v2-override/\n- Fold react-native-migration.md into beta-v2/native.md, delete original\n- Fix TOML/JSON publishing contradiction in composable.md\n- Mark wayfinder tickets 01, 02 as RESOLVED; 06 as PARTIALLY RESOLVED\n- Rewrite plans/README.md with new directory structure and ticket status table\n- Update ~45 cross-references across all plan docs\n- Add .gitignore exceptions for prototype source files (*.css, *.gen.ts)\n\n* docs(contributing): add community onboarding and Telegram group\n\n* fix(dev): fix fresh-clone dev flow — commit docker-compose, boot CLI from source, drop postinstall\n\n- Commit docker-compose.yml (was gitignored and generated after preflight,\n  creating a chicken-and-egg where bun run dev exited before the file was\n  written). Provisions postgres-api (5432/api_db) and postgres-auth\n  (5433/auth_db); plugins isolate via plugin_<pluginId> schemas.\n- Add paths to packages/everything-dev/tsconfig.json mapping every-plugin\n  and subpath exports to source so bun''s runtime resolver finds them\n  without pre-built dist.\n- Remove postinstall: bun run types:gen (dead code under ignore-scripts).\n- Update AGENTS.md Quick Reference with docker compose step and plugin\n  schema isolation docs.\n\n* feat(ci): convert to downstream app-only deploy with testnet staging\n\n- Add optional  to BosStagingSchema, use staging.account in\n  publishToFastKv when --env staging (enables testnet account switching)\n- Add staging block to bos.config.json: v1.citynode.testnet on\n  testnet.citynode.app\n- Deploy workflow: trigger from ci-main-success (not release-completed),\n  exclude host via --packages, remove Postgres services and infra plan\n- Staging workflow: use NEAR_TESTNET_PRIVATE_KEY, exclude host\n- Release workflow: manual-only (remove ci-main-success trigger, remove\n  docker and notify-deploy jobs)\n- Docker workflow: remove push triggers on main/staging\n- Update workflow README to document downstream flow\n\n* docs: add Railway deploy button and conceptual env var descriptions\n\n- Root README: Deploy section with Railway button and BOS_ACCOUNT,\n  BOS_GATEWAY, BETTER_AUTH_SECRET table\n- host/README: add BOS_ACCOUNT/BOS_GATEWAY to env var table with\n  conceptual descriptions, refine tenant-mode example\n- init.ts: generated AGENTS.md now includes Railway deploy hint with\n  env var table\n\n* readme\n\n* docs: add self-deployed development workflow to AGENTS.md and child scaffold (#21)\n\n* fix(dev): stop showing UI-SSR running when SSR is off (#22)\n\nGate ui-ssr service descriptor on runtimeConfig.ui.ssrUrl so the\nplanner path matches service-descriptor.ts. Without this, the\norchestrator marked the missing descriptor as a ready Remote\nservice, printing ''UI-SSR running'' despite no dev:ssr process.\n\n* Clean up  (#23)\n\n* wip\n\n* wip\n\n* feat(ui): unify shells, public header, and page widths\n\n- Landing: left-aligned \"What are City Nodes\" + NodeDirectory table (shared\n  pathless n/-node-directory.tsx), healthy top spacing; /n/$slug adopts the\n  same directory + stake rows\n- Chrome: PublicShell for _public/_anon (showConnect hides connect on login),\n  AppShell (AppSidebar/AppHeader/MobileTabBar/NAV_ITEMS) for _authenticated/_admin,\n  BetaBanner extracted into _layout; auth-shell.tsx and stale root-level\n  user-nav/near-branding/theme-toggle/org-switcher deleted\n- Login: no brand element or anonymous option; single \"connect with NEAR\" CTA\n- Widths: public children default, app children wide; dashboard.tsx becomes a\n  layout route (content moved to dashboard/index.tsx, URLs unchanged); nested\n  container removed from admin/tenants/new\n- Buttons: hand-rolled inline-class links replaced with Button variants across\n  dashboard, admin, orgs, tenant, things, apply; hardcoded rgb border swapped\n  for semantic token\n- Changesets: directory-design-alignment, shell-consolidation\n\n* Fix/merge UI normalization (#24)\n\n* wip\n\n* wip\n\n* fix(deploy): retry Zephyr exit-code-1 crashes and fix xpack SSR misdetection (#25)\n\n- Move Zephyr error detection (ZE regex) before the exitCode !== 0 guard\n  in runBuildAttempt so Zephyr-caused build crashes (exit code 1) are\n  classified as retriable instead of failing immediately\n- Replace single retry with up to 3 retries using exponential backoff\n  (2s, 5s, 10s) for Zephyr edge provider errors\n- Add snapshotType: ''csr'' to UI server and host withZephyr calls to\n  prevent xpack coordinator from inferring ''ssr'' (triggered by\n  target: ''async-node'') and failing to find a server entrypoint or\n  hiding remoteEntry.js behind a 404\n\n* Update  (#26)\n\n* fix(deploy): retry Zephyr exit-code-1 crashes and fix xpack SSR misdetection\n\n- Move Zephyr error detection (ZE regex) before the exitCode !== 0 guard\n  in runBuildAttempt so Zephyr-caused build crashes (exit code 1) are\n  classified as retriable instead of failing immediately\n- Replace single retry with up to 3 retries using exponential backoff\n  (2s, 5s, 10s) for Zephyr edge provider errors\n- Add snapshotType: ''csr'' to UI server and host withZephyr calls to\n  prevent xpack coordinator from inferring ''ssr'' (triggered by\n  target: ''async-node'') and failing to find a server entrypoint or\n  hiding remoteEntry.js behind a 404\n\n* feat(ui): strip public header to user-nav only, default light theme, move Apply button to directory heading\n\n- Remove logo, border, and background from public shell header, keeping only UserNav\n- Change default theme from ''system'' to ''light'' in ThemeProvider and no-flash init script\n- Move Apply button from bottom section to top-right of Directory section heading\n\n* Clean up ui/public placeholder icons and stale docs\n\n- Renamed near.svg → icon.svg and logo.png → icon-512.png (placeholder\n  dot icons, named for replacement); updated site.webmanifest icon srcs\n- Removed dead public files: README.md (about route fetches from GitHub\n  raw), near_rev.svg (unreferenced), bos.png (orphan)\n- Rewrote llms.txt to follow standard llms.txt format\n- Removed /README.md from skill.md public entry points\n- Updated host integration test /near.svg → /icon.svg\n\n* organize\n\n* feat: audit and fix agent information flow for first-load discovery\n\n- Rewrite skill.md with two agent modes (MCP/REST + clone & modify)\n- Expand llms.txt with API, MCP, auth, and source sections\n- Add /.well-known/mcp.json host route for MCP discovery\n- Delete stale LLM.txt (superseded by AGENTS.md)\n- Create docs/agents/ files (issue-tracker, triage-labels, domain)\n- Add agent communication surface and .agents/skills/ sections to AGENTS.md\n- Add /settings/api-keys route with create/list/delete UI\n- Expose auth and plugin router routes as MCP tools\n- Update init.ts child AGENTS.md with MCP/API-key sections\n- Add child llms.txt and skill.md template generation in init.ts\n- Add MCP, agent surface, and settings API keys regression tests\n\n* fix(mcp): remove pluginRouters and authHealth, rely on base API''s composed spec\n\nThe base API router already composes all plugin routes (auth, registry,\nproposals, votes) via pluginsClient, so its OpenAPI spec already includes\nevery operation. Passing pluginRouters separately caused every auth tool\nto register as a duplicate.\n\n- Removed pluginRouters parameter from mountMcpRoute\n- Removed authHealth from base API contract and router (was a passthrough\n  to the auth plugin''s own health endpoint, now redundant)\n- Kept duplicate-skip safety net for future collisions\n- Simplified mcp.ts back to single-router registration\n\n* fix(ui): rebuild dashboard shell on shadcn Sidebar, fix double-header bug\n\nReplaces hand-rolled AppShell/AppSidebar/AppHeader/MobileTabBar with\nshadcn''s Sidebar/SidebarProvider/SidebarInset composition. Fixes a\ndouble-header render bug on dashboard routes from an interim\n\"global header\" experiment (sidebar wasn''t spanning full height,\nbreadcrumb bar visually disconnected from the identity nav above it).\n\n- Sidebar defaults expanded with icon+label, collapsible via trigger/cmd+b\n- Mobile nav is now the sidebar''s built-in off-canvas sheet, replacing\n  the persistent bottom tab bar\n- Split OrgSwitcher/UserNav into shell-appropriate variants sharing\n  session/org/profile/sign-out logic via a new useIdentity hook\n- UserNav moved back into PublicShell''s own header for non-sidebar\n  routes (/, /things/*, /login, /things/new)\n- Added Breadcrumb primitive to AppHeader, replacing plain text\n- Rebuilt NetworkToggle on ToggleGroup, moved to components/layout/\n- Added toggle.tsx, toggle-group.tsx, breadcrumb.tsx, sidebar.tsx\n  shadcn primitives (Radix flavor, adapted to project conventions)\n\nNo URL changes; the auth-guard vs dashboard-layout route separation\nis unaffected.\n\n* fix(db): eliminate pg-pool search_path race that crashed the host\n\n- Set search_path via pool connection options instead of an unawaited\n  async on(\"connect\") listener, so it''s applied atomically before any\n  query can run on a fresh connection.\n- Move one-time CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS to driver init instead of\n  re-running it racily on every reconnect.\n- Add uncaughtException/unhandledRejection handlers in\n  host/src/program.ts so a dropped DB connection logs an error instead\n  of killing the host process and cascading SIGTERM to every service.\n\nImplements the fix described in .changeset/db-search-path-race-fix.md\n(previously committed as docs-only, without the code changes).\n\n* fix(ui): update sidebar to Tailwind v4 arbitrary-property syntax\n\nsidebar.tsx, sidebar-org-switcher.tsx, and sidebar-user-nav.tsx used\nTailwind v3''s bracket syntax for CSS variable references\n(e.g. w-[--sidebar-width]), which Tailwind v4 no longer recognizes as\na variable reference — it fell back to no explicit width. Switch to\nv4''s arbitrary-property shorthand (w-(--sidebar-width)), including the\ncalc() variants that referenced the removed theme(spacing.4) helper,\nnow --spacing(4).\n\nAlso drops a stray trailing blank line in cli/init.ts and applies\nformatting cleanup to api-keys.tsx (no behavior change).\n\n* feat: add --env staging to bos key generate, extract shared UI menu components\n\nCLI:\n- Add --env staging flag to bos key generate; resolves staging account\n  from bos.config.json staging.account (falls back to top-level account)\n- Suggest NEAR_TESTNET_PRIVATE_KEY for staging, NEAR_PRIVATE_KEY for production\n- Remove unused account param from buildChildSkillMd in init scaffold\n- Remove unused packages:write permission from staging.yml workflow\n\nUI:\n- Extract OrgSwitcherMenuContent and UserNavMenuContent into shared components\n- Add useSwitchOrganization hook (replaces inline handleOrgSwitch in 3 places)\n- Add PublicHeader component; pass runtimeConfig to PublicShell\n- Remove handleOrgSwitch from useIdentity (query invalidation now in hook)\n- Remove mobile home link from AppHeader\n\nConfig:\n- Update deployment URLs and integrity hashes\n- Switch top-level account to v1.citynode.testnet (pre-mainnet)\n\n* hardcode testnet\n\n* fix: testnet FastKV registry namespace defaulted to mainnet account\n\nTestnet namespace was hardcoded to dev.everything.near (a mainnet account)\ninstead of dev.allthethings.testnet. Remove REGISTRY_FASTKV_* env var\noverrides, add --registry flag to publish/deploy/key generate for CLI override.\n\n* fix: add --registry to bos start, remove dead postinstall from Dockerfile\n\n- Thread --registry override through resolveRemoteConfigChain and\n  fetchPublishedConfig so bos start fetches from the correct FastKV\n  registry contract.\n- Remove RUN bun run postinstall from Dockerfile — the script was\n  removed from package.json in a prior commit but the Dockerfile was\n  never updated, causing Docker builds to fail.\n\n* deploy\n\n* fix railway\n\n* dockerfile\n\n* fix: respect process.env.PORT in production runtime config\n\nbuildRuntimeConfig hardcoded host.url and host.port to localhost:3000\nin production, ignoring PORT. The HTTP server listened on the correct\nport (from process.env.PORT) but config.host.url pointed at 3000,\ncausing the binding resolver to fetch /api/tenants/bindings from the\nwrong port and get 503.\n\n* add node aggregation api routes (#27)\n\n* feat: add node-scoped admin dashboard (#28)\n\n* feat: add node-scoped admin dashboard\n\n* fix: pass testnet parent key to auth\n\n* Revert \"fix: pass testnet parent key to auth\"\n\nThis reverts commit 14b645d6ec8fbf19c4715a4bb5ac3881e5816643.\n\n* fix: make tenant deployment network-aware\n\n* fix: align node proposal review permissions\n\n* Revert \"fix: make tenant deployment network-aware\"\n\nThis reverts commit 788d9fe9f83a69a3b3e6ceffcd0b50ecaf24aa96.\n\n* fix: make tenant deployment network-aware\n\n* feat: add platform admin structure reporting (#31)\n\n* feat: add admin structure reporting\n\n* fix: generate fallback remote auth types\n\n* test: align infra fixtures with shared database\n\n* fix: report visible data table rows\n\n* feat: add admin node management (#32)\n\n* fix(ci): workflow_run deploys, drop commit-back, remove dead postinstall\n\n- Deploy/staging trigger via workflow_run + head_sha checkout; notify/repository_dispatch removed\n- Commit-back of bos.config.json removed — runtime reads FastKV via BOS_ACCOUNT/BOS_GATEWAY (#33, everything-dev#243)\n- postinstall steps removed from all workflows and child scaffolding (dead under ignore-scripts)\n- release.yml permission cleanup; docker.yml dead workflow_call dropped; @railway/cli pinned\n\n* feat(cli): nostr-signed publish transport for FastKV registry writes\n\n- bos publish signs a NIP-78 kind-30078 event (d = registry key, content = config JSON)\n  and POSTs it to the apps plugin nostrRelayKvWrite route (#34)\n- Effect-based transport with typed errors: NostrKeyMissing, PayloadTooLarge, RelayRejected\n- no-op skip when FastKV already holds the identical config\n- NEAR signing path removed from publish.ts; near-signer dropped; near-kit dep\n  replaced by nostr-tools (key management trio stays for bos relay key in T2b)\n\n* feat(config): register remote nostr plugin; apps plugin composes it via pluginsClient\n\n- plugins.nostr remote-only entry (production URL + integrity) with dependsOn auth\n- apps dependsOn nostr so Phase-1 loading injects a typed client factory\n- siwn relayer whitelistedContracts += contextual.near (mainnet; no testnet contract exists)\n- apps switched to createPlugin.withPlugins<PluginsClient>() (#36)\n\n* Revert \"feat(config): register remote nostr plugin; apps plugin composes it via pluginsClient\"\n\nThis reverts commit d0ee9ddadf24b8946db57aa0f913f39da7233663.\n\n* feat(cli): in-process near-kit signing for bos publish; drop nostr transport\n\nSpike finding: FastKV reads are indexed by tx signer (predecessor_id), so the\nconfig namespace is self-authenticating and a relayer-signed write would be\ninvisible at bos://<account>/<gateway>. Nostr cannot authorize a namespace it\ndoes not sign for — dropped from the publish path entirely (reverts the nostr\ntransport and the nostr plugin registration).\n\n- bos publish signs the registry transaction via near-kit in-process (no\n  near-cli-rs install in CI, no argv key passing, real tx hashes)\n- key chain: flag/env (NEAR_PRIVATE_KEY | BOS_NEAR_PRIVATE_KEY) →\n  ~/.near-credentials via FileKeyStore → actionable error\n- no-op skip when FastKV already holds the identical config\n- near-cli.ts slimmed to key management (bos key generate unchanged)\n- CI: NEAR CLI install/verify steps removed; NEAR secrets retained\n\n* feat(cli): bos registry use — compose published runtime sections into local config\n\n- bos registry use <account>/<gateway> --sections app.ui,app.host,plugins.<key>\n  fetches the published config from FastKV and merges selected sections into\n  local bos.config.json (preserves account/domain/extends/development URLs)\n- --dry-run preview; unknown sections fail with the available list\n- new registry skill: key layout, namespace=signer law, read/write patterns\n- publish-sync skill + AGENTS.md updated for in-process signing, no commit-back,\n  workflow_run deploys (#40, #41)\n\n* chore: drop unused colors import from near-cli\n\n* fix(review): drop stale nostr changeset, write namespace=signer ADR, review fixes\n\n- remove .changeset/nostr-publish-transport.md (described the dropped transport;\n  its deletion was never staged in d9bd3bd)\n- ADR 0001: FastKV namespaces are self-authenticating (predecessor_id indexing);\n  publishes sign with the publisher''s own NEAR key; nostr dropped from publish\n- near-signer: stop echoing key material fragments in format errors\n- publish: accurate key-origin log message\n- near-signer tests: class-based Near mock (biome useArrowFunction rewrote\n  constructable function expressions into arrows)\n- biome import organization (#41 findings)\n\n* docs: remove stale postinstall claims and near-cli-rs publish references\n\n- skills (plugin-client, dev-workflow): types regenerate on typecheck/bos dev/\n  build/pluginAdd — no postinstall hook exists\n- AGENTS.md: near-cli-rs quick reference now scoped to key management/account\n  flows; bos publish signs in-process via near-kit\n- local .scratch/nostr-registry-publish drafts removed (GitHub issues #33-41\n  carry the corrected record)\n\n* fix(publish): submit registry writes with waitUntil NONE\n\nThe FastKV registry is action-indexed, not execution-verified: dev.everything.near''s\n__fastdata_kv is a stub, so execution fails with CompilationError CodeDoesNotExist\neven though the indexer records the write (the legacy CLI tolerated exactly this).\nnear-kit''s default EXECUTED_OPTIMISTIC surfaced that benign failure as a hard error.\n\n- send({ waitUntil: \"NONE\" }): submit-and-return-hash; no execution-status parsing,\n  real tx hash on this path, no error-string matching\n- submission-level failures (invalid signature, exhausted allowance) still abort\n- waitForPublishedConfig remains the authoritative success check\n- ADR 0001 (now actually tracked — docs/adr was caught by the global *.md ignore)\n  gains an addendum: registry writes are action-indexed, not execution-verified\n\n* fix(publish): restore near-cli-rs keychain signing for local publishers\n\nnear-cli-rs stores keys in the OS keychain (accounts.json is metadata only) — the\ncredentials-file fallback never sees them, breaking local publishes after the\nnear-kit rewrite.\n\n- near-cli.ts: executeKeychainTransaction restored (TTY-gated, sign-with-keychain,\n  CodeDoesNotExist-tolerant per the action-indexed registry)\n- near-signer.ts: resolveSigningStrategy chain — env/flag key → credentials file →\n  near-cli-rs keychain (interactive only) → actionable error; submitRegistryWrite\n  picks the near-kit or keychain path and reports signedWith\n- CI is unaffected: env keys resolve to the near-kit path before the TTY fallback\n- docs/ADR/changeset updated with the keychain step\n\n* style: near-signer import order and unused import\n\n* style: drop unused colors import from near-signer\n\n* deploy\n\n* implement Proposals + votes demo & admin review UI (#42)\n\n* implement Proposals + votes demo & admin review UI\n\n* feat(tenants): DAO-owned tenants via Trezu-spawned near-kit wallet\n\nTenant creation on the admin dashboard now requires connecting a sputnik-dao\naccount via the Trezu wallet (separate from the existing SIWN session\nwallet). The connected DAO account owns the new tenant: tenants.accountId\nis the DAO, bos.config.json is published at bos://<dao>/<gateway> and\ninherits the platform base via the extends lineage.\n\nAdds a requireAdmin + server-side get_policy view call that confirms the\nsession user''s primary NEAR account appears in an explicit DAO policy\ngroup before accepting the create. tenants.owner_kind (default platform)\nflags DAO-owned rows so the tenant detail page routes republish/update\nthrough the DAO connector instead of the session-wallet/relayer path.\n\nThe platform subaccount flow (siwn.subAccount.*,\nNEAR_SUB_ACCOUNT_PARENT_KEY_*) is removed; the auth plugin endpoints stay\nintact but are no longer called from the wizard.\n\n* fix(ui): reactively track NEAR account for wallet-gated UI\n\nRead the SIWN near account via a new useNearAccount hook that subscribes\nto the auth client''s nearState atom instead of a one-shot getAccountId()\nread, which missed the async wallet/session restore after mount. Fixes\nBuy with Ping staying disabled after NEAR sign-in; adopted across stake,\nidentity, settings, dashboard, app detail, and admin pages.\n\n* fix(registry): publish tenant configs to the global FastKV namespace\n\nThe apps plugin''s registryNamespace override pointed the wizard''s config\npublishes at a project-local FastKV trie (v1.citynode.near) while the\nhost''s bos:// resolution and extends-chain loading always read the global\ndev.everything.near registry — so published tenant configs were\nunresolvable by the host. Remove the override so writer, host reader, and\nbos publish all converge on the global registry, and pin the contract\nwith a cross-package test.\n\nDiscovery moves to the project database: a new public GET /tenants/apps\nroute lists active tenants joined with their primary domain binding and\nattached node, and the landing-page directory is now powered by it —\nrows link via their stored binding hostname instead of deriving\nslug.gateway. The wizard''s publish re-check reuses the shared\nbuildRegistryConfigUrl helper. Adds the generic fastkv-registry skill\ncovering the (receiver, signer, key) read-URL invariant and the\npublish-vs-discovery plane split.\n\n* refactor(ui): share NodeDirectory via the components barrel\n\nPromote the public node directory into a reusable component and export it\nfrom the barrel; the landing page, public node pages, and the stake page\nnow consume it from @/components. The stake page additionally renders the\ntenant-app discovery listing (GET /tenants/apps) when no node is selected,\nand exports the Breadcrumb primitives for reuse.\n\n* feat(tenants): slug-addressable tenant URLs, node config, and audit seat\n\nTenant pages resolve /tenant/<slug> via the primary domain binding (node\nslug fallback), /tenant/<accountId> via the public account resolver, and\nkeep /tenant/<uuid> working; visibility is still gated by the authed\ntenant lookup, so access semantics are unchanged. Tenant detail gains a\nbreadcrumb showing the directory slug, and every tenant link the UI\ngenerates (admin tenants list, wizard post-creation) prefers the slug.\n\nThe place team now configures its node from the tenant page: rename the\nattached node and manage validators (add/remove/role/default) with the\npool owner read on-chain per validator via owner_id() — never stored.\nThe platform audit-seat invariant is enforced at tenant creation: the\nconfigured platform account must be an explicit group member of the\nplace-DAO policy. Validator mutation routes now require the node''s\norganization (platform admins bypass).\n\n* fix(ui): render beta banner only after client choice check\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com>\n\n* UI polish: header branding removal, node bindings NEAR DNS link, TanStack Form orgs page (#43)\n\n* implement Proposals + votes demo & admin review UI\n\n* feat(tenants): DAO-owned tenants via Trezu-spawned near-kit wallet\n\nTenant creation on the admin dashboard now requires connecting a sputnik-dao\naccount via the Trezu wallet (separate from the existing SIWN session\nwallet). The connected DAO account owns the new tenant: tenants.accountId\nis the DAO, bos.config.json is published at bos://<dao>/<gateway> and\ninherits the platform base via the extends lineage.\n\nAdds a requireAdmin + server-side get_policy view call that confirms the\nsession user''s primary NEAR account appears in an explicit DAO policy\ngroup before accepting the create. tenants.owner_kind (default platform)\nflags DAO-owned rows so the tenant detail page routes republish/update\nthrough the DAO connector instead of the session-wallet/relayer path.\n\nThe platform subaccount flow (siwn.subAccount.*,\nNEAR_SUB_ACCOUNT_PARENT_KEY_*) is removed; the auth plugin endpoints stay\nintact but are no longer called from the wizard.\n\n* fix(ui): reactively track NEAR account for wallet-gated UI\n\nRead the SIWN near account via a new useNearAccount hook that subscribes\nto the auth client''s nearState atom instead of a one-shot getAccountId()\nread, which missed the async wallet/session restore after mount. Fixes\nBuy with Ping staying disabled after NEAR sign-in; adopted across stake,\nidentity, settings, dashboard, app detail, and admin pages.\n\n* fix(registry): publish tenant configs to the global FastKV namespace\n\nThe apps plugin''s registryNamespace override pointed the wizard''s config\npublishes at a project-local FastKV trie (v1.citynode.near) while the\nhost''s bos:// resolution and extends-chain loading always read the global\ndev.everything.near registry — so published tenant configs were\nunresolvable by the host. Remove the override so writer, host reader, and\nbos publish all converge on the global registry, and pin the contract\nwith a cross-package test.\n\nDiscovery moves to the project database: a new public GET /tenants/apps\nroute lists active tenants joined with their primary domain binding and\nattached node, and the landing-page directory is now powered by it —\nrows link via their stored binding hostname instead of deriving\nslug.gateway. The wizard''s publish re-check reuses the shared\nbuildRegistryConfigUrl helper. Adds the generic fastkv-registry skill\ncovering the (receiver, signer, key) read-URL invariant and the\npublish-vs-discovery plane split.\n\n* refactor(ui): share NodeDirectory via the components barrel\n\nPromote the public node directory into a reusable component and export it\nfrom the barrel; the landing page, public node pages, and the stake page\nnow consume it from @/components. The stake page additionally renders the\ntenant-app discovery listing (GET /tenants/apps) when no node is selected,\nand exports the Breadcrumb primitives for reuse.\n\n* feat(tenants): slug-addressable tenant URLs, node config, and audit seat\n\nTenant pages resolve /tenant/<slug> via the primary domain binding (node\nslug fallback), /tenant/<accountId> via the public account resolver, and\nkeep /tenant/<uuid> working; visibility is still gated by the authed\ntenant lookup, so access semantics are unchanged. Tenant detail gains a\nbreadcrumb showing the directory slug, and every tenant link the UI\ngenerates (admin tenants list, wizard post-creation) prefers the slug.\n\nThe place team now configures its node from the tenant page: rename the\nattached node and manage validators (add/remove/role/default) with the\npool owner read on-chain per validator via owner_id() — never stored.\nThe platform audit-seat invariant is enforced at tenant creation: the\nconfigured platform account must be an explicit group member of the\nplace-DAO policy. Validator mutation routes now require the node''s\norganization (platform admins bypass).\n\n* fix(ui): render beta banner only after client choice check\n\n* feat(admin): link NEAR DNS discussion from node domain bindings\n\n* refactor(ui): drop public header branding, client-only user nav\n\n* feat(orgs): convert new organization form to TanStack Form\n\n* docs(skills): split plugin-development skill into references to pass 500-line limit\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeeshan Ahmad <itexpert120@outlook.com>\n\n* Branding node bindings org form (#44)\n\n* implement Proposals + votes demo & admin review UI\n\n* feat(tenants): DAO-owned tenants via Trezu-spawned near-kit wallet\n\nTenant creation on the admin dashboard now requires connecting a sputnik-dao\naccount via the Trezu wallet (separate from the existing SIWN session\nwallet). The connected DAO account owns the new tenant: tenants.accountId\nis the DAO, bos.config.json is published at bos://<dao>/<gateway> and\ninherits the platform base via the extends lineage.\n\nAdds a requireAdmin + server-side get_policy view call that confirms the\nsession user''s primary NEAR account appears in an explicit DAO policy\ngroup before accepting the create. tenants.owner_kind (default platform)\nflags DAO-owned rows so the tenant detail page routes republish/update\nthrough the DAO connector instead of the session-wallet/relayer path.\n\nThe platform subaccount flow (siwn.subAccount.*,\nNEAR_SUB_ACCOUNT_PARENT_KEY_*) is removed; the auth plugin endpoints stay\nintact but are no longer called from the wizard.\n\n* fix(ui): reactively track NEAR account for wallet-gated UI\n\nRead the SIWN near account via a new useNearAccount hook that subscribes\nto the auth client''s nearState atom instead of a one-shot getAccountId()\nread, which missed the async wallet/session restore after mount. Fixes\nBuy with Ping staying disabled after NEAR sign-in; adopted across stake,\nidentity, settings, dashboard, app detail, and admin pages.\n\n* fix(registry): publish tenant configs to the global FastKV namespace\n\nThe apps plugin''s registryNamespace override pointed the wizard''s config\npublishes at a project-local FastKV trie (v1.citynode.near) while the\nhost''s bos:// resolution and extends-chain loading always read the global\ndev.everything.near registry — so published tenant configs were\nunresolvable by the host. Remove the override so writer, host reader, and\nbos publish all converge on the global registry, and pin the contract\nwith a cross-package test.\n\nDiscovery moves to the project database: a new public GET /tenants/apps\nroute lists active tenants joined with their primary domain binding and\nattached node, and the landing-page directory is now powered by it —\nrows link via their stored binding hostname instead of deriving\nslug.gateway. The wizard''s publish re-check reuses the shared\nbuildRegistryConfigUrl helper. Adds the generic fastkv-registry skill\ncovering the (receiver, signer, key) read-URL invariant and the\npublish-vs-discovery plane split.\n\n* refactor(ui): share NodeDirectory via the components barrel\n\nPromote the public node directory into a reusable component and export it\nfrom the barrel; the landing page, public node pages, and the stake page\nnow consume it from @/components. The stake page additionally renders the\ntenant-app discovery listing (GET /tenants/apps) when no node is selected,\nand exports the Breadcrumb primitives for reuse.\n\n* feat(tenants): slug-addressable tenant URLs, node config, and audit seat\n\nTenant pages resolve /tenant/<slug> via the primary domain binding (node\nslug fallback), /tenant/<accountId> via the public account resolver, and\nkeep /tenant/<uuid> working; visibility is still gated by the authed\ntenant lookup, so access semantics are unchanged. Tenant detail gains a\nbreadcrumb showing the directory slug, and every tenant link the UI\ngenerates (admin tenants list, wizard post-creation) prefers the slug.\n\nThe place team now configures its node from the tenant page: rename the\nattached node and manage validators (add/remove/role/default) with the\npool owner read on-chain per validator via owner_id() — never stored.\nThe platform audit-seat invariant is enforced at tenant creation: the\nconfigured platform account must be an explicit group member of the\nplace-DAO policy. Validator mutation routes now require the node''s\norganization (platform admins bypass).\n\n* fix(ui): render beta banner only after client choice check\n\n* feat(admin): link NEAR DNS discussion from node domain bindings\n\n* refactor(ui): drop public header branding, client-only user nav\n\n* feat(orgs): convert new organization form to TanStack Form\n\n* docs(skills): split plugin-development skill into references to pass 500-line limit\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeeshan Ahmad <itexpert120@outlook.com>\n\n* fix(plugins): race-safe journal migrations, resilient API init, clearer host failure logs\n\n- Retry journal-init CREATE SCHEMA/TABLE with duplicate-tolerant handling in api, proposals, votes, and the _template scaffold (shared isRetryableMigrationError in everything-dev/db) — concurrent boot migrations raced on the shared drizzle journal schema\n- API plugin initialize tolerates failed dependency plugins; template-backed routes return clean errors instead of crashing the API (fixes /api 503s breaking tenant bindings/SSR)\n- /health returns a JSON ready/degraded summary (still 200) instead of hardcoded OK\n- Startup banner + 503 stub detail when the API plugin fails; BindingResolver reports API-unavailable clearly, negative-caches failures 10s, serves stale bindings\n- Never-empty plugin bootstrap error messages; masked DB-URL hints for any plugin with a *_DATABASE_URL secret\n- Track proposals/votes plugin sources in this repo\n\n* fix(cli): staleness-aware dist rebuilds, accurate plugin status, pg deprecation filter\n\n- bos dev rebuilds everything-dev/every-plugin dists when sources are newer than dist, instead of skipping whenever dist exists — rspack dev servers bundle workspace packages from dist, so a stale dist shipped old exports to dev bundles\n- Plugin error patterns tightened to real compile-failure signals (ERROR in / failed to compile / Module not found / Cannot find module); the broad /error/i pattern false-matched identifiers in warning text and marked healthy servers failed\n- A later ready signal clears an earlier Process failed status (rspack watch-mode recovery)\n- suppressPgQueryQueueDeprecation() in host+api boot: drops pg''s once-per-process query-queue deprecation from pg-pool''s internal dispatch (node-postgres#3612) and re-prints all other warnings; removes Node''s default warning handler since it prints even with listeners attached\n- bun.lock registers the moved proposals/votes plugin workspaces\n\n* chore(deps): bump TanStack Router/Query/Table to latest, ship TanStack Intent skills, migrate DataTable to react-table v9\n\n* resolve slug/tenant name sync issue (#52)\n\n* resolve slug/tenant name sync issue\n\n* fix ci\n\n* 46 tenant wizard (#54)\n\n* resolve slug/tenant name sync issue\n\n* fix ci\n\n* resolve drive data via router loaders\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com>\n\n* feat(auth): vendor better-near-auth, adopt local auth plugin, wire catalog and release workflows (#53)\n\n* feat(auth): vendor better-near-auth, adopt local auth plugin, wire catalog and release workflows\n\n- Vendor better-near-auth into packages/better-near-auth (workspace member):\n  development export conditions -> src, pnpm artifacts stripped, npm metadata\n  pointed at NEARBuilders/citynode.app for provenance, ML-DSA-65 post-quantum\n  NEP-413 verification, near-kit ^0.19.0, react/store entrypoints\n- plugins/auth adopted as a local plugin (app.auth -> local:plugins/auth) with\n  all dependencies on the root catalog; fix plugin.dev.ts to use staging.account\n- Root workspaces use packages/*; catalog: better-near-auth ^1.10.2,\n  near-kit ^0.19.0; sync-catalog-versions includes better-near-auth so\n  changesets bumps propagate\n- everything-dev: staleness-aware buildBetterNearAuthQuietly wired into\n  bos build/dev so production rspack plugin builds resolve its dist\n- Workflows: ci/deploy/staging build better-near-auth, CI runs its vitest,\n  detect-changes includes it; release loop publishes it from packages/*\n- Changesets: minor for better-near-auth, patch for everything-dev and\n  @everything-dev/auth-plugin; drop stale ephemeral-marker changeset (the\n  vendored strict relayer schema has no ephemeral flag)\n\n* refactor(better-near-auth): resolve biome warnings and infos\n\n- useLiteralKeys: headers.Authorization instead of computed string keys\n- useOptionalChain: collapse relayerCfg guard to !relayerCfg?.accountId\n- relay-status catch: log the RPC failure before the pending fallback\n- profile catch: drop unused binding (silent null is the intended contract)\n- tests: delete dead makeNonceBytes (superseded by makeUniqueNonce) and\n  unused SessionAtom alias, drop unused destructures, assert error ?? data\n  in the relay transaction test instead of a vacuous if (error) check\n\nbun run lint is now clean (0 diagnostics) across the repo.\n\n* align\n\n* fix(db): derive database identity from workspace, materialize child env for drizzle-kit\n\ndrizzle-kit evaluates drizzle.config.ts via its bundled tsx CJS transform which\ndefines import.meta.url but not import.meta.dirname, so configs fell back to\nnpm_package_name ?? ''unknown'', looked up UNKNOWN_DATABASE_URL, and silently\nconnected with a pglite pseudo-URL — surfacing as ''SASL: client password must\nbe a string'' in db studio for local plugins.\n\nIntroduce pure identity primitives (workspaceIdentityFromModuleUrl /\nworkspaceIdentityFromWorkspaceDir), resolveDatabaseUrl with loud failure for\nconnection-requiring drizzle-kit commands, and DatabaseBindings/DrizzleKit\nEffect services that materialize the canonical secret into every spawned\ndrizzle-kit child (also fixes db repair). All workspace drizzle configs now\nshare one identity-based shape.\n\n* passing regression tests\n\n* fix(cli): tear down detached dev process trees; harden regression harness against stale stacks\n\nRoot cause: the service kill sent SIGTERM only to the direct child, so when\nthe wrapper exited quickly the group-SIGKILL fallback never ran and the\ndetached grandchildren (rspack/tsx) were never signaled. An ungraceful CLI\ndeath (SIGKILL/crash/abort) leaked the whole tree — one stack from Aug 20\nsurvived 14 days. Aborted runs then poisoned the next browser suite run via\nPlaywright''s reuseExistingServer, producing \"SSR unavailable\" and\nERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED failures.\n\n- orchestrator kill: group SIGTERM -> 3s grace -> group SIGKILL\n- dev-session: emergency group-kill on force-exit; child pids persisted\n- bos kill: group-signals each child process tree\n- browser harness: kill stale port squatters before boot (Go-harness\n  parity), never reuse an existing server\n- add dev-teardown-check.mjs: boot stack, SIGTERM/SIGKILL it, assert no\n  leaked listeners (red before the fix, green after)\n- biome format and import fixes across tests/regression\n\n* feat(infra): isolate test databases and ports from dev\n\nGenerated infra now provisions postgres-api-test (5434, api_test_db) and\npostgres-auth-test (5435, auth_test_db) alongside a committed .env.test.\nRegression runs boot through start-stack.mjs with test env and fail-fast\nguards that refuse dev database URLs or the dev auth secret. Api vitest\npins to in-memory pglite (TEST_DATABASE=postgres opts into .env.test)\nand binds OS-assigned ephemeral ports. The planner skips persisting port\nstate under NODE_ENV=test / BOS_TEST=1 so test runs can never repin dev\nports. CI regression job and AGENTS.md updated to match.\n\n* fix(cli): generate plugins-client types for local auth plugins in types gen\n\n* fix(ui): adopt (builder, receiverId) callback shape for buildSignedDelegateAction and make init regression test permissive\n\nAlign citynode UI with the better-near-auth 1.10.x callback signature in\nui/src/components/ui/app-detail-content.tsx (publish + signDelegate mutations)\nand ui/src/routes/_layout/_authenticated/_dashboard/tenant/$tenantId.tsx\n(tenant config relayer): pass the receiverId through to functionCall instead\nof hard-coding prepared.data.contractId. Matches the near-connect-transactions\nskill convention and resolves the TS2345 failures triggered by better-near-auth''s\nnested near-kit@0.10.0 expressing a different TransactionBuilder shape than\nthe testDir-hoisted near-kit@0.19.0.\n\nMake packages/everything-dev/tests/integration/init.full.test.ts permissive\nabout custom UI/API implementations: scope plugins to [''template''] only,\nwrite a permissive api-types.gen.ts stub after types:gen runs, and typecheck\napi + plugins/_template only. The UI typecheck moved out of the regression\nbecause ContractRouterClient<T> reproduces its conditional shape for any\nstubbed T, and pinning the regression against citynode-specific\nplugin-namespace calls would couple it to a particular plugin configuration.\n\nRestore checkCdnProviderDeployable in packages/everything-dev/src/build.ts\nso the framework tarball build (a prerequisite of the test) no longer fails\non the pre-existing broken publish.ts -> build re-export.\n\n* 47 apply page (#55)\n\n* resolve slug/tenant name sync issue\n\n* fix ci\n\n* resolve drive data via router loaders\n\n* local apply page\n\n* fix issues\n\n* 48 node empty state (#56)\n\n* fix(ui): route node empty states by reason and role (#48)\n\n* fix ci\n\n* feat: improve admin lists and Things routes (#59)\n\n* fix issues (#60)\n\n* regression\n\n* test\n\n* fix infra, regression\n\n* regression tests\n\n* lint\n\n* ci auth\n\n* resiliance\n\n* ci\n\n* plugin key\n\n* regression test\n\n* auth remote name\n\n* fix(ui): react-doctor pass 1 — accessibility, hooks, module-scope, transitions\n\nClears 11 react-doctor findings (83 → 72; both ERROR rules to 0).\n\n- a11y: add <MotionConfig reducedMotion=\"user\"> in __root.tsx so framer-motion\n  honours the OS ''reduce motion'' setting (under-construction''s 3D wobble\n  stops for vestibular-disorder users). WCAG 2.3.3.\n- bugs: drop optional auth param from useRelayerInfoQuery and hoist\n  useAuthClient() above useQuery (rules-of-hooks — default-arg hooks\n  were a footgun).\n- maintainability: lift 5 dead-state handlers to module scope in\n  connect-dao.tsx, login.tsx, orgs/$slug.tsx, api-keys.tsx (the per-render\n  allocation forces memoised children to bail).\n- perf: replace 4 transition-all Tailwind classes with named properties\n  — header (transition-colors), theme-toggle icons (transition-transform),\n  admin relayer-banner (transition-colors).\n\n* implement stake overview (#73)\n\n* Prototype of node lifecycle (#74)\n\n* feat(ui): node lifecycle prototype, collapsible sidebar nav, tenant url helper, badge chips\n\n* feat(ui,api): org-pinned node lifecycle — org slug + linked DAO, conflict preflight, refresh + cleanup\n\n* fix(ui,auth): trezu-linked team wallet — connect buttons replace unset inputs, host-session requireAuth\n\n* feat(ui): tenant publish visibility — config-live gating, tenant record card, mark-applied, tenant identity header\n\n* fix(ui): drop public header branding — tenant identity via document title only\n\n* dao policy prototype\n\n* Improve codebase (#75)\n\n* fix(ui): stabilize shared bootstrap, fallbacks, and list identity (#67, #71, #72)\n\n* refactor(ui): split registry app detail without changing metadata writes (#69)\n\n* refactor(admin): separate navigation and statistics (#69)\n\n* refactor(admin): separate proposal list filters and table states (#69)\n\n* refactor(admin): separate proposal review views and controls (#69)\n\n* refactor(admin): separate relayer status, funding, and history (#69)\n\n* fix(admin): keep tenant table derivations stable (#67)\n\n* refactor(admin): split tenant creation phases while preserving rollback (#69)\n\n* fix(apply): refresh proposal reviews and split application views (#68, #70)\n\n* refactor(dashboard): separate workspace identity and tenant summary (#70)\n\n* refactor(orgs): separate organization management sections (#67, #70)\n\n* fix(stake): refresh the executed pool and split staking views (#67, #68, #70)\n\n* fix(tenants): refresh persisted changes even when publication fails (#68, #70)\n\n* fix(things): reconcile proposal and deletion caches and split detail views (#67, #68, #70)\n\n* refactor(settings): separate authentication methods and stabilize passkey queries (#67, #71)\n\n* fix(settings): preserve the current session when revoking other sessions (#68, #71)\n\n* fix(settings): refresh the authoritative session after profile updates (#68)\n\n* fix(things): guard late subscriptions and preserve event row identity (#67)\n\n* chore: record UI fixes and framework sync patch releases\n\n* chore: update gitignore\n\n* fix(test): centralize regression inputs and preserve CI failures\n\n* fix(release): tag the exact checked-out package commit\n\n* fix(host): reject malformed request origins without throwing\n\n* fix(api): enforce node hierarchy and atomic validator defaults\n\n* fix(host): recover failed tenant integrity refreshes\n\n* fix(votes): paginate feeds with stable timestamp cursors\n\n* fix(test): supply remote auth secrets and guard sandbox cleanup\n\n* fix(test): isolate stale-port cleanup from browser workers\n\n* fix(runtime): share initialization and guarantee plugin cleanup\n\n* fix(config): refresh discovery and deduplicate runtime dependencies\n\n* fix(auth): bind signed recipients and wallet state to networks\n\n* test(votes): assert cursor records without implicit any callbacks\n\n* fix(ui): preserve exact NEAR amounts and validate staking context\n\n* fix(ui): enforce tenant owner wallet before publishing\n\n* fix(ui): clear private query state and prevent session resurrection\n\n* fix(runtime): canonical JSON cache keys and per-test producers\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com>\n\n* fix(ui): resolve signed-in NEAR account through better-near-auth\n\n* fix(ui): bind Trezu DAO session to the SIWN identity\n\n* csp nonce\n\n* ci check changes less\n\n* add floor\n\n* thinner ci\n\n* ordering\n\n* Keep User Nav in the top-right of every shell. (#78)\n\n* Keep User Nav in the top-right of every shell.\n\nDashboard and admin already share App Shell, so moving the account menu into the header (and dropping the sidebar footer row) makes identity consistent with public pages.\n\nFixes #76\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* update git ignore\n\n* cleanup: remove md\n\n* chore: fix ci\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Node reward + unstake (#79)\n\n* Keep User Nav in the top-right of every shell.\n\nDashboard and admin already share App Shell, so moving the account menu into the header (and dropping the sidebar footer row) makes identity consistent with public pages.\n\nFixes #76\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* update git ignore\n\n* cleanup: remove md\n\n* chore: fix ci\n\n* feat(ui): show team stake as available rewards on My Node\n\nThe dashboard was missing the team DAO''s pool staked_balance, which is the\namount later unstaked to confidential treasury. Show that figure, not the\nwhole-pool total.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* add unstaking\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Feat/node maps (#98)\n\n* remove node stat cards\n\n* feat(discovery): publish profiles and explore geographic nodes (#93)\n\n* feat(discovery): publish events socials and activity evidence (#94)\n\n* feat(discovery): curate features and moderate reports (#95)\n\n* feat(discovery): measure engagement and prepare pilot validation (#96)\n\n* fix(discovery): address review and validate navigation fallbacks\n\n* feat(discovery): import Luma calendars alongside manual events\n\n* improve events\n\n* fix discovery explorer bug\n\n* address review: document discovery tables, fix dev CSP imgSrc\n\n- Add one-line comments to discovery_* tables in schema.ts explaining\n  what each one is for (profile, audit log, activities, curators,\n  featured nodes, reports, measurements, luma connections).\n- imgSrc previously only allowed https: in prod and http: in dev,\n  so the explicit tile.openstreetmap.org entry was needed to load\n  map tiles locally. Make https: unconditional (dev additionally\n  allows http:) so it actually covers the tile origin as expected,\n  and drop the now-redundant explicit entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* address review: squash discovery migrations, drop stray browser test harness\n\n- Collapse migrations 0002-0007 into a single 0002_living_odin.sql\n  since none were deployed yet.\n- Revert the discovery_* table comments from the previous commit;\n  the reviewer''s confusion was answered directly on the PR thread\n  instead.\n- Remove tests/discovery-browser and its integration test\n  (api/tests/integration/discovery-browser.test.ts) per review.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: run biome formatting on generated migration snapshot\n\ndrizzle-kit generate doesn''t match this repo''s biome formatting\nrules for JSON arrays, so bun biome ci . was failing on the\nsquashed migration''s snapshot.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(discovery): rename studio to /discover, stop map flashing\n\n- rename discovery studio page/component to /discover\n- keep explorer map mounted during search via keepPreviousData, avoid rebuild/flash on refetch\n- remove beta database banner and its export\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: rework node lifecycle POC to the real on-chain flow (#80)\n\n* feat: rework node lifecycle poc to the real on-chain flow\n\n* fix: hash tenant ui bundle entry urls when verifying integrity\n\n* feat!: Effect 4 + oRPC v2 — effect-native plugins, Layer initialize, router merging (#97)\n\n* feat: rework node lifecycle poc to the real on-chain flow\n\n* fix: hash tenant ui bundle entry urls when verifying integrity\n\n* wip\n\n* refactor(every-plugin): drop dead orpc-openapi and zod-core barrels\n\n* spike: bump effect 4.0.0-rc.112 + orpc 2.0.0-beta.35, regenerate bun.lock\n\n* spike(a1): record effect 4 + orpc v2 feasibility findings — GO\n\n* feat(every-plugin): migrate runtime to effect 4 + orpc v2\n\n- Context.Tag/Effect.Service class services -> Context.Service keys with\n  explicit Layer.effect definitions (static Default/Live preserved)\n- Effect.catchAll/catchAllCause -> catch/catchCause, Effect.async ->\n  callback, Cause.failureOption -> findErrorOption\n- Layer.scoped -> Layer.effect (build scope auto-provided)\n- oRPC v2: route extension preload in barrel, @orpc/publisher swap,\n  ContractedRouter types, OpenAPIReferenceHandlerPlugin + generator\n  converters/base, RPCLink origin/url split\n- zod 4.6.5 per @orpc/zod@2 peer; prune stale nested @orpc copies\n\n* feat(every-plugin): v2 error status map + integration fixes\n\n- PLUGIN_ERROR_STATUS_MAP preserves v1 wire statuses (TIMEOUT 504,\n  CONNECTION_ERROR 502) at the handler boundary; wired into dev-server\n  middleware handlers\n- rebuild dist against migrated source (fixture MF loading was bundling\n  stale pre-migration dist)\n- integration tests: assert code/data (v2 ORPCError drops .status),\n  RPCLink origin/url split, generator converters/base options\n\n* feat(every-plugin)!: layer-based initialize replaces tools/buildService (b2)\n\n- initialize: (config, plugins) => Effect<TDeps, Error, Scope>; plugins\n  compose Layers and build via Layer.buildWithScope(layer, yield* Effect.scope)\n- PluginServicesTools/buildService and per-plugin MemoMap machinery removed\n- service Default layers exported as consts (XServiceDefault) with full\n  inference; PluginServiceLive composes them\n- shared runEffect effect-oRPC bridge exported from every-plugin (replaces\n  per-plugin context-bridge modules)\n\n* feat(api,plugins)!: migrate api + all plugins to layer-based initialize (b3/b4)\n\n- initialize: (config, plugins) => Effect with Layer.buildWithScope +\n  Context.get replacing tools.buildService (api, _template, apps, auth,\n  votes, proposals)\n- Context.Tag -> Context.Service keys everywhere (api services, plugin\n  service tags, everything-dev db bindings/drizzle-kit)\n- Layer.scoped -> Layer.effect; Effect.catchAll -> Effect.catch;\n  Effect.either -> tagged-result catch in db/migrate.ts (api, auth,\n  votes, proposals)\n- MemoryPublisher resumeRetentionSeconds -> resume { enabled, seconds }\n- RPCLink url split into origin + url (api/_template test setups)\n- DecoratedMiddleware 6 -> 5 type args (api, votes, proposals lib/auth)\n- every-plugin initialize type widened to R = Scope | PluginIdTag\n  (DatabaseLive yields PluginIdTag, loader provides it at runtime)\n- everything-dev http-client: Duration.Input, Schedule.upTo\n  {duration,times} replacing intersect; drizzle-kit Effect.callback;\n  dist rebuilt\n\n* feat(everything-dev)!: migrate cli runtime to effect 4 (b5)\n\n- orchestrator: @effect/platform Command -> node child_process.spawn with\n  Effect.callback exit + web-stream stdout/stderr into Effect Streams\n- dev-session: drop @effect/platform-node NodeContext (no effect 4\n  release); Effect.catch/catchDefect renames\n- Context.Tag -> Context.Service (PortAllocator, InfraMaterializer,\n  ServiceDescriptorMap, DevRuntimeConfig)\n- Effect.async -> Effect.callback (app probePortBindable, preflight\n  checkTcpReachable); http-client Duration.Input + Schedule.upTo\n  {duration,times}\n- plugin.ts initialize: tools.buildService -> Layer.buildWithScope +\n  Context.get over merged db/drizzle-kit layers\n- upgrade codemod now emits Layer.buildWithScope + Context.get form\n  (with import fixer) instead of tools.buildService; tests updated\n- parse.ts: zod 4 def introspection + oRPC v2 inputSchemas[0] (was\n  ~orpc.inputSchema) — fixes boolean/negated flag parsing\n- dist rebuilt\n\n* feat(host)!: migrate host runtime to effect 4 + orpc v2 (b5)\n\n- Context.Tag -> Context.Service for ConfigService, PluginsService, SecurityMiddleware\n- Effect.either -> runPromiseExit + Cause.squash in ssr paths and tests\n- Config module reads replaced with process.env (readCorsOrigins, readDbSecret)\n- oRPC v2 OpenAPIGenerator/OpenAPIReferenceHandlerPlugin + errorStatusMap wiring\n- federation retry schedule addDelay returns Effect\n- every-plugin initialize R widened with PluginIdTag for DatabaseLive composition\n\nHost tsc 0 errors; 150/152 tests (2 runtime-remote failures are deploy-gated:\nthey load production v1 remotes incompatible with the v2 host).\n\n* fix(every-plugin)!: preserve prerelease in getMajorMinorVersion range\n\n4.0.0-rc.112 previously derived ^4.0.0, which excludes rc versions under\nsemver prerelease range rules. Plugin/host lockstep on effect 4 RCs\nrequires ^4.0.0-rc.112.\n\n* feat(ui)!: orpc v2 RPCLink origin/url split + repo lint autofix (b6)\n\n- ui/src/lib/api.ts: RPCLink url narrowed to `\\${string}` with origin split\n- biome --write across migrated workspaces (import sorting, unused imports,\n  formatting)\n\n* fix(every-plugin)!: PLUGIN_ERROR_STATUS_MAP spreads COMMON_ERROR_STATUS_MAP\n\noRPC v2 replaces the default status map entirely when errorStatusMap is\nprovided; the 2-entry override wiped standard codes (BAD_REQUEST etc all\nfell back to 500). Spread the default and keep the v1 TIMEOUT/CONNECTION\noverrides.\n\n* chore: add effect 4 + orpc v2 migration changeset\n\n* chore: code-review fixes — v2 type names, AGENTS.md layer guidance, audit notes\n\n- everything-dev emitters + sdk emit RouterContract/RouterContractClient\n  (v2 names; old names are deprecated aliases)\n- formatORPCError drops stale `.status` fallback (v2 resolves status via\n  errorStatusMap at the handler boundary)\n- AGENTS.md scoped-resources section rewritten for Layer-based initialize\n- middleware dedup audit outcome recorded in the b2 ticket\n\n* style: sort sdk exports\n\n* docs: advisor plans for post-migration improvement survey (16 plans)\n\nSurvey of the Effect 4 + oRPC v2 aftermath: plugin-dev simplification,\ntype-safety, deduplication, CLI DX. Plans in advisor-plans/ with\ndependency-ordered execution waves. Direction tickets published as\nGitHub issues #89-91.\n\n* refactor(host): adopt effect 4 Config module for env/secret reads + shared maskDbUrl (#91)\n\n- readCorsOrigins / readDbSecret / secretsFromEnv on Config.string/redacted\n  with withDefault/option preserving the soft-fail UX and the unset sentinel\n- secrets and DB URLs carried as Redacted; unredacted only at the usePlugin\n  args boundary and the deliberate maskDbUrl site in the bootstrap error path\n- one shared maskDbUrl() replaces both hand-rolled masking sites; regex\n  tightened to /:[^:@\\/]+@/ so user-without-password URLs are not mangled\n- tests: host/tests/unit/{mask-db-url,env-reads}.test.ts (fresh ConfigProvider\n  per read — the default env provider snapshots process.env)\n\n* docs: #89/#90 resolutions — db/auth absorption design + prototype, minimal-scaffold decision\n\n- plans/v1-current/every-plugin-db-auth-absorption.md: #89 spike design\n  (D1 slug semantics, D2 driver externals, D3 tooling home, D4 sync ownership;\n  PluginIdTag hides via PluginInitializeInput.pluginId — FiberRef is gone in\n  effect 4.0.0-rc.112)\n- plans/prototypes/db-auth-absorption/: throwaway prototype proving the\n  contract+service+index file list, R channel = Scope only, schema/journal\n  semantics, migration idempotence, auth middleware generics\n- advisor-plans 017-019: facade landing, workspace migration, sync cutover\n- advisor-plans 020: #90 decision — minimal scaffold by default, sparse fetch\n  for vendored workspaces, config snapshot for sync, --full opt-out\n\n* docs: effect-native-plugins plan — handler-idiom half of the orpc-v2 migration\n\n- plans/infra/effect-native-plugins.md: .effect() handlers, Layer-returning\n  initialize, nested router merging, every-plugin barrel removal (phases 0-5)\n- orpc-v2-effect-migration.md: status note pointing at the follow-up plan\n- Phase 1.2 includes the pluginId addition to PluginInitializeInput (from the\n  #89 amended design — db layers derive plugin_<slug> from it, PluginIdTag\n  stays only through a migration window)\n\n* docs: amend #89 — database layer lands in everything-dev/db, not every-plugin/db\n\nPost orpc-v2 / effect-native-plugins review:\n\n- home flips to everything-dev/db (effect-native Phase 5 removes the\n  every-plugin barrels; 4/5 workspaces already runtime-import it; alchemy\n  decisions 13/16 make the deploy package the long-term migration owner)\n- exports: pluginSchemaName, createDatabaseDriver (engine by URL scheme,\n  namespace-per-engine isolation), databaseLayer (shared factory,\n  plugin-owned typed tag), runMigrations (008''s runner)\n- no every-plugin/auth — plan 007 is the resting point\n- journal standardized on drizzle.__dr…\n\n* feat(v2): simplify to the upstream everything.dev shell\n\nStrip the citynode product surface so this repo is the simple upstream\napp that citynode.app extends:\n\n- Delete discovery, stake, node-directory, apply flow, POC stations,\n  admin nodes/proposals UI, and the proposals/votes plugin sources\n- Delete routes broken by that surface (dashboard/node, tenant detail,\n  onboarding station, orgs node-config, explore)\n- Re-point bos.config.json to the everything.dev identity\n  (dev.everything.near / everything.dev); drop proposals/votes plugin\n  entries and the LUMA secret\n- Things suite becomes pure _template CRUD (no votes/proposals)\n- Restore the original everything.dev landing: hero with rotating\n  subtitles, runtime label, construction gif, /launch stub route\n- Trim sidebar/next-steps to the surviving shell (dashboard, orgs,\n  things, admin: overview/sites/relayer/system)\n- better-near-auth: guarded next-tick defer so browser-context\n  typechecks pass without node globals\n\nPlan and tickets: .scratch/v2-shell/ (issues 01-03, 05 done; 04/06-08\nto follow). Deploy-ordering risk for citynode production is recorded\nin ticket 04.\n\n* refactor(v2): remove sputnik/dao surface and de-citynode branding\n\nCode-review fixes for the v2 shell:\n\n- Delete the admin tenant wizard (admin/tenants) and the sputnik-dao\n  helpers it propped up (connect-dao, dao-connect, dao-policy,\n  tenant-deploy); admin drops the Sites stat/row — self-serve node\n  creation goes through /launch, the Nodes manage list lands with the\n  API collapse ticket\n- team-workspace and workspace-synchronization stay (live consumers in\n  the shell''s org/team switchers)\n- De-citynode branding: page-title, logo fallback, breadcrumbs,\n  account profile meta, about description\n- Trim stale breadcrumbs cases and the tab crumb-context\n- Drop the orphaned plugins.ai env block (plugin is uncommitted WIP)\n- Small cleanups: near.org link opens safely, uniform JSX subtitles,\n  ReactElement type import, unwrapped Badge, tenantStatusTone removed\n- return-path test updated now the onboarding station is gone\n\nKnown pre-existing failure on this branch (unrelated, unchanged code):\npackages/everything-dev bos-app-loader \"both forms coexist\" test.\n\n* fix(v2): restore bos.config.json (unintended deletion in refactor commit)\n\n* chore(v2): drop minio storage services from compose\n\nMinIO removed its community images from Docker Hub (2025) — both\nminio/minio and minio/mc return 404 there, and quay.io refuses\nanonymous pulls, so every cold-cache `docker compose up` failed with\n\"pull access denied\". Nothing in dev actually used them: the storage\nservice falls back to in-memory when BOS_STORAGE_* is unset (the dev\ndefault), and tests never touch the containers.\n\nCompose now provisions exactly the four Postgres services; exercising\nthe real S3 path locally means pointing BOS_STORAGE_* at any\nS3-compatible endpoint (documented in .env.example).\n\n* Merge citynode/main into v2 — un-fork the platform (#295)\n\n* implement Proposals + votes demo & admin review UI (#42)\n\n* implement Proposals + votes demo & admin review UI\n\n* feat(tenants): DAO-owned tenants via Trezu-spawned near-kit wallet\n\nTenant creation on the admin dashboard now requires connecting a sputnik-dao\naccount via the Trezu wallet (separate from the existing SIWN session\nwallet). The connected DAO account owns the new tenant: tenants.accountId\nis the DAO, bos.config.json is published at bos://<dao>/<gateway> and\ninherits the platform base via the extends lineage.\n\nAdds a requireAdmin + server-side get_policy view call that confirms the\nsession user''s primary NEAR account appears in an explicit DAO policy\ngroup before accepting the create. tenants.owner_kind (default platform)\nflags DAO-owned rows so the tenant detail page routes republish/update\nthrough the DAO connector instead of the session-wallet/relayer path.\n\nThe platform subaccount flow (siwn.subAccount.*,\nNEAR_SUB_ACCOUNT_PARENT_KEY_*) is removed; the auth plugin endpoints stay\nintact but are no longer called from the wizard.\n\n* fix(ui): reactively track NEAR account for wallet-gated UI\n\nRead the SIWN near account via a new useNearAccount hook that subscribes\nto the auth client''s nearState atom instead of a one-shot getAccountId()\nread, which missed the async wallet/session restore after mount. Fixes\nBuy with Ping staying disabled after NEAR sign-in; adopted across stake,\nidentity, settings, dashboard, app detail, and admin pages.\n\n* fix(registry): publish tenant configs to the global FastKV namespace\n\nThe apps plugin''s registryNamespace override pointed the wizard''s config\npublishes at a project-local FastKV trie (v1.citynode.near) while the\nhost''s bos:// resolution and extends-chain loading always read the global\ndev.everything.near registry — so published tenant configs were\nunresolvable by the host. Remove the override so writer, host reader, and\nbos publish all converge on the global registry, and pin the contract\nwith a cross-package test.\n\nDiscovery moves to the project database: a new public GET /tenants/apps\nroute lists active tenants joined with their primary domain binding and\nattached node, and the landing-page directory is now powered by it —\nrows link via their stored binding hostname instead of deriving\nslug.gateway. The wizard''s publish re-check reuses the shared\nbuildRegistryConfigUrl helper. Adds the generic fastkv-registry skill\ncovering the (receiver, signer, key) read-URL invariant and the\npublish-vs-discovery plane split.\n\n* refactor(ui): share NodeDirectory via the components barrel\n\nPromote the public node directory into a reusable component and export it\nfrom the barrel; the landing page, public node pages, and the stake page\nnow consume it from @/components. The stake page additionally renders the\ntenant-app discovery listing (GET /tenants/apps) when no node is selected,\nand exports the Breadcrumb primitives for reuse.\n\n* feat(tenants): slug-addressable tenant URLs, node config, and audit seat\n\nTenant pages resolve /tenant/<slug> via the primary domain binding (node\nslug fallback), /tenant/<accountId> via the public account resolver, and\nkeep /tenant/<uuid> working; visibility is still gated by the authed\ntenant lookup, so access semantics are unchanged. Tenant detail gains a\nbreadcrumb showing the directory slug, and every tenant link the UI\ngenerates (admin tenants list, wizard post-creation) prefers the slug.\n\nThe place team now configures its node from the tenant page: rename the\nattached node and manage validators (add/remove/role/default) with the\npool owner read on-chain per validator via owner_id() — never stored.\nThe platform audit-seat invariant is enforced at tenant creation: the\nconfigured platform account must be an explicit group member of the\nplace-DAO policy. Validator mutation routes now require the node''s\norganization (platform admins bypass).\n\n* fix(ui): render beta banner only after client choice check\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com>\n\n* UI polish: header branding removal, node bindings NEAR DNS link, TanStack Form orgs page (#43)\n\n* implement Proposals + votes demo & admin review UI\n\n* feat(tenants): DAO-owned tenants via Trezu-spawned near-kit wallet\n\nTenant creation on the admin dashboard now requires connecting a sputnik-dao\naccount via the Trezu wallet (separate from the existing SIWN session\nwallet). The connected DAO account owns the new tenant: tenants.accountId\nis the DAO, bos.config.json is published at bos://<dao>/<gateway> and\ninherits the platform base via the extends lineage.\n\nAdds a requireAdmin + server-side get_policy view call that confirms the\nsession user''s primary NEAR account appears in an explicit DAO policy\ngroup before accepting the create. tenants.owner_kind (default platform)\nflags DAO-owned rows so the tenant detail page routes republish/update\nthrough the DAO connector instead of the session-wallet/relayer path.\n\nThe platform subaccount flow (siwn.subAccount.*,\nNEAR_SUB_ACCOUNT_PARENT_KEY_*) is removed; the auth plugin endpoints stay\nintact but are no longer called from the wizard.\n\n* fix(ui): reactively track NEAR account for wallet-gated UI\n\nRead the SIWN near account via a new useNearAccount hook that subscribes\nto the auth client''s nearState atom instead of a one-shot getAccountId()\nread, which missed the async wallet/session restore after mount. Fixes\nBuy with Ping staying disabled after NEAR sign-in; adopted across stake,\nidentity, settings, dashboard, app detail, and admin pages.\n\n* fix(registry): publish tenant configs to the global FastKV namespace\n\nThe apps plugin''s registryNamespace override pointed the wizard''s config\npublishes at a project-local FastKV trie (v1.citynode.near) while the\nhost''s bos:// resolution and extends-chain loading always read the global\ndev.everything.near registry — so published tenant configs were\nunresolvable by the host. Remove the override so writer, host reader, and\nbos publish all converge on the global registry, and pin the contract\nwith a cross-package test.\n\nDiscovery moves to the project database: a new public GET /tenants/apps\nroute lists active tenants joined with their primary domain binding and\nattached node, and the landing-page directory is now powered by it —\nrows link via their stored binding hostname instead of deriving\nslug.gateway. The wizard''s publish re-check reuses the shared\nbuildRegistryConfigUrl helper. Adds the generic fastkv-registry skill\ncovering the (receiver, signer, key) read-URL invariant and the\npublish-vs-discovery plane split.\n\n* refactor(ui): share NodeDirectory via the components barrel\n\nPromote the public node directory into a reusable component and export it\nfrom the barrel; the landing page, public node pages, and the stake page\nnow consume it from @/components. The stake page additionally renders the\ntenant-app discovery listing (GET /tenants/apps) when no node is selected,\nand exports the Breadcrumb primitives for reuse.\n\n* feat(tenants): slug-addressable tenant URLs, node config, and audit seat\n\nTenant pages resolve /tenant/<slug> via the primary domain binding (node\nslug fallback), /tenant/<accountId> via the public account resolver, and\nkeep /tenant/<uuid> working; visibility is still gated by the authed\ntenant lookup, so access semantics are unchanged. Tenant detail gains a\nbreadcrumb showing the directory slug, and every tenant link the UI\ngenerates (admin tenants list, wizard post-creation) prefers the slug.\n\nThe place team now configures its node from the tenant page: rename the\nattached node and manage validators (add/remove/role/default) with the\npool owner read on-chain per validator via owner_id() — never stored.\nThe platform audit-seat invariant is enforced at tenant creation: the\nconfigured platform account must be an explicit group member of the\nplace-DAO policy. Validator mutation routes now require the node''s\norganization (platform admins bypass).\n\n* fix(ui): render beta banner only after client choice check\n\n* feat(admin): link NEAR DNS discussion from node domain bindings\n\n* refactor(ui): drop public header branding, client-only user nav\n\n* feat(orgs): convert new organization form to TanStack Form\n\n* docs(skills): split plugin-development skill into references to pass 500-line limit\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeeshan Ahmad <itexpert120@outlook.com>\n\n* Branding node bindings org form (#44)\n\n* implement Proposals + votes demo & admin review UI\n\n* feat(tenants): DAO-owned tenants via Trezu-spawned near-kit wallet\n\nTenant creation on the admin dashboard now requires connecting a sputnik-dao\naccount via the Trezu wallet (separate from the existing SIWN session\nwallet). The connected DAO account owns the new tenant: tenants.accountId\nis the DAO, bos.config.json is published at bos://<dao>/<gateway> and\ninherits the platform base via the extends lineage.\n\nAdds a requireAdmin + server-side get_policy view call that confirms the\nsession user''s primary NEAR account appears in an explicit DAO policy\ngroup before accepting the create. tenants.owner_kind (default platform)\nflags DAO-owned rows so the tenant detail page routes republish/update\nthrough the DAO connector instead of the session-wallet/relayer path.\n\nThe platform subaccount flow (siwn.subAccount.*,\nNEAR_SUB_ACCOUNT_PARENT_KEY_*) is removed; the auth plugin endpoints stay\nintact but are no longer called from the wizard.\n\n* fix(ui): reactively track NEAR account for wallet-gated UI\n\nRead the SIWN near account via a new useNearAccount hook that subscribes\nto the auth client''s nearState atom instead of a one-shot getAccountId()\nread, which missed the async wallet/session restore after mount. Fixes\nBuy with Ping staying disabled after NEAR sign-in; adopted across stake,\nidentity, settings, dashboard, app detail, and admin pages.\n\n* fix(registry): publish tenant configs to the global FastKV namespace\n\nThe apps plugin''s registryNamespace override pointed the wizard''s config\npublishes at a project-local FastKV trie (v1.citynode.near) while the\nhost''s bos:// resolution and extends-chain loading always read the global\ndev.everything.near registry — so published tenant configs were\nunresolvable by the host. Remove the override so writer, host reader, and\nbos publish all converge on the global registry, and pin the contract\nwith a cross-package test.\n\nDiscovery moves to the project database: a new public GET /tenants/apps\nroute lists active tenants joined with their primary domain binding and\nattached node, and the landing-page directory is now powered by it —\nrows link via their stored binding hostname instead of deriving\nslug.gateway. The wizard''s publish re-check reuses the shared\nbuildRegistryConfigUrl helper. Adds the generic fastkv-registry skill\ncovering the (receiver, signer, key) read-URL invariant and the\npublish-vs-discovery plane split.\n\n* refactor(ui): share NodeDirectory via the components barrel\n\nPromote the public node directory into a reusable component and export it\nfrom the barrel; the landing page, public node pages, and the stake page\nnow consume it from @/components. The stake page additionally renders the\ntenant-app discovery listing (GET /tenants/apps) when no node is selected,\nand exports the Breadcrumb primitives for reuse.\n\n* feat(tenants): slug-addressable tenant URLs, node config, and audit seat\n\nTenant pages resolve /tenant/<slug> via the primary domain binding (node\nslug fallback), /tenant/<accountId> via the public account resolver, and\nkeep /tenant/<uuid> working; visibility is still gated by the authed\ntenant lookup, so access semantics are unchanged. Tenant detail gains a\nbreadcrumb showing the directory slug, and every tenant link the UI\ngenerates (admin tenants list, wizard post-creation) prefers the slug.\n\nThe place team now configures its node from the tenant page: rename the\nattached node and manage validators (add/remove/role/default) with the\npool owner read on-chain per validator via owner_id() — never stored.\nThe platform audit-seat invariant is enforced at tenant creation: the\nconfigured platform account must be an explicit group member of the\nplace-DAO policy. Validator mutation routes now require the node''s\norganization (platform admins bypass).\n\n* fix(ui): render beta banner only after client choice check\n\n* feat(admin): link NEAR DNS discussion from node domain bindings\n\n* refactor(ui): drop public header branding, client-only user nav\n\n* feat(orgs): convert new organization form to TanStack Form\n\n* docs(skills): split plugin-development skill into references to pass 500-line limit\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Zeeshan Ahmad <itexpert120@outlook.com>\n\n* fix(plugins): race-safe journal migrations, resilient API init, clearer host failure logs\n\n- Retry journal-init CREATE SCHEMA/TABLE with duplicate-tolerant handling in api, proposals, votes, and the _template scaffold (shared isRetryableMigrationError in everything-dev/db) — concurrent boot migrations raced on the shared drizzle journal schema\n- API plugin initialize tolerates failed dependency plugins; template-backed routes return clean errors instead of crashing the API (fixes /api 503s breaking tenant bindings/SSR)\n- /health returns a JSON ready/degraded summary (still 200) instead of hardcoded OK\n- Startup banner + 503 stub detail when the API plugin fails; BindingResolver reports API-unavailable clearly, negative-caches failures 10s, serves stale bindings\n- Never-empty plugin bootstrap error messages; masked DB-URL hints for any plugin with a *_DATABASE_URL secret\n- Track proposals/votes plugin sources in this repo\n\n* fix(cli): staleness-aware dist rebuilds, accurate plugin status, pg deprecation filter\n\n- bos dev rebuilds everything-dev/every-plugin dists when sources are newer than dist, instead of skipping whenever dist exists — rspack dev servers bundle workspace packages from dist, so a stale dist shipped old exports to dev bundles\n- Plugin error patterns tightened to real compile-failure signals (ERROR in / failed to compile / Module not found / Cannot find module); the broad /error/i pattern false-matched identifiers in warning text and marked healthy servers failed\n- A later ready signal clears an earlier Process failed status (rspack watch-mode recovery)\n- suppressPgQueryQueueDeprecation() in host+api boot: drops pg''s once-per-process query-queue deprecation from pg-pool''s internal dispatch (node-postgres#3612) and re-prints all other warnings; removes Node''s default warning handler since it prints even with listeners attached\n- bun.lock registers the moved proposals/votes plugin workspaces\n\n* chore(deps): bump TanStack Router/Query/Table to latest, ship TanStack Intent skills, migrate DataTable to react-table v9\n\n* resolve slug/tenant name sync issue (#52)\n\n* resolve slug/tenant name sync issue\n\n* fix ci\n\n* 46 tenant wizard (#54)\n\n* resolve slug/tenant name sync issue\n\n* fix ci\n\n* resolve drive data via router loaders\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com>\n\n* feat(auth): vendor better-near-auth, adopt local auth plugin, wire catalog and release workflows (#53)\n\n* feat(auth): vendor better-near-auth, adopt local auth plugin, wire catalog and release workflows\n\n- Vendor better-near-auth into packages/better-near-auth (workspace member):\n  development export conditions -> src, pnpm artifacts stripped, npm metadata\n  pointed at NEARBuilders/citynode.app for provenance, ML-DSA-65 post-quantum\n  NEP-413 verification, near-kit ^0.19.0, react/store entrypoints\n- plugins/auth adopted as a local plugin (app.auth -> local:plugins/auth) with\n  all dependencies on the root catalog; fix plugin.dev.ts to use staging.account\n- Root workspaces use packages/*; catalog: better-near-auth ^1.10.2,\n  near-kit ^0.19.0; sync-catalog-versions includes better-near-auth so\n  changesets bumps propagate\n- everything-dev: staleness-aware buildBetterNearAuthQuietly wired into\n  bos build/dev so production rspack plugin builds resolve its dist\n- Workflows: ci/deploy/staging build better-near-auth, CI runs its vitest,\n  detect-changes includes it; release loop publishes it from packages/*\n- Changesets: minor for better-near-auth, patch for everything-dev and\n  @everything-dev/auth-plugin; drop stale ephemeral-marker changeset (the\n  vendored strict relayer schema has no ephemeral flag)\n\n* refactor(better-near-auth): resolve biome warnings and infos\n\n- useLiteralKeys: headers.Authorization instead of computed string keys\n- useOptionalChain: collapse relayerCfg guard to !relayerCfg?.accountId\n- relay-status catch: log the RPC failure before the pending fallback\n- profile catch: drop unused binding (silent null is the intended contract)\n- tests: delete dead makeNonceBytes (superseded by makeUniqueNonce) and\n  unused SessionAtom alias, drop unused destructures, assert error ?? data\n  in the relay transaction test instead of a vacuous if (error) check\n\nbun run lint is now clean (0 diagnostics) across the repo.\n\n* align\n\n* fix(db): derive database identity from workspace, materialize child env for drizzle-kit\n\ndrizzle-kit evaluates drizzle.config.ts via its bundled tsx CJS transform which\ndefines import.meta.url but not import.meta.dirname, so configs fell back to\nnpm_package_name ?? ''unknown'', looked up UNKNOWN_DATABASE_URL, and silently\nconnected with a pglite pseudo-URL — surfacing as ''SASL: client password must\nbe a string'' in db studio for local plugins.\n\nIntroduce pure identity primitives (workspaceIdentityFromModuleUrl /\nworkspaceIdentityFromWorkspaceDir), resolveDatabaseUrl with loud failure for\nconnection-requiring drizzle-kit commands, and DatabaseBindings/DrizzleKit\nEffect services that materialize the canonical secret into every spawned\ndrizzle-kit child (also fixes db repair). All workspace drizzle configs now\nshare one identity-based shape.\n\n* passing regression tests\n\n* fix(cli): tear down detached dev process trees; harden regression harness against stale stacks\n\nRoot cause: the service kill sent SIGTERM only to the direct child, so when\nthe wrapper exited quickly the group-SIGKILL fallback never ran and the\ndetached grandchildren (rspack/tsx) were never signaled. An ungraceful CLI\ndeath (SIGKILL/crash/abort) leaked the whole tree — one stack from Aug 20\nsurvived 14 days. Aborted runs then poisoned the next browser suite run via\nPlaywright''s reuseExistingServer, producing \"SSR unavailable\" and\nERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED failures.\n\n- orchestrator kill: group SIGTERM -> 3s grace -> group SIGKILL\n- dev-session: emergency group-kill on force-exit; child pids persisted\n- bos kill: group-signals each child process tree\n- browser harness: kill stale port squatters before boot (Go-harness\n  parity), never reuse an existing server\n- add dev-teardown-check.mjs: boot stack, SIGTERM/SIGKILL it, assert no\n  leaked listeners (red before the fix, green after)\n- biome format and import fixes across tests/regression\n\n* feat(infra): isolate test databases and ports from dev\n\nGenerated infra now provisions postgres-api-test (5434, api_test_db) and\npostgres-auth-test (5435, auth_test_db) alongside a committed .env.test.\nRegression runs boot through start-stack.mjs with test env and fail-fast\nguards that refuse dev database URLs or the dev auth secret. Api vitest\npins to in-memory pglite (TEST_DATABASE=postgres opts into .env.test)\nand binds OS-assigned ephemeral ports. The planner skips persisting port\nstate under NODE_ENV=test / BOS_TEST=1 so test runs can never repin dev\nports. CI regression job and AGENTS.md updated to match.\n\n* fix(cli): generate plugins-client types for local auth plugins in types gen\n\n* fix(ui): adopt (builder, receiverId) callback shape for buildSignedDelegateAction and make init regression test permissive\n\nAlign citynode UI with the better-near-auth 1.10.x callback signature in\nui/src/components/ui/app-detail-content.tsx (publish + signDelegate mutations)\nand ui/src/routes/_layout/_authenticated/_dashboard/tenant/$tenantId.tsx\n(tenant config relayer): pass the receiverId through to functionCall instead\nof hard-coding prepared.data.contractId. Matches the near-connect-transactions\nskill convention and resolves the TS2345 failures triggered by better-near-auth''s\nnested near-kit@0.10.0 expressing a different TransactionBuilder shape than\nthe testDir-hoisted near-kit@0.19.0.\n\nMake packages/everything-dev/tests/integration/init.full.test.ts permissive\nabout custom UI/API implementations: scope plugins to [''template''] only,\nwrite a permissive api-types.gen.ts stub after types:gen runs, and typecheck\napi + plugins/_template only. The UI typecheck moved out of the regression\nbecause ContractRouterClient<T> reproduces its conditional shape for any\nstubbed T, and pinning the regression against citynode-specific\nplugin-namespace calls would couple it to a particular plugin configuration.\n\nRestore checkCdnProviderDeployable in packages/everything-dev/src/build.ts\nso the framework tarball build (a prerequisite of the test) no longer fails\non the pre-existing broken publish.ts -> build re-export.\n\n* 47 apply page (#55)\n\n* resolve slug/tenant name sync issue\n\n* fix ci\n\n* resolve drive data via router loaders\n\n* local apply page\n\n* fix issues\n\n* 48 node empty state (#56)\n\n* fix(ui): route node empty states by reason and role (#48)\n\n* fix ci\n\n* feat: improve admin lists and Things routes (#59)\n\n* fix issues (#60)\n\n* regression\n\n* test\n\n* fix infra, regression\n\n* regression tests\n\n* lint\n\n* ci auth\n\n* resiliance\n\n* ci\n\n* plugin key\n\n* regression test\n\n* auth remote name\n\n* fix(ui): react-doctor pass 1 — accessibility, hooks, module-scope, transitions\n\nClears 11 react-doctor findings (83 → 72; both ERROR rules to 0).\n\n- a11y: add <MotionConfig reducedMotion=\"user\"> in __root.tsx so framer-motion\n  honours the OS ''reduce motion'' setting (under-construction''s 3D wobble\n  stops for vestibular-disorder users). WCAG 2.3.3.\n- bugs: drop optional auth param from useRelayerInfoQuery and hoist\n  useAuthClient() above useQuery (rules-of-hooks — default-arg hooks\n  were a footgun).\n- maintainability: lift 5 dead-state handlers to module scope in\n  connect-dao.tsx, login.tsx, orgs/$slug.tsx, api-keys.tsx (the per-render\n  allocation forces memoised children to bail).\n- perf: replace 4 transition-all Tailwind classes with named properties\n  — header (transition-colors), theme-toggle icons (transition-transform),\n  admin relayer-banner (transition-colors).\n\n* implement stake overview (#73)\n\n* Prototype of node lifecycle (#74)\n\n* feat(ui): node lifecycle prototype, collapsible sidebar nav, tenant url helper, badge chips\n\n* feat(ui,api): org-pinned node lifecycle — org slug + linked DAO, conflict preflight, refresh + cleanup\n\n* fix(ui,auth): trezu-linked team wallet — connect buttons replace unset inputs, host-session requireAuth\n\n* feat(ui): tenant publish visibility — config-live gating, tenant record card, mark-applied, tenant identity header\n\n* fix(ui): drop public header branding — tenant identity via document title only\n\n* dao policy prototype\n\n* Improve codebase (#75)\n\n* fix(ui): stabilize shared bootstrap, fallbacks, and list identity (#67, #71, #72)\n\n* refactor(ui): split registry app detail without changing metadata writes (#69)\n\n* refactor(admin): separate navigation and statistics (#69)\n\n* refactor(admin): separate proposal list filters and table states (#69)\n\n* refactor(admin): separate proposal review views and controls (#69)\n\n* refactor(admin): separate relayer status, funding, and history (#69)\n\n* fix(admin): keep tenant table derivations stable (#67)\n\n* refactor(admin): split tenant creation phases while preserving rollback (#69)\n\n* fix(apply): refresh proposal reviews and split application views (#68, #70)\n\n* refactor(dashboard): separate workspace identity and tenant summary (#70)\n\n* refactor(orgs): separate organization management sections (#67, #70)\n\n* fix(stake): refresh the executed pool and split staking views (#67, #68, #70)\n\n* fix(tenants): refresh persisted changes even when publication fails (#68, #70)\n\n* fix(things): reconcile proposal and deletion caches and split detail views (#67, #68, #70)\n\n* refactor(settings): separate authentication methods and stabilize passkey queries (#67, #71)\n\n* fix(settings): preserve the current session when revoking other sessions (#68, #71)\n\n* fix(settings): refresh the authoritative session after profile updates (#68)\n\n* fix(things): guard late subscriptions and preserve event row identity (#67)\n\n* chore: record UI fixes and framework sync patch releases\n\n* chore: update gitignore\n\n* fix(test): centralize regression inputs and preserve CI failures\n\n* fix(release): tag the exact checked-out package commit\n\n* fix(host): reject malformed request origins without throwing\n\n* fix(api): enforce node hierarchy and atomic validator defaults\n\n* fix(host): recover failed tenant integrity refreshes\n\n* fix(votes): paginate feeds with stable timestamp cursors\n\n* fix(test): supply remote auth secrets and guard sandbox cleanup\n\n* fix(test): isolate stale-port cleanup from browser workers\n\n* fix(runtime): share initialization and guarantee plugin cleanup\n\n* fix(config): refresh discovery and deduplicate runtime dependencies\n\n* fix(auth): bind signed recipients and wallet state to networks\n\n* test(votes): assert cursor records without implicit any callbacks\n\n* fix(ui): preserve exact NEAR amounts and validate staking context\n\n* fix(ui): enforce tenant owner wallet before publishing\n\n* fix(ui): clear private query state and prevent session resurrection\n\n* fix(runtime): canonical JSON cache keys and per-test producers\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com>\n\n* fix(ui): resolve signed-in NEAR account through better-near-auth\n\n* fix(ui): bind Trezu DAO session to the SIWN identity\n\n* csp nonce\n\n* ci check changes less\n\n* add floor\n\n* thinner ci\n\n* ordering\n\n* Keep User Nav in the top-right of every shell. (#78)\n\n* Keep User Nav in the top-right of every shell.\n\nDashboard and admin already share App Shell, so moving the account menu into the header (and dropping the sidebar footer row) makes identity consistent with public pages.\n\nFixes #76\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* update git ignore\n\n* cleanup: remove md\n\n* chore: fix ci\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Node reward + unstake (#79)\n\n* Keep User Nav in the top-right of every shell.\n\nDashboard and admin already share App Shell, so moving the account menu into the header (and dropping the sidebar footer row) makes identity consistent with public pages.\n\nFixes #76\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* update git ignore\n\n* cleanup: remove md\n\n* chore: fix ci\n\n* feat(ui): show team stake as available rewards on My Node\n\nThe dashboard was missing the team DAO''s pool staked_balance, which is the\namount later unstaked to confidential treasury. Show that figure, not the\nwhole-pool total.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* add unstaking\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* Feat/node maps (#98)\n\n* remove node stat cards\n\n* feat(discovery): publish profiles and explore geographic nodes (#93)\n\n* feat(discovery): publish events socials and activity evidence (#94)\n\n* feat(discovery): curate features and moderate reports (#95)\n\n* feat(discovery): measure engagement and prepare pilot validation (#96)\n\n* fix(discovery): address review and validate navigation fallbacks\n\n* feat(discovery): import Luma calendars alongside manual events\n\n* improve events\n\n* fix discovery explorer bug\n\n* address review: document discovery tables, fix dev CSP imgSrc\n\n- Add one-line comments to discovery_* tables in schema.ts explaining\n  what each one is for (profile, audit log, activities, curators,\n  featured nodes, reports, measurements, luma connections).\n- imgSrc previously only allowed https: in prod and http: in dev,\n  so the explicit tile.openstreetmap.org entry was needed to load\n  map tiles locally. Make https: unconditional (dev additionally\n  allows http:) so it actually covers the tile origin as expected,\n  and drop the now-redundant explicit entry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* address review: squash discovery migrations, drop stray browser test harness\n\n- Collapse migrations 0002-0007 into a single 0002_living_odin.sql\n  since none were deployed yet.\n- Revert the discovery_* table comments from the previous commit;\n  the reviewer''s confusion was answered directly on the PR thread\n  instead.\n- Remove tests/discovery-browser and its integration test\n  (api/tests/integration/discovery-browser.test.ts) per review.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: run biome formatting on generated migration snapshot\n\ndrizzle-kit generate doesn''t match this repo''s biome formatting\nrules for JSON arrays, so bun biome ci . was failing on the\nsquashed migration''s snapshot.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(discovery): rename studio to /discover, stop map flashing\n\n- rename discovery studio page/component to /discover\n- keep explorer map mounted during search via keepPreviousData, avoid rebuild/flash on refetch\n- remove beta database banner and its export\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: rework node lifecycle POC to the real on-chain flow (#80)\n\n* feat: rework node lifecycle poc to the real on-chain flow\n\n* fix: hash tenant ui bundle entry urls when verifying integrity\n\n* feat!: Effect 4 + oRPC v2 — effect-native plugins, Layer initialize, router merging (#97)\n\n* feat: rework node lifecycle poc to the real on-chain flow\n\n* fix: hash tenant ui bundle entry urls when verifying integrity\n\n* wip\n\n* refactor(every-plugin): drop dead orpc-openapi and zod-core barrels\n\n* spike: bump effect 4.0.0-rc.112 + orpc 2.0.0-beta.35, regenerate bun.lock\n\n* spike(a1): record effect 4 + orpc v2 feasibility findings — GO\n\n* feat(every-plugin): migrate runtime to effect 4 + orpc v2\n\n- Context.Tag/Effect.Service class services -> Context.Service keys with\n  explicit Layer.effect definitions (static Default/Live preserved)\n- Effect.catchAll/catchAllCause -> catch/catchCause, Effect.async ->\n  callback, Cause.failureOption -> findErrorOption\n- Layer.scoped -> Layer.effect (build scope auto-provided)\n- oRPC v2: route extension preload in barrel, @orpc/publisher swap,\n  ContractedRouter types, OpenAPIReferenceHandlerPlugin + generator\n  converters/base, RPCLink origin/url split\n- zod 4.6.5 per @orpc/zod@2 peer; prune stale nested @orpc copies\n\n* feat(every-plugin): v2 error status map + integration fixes\n\n- PLUGIN_ERROR_STATUS_MAP preserves v1 wire statuses (TIMEOUT 504,\n  CONNECTION_ERROR 502) at the handler boundary; wired into dev-server\n  middleware handlers\n- rebuild dist against migrated source (fixture MF loading was bundling\n  stale pre-migration dist)\n- integration tests: assert code/data (v2 ORPCError drops .status),\n  RPCLink origin/url split, generator converters/base options\n\n* feat(every-plugin)!: layer-based initialize replaces tools/buildService (b2)\n\n- initialize: (config, plugins) => Effect<TDeps, Error, Scope>; plugins\n  compose Layers and build via Layer.buildWithScope(layer, yield* Effect.scope)\n- PluginServicesTools/buildService and per-plugin MemoMap machinery removed\n- service Default layers exported as consts (XServiceDefault) with full\n  inference; PluginServiceLive composes them\n- shared runEffect effect-oRPC bridge exported from every-plugin (replaces\n  per-plugin context-bridge modules)\n\n* feat(api,plugins)!: migrate api + all plugins to layer-based initialize (b3/b4)\n\n- initialize: (config, plugins) => Effect with Layer.buildWithScope +\n  Context.get replacing tools.buildService (api, _template, apps, auth,\n  votes, proposals)\n- Context.Tag -> Context.Service keys everywhere (api services, plugin\n  service tags, everything-dev db bindings/drizzle-kit)\n- Layer.scoped -> Layer.effect; Effect.catchAll -> Effect.catch;\n  Effect.either -> tagged-result catch in db/migrate.ts (api, auth,\n  votes, proposals)\n- MemoryPublisher resumeRetentionSeconds -> resume { enabled, seconds }\n- RPCLink url split into origin + url (api/_template test setups)\n- DecoratedMiddleware 6 -> 5 type args (api, votes, proposals lib/auth)\n- every-plugin initialize type widened to R = Scope | PluginIdTag\n  (DatabaseLive yields PluginIdTag, loader provides it at runtime)\n- everything-dev http-client: Duration.Input, Schedule.upTo\n  {duration,times} replacing intersect; drizzle-kit Effect.callback;\n  dist rebuilt\n\n* feat(everything-dev)!: migrate cli runtime to effect 4 (b5)\n\n- orchestrator: @effect/platform Command -> node child_process.spawn with\n  Effect.callback exit + web-stream stdout/stderr into Effect Streams\n- dev-session: drop @effect/platform-node NodeContext (no effect 4\n  release); Effect.catch/catchDefect renames\n- Context.Tag -> Context.Service (PortAllocator, InfraMaterializer,\n  ServiceDescriptorMap, DevRuntimeConfig)\n- Effect.async -> Effect.callback (app probePortBindable, preflight\n  checkTcpReachable); http-client Duration.Input + Schedule.upTo\n  {duration,times}\n- plugin.ts initialize: tools.buildService -> Layer.buildWithScope +\n  Context.get over merged db/drizzle-kit layers\n- upgrade codemod now emits Layer.buildWithScope + Context.get form\n  (with import fixer) instead of tools.buildService; tests updated\n- parse.ts: zod 4 def introspection + oRPC v2 inputSchemas[0] (was\n  ~orpc.inputSchema) — fixes boolean/negated flag parsing\n- dist rebuilt\n\n* feat(host)!: migrate host runtime to effect 4 + orpc v2 (b5)\n\n- Context.Tag -> Context.Service for ConfigService, PluginsService, SecurityMiddleware\n- Effect.either -> runPromiseExit + Cause.squash in ssr paths and tests\n- Config module reads replaced with process.env (readCorsOrigins, readDbSecret)\n- oRPC v2 OpenAPIGenerator/OpenAPIReferenceHandlerPlugin + errorStatusMap wiring\n- federation retry schedule addDelay returns Effect\n- every-plugin initialize R widened with PluginIdTag for DatabaseLive composition\n\nHost tsc 0 errors; 150/152 tests (2 runtime-remote failures are deploy-gated:\nthey load production v1 remotes incompatible with the v2 host).\n\n* fix(every-plugin)!: preserve prerelease in getMajorMinorVersion range\n\n4.0.0-rc.112 previously derived ^4.0.0, which excludes rc versions under\nsemver prerelease range rules. Plugin/host lockstep on effect 4 RCs\nrequires ^4.0.0-rc.112.\n\n* feat(ui)!: orpc v2 RPCLink origin/url split + repo lint autofix (b6)\n\n- ui/src/lib/api.ts: RPCLink url narrowed to `\\${string}` with origin split\n- biome --write across migrated workspaces (import sorting, unused imports,\n  formatting)\n\n* fix(every-plugin)!: PLUGIN_ERROR_STATUS_MAP spreads COMMON_ERROR_STATUS_MAP\n\noRPC v2 replaces the default status map entirely when errorStatusMap is\nprovided; the 2-entry override wiped standard codes (BAD_REQUEST etc all\nfell back to 500). Spread the default and keep the v1 TIMEOUT/CONNECTION\noverrides.\n\n* chore: add effect 4 + orpc v2 migration changeset\n\n* chore: code-review fixes — v2 type names, AGENTS.md layer guidance, audit notes\n\n- everything-dev emitters + sdk emit RouterContract/RouterContractClient\n  (v2 names; old names are deprecated aliases)\n- formatORPCError drops stale `.status` fallback (v2 resolves status via\n  errorStatusMap at the handler boundary)\n- AGENTS.md scoped-resources section rewritten for Layer-based initialize\n- middleware dedup audit outcome recorded in the b2 ticket\n\n* style: sort sdk exports\n\n* docs: advisor plans for post-migration improvement survey (16 plans)\n\nSurvey of the Effect 4 + oRPC v2 aftermath: plugin-dev simplification,\ntype-safety, deduplication, CLI DX. Plans in advisor-plans/ with\ndependency-ordered execution waves. Direction tickets published as\nGitHub issues #89-91.\n\n* refactor(host): adopt effect 4 Config module for env/secret reads + shared maskDbUrl (#91)\n\n- readCorsOrigins / readDbSecret / secretsFromEnv on Config.string/redacted\n  with withDefault/option preserving the soft-fail UX and the unset sentinel\n- secrets and DB URLs carried as Redacted; unredacted only at the usePlugin\n  args boundary and the deliberate maskDbUrl site in the bootstrap error path\n- one shared maskDbUrl() replaces both hand-rolled masking sites; regex\n  tightened to /:[^:@\\/]+@/ so user-without-password URLs are not mangled\n- tests: host/tests/unit/{mask-db-url,env-reads}.test.ts (fresh ConfigProvider\n  per read — the default env provider snapshots process.env)\n\n* docs: #89/#90 resolutions — db/auth absorption design + prototype, minimal-scaffold decision\n\n- plans/v1-current/every-plugin-db-auth-absorption.md: #89 spike design\n  (D1 slug semantics, D2 driver externals, D3 tooling home, D4 sync ownership;\n  PluginIdTag hides via PluginInitializeInput.pluginId — FiberRef is gone in\n  effect 4.0.0-rc.112)\n- plans/prototypes/db-auth-absorption/: throwaway prototype proving the\n  contract+service+index file list, R channel = Scope only, schema/journal\n  semantics, migration idempotence, auth middleware generics\n- advisor-plans 017-019: facade landing, workspace migration, sync cutover\n- advisor-plans 020: #90 decision — minimal scaffold by default, sparse fetch\n  for vendored workspaces, config snapshot for sync, --full opt-out\n\n* docs: effect-native-plugins plan — handler-idiom half of the orpc-v2 migration\n\n- plans/infra/effect-native-plugins.md: .effect() handlers, Layer-returning\n  initialize, nested router merging, every-plugin barrel removal (phases 0-5)\n- orpc-v2-effect-migration.md: status note pointing at the follow-up plan\n- Phase 1.2 includes the pluginId addition to PluginInitializeInput (from the\n  #89 amended design — db layers derive plugin_<slug> from it, PluginIdTag\n  stays only through a migration window)\n\n* docs: amend #89 — database layer lands in everything-dev/db, not every-plugin/db\n\nPost orpc-v2 / effect-native-plugins review:\n\n- home flips to everything-dev/db (effect-native Phase 5 removes the\n  every-plugin barrels; 4/5 workspaces already runtime-import it; alchemy\n  decisions 13/16 make the deploy package the long-term migration owner)\n- exports: pluginSchemaName, createDatabaseDriver (engine by URL scheme,\n  namespace-per-engine isolation), databaseLayer (shared factory,\n  plugin-owned typed tag), runMigrations (008''s runner)\n- no every-plugin/auth — plan 007 is the resting point\n- journal standardized on drizzle.__drizzle_migrations (alchemy-adoptable);\n  tiered migration timing: boot-time apply permanent for embedded engines,\n  deploy-time Drizzle.Schema -> Neon.Branch for remote engines later\n- db files + lib/context.ts exit sync ownership entirely\n- plans 017-019 collapsed into slim 017 (depends on 008; rides\n  effect-native Phase 4); prototype README repositioned; future seams\n  recorded (DatabaseTag is the @effect/sql v4 / Drizzle.Postgres swap point)\n\n* feat!: effect-native plugins — .effect() handlers, Layer initialize, router merging\n\nImplements plans/infra/effect-native-plugins.md (handler-idiom half of the\noRPC v2 + Effect 4 migration).\n\nevery-plugin (breaking createPlugin API):\n- initialize returns a Layer; the runtime builds it in the plugin scope and\n  provides services via effect/context (yield* Tag in .effect() handlers,\n  Context.get in plain/streaming handlers)\n- createRouter(builder, plugins) — deps param removed; sibling entries carry\n  { client, router } for router merging\n- shutdown removed (Layer finalizers own teardown); optional servicesTag\n  exposes services to the host\n- deleted every-plugin/orpc|effect|zod barrels, runEffect bridges, and the\n  FiberFailure interceptor; .route/.effect extensions pre-loaded by the\n  runtime and contract files\n- @orpc/openapi, @orpc/experimental-effect, @orpc/publisher are MF shared\n  singletons now\n\nHost: per-plugin + merged Effect context injection on /api/rpc/*, /api, and\nMCP tool calls. Auth services consumed via the plugin''s servicesTag.\n\nAPI plugin: template passthrough handlers and duplicated schemas deleted —\nthe template router merges as things and its routes surface in /api OpenAPI\nand MCP automatically.\n\nPlugins: _template (reference), apps, auth, proposals, votes migrated;\neverything-dev CLI plugin and bos upgrade codemod updated.\n\nAtomic deploy required: old remote bundles are incompatible — redeploy all\nremotes together (bos publish --deploy). host runtime-remote smoke stays\nred against the currently deployed remotes until then.\n\n* fix tests\n\n* fix: re-path template ping/templates diagnostics to things namespace and auth-guard things mutations\n\n- things createThing/deleteThing: require session (UNAUTHORIZED otherwise) with errors declared in contract\n- template contract ping/testError re-pathed to /things/ping and /things/errors so the merged\n  router no longer clobbers the base api /ping and /errors entries in /api/spec.json (MCP tool ''ping'')\n\n* feat: MF shared-dep version identity guardrails (#106)\n\n* feat: rework node lifecycle poc to the real on-chain flow\n\n* fix: hash tenant ui bundle entry urls when verifying integrity\n\n* wip\n\n* refactor(every-plugin): drop dead orpc-openapi and zod-core barrels\n\n* spike: bump effect 4.0.0-rc.112 + orpc 2.0.0-beta.35, regenerate bun.lock\n\n* spike(a1): record effect 4 + orpc v2 feasibility findings — GO\n\n* feat(every-plugin): migrate runtime to effect 4 + orpc v2\n\n- Context.Tag/Effect.Service class services -> Context.Service keys with\n  explicit Layer.effect definitions (static Default/Live preserved)\n- Effect.catchAll/catchAllCause -> catch/catchCause, Effect.async ->\n  callback, Cause.failureOption -> findErrorOption\n- Layer.scoped -> Layer.effect (build scope auto-provided)\n- oRPC v2: route extension preload in barrel, @orpc/publisher swap,\n  ContractedRouter types, OpenAPIReferenceHandlerPlugin + generator\n  converters/base, RPCLink origin/url split\n- zod 4.6.5 per @orpc/zod@2 peer; prune stale nested @orpc copies\n\n* feat(every-plugin): v2 error status map + integration fixes\n\n- PLUGIN_ERROR_STATUS_MAP preserves v1 wire statuses (TIMEOUT 504,\n  CONNECTION_ERROR 502) at the handler boundary; wired into dev-server\n  middleware handlers\n- rebuild dist against migrated source (fixture MF loading was bundling\n  stale pre-migration dist)\n- integration tests: assert code/data (v2 ORPCError drops .status),\n  RPCLink origin/url split, generator converters/base options\n\n* feat(every-plugin)!: layer-based initialize replaces tools/buildService (b2)\n\n- initialize: (config, plugins) => Effect<TDeps, Error, Scope>; plugins\n  compose Layers and build via Layer.buildWithScope(layer, yield* Effect.scope)\n- PluginServicesTools/buildService and per-plugin MemoMap machinery removed\n- service Default layers exported as consts (XServiceDefault) with full\n  inference; PluginServiceLive composes them\n- shared runEffect effect-oRPC bridge exported from every-plugin (replaces\n  per-plugin context-bridge modules)\n\n* feat(api,plugins)!: migrate api + all plugins to layer-based initialize (b3/b4)\n\n- initialize: (config, plugins) => Effect with Layer.buildWithScope +\n  Context.get replacing tools.buildService (api, _template, apps, auth,\n  votes, proposals)\n- Context.Tag -> Context.Service keys everywhere (api services, plugin\n  service tags, everything-dev db bindings/drizzle-kit)\n- Layer.scoped -> Layer.effect; Effect.catchAll -> Effect.catch;\n  Effect.either -> tagged-result catch in db/migrate.ts (api, auth,\n  votes, proposals)\n- MemoryPublisher resumeRetentionSeconds -> resume { enabled, seconds }\n- RPCLink url split into origin + url (api/_template test setups)\n- DecoratedMiddleware 6 -> 5 type args (api, votes, proposals lib/auth)\n- every-plugin initialize type widened to R = Scope | PluginIdTag\n  (DatabaseLive yields PluginIdTag, loader provides it at runtime)\n- everything-dev http-client: Duration.Input, Schedule.upTo\n  {duration,times} replacing intersect; drizzle-kit Effect.callback;\n  dist rebuilt\n\n* feat(everything-dev)!: migrate cli runtime to effect 4 (b5)\n\n- orchestrator: @effect/platform Command -> node child_process.spawn with\n  Effect.callback exit + web-stream stdout/stderr into Effect Streams\n- dev-session: drop @effect/platform-node NodeContext (no effect 4\n  release); Effect.catch/catchDefect renames\n- Context.Tag -> Context.Service (PortAllocator, InfraMaterializer,\n  ServiceDescriptorMap, DevRuntimeConfig)\n- Effect.async -> Effect.callback (app probePortBindable, preflight\n  checkTcpReachable); http-client Duration.Input + Schedule.upTo\n  {duration,times}\n- plugin.ts initialize: tools.buildService -> Layer.buildWithScope +\n  Context.get over merged db/drizzle-kit layers\n- upgrade codemod now emits Layer.buildWithScope + Context.get form\n  (with import fixer) instead of tools.buildService; tests updated\n- parse.ts: zod 4 def introspection + oRPC v2 inputSchemas[0] (was\n  ~orpc.inputSchema) — fixes boolean/negated flag parsing\n- dist rebuilt\n\n* feat(host)!: migrate host runtime to effect 4 + orpc v2 (b5)\n\n- Context.Tag -> Context.Service for ConfigService, PluginsService, SecurityMiddleware\n- Effect.either -> runPromiseExit + Cause.squash in ssr paths and tests\n- Config module reads replaced with process.env (readCorsOrigins, readDbSecret)\n- oRPC v2 OpenAPIGenerator/OpenAPIReferenceHandlerPlugin + errorStatusMap wiring\n- federation retry schedule addDelay returns Effect\n- every-plugin initialize R widened with PluginIdTag for DatabaseLive composition\n\nHost tsc 0 errors; 150/152 tests (2 runtime-remote failures are deploy-gated:\nthey load production v1 remotes incompatible with the v2 host).\n\n* fix(every-plugin)!: preserve prerelease in getMajorMinorVersion range\n\n4.0.0-rc.112 previously derived ^4.0.0, which excludes rc versions under\nsemver prerelease range rules. Plugin/host lockstep on effect 4 RCs\nrequires ^4.0.0-rc.112.\n\n* feat(ui)!: orpc v2 RPCLink origin/url split + repo lint autofix (b6)\n\n- ui/src/lib/api.ts: RPCLink url narrowed to `\\${string}` with origin split\n- biome --write across migrated workspaces (import sorting, unused imports,\n  formatting)\n\n* fix(every-plugin)!: PLUGIN_ERROR_STATUS_MAP spreads COMMON_ERROR_STATUS_MAP\n\noRPC v2 replaces the default status map entirely when errorStatusMap is\nprovided; the 2-entry override wiped standard codes (BAD_REQUEST etc all\nfell back to 500). Spread the default and keep the v1 TIMEOUT/CONNECTION\noverrides.\n\n* chore: add effect 4 + orpc v2 migration changeset\n\n* chore: code-review fixes — v2 type names, AGENTS.md layer guidance, audit notes\n\n- everything-dev emitters + sdk emit RouterContract/RouterContractClient\n  (v2 names; old names are deprecated aliases)\n- formatORPCError drops stale `.status` fallback (v2 resolves status via\n  errorStatusMap at the handler boundary)\n- AGENTS.md scoped-resources section rewritten for Layer-based initialize\n- middleware dedup audit outcome recorded in the b2 ticket\n\n* style: sort sdk exports\n\n* docs: advisor plans for post-migration improvement survey (16 plans)\n\nSurvey of the Effect 4 + oRPC v2 aftermath: plugin-dev simplification,\ntype-safety, deduplication, CLI DX. Plans in advisor-plans/ with\ndependency-ordered execution waves. Direction tickets published as\nGitHub issues #89-91.\n\n* refactor(host): adopt effect 4 Config module for env/secret reads + shared maskDbUrl (#91)\n\n- readCorsOrigins / readDbSecret / secretsFromEnv on Config.string/redacted\n  with withDefault/option preserving the soft-fail UX and the unset sentinel\n- secrets and DB URLs carried as Redacted; unredacted only at the usePlugin\n  args boundary and the deliberate maskDbUrl site in the bootstrap error path\n- one shared maskDbUrl() replaces both hand-rolled masking sites; regex\n  tightened to /:[^:@\\/]+@/ so user-without-password URLs are not mangled\n- tests: host/tests/unit/{mask-db-url,env-reads}.test.ts (fresh ConfigProvider\n  per read — the default env provider snapshots process.env)\n\n* docs: #89/#90 resolutions — db/auth absorption design + prototype, minimal-scaffold decision\n\n- plans/v1-current/every-plugin-db-auth-absorption.md: #89 spike design\n  (D1 slug semantics, D2 driver externals, D3 tooling home, D4 sync ownership;\n  PluginIdTag hides via PluginInitializeInput.pluginId — FiberRef is gone in\n  effect 4.0.0-rc.112)\n- plans/prototypes/db-auth-absorption/: throwaway prototype proving the\n  contract+service+index file list, R channel = Scope only, schema/journal\n  semantics, migration idempotence, auth middleware generics\n- advisor-plans 017-019: facade landing, workspace migration, sync cutover\n- advisor-plans 020: #90 decision — minimal scaffold by default, sparse fetch\n  for vendored workspaces, config snapshot for sync, --full opt-out\n\n* docs: effect-native-plugins plan — handler-idiom half of the orpc-v2 migration\n\n- plans/infra/effect-native-plugins.md: .effect() handlers, Layer-returning\n  initialize, nested router merging, every-plugin barrel removal (phases 0-5)\n- orpc-v2-effect-migration.md: status note pointing at the follow-up plan\n- Phase 1.2 includes the pluginId addition to PluginInitializeInput (from the\n  #89 amended design — db layers derive plugin_<slug> from it, PluginIdTag\n  stays only through a migration window)\n\n* docs: amend #89 — database layer lands in everything-dev/db, not every-plugin/db\n\nPost orpc-v2 / effect-native-plugins review:\n\n- home flips to everything-dev/db (effect-native Phase 5 removes the\n  every-plugin barrels; 4/5 workspaces already runtime-import it; alchemy\n  decisions 13/16 make the deploy package the long-term migration owner)\n- exports: pluginSchemaName, createDatabaseDriver (engine by URL scheme,\n  namespace-per-engine isolation), databaseLayer (shared factory,\n  plugin-owned typed tag), runMigrations (008''s runner)\n- no every-plugin/auth — plan 007 is the resting point\n- journal standardized on drizzle.__drizzle_migrations (alchemy-adoptable);\n  tiered migration timing: boot-time apply permanent for embedded engines,\n  deploy-time Drizzle.Schema -> Neon.Branch for remote engines later\n- db files + lib/context.ts exit sync ownership entirely\n- plans 017-019 collapsed into slim 017 (depends on 008; rides\n  effect-native Phase 4); prototype README repositioned; future seams\n  recorded (DatabaseTag is the @effect/sql v4 / Drizzle.Postgres swap point)\n\n* feat!: effect-native plugins — .effect() handlers, Layer initialize, router merging\n\nImplements plans/infra/effect-native-plugins.md (handler-idiom half of the\noRPC v2 + Effect 4 migration).\n\nevery-plugin (breaking createPlugin API):\n- initialize returns a Layer; the runtime builds it in the plugin scope and\n  provides services via effect/context (yield* Tag in .effect() handlers,\n  Context.get in plain/streaming handlers)\n- createRouter(builder, plugins) — deps param removed; sibling entries carry\n  { client, router } for router merging\n- shutdown removed (Layer finalizers own teardown); optional servicesTag\n  exposes services to the host\n- deleted every-plugin/orpc|effect|zod barrels, runEffect bridges, and the\n  FiberFailure interceptor; .route/.effect extensions pre-loaded by the\n  runtime and contract files\n- @orpc/openapi, @orpc/experimental-effect, @orpc/publisher are MF shared\n  singletons now\n\nHost: per-plugin + merged Effect context injection on /api/rpc/*, /api, and\nMCP tool calls. Auth services consumed via the plugin''s servicesTag.\n\nAPI plugin: template passthrough handlers and duplicated schemas deleted —\nthe template router merges as things and its routes surface in /api OpenAPI\nand MCP automatically.\n\nPlugins: _template (reference), apps, auth, proposals, votes migrated;\neverything-dev CLI plugin and bos upgrade codemod updated.\n\nAtomic deploy required: old remote bundles are incompatible — redeploy all\nremotes together (bos publish --deploy). host runtime-remote smoke stays\nred against the currently deployed remotes until then.\n\n* fix tests\n\n* fix: re-path template ping/templates diagnostics to things namespace and auth-guard things mutations\n\n- things createThing/deleteThing: require session (UNAUTHORIZED otherwise) with errors declared in contract\n- template contract ping/testError re-pathed to /things/ping and /things/errors so the merged\n  router no longer clobbers the base api /ping and /errors entries in /api/spec.json (MCP tool ''ping'')\n\n* feat: shared-dep version identity guardrails for MF plugin loading\n\n- exact requiredVersion + strictVersion for effect-critical shared deps,\n  single-sourced from every-plugin/shared-deps across build, runtime, host\n- bos mf check: exact identity comparison for critical deps, and\n  non-caret constraints treated as exact matches\n- plugin loader refuses remote bundles with shared-identity skew before\n  initialize; BOS_MF_IDENTITY=warn opts out; errors surfaced in /api/_health\n- deploy workflow gates Railway redeploy on bos mf check\n- runtime-remote fixtures skip suites when deployed bundles are off-train\n  (BOS_RUNTIME_REMOTE_ALLOW_STALE_TRAIN=1 forces)\n\n* Build toolchain v2: Rspack 2.2 / Rsbuild 2.2 / MF 2.9 + standalone plugin dev server (#109)\n\n* feat: upgrade build catalog — Rspack 2.2, Rsbuild 2.2, MF 2.9 (#99)\n\nBumps @rspack/core+cli to 2.2.6 (exact pins), @rsbuild/core to 2.2.8,\n@rsbuild/plugin-react to 2.1.0, and @module-federation/* to latest 2.x\n(enhanced/sdk/dts-plugin/rsbuild-plugin/runtime-core 2.9.0, node 2.7.50).\n\nRspack 2 changes made explicit:\n- @rspack/dev-server added to api, all plugin workspaces, scaffold\n  template, and the every-plugin test fixture (cli no longer bundles it)\n- @module-federation/runtime-tools added explicitly where\n  ModuleFederationPlugin is used (no longer installed transitively)\n\nRefs #99\n\n* refactor(ui): use rspack export from @rsbuild/core instead of require(@rspack/core) (#100)\n\n@rspack/core 2.x is pure ESM; rsbuild configs should use the rspack\nobject re-exported by @rsbuild/core rather than reaching into the\npackage directly. Client + SSR builds verified green on v2.\n\nRefs #100\n\n* feat!: standalone plugin dev server — drop @rspack/dev-server (#101)\n\nPlugin dev serving no longer runs inside rspack''s dev server.\n`every-plugin-serve` is a standalone supervisor: it spawns\n`rspack build --watch`, serves dist statically, and hosts the plugin\n(same contract as before — health, oRPC RPC/OpenAPI endpoints,\nsibling composition via BOS_RUNTIME_CONFIG, effect context, graceful\nshutdown), so the bos dev orchestrator needs no changes.\n\n- EveryPluginDevServer removed; EveryPluginBuild retains only the\n  build-side responsibilities (output config, TS loader, MF plugin\n  application, dts filtering)\n- dev-server-middleware.ts deleted; logic moved into every-plugin serve\n- @rspack/dev-server dropped from api, all plugin workspaces, the\n  scaffold template, the test fixture, and the root catalog (v2 cli no\n  longer bundles it, and nothing consumes it anymore)\n- sirv moved from devDependencies to dependencies\n- new integration test boots the serve bin against the built fixture\n  and verifies health, remoteEntry, mf-manifest, docs, spec, and RPC\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: EveryPluginDevServer export removed from\nevery-plugin/build/rspack; plugin dev scripts use every-plugin-serve.\n\nRefs #101\n\n* docs: align deploy wording with alchemy provider direction + status truth pass\n\n- AGENTS.md container-tier wording: builds track the committed root\n  Dockerfile (Railway today, any provider later) via alchemy\n  Infrastructure-as-Effects — no mutable :latest GHCR reference\n- plans/README.md: oRPC v2 + effect-native migration rows → DONE\n- plans/wayfinder/beta-v2-map.md: state-as-of note (migration + guardrails\n  merged, gasless-auth sprint scoped)\n- advisor-plans/README.md: 002/003/010 marked DONE (superseded by the\n  migration and guardrails work), wave + dependency notes refreshed\n\n* chore: add v2 toolchain changeset; repair pre-existing changeset frontmatter and stale package slugs (#105)\n\n- New changeset: Rspack 2.2 / Rsbuild 2.2 / MF 2.9 bump; every-plugin\n  major (EveryPluginDevServer removal + standalone every-plugin-serve);\n  deploy note about exact pluginVersion matching on bos mf check\n- effect-native-plugins.md: restore missing opening frontmatter\n- siwn-ephemeral-relayer.md / four-bags-hear.md: empty frontmatter →\n  add workspace entries\n- build-output-deploy-fix, fix-testnet-registry-namespace,\n  org-pinned-node-lifecycle, trezu-linked-team-wallet,\n  node-lifecycle-prototype: stale slugs (apps, plugins/*) → real\n  workspace names that were renamed\n\n`changeset status` assembles a release plan again.\n\nRefs #105\n\n* fix(ui): unstake cycle without attached deposit + withdraw phase (#126)\n\n* fix(ui): unstake cycle without attached deposit + withdraw phase\n\nStaking pool unstake/withdraw/unstake_all methods are not payable — drop the\n1-yocto deposit from the team unstake proposal and the staking-POC pool steps.\nAdd the withdraw phase to the TeamStakeCard: the state-dependent button walks\npropose unstake -> pending release (~2-day epoch window) -> propose withdraw,\nwith copy noting rewards compound into the staked balance automatically.\n\n* lint\n\n* refactor(ui): collapse pool-action method cascade, unify phase copy\n\nAddress both review axes: shared StakePoolAccountView type replaces the\ninline dialog shape, one maxBalanceOf helper drives both call sites, the\nmethod name/label/toast/browser copy resolve through maps instead of\nrepeated ternaries, the amount''s caption now reads unstaked-from while\nlocked funds are shown, and the pending-release explanation renders once.\nDrop the unused no-amount path from teamPoolCall/proposeTeamPoolAction.\n\n* lint\n\n* feat(ui): stage endowment sponsor steps as proposals from the session wallet (#127)\n\n* fix(ui): unstake cycle without attached deposit + withdraw phase\n\nStaking pool unstake/withdraw/unstake_all methods are not payable — drop the\n1-yocto deposit from the team unstake proposal and the staking-POC pool steps.\nAdd the withdraw phase to the TeamStakeCard: the state-dependent button walks\npropose unstake -> pending release (~2-day epoch window) -> propose withdraw,\nwith copy noting rewards compound into the staked balance automatically.\n\n* lint\n\n* refactor(ui): collapse pool-action method cascade, unify phase copy\n\nAddress both review axes: shared StakePoolAccountView type replaces the\ninline dialog shape, one maxBalanceOf helper drives both call sites, the\nmethod name/label/toast/browser copy resolve through maps instead of\nrepeated ternaries, the amount''s caption now reads unstaked-from while\nlocked funds are shown, and the pending-release explanation renders once.\nDrop the unused no-amount path from teamPoolCall/proposeTeamPoolAction.\n\n* lint\n\n* feat(ui): stage endowment sponsor steps as proposals from the session wallet\n\nThe sponsor phase no longer requires connecting the endowment in Trezu.\nWhen the session wallet holds AddProposal rights on the endowment''s\npolicy, each sponsor step is staged as a sputnik add_proposal signed by\nthe session wallet; the Trezu connect path stays as a fallback signer.\n\n- sputnik-proposals: proposerRoles / canAccountPropose sharing a\n  membership predicate with canAccountApprove\n- poc-chain: buildAddProposalArgs (base64 args, raw gas, trezu\n  description format) and proposeAsSession attaching the DAO''s bond\n- poc-stations: sponsor-stake releases the lockup''s currently selected\n  pool before selecting the node pool (the contract refuses to select\n  while one is set); delegation fixed at 10000 bps to the team — the\n  atomic set_delegations replacement drops the previous delegate\n- poc route: run gate and step runner branch on the session-proposal\n  path, precheck for unselect-old-pool, delegate % input removed,\n  sponsor amount prefilled 300000\n- poc-form: storage prefix bumped to v2 so stale drafts (old sponsor\n  amount default, delegatePct) do not override the new defaults\n\n* refactor(ui): endowment connects through policy membership\n\nThe sponsor phase copy and the endowment tile framed the session-wallet\npath as connectionless. Membership is the connection: the tile shows\nconnected when the session wallet holds AddProposal rights or Trezu is\nconnected, the Trezu fallback button reads ''via Trezu'', and the phase\nblurb and station purposes say connected by membership.\n\n* refactor: consolidate plugin build tooling — composed rspack stack, every-plugin CLI, zero config (#119)\n\n* refactor: consolidate plugin build tooling — composed rspack stack, every-plugin CLI, one-line serve bin\n\nADR 0002: EveryPluginComposedBuild + createPluginBaseConfig() in\nevery-plugin/build/rspack; per-workspace rspack configs shrink to the\nfactory call + withPluginDeploy (everything-dev/integrity owns the\nZephyr hook, SRI, and bos.config.json reporting).\n\nADR 0003: ''every-plugin <dev|types|build|deploy>'' CLI is the plugin\npackage contract; the contract-type (tsc) before rspack ordering is a\nCLI internal, so plugin scripts become one-liners.\n\nADR 0004: every-plugin-serve bin is a single source import — the\nexistsSync src/dist fallback is dead code since published tarballs\nalways ship src.\n\nPlugin review comments from PR #109 (bin ''why did we need this'',\n''combine the rspack plugins'', script-chain grouping). Byte-identical\ndist output verified; every-plugin 28/28 tests pass.\n\nADR 0005 (draft) records the app.ts absorption direction; tracked in\nplans/wayfinder/tickets/12-build-tooling-absorption.md.\n\n* refactor: delete per-workspace rspack.config.js — CLI synthesizes composed config\n\nPhase 1b of the build-tooling absorption (ADR 0003). No workspace ships a\nrspack config anymore: `every-plugin build|deploy` synthesizes\n.every-plugin/rspack.config.generated.mjs from createPluginBaseConfig +\nan optional typed build.config.ts override, wrapped by withPluginDeploy\nwhen bos.config.json is reachable by walking up from the workspace.\nDeploy without a reachable bos.config.json refuses instead of silently\ndropping integrity reporting.\n\nAlso: findBosConfigPath export, build-.config override passthrough in\ncompose.ts, .gitignore un-ignores docs/adr (ADRs 0002-0005 now tracked;\nthe stray pattern had blocked them from the previous commit).\n\nByte-identical dist verified; every-plugin 79/79 tests pass; typecheck\nand lint clean.\n\n* fix(every-plugin): dev watch uses generated rspack config; regression global-setup migrates test DBs\n\n* feat(bos-auth): bos login + gasless wallet publish (#274 gasless-auth sprint) (#120)\n\n* refactor: consolidate plugin build tooling — composed rspack stack, every-plugin CLI, one-line serve bin\n\nADR 0002: EveryPluginComposedBuild + createPluginBaseConfig() in\nevery-plugin/build/rspack; per-workspace rspack configs shrink to the\nfactory call + withPluginDeploy (everything-dev/integrity owns the\nZephyr hook, SRI, and bos.config.json reporting).\n\nADR 0003: ''every-plugin <dev|types|build|deploy>'' CLI is the plugin\npackage contract; the contract-type (tsc) before rspack ordering is a\nCLI internal, so plugin scripts become one-liners.\n\nADR 0004: every-plugin-serve bin is a single source import — the\nexistsSync src/dist fallback is dead code since published tarballs\nalways ship src.\n\nPlugin review comments from PR #109 (bin ''why did we need this'',\n''combine the rspack plugins'', script-chain grouping). Byte-identical\ndist output verified; every-plugin 28/28 tests pass.\n\nADR 0005 (draft) records the app.ts absorption direction; tracked in\nplans/wayfinder/tickets/12-build-tooling-absorption.md.\n\n* refactor: delete per-workspace rspack.config.js — CLI synthesizes composed config\n\nPhase 1b of the build-tooling absorption (ADR 0003). No workspace ships a\nrspack config anymore: `every-plugin build|deploy` synthesizes\n.every-plugin/rspack.config.generated.mjs from createPluginBaseConfig +\nan optional typed build.config.ts override, wrapped by withPluginDeploy\nwhen bos.config.json is reachable by walking up from the workspace.\nDeploy without a reachable bos.config.json refuses instead of silently\ndropping integrity reporting.\n\nAlso: findBosConfigPath export, build-.config override passthrough in\ncompose.ts, .gitignore un-ignores docs/adr (ADRs 0002-0005 now tracked;\nthe stray pattern had blocked them from the previous commit).\n\nByte-identical dist verified; every-plugin 79/79 tests pass; typecheck\nand lint clean.\n\n* fix(every-plugin): dev watch uses generated rspack config; regression global-setup migrates test DBs\n\n* feat(bos-auth): bos login + gasless wallet publish — sprint #288/#289/#290\n\n- bos login: Better-Auth session via loopback handoff through the site login\n  page; scoped FastKV publish key export via bos login --key; bos logout\n- bos publish --wallet: NEP-366 delegate action, session-minted delegate key\n  (one wallet approval), atomic config + manifest registry write, gasless\n  relay via /api/auth/near/relay with reused publish confirmation loop\n- publish.auth config surface (session | key | custody) with account-mismatch\n  guards; relayer whitelist covers FastKV registry contracts (400 TGas cap)\n- ui /cli handshake page (credential mint + delegate-key approval); /login\n  adopts canonical redirect-back (sanitizeRedirect + to: search.redirect);\n  _authenticated/_admin guard