7e0d3ed7b552238bbec893c36e43180903"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/6f7bee0a2aef7fbbbeb3c0dcc2eda93bc4078f1b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/6f7bee0a2aef7fbbbeb3c0dcc2eda93bc4078f1b","node_id":"C_kwDORq8oVtoAKDZmN2JlZTBhMmFlZjdmYmJiZWIzYzBkY2MyZWRhOTNiYzQwNzhmMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commit/ada1cd236e219f75e62eb98b559d8c5feb361f98","sha":"ada1cd236e219f75e62eb98b559d8c5feb361f98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/ada1cd236e219f75e62eb98b559d8c5feb361f98"}],"sha":"6f7bee0a2aef7fbbbeb3c0dcc2eda93bc4078f1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/6f7bee0a2aef7fbbbeb3c0dcc2eda93bc4078f1b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16282460?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/elliotBraem","id":16282460,"login":"elliotBraem","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjgyNDYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotBraem","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/commits/ada1cd236e219f75e62eb98b559d8c5feb361f98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:47:24Z","email":"elliot@ejlbraem.com","name":"Elliot Braem"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T17:47:24Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: make tenant creation atomic with DB-middle flow (#227)\n\n* feat: tenant lifecycle with status gating and tenant detail UI\n\nAdd a full tenant lifecycle across the API, host, and UI:\n\n- API: extend tenants table with status/updated_at/deleted_at (soft-delete),\n  add update/softDelete/suspend/reactivate, resolveTenantByOrgId, and\n  tenantPreflight routes; listTenants uses requireAuth consistently\n- Host: gate tenant resolution on a published config status field\n  (suspended -> 503, pending_deletion -> 410) without an API round-trip\n- UI: add tenant detail/edit/suspend/delete page that republishes the tenant\n  config with the matching status; fix accountId fallback and drop the\n  wikiAccountId org coupling in the creation flow and orgs list\n- everything-dev: allow optional status in BosConfigInput\n- template plugin: move things CRUD to a DB-backed demonstration\n\n* fix: republish config on tenant edits, add preflight and retry publish\n\n* feat: remove _viewer, add testError surface, and regression tests for error/security responses\n\nRemove _viewer paths/CSP conditionals from host, add structured testError route to core API and template plugin, and add regression tests verifying error response shapes, security headers, CSRF protection, body-size limiting, and rate limiting.\n\n* feat: append template thing routes to API router via plugin client passthrough\n\nAdd createThing/getThing/listThings/deleteThing to API contract and delegate to template plugin via _plugins.template(). Route with requireAuth, restoring /api/things surface at the host.\n\nUpdate regression tests to match template plugin''s ThingSchema response shape.\n\nAdd router composition section (Phase 1.7) to oRPC V2 migration plan.\n\n* fix: make getThing/listThings public, remove requireAuth; fix test body shapes\n\nOnly createThing/deleteThing require auth (writes are gated). getThing/listThings are public reads matching the template plugin''s behavior.\n\nFix auth_api_key_flow_test.go: pluginId→thingId body shape, remove pluginId from response assertions (match ThingSchema/CreatedThingSchema).\n\n* fix: standalone plugin dev servers load dependsOn siblings, fix test type errors\n\n- Set BOS_RUNTIME_CONFIG env for all dev processes (not just host)\n- dev-server-middleware reads BOS_RUNTIME_CONFIG, registers local sibling deps,\n  loads them with retry, and passes client factories as 3rd arg to usePlugin\n- bos.config.json: add dependsOn: [\"template\"] to api entry\n- Fix scope-lifecycle.test.ts: createRouter returns contract shape, createClient() without args\n\n* feat: migrate template plugin regression tests to Docker Postgres\n\n- Add postgres-template container to docker-compose.yml (port 5434)\n- Set TEMPLATE_DATABASE_URL in regression test harness env\n- Auto-create things table in DatabaseLive Postgres path (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS)\n- Add TruncateThings() cleanup before each test run via docker exec\n- Eliminates PGlite in-memory state persistence issues between test runs\n\n* fix: add TEMPLATE_DATABASE_URL to template plugin secrets in bos.config.json\n\nRequired for the host to pass the env var to the template plugin''s initialize, enabling Postgres in regression tests and production.\n\n* fix: remove redundant auto-DDL from template DatabaseLive\n\nThe template already has a migration system (unplugin-drizzle-orm-migrations) that creates tables on init. My pool.query CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS was running before the migration, causing the migration''s CREATE TABLE (without IF NOT EXISTS) to fail with ''relation already exists''.\n\n* fix: drop template tables before server start instead of wiping after\n\nMigration runs during plugin init at startup — cleanup was too late (post-server-ready). Now DROP TABLE IF EXISTS things, drizzle_migrations CASCADE before bos dev starts, giving the migration system a clean slate.\n\n* fix: propagate api.dependsOn to RuntimeConfig and fix broken browser test selectors\n\n- config.ts: add dependsOn to result.api in buildRuntimeConfig\n- types.ts: extend ApiPluginConfigSchema with dependsOn, use it in BosConfig.app.api\n- app-load.spec.ts: replace fictional ''open assistant'' test with real /about → /skill navigation\n- auth-client.spec.ts: fix ''Workspace'' selector (was inside h1, now sibling div) and fix ''Settings'' case mismatch\n\n* fix: use ''Identity Status'' instead of ''Workspace'' for home page verification\n\nWorkspace text exists in the header div but was not found by Playwright after anonymous sign-in. Identity Status renders inside the user-loaded card, confirming session data actually resolved.\n\n* fix: use always-rendered ''settings'' link to verify home page, fix duplicate theme toggle\n\n- auth-client, logout, org-switcher: replace Identity Status (conditional on session data) with ''settings'' link (always in header)\n- theme: add .first() to resolve strict mode violation from duplicate aria-label buttons\n\n* tenancy\n\n* lint\n\n* add tenant config\n\n* feat: relayer-aware FastKV publish for tenant creation\n\nFall back to a direct transaction (signed by the user''s wallet as the new\nsubaccount) when the relayer is not configured, keeping the delegate-action +\nrelay path when it is. Update the tenant creation changeset accordingly.\n\n* fix: make tenant creation atomic with DB-middle flow\n\nReorders the tenant creation mutation so the DB row is inserted before\nthe NEAR subaccount is created, eliminating orphaned on-chain subaccounts\nwhen later steps fail.\n\n- Insert tenant in ''pending'' status after org creation\n- Create NEAR subaccount, rollback org + delete DB row on failure\n- Activate tenant (status -> ''active'') after subaccount succeeds\n- Fix createTenant orgId bug: use input.orgId instead of context''s\n  active organization id; drop requireOrganization since the org is\n  created within the same flow\n- Add ''pending'' to tenant_status enum + migration\n- Allow updateTenant to set accountId and status\n- Exclude ''pending'' (transient) from config republish status\n\n* feat: plugin connectSrc config field for host CSP whitelisting\n\n* lint\n\n* tenant order\n\n* lint\n\n* typecheck utils\n\n* fix: provision postgres-template for regression and report truthful API health\n\nThe regression suite failed with 503 on every /api/* route because the\ntemplate plugin''s database was unreachable: CI only provisioned postgres\nfor api (5432) and auth (5433), but the harness forces\nTEMPLATE_DATABASE_URL to 127.0.0.1:5434. When the template plugin fails,\nthe API plugin''s initialize (plugins.template()) fails too, leaving the\nAPI router null.\n\n- Add postgres-template service (5434) to the CI regression job\n- Report degraded/failed status from /api/_health when the API plugin\n  is not mounted, instead of the hardcoded \"ready\" that masked the issue\n\n* feat: guard template client usage and improve typecheck diagnostics\n\n- Guard thing routes against a missing template client instead of\n  throwing a non-serializable error\n- Skip live stream when template plugin is absent\n- Improve typecheck integration diagnostics for non-zero exits\n- Regenerate .env.example from configured bos secrets\n\n* fix: generate optional PluginsClient properties for unresolved dependsOn\n\nWhen api.dependsOn references a plugin not registered in the config,\nwritePluginClientGen now generates an optional property with a generic\nClientFactory<AnyContractRouter> signature instead of silently dropping\nthe dependency. This lets API entry points use optional chaining\n(plugins.key?.()) without TS18048/TS2722 errors in projects with\nnoUncheckedIndexedAccess: true.\n\nRemoves the unsafe Partial cast in api/src/index.ts now that PluginsClient\naccurately models unresolved deps as optional.\n\n* feat: route things through template plugin and drop api proxy\n\nRemove the things CRUD routes from the parent api contract and router\n(they now live in plugins/_template), drop the api dependsOn template\nwiring in bos.config.json, and point the UI at the namespaced\napiClient.template.* client instead of the removed top-level methods.\n\nThe template plugin''s createThing/deleteThing handlers now use the\nrequireAuth middleware instead of manual context.userId checks.\n\nUpdate the init integration tests to scaffold the template plugin\n(with pluginDirMap mapping template -> _template so its files are\ncopied) and remove the superseded no-apps variant.\n\n* fix: drop requireAuth from template things and keep api proxy\n\nThe template plugin''s createThing/deleteThing no longer enforce auth\nthemselves; auth stays at the API boundary so in-process plugin client\ncalls don''t fail with a 401 due to empty auth context. Updates the\nchangesets to match the final proxy behavior.\n\n* chore: ignore .bos/sync-backup directory","tree":{"sha":"54a4b3971ecccad67b8806eb0dd17224a78bf9a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/trees/54a4b3971ecccad67b8806eb0dd17224a78bf9a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NEARBuilders/everything-dev/git/commits/ada1cd236e219f75e62eb98b559d8c5feb361f98","verification":{"payload":"tree 54a4b3971ecccad67b8806eb0dd17224a78bf9a5\nparent d456e6d718adb382f1711be19b5a7e2a2e1e8255\nauthor Elliot Braem <elliot@ejlbraem.com> 1786470444 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786470444 -0500\n\nfix: make tenant creation atomic with DB-middle flow (#227)\n\n* feat: tenant lifecycle with status gating and tenant detail UI\n\nAdd a full tenant lifecycle across the API, host, and UI:\n\n- API: extend tenants table with status/updated_at/deleted_at (soft-delete),\n  add update/softDelete/suspend/reactivate, resolveTenantByOrgId, and\n  tenantPreflight routes; listTenants uses requireAuth consistently\n- Host: gate tenant resolution on a published config status field\n  (suspended -> 503, pending_deletion -> 410) without an API round-trip\n- UI: add tenant detail/edit/suspend/delete page that republishes the tenant\n  config with the matching status; fix accountId fallback and drop the\n  wikiAccountId org coupling in the creation flow and orgs list\n- everything-dev: allow optional status in BosConfigInput\n- template plugin: move things CRUD to a DB-backed demonstration\n\n* fix: republish config on tenant edits, add preflight and retry publish\n\n* feat: remove _viewer, add testError surface, and regression tests for error/security responses\n\nRemove _viewer paths/CSP conditionals from host, add structured testError route to core API and template plugin, and add regression tests verifying error response shapes, security headers, CSRF protection, body-size limiting, and rate limiting.\n\n* feat: append template thing routes to API router via plugin client passthrough\n\nAdd createThing/getThing/listThings/deleteThing to API contract and delegate to template plugin via _plugins.template(). Route with requireAuth, restoring /api/things surface at the host.\n\nUpdate regression tests to match template plugin''s ThingSchema response shape.\n\nAdd router composition section (Phase 1.7) to oRPC V2 migration plan.\n\n* fix: make getThing/listThings public, remove requireAuth; fix test body shapes\n\nOnly createThing/deleteThing require auth (writes are gated). getThing/listThings are public reads matching the template plugin''s behavior.\n\nFix auth_api_key_flow_test.go: pluginId→thingId body shape, remove pluginId from response assertions (match ThingSchema/CreatedThingSchema).\n\n* fix: standalone plugin dev servers load dependsOn siblings, fix test type errors\n\n- Set BOS_RUNTIME_CONFIG env for all dev processes (not just host)\n- dev-server-middleware reads BOS_RUNTIME_CONFIG, registers local sibling deps,\n  loads them with retry, and passes client factories as 3rd arg to usePlugin\n- bos.config.json: add dependsOn: [\"template\"] to api entry\n- Fix scope-lifecycle.test.ts: createRouter returns contract shape, createClient() without args\n\n* feat: migrate template plugin regression tests to Docker Postgres\n\n- Add postgres-template container to docker-compose.yml (port 5434)\n- Set TEMPLATE_DATABASE_URL in regression test harness env\n- Auto-create things table in DatabaseLive Postgres path (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS)\n- Add TruncateThings() cleanup before each test run via docker exec\n- Eliminates PGlite in-memory state persistence issues between test runs\n\n* fix: add TEMPLATE_DATABASE_URL to template plugin secrets in bos.config.json\n\nRequired for the host to pass the env var to the template plugin''s initialize, enabling Postgres in regression tests and production.\n\n* fix: remove redundant auto-DDL from template DatabaseLive\n\nThe template already has a migration system (unplugin-drizzle-orm-migrations) that creates tables on init. My pool.query CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS was running before the migration, causing the migration''s CREATE TABLE (without IF NOT EXISTS) to fail with ''relation already exists''.\n\n* fix: drop template tables before server start instead of wiping after\n\nMigration runs during plugin init at startup — cleanup was too late (post-server-ready). Now DROP TABLE IF EXISTS things, drizzle_migrations CASCADE before bos dev starts, giving the migration system a clean slate.\n\n* fix: propagate api.dependsOn to RuntimeConfig and fix broken browser test selectors\n\n- config.ts: add dependsOn to result.api in buildRuntimeConfig\n- types.ts: extend ApiPluginConfigSchema with dependsOn, use it in BosConfig.app.api\n- app-load.spec.ts: replace fictional ''open assistant'' test with real /about → /skill navigation\n- auth-client.spec.ts: fix ''Workspace'' selector (was inside h1, now sibling div) and fix ''Settings'' case mismatch\n\n* fix: use ''Identity Status'' instead of ''Workspace'' for home page verification\n\nWorkspace text exists in the header div but was not found by Playwright after anonymous sign-in. Identity Status renders inside the user-loaded card, confirming session data actually resolved.\n\n* fix: use always-rendered ''settings'' link to verify home page, fix duplicate theme toggle\n\n- auth-client, logout, org-switcher: replace Identity Status (conditional on session data) with ''settings'' link (always in header)\n- theme: add .first() to resolve strict mode violation from duplicate aria-label buttons\n\n* tenancy\n\n* lint\n\n* add tenant config\n\n* feat: relayer-aware FastKV publish for tenant creation\n\nFall back to a direct transaction (signed by the user''s wallet as the new\nsubaccount) when the relayer is not configured, keeping the delegate-action +\nrelay path when it is. Update the tenant creation changeset accordingly.\n\n* fix: make tenant creation atomic with DB-middle flow\n\nReorders the tenant creation mutation so the DB row is inserted before\nthe NEAR subaccount is created, eliminating orphaned on-chain subaccounts\nwhen later steps fail.\n\n- Insert tenant in ''pending'' status after org creation\n- Create NEAR subaccount, rollback org + delete DB row on failure\n- Activate tenant (status -> ''active'') after subaccount succeeds\n- Fix createTenant orgId bug: use input.orgId instead of context''s\n  active organization id; drop requireOrganization since the org is\n  created within the same flow\n- Add ''pending'' to tenant_status enum + migration\n- Allow updateTenant to set accountId and status\n- Exclude ''pending'' (transient) from config republish status\n\n* feat: plugin connectSrc config field for host CSP whitelisting\n\n* lint\n\n* tenant order\n\n* lint\n\n* typecheck utils\n\n* fix: provision postgres-template for regression and report truthful API health\n\nThe regression suite failed with 503 on every /api/* route because the\ntemplate plugin''s database was unreachable: CI only provisioned postgres\nfor api (5432) and auth (5433), but the harness forces\nTEMPLATE_DATABASE_URL to 127.0.0.1:5434. When the template plugin fails,\nthe API plugin''s initialize (plugins.template()) fails too, leaving the\nAPI router null.\n\n- Add postgres-template service (5434) to the CI regression job\n- Report degraded/failed status from /api/_health when the API plugin\n  is not mounted, instead of the hardcoded \"ready\" that masked the issue\n\n* feat: guard template client usage and improve typecheck diagnostics\n\n- Guard thing routes against a missing template client instead of\n  throwing a non-serializable error\n- Skip live stream when template plugin is absent\n- Improve typecheck integration diagnostics for non-zero exits\n- Regenerate .env.example from configured bos secrets\n\n* fix: generate optional PluginsClient properties for unresolved dependsOn\n\nWhen api.dependsOn references a plugin not registered in the config,\nwritePluginClientGen now generates an optional property with a generic\nClientFactory<AnyContractRouter> signature instead of silently dropping\nthe dependency. This lets API entry points use optional chaining\n(plugins.key?.()) without TS18048/TS2722 errors in projects with\nnoUncheckedIndexedAccess: true.\n\nRemoves the unsafe Partial cast in api/src/index.ts now that PluginsClient\naccurately models unresolved deps as optional.\n\n* feat: route things through template plugin and drop api proxy\n\nRemove the things CRUD routes from the parent api contract and router\n(they now live in plugins/_template), drop the api dependsOn template\nwiring in bos.config.json, and point the UI at the namespaced\napiClient.template.* client instead of the removed top-level methods.\n\nThe template plugin''s createThing/deleteThing handlers now use the\nrequireAuth middleware instead of manual context.userId checks.\n\nUpdate the init integration tests to scaffold the template plugin\n(with pluginDirMap mapping template -> _template so its files are\ncopied) and remove the superseded no-apps variant.\n\n* fix: drop requireAuth from template things and keep api proxy\n\nThe template plugin''s createThing/deleteThing no longer enforce auth\nthemselves; auth stays at the API boundary so in-process plugin client\ncalls don''t fail with a 401 due to empty auth context. Updates the\nchangesets to match the final proxy behavior.\n\n* chore: ignore .bos/sync-backup directory","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqe2AsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkHAQAHnX7PWAX4ejWkvlEUBpmR2N\nWp8x79p+QwzTjB324cYvwaWUUSesY6DTOxd1/0jQ5jKG/ckC+Ur0GMPh05G7n/pv\npFvn52bOpejGwHwc+kNxg+XzsIevpZ98EFEX6+Xpwfh/WnL/LR+lQAK1rirGxYRW\nlm0yWFIt1FXoCSe/T9de6BFG4TBfouVbOrDhkfcIjuC+nDpSuEtXO5Tz565l5fLr\n1pbLc80gavqp83y10sAmHKxgMrbd2cEeyoZGP963SQOmrNp75Xc3kDxQZBswVzmn\n0MMVeqRpEVgojQvNBHdnla+XYTUYkaHpuvEmwR1s4THa0XENh5zVCtJRIBTDE7H3\nCM4ewZO1