nce, exclusions,\ndisabled), auto-assign (confident pick, low-confidence revert, manual\nskip), jev_condition routing (match, provider error, low confidence,\ninvalid config), and unconfigured projects never reaching Jev.\n\nTo make that possible:\n- TaskAutofillConsumer/TaskAutoAssignConsumer gain WithConsumerGroup,\n  mirroring AutomationConsumer, so parallel tests don''t share a group.\n- The automation Jev node now uses the consumer''s HTTP client (SSRF-safe\n  by default), so WithHTTPClient covers its Jev calls like call_api.\n- The e2e harness wires the Jev config service and the autofill\n  provenance repo the way bootstrap does.\n\nPlaywright (apps/e2e/tests/projects/jev.spec.ts + feature file): Settings\n> Jev AI states, saving credentials without exposing the key, stubbed\nconnection test, feature settings persistence, and Jev Condition palette\ngating.\n\nUnit tests: jev.ClientForProject/APIError, agent/project Jev helpers,\nprojectsvc.UpdateJevConfig (trim, encrypt, clear), the jev-config PATCH\nhandler, resolveJevAnswer paths, JevSettings component, useJevEnabled,\nand the Jev project-api calls.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EWTZBUJ3onPz8ZumN5tznU","tree":{"sha":"449855dbadb5e998fa0e669509e61aaeb6044c73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Paca-AI/paca/git/trees/449855dbadb5e998fa0e669509e61aaeb6044c73"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Paca-AI/paca/git/commits/c4e7c4125930c6f6dc09610a2054590e2bd8206e","verification":{"payload":"tree 449855dbadb5e998fa0e669509e61aaeb6044c73\nparent cc3bf31a1cfb4c3a60b2d185458fa8d8c282c5d6\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790233538 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1790233538 +0000\n\ntest(jev): add e2e coverage and fill unit test gaps for Jev integration\n\nAPI e2e (services/api/test/e2e/jev_integration_test.go): drives the real\nHTTP API, Postgres, Valkey streams and the autofill/auto-assign/automation\nworkers against a local fake Jev server — config lifecycle and authz,\nautofill (blank fields, human-set fields, low confidence, exclusions,\ndisabled), auto-assign (confident pick, low-confidence revert, manual\nskip), jev_condition routing (match, provider error, low confidence,\ninvalid config), and unconfigured projects never reaching Jev.\n\nTo make that possible:\n- TaskAutofillConsumer/TaskAutoAssignConsumer gain WithConsumerGroup,\n  mirroring AutomationConsumer, so parallel tests don''t share a group.\n- The automation Jev node now uses the consumer''s HTTP client (SSRF-safe\n  by default), so WithHTTPClient covers its Jev calls like call_api.\n- The e2e harness wires the Jev config service and the autofill\n  provenance repo the way bootstrap does.\n\nPlaywright (apps/e2e/tests/projects/jev.spec.ts + feature file): Settings\n> Jev AI states, saving credentials without exposing the key, stubbed\nconnection test, feature settings persistence, and Jev Condition palette\ngating.\n\nUnit tests: jev.ClientForProject/APIError, agent/project Jev helpers,\nprojectsvc.UpdateJevConfig (trim, encrypt, clear), the jev-config PATCH\nhandler, resolveJevAnswer paths, JevSettings component, useJevEnabled,\nand the Jev project-api calls.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EWTZBUJ3onPz8ZumN5tznU\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO8elSMJ\nQ6SvTxMTzo2SwK310MlWgApXoUPD/EKjcbDIMdBHhU91REzKJ85RSYM8kGxaGWl9Kg8mOK2ZL8+C\nmQo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T07:05:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.githu