pe":"User"},"email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-07T14:51:07Z","committedDate":"2026-08-07T14:57:26Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"matteocodogno","providerType":"User"},"email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:16:37.067Z","repositoryId":1187237340,"sha":"f328f0285239078d6d6d83910be76c0534f26a24"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"matteocodogno","providerType":"User"},"email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-07T14:53:50Z","committedDate":"2026-08-07T14:57:26Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"matteocodogno","providerType":"User"},"email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:16:37.067Z","repositoryId":1187237340,"sha":"4c3054b314fa26c16eaf2d7e4eeda8cfa208d458"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"matteocodogno","providerType":"User"},"email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-07T14:45:01Z","committedDate":"2026-08-07T14:45:01Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"matteocodogno","providerType":"User"},"email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:16:37.067Z","repositoryId":1187237340,"sha":"b99cd0dc8294f5e603e6a7cace0ae688e25465d0"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T22:16:37.067Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/81f700e6c9bece424c7c927029f51651ead43b58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T09:40:42Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T09:40:42Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"feat(refund-api): lay the archive PDF out as a document, print-adapted\n\nThe page was nine stacked label-value lines followed by three stacked\nsentences per expense. Nothing could be scanned, rows could not be compared,\nand the total was the least prominent number on a page whose reason for\nexisting is that total.\n\nLetterhead with the issuing entity and a brand rule; title block with the\nstatus as a chip rather than a \"Status:\" text row; the metadata split into two\ngrouped columns (Request / Processing), which halves its height and gives the\nreader two questions to choose between instead of nine identical shapes.\n\nThe expenses are a real table — #, Date, Description, Detail, Requested,\nApproved — with a ruled header, hairline row separators, and both money\ncolumns right-aligned. The rate breakdown moves to the Detail column at\nlabel.small in grey: it explains how an amount was reached, it is not a figure\nanyone sums, and at body weight it competed with the money.\n\nThe total is now the most prominent figure: bold, under a brand rule, in the\nsame columns as the lines above it, with the kilometre total beside it as a\ncross-check the reader can actually perform. It is summed from the LINES this\ndocument printed rather than from `input.subtotals` — the two agree by\nconstruction, but summing what is on the page means the total can never\ndisagree with the figures it totals, which is the one thing checked by hand.\nA multi-currency request repeats that whole block per currency, so the\n\"special case\" is the same block twice and never a grand total across them.\n\nReceipts move into a framed note under the table, listed by filename and the\npage a reader turns to. Those page numbers are computed from each receipt''s\nreal page span before any is appended, because a reference that is present but\nwrong is worse than none.\n\nColour is an accent, never a carrier. Every one of these will be printed or\nphotocopied in monochrome, so the status chip states its own word, the total is\ndistinguished by weight and a rule, and no figure is told apart by colour.\n\nASSET GAP, isolated rather than faked. The brand kit specifies Ubuntu\n(Light/Medium/Regular), Noto Serif for prose and `wordmark-red.svg`; none of\nthose files exist in this repository — `src/batches/fonts/` holds only NotoSans\nRegular and Bold and there is no brand asset directory. `documentTheme.ts`\ntherefore exposes ROLES (title/label/value/prose), all resolving to Noto Sans\ntoday, with the three-step swap documented at the top. The wordmark is drawn as\nbrand-red type, a visible placeholder rather than a silent omission.\n\nTabular figures needed no OpenType feature — which is fortunate, since pdf-lib\ncannot apply one. Noto Sans''s lining figures are already tabular: all ten\ndigits measure 5.72pt at size 10, verified before relying on it. Any\nreplacement face must have the same property natively.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"cd406970ec9b1ecd4c6836d5ee2b61302f9e0c12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/cd406970ec9b1ecd4c6836d5ee2b61302f9e0c12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/81f700e6c9bece424c7c927029f51651ead43b58","verification":{"payload":"tree cd406970ec9b1ecd4c6836d5ee2b61302f9e0c12\nparent a1f78cd4fc7c6bd788e2299ec01b3290180e23d6\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788946842 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788946842 +0200\n\nfeat(refund-api): lay the archive PDF out as a document, print-adapted\n\nThe page was nine stacked label-value lines followed by three stacked\nsentences per expense. Nothing could be scanned, rows could not be compared,\nand the total was the least prominent number on a page whose reason for\nexisting is that total.\n\nLetterhead with the issuing entity and a brand rule; title block with the\nstatus as a chip rather than a \"Status:\" text row; the metadata split into two\ngrouped columns (Request / Processing), which halves its height and gives the\nreader two questions to choose between instead of nine identical shapes.\n\nThe expenses are a real table — #, Date, Description, Detail, Requested,\nApproved — with a ruled header, hairline row separators, and both money\ncolumns right-aligned. The rate breakdown moves to the Detail column at\nlabel.small in grey: it explains how an amount was reached, it is not a figure\nanyone sums, and at body weight it competed with the money.\n\nThe total is now the most prominent figure: bold, under a brand rule, in the\nsame columns as the lines above it, with the kilometre total beside it as a\ncross-check the reader can actually perform. It is summed from the LINES this\ndocument printed rather than from `input.subtotals` — the two agree by\nconstruction, but summing what is on the page means the total can never\ndisagree with the figures it totals, which is the one thing checked by hand.\nA multi-currency request repeats that whole block per currency, so the\n\"special case\" is the same block twice and never a grand total across them.\n\nReceipts move into a framed note under the table, listed by filename and the\npage a reader turns to. Those page numbers are computed from each receipt''s\nreal page span before any is appended, because a reference that is present but\nwrong is worse than none.\n\nColour is an accent, never a carrier. Every one of these will be printed or\nphotocopied in monochrome, so the status chip states its own word, the total is\ndistinguished by weight and a rule, and no figure is told apart by colour.\n\nASSET GAP, isolated rather than faked. The brand kit specifies Ubuntu\n(Light/Medium/Regular), Noto Serif for prose and `wordmark-red.svg`; none of\nthose files exist in this repository — `src/batches/fonts/` holds only NotoSans\nRegular and Bold and there is no brand asset directory. `documentTheme.ts`\ntherefore exposes ROLES (title/label/value/prose), all resolving to Noto Sans\ntoday, with the three-step swap documented at the top. The wordmark is drawn as\nbrand-red type, a visible placeholder rather than a silent omission.\n\nTabular figures needed no OpenType feature — which is fortunate, since pdf-lib\ncannot apply one. Noto Sans''s lining figures are already tabular: all ten\ndigits measure 5.72pt at size 10, verified before relying on it. Any\nreplacement face must have the same property natively.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAIsRokHuuwn615+BUZ/EiRrlTnQzyZf4aeaeybTSSKq+KJ9NLm7+uBCGwAUB0DaqB\nZulZ/m8DdQU3cm3PoqBgM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/81f700e6c9bece424c7c927029f51651ead43b58","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKDgxZjcwMGU2YzliZWNlNDI0YzdjOTI3MDI5ZjUxNjUxZWFkNDNiNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/a1f78cd4fc7c6bd788e2299ec01b3290180e23d6","sha":"a1f78cd4fc7c6bd788e2299ec01b3290180e23d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/a1f78cd4fc7c6bd788e2299ec01b3290180e23d6"}],"sha":"81f700e6c9bece424c7c927029f51651ead43b58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/81f700e6c9bece424c7c927029f51651ead43b58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/a1f78cd4fc7c6bd788e2299ec01b3290180e23d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T09:12:56Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T09:12:56Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"fix(refund): name the people, letterhead the page, and fix the non-uniform cases\n\nEmployee, decider and exporter were bare addresses. They now read \"Luigi\nGambardella (luigi.gambardella@welld.ch)\", mirroring refund-ui''s ownerDisplay:\na document a human reads and files should lead with the human. The decider''s\nname is a SNAPSHOT taken at decision time (a new decidedByName column,\nmirroring the existing ownerName) rather than resolved live — an archived PDF''s\ncontents must not change because that person''s record later did. Rows decided\nbefore the column existed fall back to the address. The exporter''s name comes\nfrom the `name` claim already on every token, simply never surfaced by\njwt.middleware until now; it is read for DISPLAY only, never identity.\n\nStatus and Settlement both led with \"Approved\" on consecutive lines. The\nsettlement line now states only the settlement.\n\nThe header assumed uniformity a request need not have. Rendering a mixed one\nshowed the totals were already correct — one row per currency, no grand total —\nbut the entity field listed both, which invites the reader to treat one as THE\nentity when per-line entity is what drives ABAC scope and which establishment\nbooks the cost. It now says \"Multiple — see each line\". The period widens to\n\"August to September 2026\" (a dash between two month-years reads as subtraction\non a page of figures), and the totals heading names itself per-currency when\nthere is more than one.\n\nRejected requests are exportable, per an ADR-0043 amendment. Grouping rejected\nwith draft/submitted was wrong: those are still moving, rejected is terminal,\nand it is the document a disputing employee most needs. The motivation renders\nABOVE the figures — on a refusal it is the content, not a footnote — and is\nword-wrapped against the real font rather than a guessed character count.\n\nReading that document then found a genuine defect: every line said \"Approved\n206,50 CHF\" while the totals said \"Approved —\". `PUT .../approved-total` works\nwhile a request is still submitted, so a reviewer can set line totals and then\nreject, and the leftovers rendered as approved money on a refused claim. A\nrejected export now shows no approved figure anywhere.\n\nThe page carries the issuing company''s letterhead — legal name, registered seat\nand tax identifier, selected from the request''s entity. Only the REGISTERED\nseat, not the operational offices: a letterhead identifies the issuer, it is\nnot a directory. A mixed request takes the Swiss headquarters, since the\nItalian establishment is a branch of it.\n\nPDF/A was considered and deliberately declined, with the reasoning and an\nescalation trigger recorded in ADR-0043. It is not adoptable while receipts are\ncopied PAGES: an arbitrary user-uploaded receipt routinely lacks embedded\nfonts, which breaks conformance for the whole file and cannot be fixed from our\nside. PDF/A-3b with receipts as embedded FILES is the named path. A document\nthat claims PDF/A and fails validation is worse than one claiming nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"ef5c26ebe82d59740571c018096da88957f8e1cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/ef5c26ebe82d59740571c018096da88957f8e1cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/a1f78cd4fc7c6bd788e2299ec01b3290180e23d6","verification":{"payload":"tree ef5c26ebe82d59740571c018096da88957f8e1cc\nparent 7f29ff7f7597cfd4d4575b3700f6be3bb7f88e2d\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788945176 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788945176 +0200\n\nfix(refund): name the people, letterhead the page, and fix the non-uniform cases\n\nEmployee, decider and exporter were bare addresses. They now read \"Luigi\nGambardella (luigi.gambardella@welld.ch)\", mirroring refund-ui''s ownerDisplay:\na document a human reads and files should lead with the human. The decider''s\nname is a SNAPSHOT taken at decision time (a new decidedByName column,\nmirroring the existing ownerName) rather than resolved live — an archived PDF''s\ncontents must not change because that person''s record later did. Rows decided\nbefore the column existed fall back to the address. The exporter''s name comes\nfrom the `name` claim already on every token, simply never surfaced by\njwt.middleware until now; it is read for DISPLAY only, never identity.\n\nStatus and Settlement both led with \"Approved\" on consecutive lines. The\nsettlement line now states only the settlement.\n\nThe header assumed uniformity a request need not have. Rendering a mixed one\nshowed the totals were already correct — one row per currency, no grand total —\nbut the entity field listed both, which invites the reader to treat one as THE\nentity when per-line entity is what drives ABAC scope and which establishment\nbooks the cost. It now says \"Multiple — see each line\". The period widens to\n\"August to September 2026\" (a dash between two month-years reads as subtraction\non a page of figures), and the totals heading names itself per-currency when\nthere is more than one.\n\nRejected requests are exportable, per an ADR-0043 amendment. Grouping rejected\nwith draft/submitted was wrong: those are still moving, rejected is terminal,\nand it is the document a disputing employee most needs. The motivation renders\nABOVE the figures — on a refusal it is the content, not a footnote — and is\nword-wrapped against the real font rather than a guessed character count.\n\nReading that document then found a genuine defect: every line said \"Approved\n206,50 CHF\" while the totals said \"Approved —\". `PUT .../approved-total` works\nwhile a request is still submitted, so a reviewer can set line totals and then\nreject, and the leftovers rendered as approved money on a refused claim. A\nrejected export now shows no approved figure anywhere.\n\nThe page carries the issuing company''s letterhead — legal name, registered seat\nand tax identifier, selected from the request''s entity. Only the REGISTERED\nseat, not the operational offices: a letterhead identifies the issuer, it is\nnot a directory. A mixed request takes the Swiss headquarters, since the\nItalian establishment is a branch of it.\n\nPDF/A was considered and deliberately declined, with the reasoning and an\nescalation trigger recorded in ADR-0043. It is not adoptable while receipts are\ncopied PAGES: an arbitrary user-uploaded receipt routinely lacks embedded\nfonts, which breaks conformance for the whole file and cannot be fixed from our\nside. PDF/A-3b with receipts as embedded FILES is the named path. A document\nthat claims PDF/A and fails validation is worse than one claiming nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKKm70SRb1eBTqcssHRM1pUe/BenqskOLw08yS5h+gZz30W0ybYAG6t0jCFV/90mm/\nP6NF0v0xWuIazfO5e3AAo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/a1f78cd4fc7c6bd788e2299ec01b3290180e23d6","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKGExZjc4Y2Q0ZmM3YzZiZDc4OGUyMjk5ZWMwMWIzMjkwMTgwZTIzZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/7f29ff7f7597cfd4d4575b3700f6be3bb7f88e2d","sha":"7f29ff7f7597cfd4d4575b3700f6be3bb7f88e2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/7f29ff7f7597cfd4d4575b3700f6be3bb7f88e2d"}],"sha":"a1f78cd4fc7c6bd788e2299ec01b3290180e23d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/a1f78cd4fc7c6bd788e2299ec01b3290180e23d6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/7f29ff7f7597cfd4d4575b3700f6be3bb7f88e2d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T20:16:43Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T20:16:43Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"fix(refund): make the request archive PDF read as a document\n\nFindings from reading an actual exported file, not the code.\n\nRaw enums were reaching the page — a line read \"travel_km — welld_ch\" and the\nheader \"Status: approved\" while the screen beside it said \"Travel — mileage\n(km)\", \"WellD CH\" and \"Approved\". Those are database values in an accounting\nartifact, and they broke CLAUDE.md''s no-hardcoded-UI-strings rule too, since a\nPDF is UI. Labels now come from `document-labels.json`, which refund-api and\nrefund-ui each assert against in their own suite. The table is duplicated\nrather than imported because the two packages are deliberately not npm-linked\n(CLAUDE.md ### Git) — the same mirroring ADR-0025 already uses for money\nvectors, and each side fails its own tests on drift.\n\nOne locale, in `documentFormat.ts`. The page mixed comma decimals for amounts,\na dot decimal for the rate (interpolated straight from the wire string) and a\nraw ISO date for the rate''s validity. Currency moved after the amount to match\nthe UI; both forms are defensible in isolation, so the tie-break is that a\nreader comparing PDF to screen should not have to notice a difference.\n\nTimestamps were raw ISO with milliseconds in UTC — a log line. Now civil time\nwith the zone named: 08.09.2026 08:45 (CEST). The zone is not decoration: UTC\nrendering silently moves the DATE for anything stamped late local evening,\nwhich on an audit artifact is not cosmetic. Europe/Zurich serves both entities\nsince Rome and Zurich share CET/CEST, so no entity had to be chosen over the\nother.\n\nSettlement is stated. An approved request and a paid one produced identical\npages, and \"is this a liability or is it settled?\" is the first question a\nrecipient asks. The line distinguishes no batch, compiled-not-paid, and paid.\n\nReceipts are stated once: per line only when the request has any, globally\nonly in the zero case. They were already embedded — the reviewed file simply\nhad none.\n\nHeader names the period and entity, both derived from LINE dates so a request\nfiled in September for an August trip still files under August. Every page\ncarries the reference and \"Page N of M\", copied receipt pages included: a\nstapled set where half the pages are unnumbered is the one that loses a page\nunnoticed.\n\nLanguage stayed English as an explicit decision, not a default — refund-ui''s\nexpenseTypes.ts already carries `labelIt` from the original paper form, so\nswitching is a column in the JSON, not a rewrite.\n\nThe ToUnicode text extractor moves from batches/pdf.test.ts to\ntest-support/pdfText.ts so both PDF suites share it — these renderers embed\nSUBSET fonts, so a naive string match against the file bytes would pass\nregardless of what the page actually says.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"99fd320e17688a10d802b36530baf131da01f74b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/99fd320e17688a10d802b36530baf131da01f74b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/7f29ff7f7597cfd4d4575b3700f6be3bb7f88e2d","verification":{"payload":"tree 99fd320e17688a10d802b36530baf131da01f74b\nparent cee00a35a5cff823cfbd533df85ec189ecc065b5\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788898603 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788898603 +0200\n\nfix(refund): make the request archive PDF read as a document\n\nFindings from reading an actual exported file, not the code.\n\nRaw enums were reaching the page — a line read \"travel_km — welld_ch\" and the\nheader \"Status: approved\" while the screen beside it said \"Travel — mileage\n(km)\", \"WellD CH\" and \"Approved\". Those are database values in an accounting\nartifact, and they broke CLAUDE.md''s no-hardcoded-UI-strings rule too, since a\nPDF is UI. Labels now come from `document-labels.json`, which refund-api and\nrefund-ui each assert against in their own suite. The table is duplicated\nrather than imported because the two packages are deliberately not npm-linked\n(CLAUDE.md ### Git) — the same mirroring ADR-0025 already uses for money\nvectors, and each side fails its own tests on drift.\n\nOne locale, in `documentFormat.ts`. The page mixed comma decimals for amounts,\na dot decimal for the rate (interpolated straight from the wire string) and a\nraw ISO date for the rate''s validity. Currency moved after the amount to match\nthe UI; both forms are defensible in isolation, so the tie-break is that a\nreader comparing PDF to screen should not have to notice a difference.\n\nTimestamps were raw ISO with milliseconds in UTC — a log line. Now civil time\nwith the zone named: 08.09.2026 08:45 (CEST). The zone is not decoration: UTC\nrendering silently moves the DATE for anything stamped late local evening,\nwhich on an audit artifact is not cosmetic. Europe/Zurich serves both entities\nsince Rome and Zurich share CET/CEST, so no entity had to be chosen over the\nother.\n\nSettlement is stated. An approved request and a paid one produced identical\npages, and \"is this a liability or is it settled?\" is the first question a\nrecipient asks. The line distinguishes no batch, compiled-not-paid, and paid.\n\nReceipts are stated once: per line only when the request has any, globally\nonly in the zero case. They were already embedded — the reviewed file simply\nhad none.\n\nHeader names the period and entity, both derived from LINE dates so a request\nfiled in September for an August trip still files under August. Every page\ncarries the reference and \"Page N of M\", copied receipt pages included: a\nstapled set where half the pages are unnumbered is the one that loses a page\nunnoticed.\n\nLanguage stayed English as an explicit decision, not a default — refund-ui''s\nexpenseTypes.ts already carries `labelIt` from the original paper form, so\nswitching is a column in the JSON, not a rewrite.\n\nThe ToUnicode text extractor moves from batches/pdf.test.ts to\ntest-support/pdfText.ts so both PDF suites share it — these renderers embed\nSUBSET fonts, so a naive string match against the file bytes would pass\nregardless of what the page actually says.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNCHMxss1QRPFFhGFEEuyjcBuhHNt7UDOIapBKhdUQ2OcsG266wzqRXkHtwzALGiQR\nNz6OWJmW2R1Wmr3fXjEgc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/7f29ff7f7597cfd4d4575b3700f6be3bb7f88e2d","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKDdmMjlmZjdmNzU5N2NmZDRkNDU3NWIzNzAwZjZiZTNiYjdmODhlMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/cee00a35a5cff823cfbd533df85ec189ecc065b5","sha":"cee00a35a5cff823cfbd533df85ec189ecc065b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/cee00a35a5cff823cfbd533df85ec189ecc065b5"}],"sha":"7f29ff7f7597cfd4d4575b3700f6be3bb7f88e2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/7f29ff7f7597cfd4d4575b3700f6be3bb7f88e2d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/cee00a35a5cff823cfbd533df85ec189ecc065b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:15:32Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:15:32Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"fix(refund-ui): downgrade the monthly-processing note to a footnote\n\nIt was a bordered, accent-tinted panel with its own accent heading, parked at\nthe bottom of every approved request — the loudest element on the page while\nbeing the least important thing on it. It says the same sentence on every\napproved request forever, carries no figure, and asks nothing of the reader:\nstanding background information, not news.\n\nIt is now muted body text directly under the totals. That placement is the\npoint, not just a smaller version of the old one: the note answers \"when does\nthis figure get paid\", so it is a footnote to the total rather than a banner\nappended after the expense lines it has nothing to do with.\n\nIts \"Monthly processing\" heading is dropped rather than restyled. At body\nweight the sentence introduces itself, and the heading existed only to anchor\nthe panel that no longer surrounds it.\n\nNo spec change is needed: AC-4.1 requires the UI to STATE the monthly cadence\nwithout promising a date or an amount, and the copy is untouched — prominence\nwas never part of the requirement.\n\nThe existing specs only checked the copy carried no date or amount, so a\nregression back to the panel would have passed them all. They now pin the\nweight (muted, no border, no accent, no heading) and the placement (same\nwrapper as the totals, ahead of the lines). Verified by mutation: restoring\nthe old panel fails them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"318453b4e68941f551ec7eb8699e525964a4d5e0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/318453b4e68941f551ec7eb8699e525964a4d5e0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/cee00a35a5cff823cfbd533df85ec189ecc065b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 318453b4e68941f551ec7eb8699e525964a4d5e0\nparent 23d6ffd30ff31af264c9fb89c3bf97e9407a50a0\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788884132 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788884132 +0200\n\nfix(refund-ui): downgrade the monthly-processing note to a footnote\n\nIt was a bordered, accent-tinted panel with its own accent heading, parked at\nthe bottom of every approved request — the loudest element on the page while\nbeing the least important thing on it. It says the same sentence on every\napproved request forever, carries no figure, and asks nothing of the reader:\nstanding background information, not news.\n\nIt is now muted body text directly under the totals. That placement is the\npoint, not just a smaller version of the old one: the note answers \"when does\nthis figure get paid\", so it is a footnote to the total rather than a banner\nappended after the expense lines it has nothing to do with.\n\nIts \"Monthly processing\" heading is dropped rather than restyled. At body\nweight the sentence introduces itself, and the heading existed only to anchor\nthe panel that no longer surrounds it.\n\nNo spec change is needed: AC-4.1 requires the UI to STATE the monthly cadence\nwithout promising a date or an amount, and the copy is untouched — prominence\nwas never part of the requirement.\n\nThe existing specs only checked the copy carried no date or amount, so a\nregression back to the panel would have passed them all. They now pin the\nweight (muted, no border, no accent, no heading) and the placement (same\nwrapper as the totals, ahead of the lines). Verified by mutation: restoring\nthe old panel fails them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNqVrYxiJ8s4QFkozDOJDK2PBokrbsSLY3HjxNf7z3XwhMIYGoSV10ev8SItuyotpE\njMWpOmDiiL7siTwe7lXQU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/cee00a35a5cff823cfbd533df85ec189ecc065b5","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKGNlZTAwYTM1YTVjZmY4MjNjZmJkNTMzZGY4NWVjMTg5ZWNjMDY1YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/23d6ffd30ff31af264c9fb89c3bf97e9407a50a0","sha":"23d6ffd30ff31af264c9fb89c3bf97e9407a50a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/23d6ffd30ff31af264c9fb89c3bf97e9407a50a0"}],"sha":"cee00a35a5cff823cfbd533df85ec189ecc065b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/cee00a35a5cff823cfbd533df85ec189ecc065b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/23d6ffd30ff31af264c9fb89c3bf97e9407a50a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:11:30Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:11:30Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"fix(refund-ui): render amounts as a right-aligned tabular column\n\nEach figure sat inline after its label, inside a wrapping row it shared with\nthe applied-rate pair, so its horizontal position moved with the length of\nwhatever preceded it — a longer type name or a rate note pushed the number\nsomewhere else, and no two rows lined up. An accountant reads a column down\nand checks it sums; there was no column to read.\n\nThe row is now two blocks: everything descriptive on the left, wrapping\nfreely, and the money in a fixed right-hand column with `tabular-nums`. The\ntotals card matches, so the per-line figures and the total they should add up\nto share one right edge.\n\n`tabular-nums` alongside `font-mono` is belt-and-braces and deliberately so.\nDM Mono is a true monospace, so equal digit advance already holds while it\nrenders — but the stack falls back to `monospace`, and where that resolves to\nsomething proportional-ish the column would quietly stop being one. This makes\nthe alignment a property of the markup rather than of which font loaded.\nVerified the utility actually emits `font-variant-numeric` in the built CSS\nrather than being an inert class name a test could pass against.\n\nThe adjustment note moves BENEATH the approved figure rather than staying an\nappended parenthetical: an inline \"(requested …, −…)\" makes each approved\nfigure start at a different x, which destroys the one property the column\nexists for. The figures stay aligned and the adjustment hangs underneath.\n\nThe applied-rate provenance stays on the descriptive side. It explains how an\namount was reached; it is not a figure anyone sums, so it must not sit in the\nmoney column diluting it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"43fb0e034b89132a94660c1b8ff904bc41b26c11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/43fb0e034b89132a94660c1b8ff904bc41b26c11"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/23d6ffd30ff31af264c9fb89c3bf97e9407a50a0","verification":{"payload":"tree 43fb0e034b89132a94660c1b8ff904bc41b26c11\nparent 3aecb6f15e61a03ab3f4f385807e1188ecb51f1a\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788883890 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788883890 +0200\n\nfix(refund-ui): render amounts as a right-aligned tabular column\n\nEach figure sat inline after its label, inside a wrapping row it shared with\nthe applied-rate pair, so its horizontal position moved with the length of\nwhatever preceded it — a longer type name or a rate note pushed the number\nsomewhere else, and no two rows lined up. An accountant reads a column down\nand checks it sums; there was no column to read.\n\nThe row is now two blocks: everything descriptive on the left, wrapping\nfreely, and the money in a fixed right-hand column with `tabular-nums`. The\ntotals card matches, so the per-line figures and the total they should add up\nto share one right edge.\n\n`tabular-nums` alongside `font-mono` is belt-and-braces and deliberately so.\nDM Mono is a true monospace, so equal digit advance already holds while it\nrenders — but the stack falls back to `monospace`, and where that resolves to\nsomething proportional-ish the column would quietly stop being one. This makes\nthe alignment a property of the markup rather than of which font loaded.\nVerified the utility actually emits `font-variant-numeric` in the built CSS\nrather than being an inert class name a test could pass against.\n\nThe adjustment note moves BENEATH the approved figure rather than staying an\nappended parenthetical: an inline \"(requested …, −…)\" makes each approved\nfigure start at a different x, which destroys the one property the column\nexists for. The figures stay aligned and the adjustment hangs underneath.\n\nThe applied-rate provenance stays on the descriptive side. It explains how an\namount was reached; it is not a figure anyone sums, so it must not sit in the\nmoney column diluting it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGNSJQrgPEdXxqJlr6vSFc/v50Jrtyls5yKZaIdwjFXupJMd4V3ahQGkqyyWmdQGf9\nt90NT81g2YokVDrv1b2gY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/23d6ffd30ff31af264c9fb89c3bf97e9407a50a0","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKDIzZDZmZmQzMGZmMzFhZjI2NGM5ZmI4OWMzYmY5N2U5NDA3YTUwYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/3aecb6f15e61a03ab3f4f385807e1188ecb51f1a","sha":"3aecb6f15e61a03ab3f4f385807e1188ecb51f1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/3aecb6f15e61a03ab3f4f385807e1188ecb51f1a"}],"sha":"23d6ffd30ff31af264c9fb89c3bf97e9407a50a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/23d6ffd30ff31af264c9fb89c3bf97e9407a50a0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/3aecb6f15e61a03ab3f4f385807e1188ecb51f1a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:05:15Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T16:05:15Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"fix(refund-ui): show one figure unless accounting adjusted the amount\n\nLine rows and the totals card both printed \"Requested X / Approved X\"\nunconditionally, so a typical request showed six numbers for three distinct\nvalues. The reader had to compare each pair to find the one that differed —\nwhich is the only fact a review screen is scanned for, and it was buried in a\nwall of duplicates.\n\nAn unadjusted amount now shows a single figure. An adjusted one reads\n\"154,00 CHF (requested 180,00, −26,00)\": currency on the approved figure only,\nsince repeating it three times in one phrase is the noise being removed. An\nincrease is signed \"+\" rather than left ambiguous — accounting raising a\nfigure is as notable as cutting one, and an unsigned delta reads as a cut.\n\nThe rule lives in one helper in lib/money.ts, not in either component. A\nper-line row and its own totals card disagreeing about whether an amount moved\nwould be worse than either being wrong alone, and two independent comparisons\nare two chances to drift.\n\nspecs/007''s AC-3.2 is amended rather than quietly contradicted. Its purpose\nclause — \"so they can see exactly where (if anywhere) an amount was adjusted\"\n— is exactly what motivated this; only its literal \"alongside\" mechanism\nchanges, and that mechanism was working against the purpose. Both values\nremain on the wire and in the API contract; this is presentation only.\n\nA null approvedTotalCents stays UNCHANGED, not unknown: refund-api treats an\nuntouched line as approved in full, so rendering it as a change would invent a\ndecision nobody made.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"f109c7ec138106f81c1b506f9ab88d749a4d3bd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/f109c7ec138106f81c1b506f9ab88d749a4d3bd7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/3aecb6f15e61a03ab3f4f385807e1188ecb51f1a","verification":{"payload":"tree f109c7ec138106f81c1b506f9ab88d749a4d3bd7\nparent 42e5f0d32dd11d1c618dec860040f38a011ae48c\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788883515 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788883515 +0200\n\nfix(refund-ui): show one figure unless accounting adjusted the amount\n\nLine rows and the totals card both printed \"Requested X / Approved X\"\nunconditionally, so a typical request showed six numbers for three distinct\nvalues. The reader had to compare each pair to find the one that differed —\nwhich is the only fact a review screen is scanned for, and it was buried in a\nwall of duplicates.\n\nAn unadjusted amount now shows a single figure. An adjusted one reads\n\"154,00 CHF (requested 180,00, −26,00)\": currency on the approved figure only,\nsince repeating it three times in one phrase is the noise being removed. An\nincrease is signed \"+\" rather than left ambiguous — accounting raising a\nfigure is as notable as cutting one, and an unsigned delta reads as a cut.\n\nThe rule lives in one helper in lib/money.ts, not in either component. A\nper-line row and its own totals card disagreeing about whether an amount moved\nwould be worse than either being wrong alone, and two independent comparisons\nare two chances to drift.\n\nspecs/007''s AC-3.2 is amended rather than quietly contradicted. Its purpose\nclause — \"so they can see exactly where (if anywhere) an amount was adjusted\"\n— is exactly what motivated this; only its literal \"alongside\" mechanism\nchanges, and that mechanism was working against the purpose. Both values\nremain on the wire and in the API contract; this is presentation only.\n\nA null approvedTotalCents stays UNCHANGED, not unknown: refund-api treats an\nuntouched line as approved in full, so rendering it as a change would invent a\ndecision nobody made.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHg4tfSTAA49j2Z5Vl8gaA7H8HwpckQ1C/BTDpf+j6NDo2KBp0pqH5UeCdyXiVHodb\nd1T9YbLfXUF92Fwdzwkg0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/3aecb6f15e61a03ab3f4f385807e1188ecb51f1a","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKDNhZWNiNmYxNWU2MWEwM2FiM2Y0ZjM4NTgwN2UxMTg4ZWNiNTFmMWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/42e5f0d32dd11d1c618dec860040f38a011ae48c","sha":"42e5f0d32dd11d1c618dec860040f38a011ae48c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/42e5f0d32dd11d1c618dec860040f38a011ae48c"}],"sha":"3aecb6f15e61a03ab3f4f385807e1188ecb51f1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/3aecb6f15e61a03ab3f4f385807e1188ecb51f1a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/42e5f0d32dd11d1c618dec860040f38a011ae48c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T15:48:47Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T15:48:47Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"fix(refund-ui): state the request''s status on the review detail\n\nThe page communicated status only by omission: an approved request was\nidentifiable by the ABSENCE of the Approve/Reject buttons plus the presence of\nthe monthly-processing note, which asks the reader to notice something that is\nnot there. Two positive signals replace that inference.\n\nA RequestStatusBadge now sits beside the \"Review detail\" heading, so the\ndetail agrees with the queue, which already badges every row.\n\nA decision stamp names who decided the request and when — \"Approved on\n22.08.2026 by chiara.rossi@welld.ch\" — the counterpart to the paid branch''s\nlong-standing \"Paid on X by Y\". Rejected gets the same stamp rather than being\nleft as the next instance of this bug: its motivation block already said WHY,\nnever who or when. A paid request shows both stamps, because the decision and\nthe payout are different events by different people and neither substitutes\nfor the other.\n\nThe stamp renders only when the record carries both halves. \"Approved on\n22.08.2026 by undefined\" would be worse than nothing — it reads as a record\nrather than as a gap.\n\nDate-only, per the requested wording, rather than the paid line''s date+time: a\ndecision is reported by the day it was made, and the exact minute is\nprovenance nobody reads off this screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"d60974fa5f03459daa246eb62bb6dc7543c86c30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/d60974fa5f03459daa246eb62bb6dc7543c86c30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/42e5f0d32dd11d1c618dec860040f38a011ae48c","verification":{"payload":"tree d60974fa5f03459daa246eb62bb6dc7543c86c30\nparent 926c7d9a54054412d29698bde8e227f8302a9da3\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788882527 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788882527 +0200\n\nfix(refund-ui): state the request''s status on the review detail\n\nThe page communicated status only by omission: an approved request was\nidentifiable by the ABSENCE of the Approve/Reject buttons plus the presence of\nthe monthly-processing note, which asks the reader to notice something that is\nnot there. Two positive signals replace that inference.\n\nA RequestStatusBadge now sits beside the \"Review detail\" heading, so the\ndetail agrees with the queue, which already badges every row.\n\nA decision stamp names who decided the request and when — \"Approved on\n22.08.2026 by chiara.rossi@welld.ch\" — the counterpart to the paid branch''s\nlong-standing \"Paid on X by Y\". Rejected gets the same stamp rather than being\nleft as the next instance of this bug: its motivation block already said WHY,\nnever who or when. A paid request shows both stamps, because the decision and\nthe payout are different events by different people and neither substitutes\nfor the other.\n\nThe stamp renders only when the record carries both halves. \"Approved on\n22.08.2026 by undefined\" would be worse than nothing — it reads as a record\nrather than as a gap.\n\nDate-only, per the requested wording, rather than the paid line''s date+time: a\ndecision is reported by the day it was made, and the exact minute is\nprovenance nobody reads off this screen.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNimCQJsYhEaGekcGHtzfl0FE30xfdQ5SIqVSHWuj/TWggXLMOojXZkFz/L3F2kYk7\nMxnHY8YXE22h+MzOAQ4gU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/42e5f0d32dd11d1c618dec860040f38a011ae48c","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKDQyZTVmMGQzMmRkMTFkMWM2MThkZWM4NjAwNDBmMzhhMDExYWU0OGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/926c7d9a54054412d29698bde8e227f8302a9da3","sha":"926c7d9a54054412d29698bde8e227f8302a9da3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/926c7d9a54054412d29698bde8e227f8302a9da3"}],"sha":"42e5f0d32dd11d1c618dec860040f38a011ae48c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/42e5f0d32dd11d1c618dec860040f38a011ae48c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/926c7d9a54054412d29698bde8e227f8302a9da3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T15:42:36Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T15:42:36Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"fix(refund-ui): make the currency and entity chips neutral\n\nGreen was carrying three different jobs on one expense row: the approved\namount, where it encodes a decision, plus the CHF chip and the WellD CH chip,\nwhere it encodes nothing. A reader had to learn which of the three greens\nmeant something. The currency chip additionally spent three more\nmeaning-bearing colours — accent, orange, red — on EUR, USD and GBP, none of\nwhich said anything the ISO code beside them did not.\n\nBoth chips now render in one neutral tone, and every variant of each shares\nit. That is not a loss of signal: the ISO code and the flag-plus-entity-name\nwere always what distinguished the variants, and admin-ui''s ConditionChip\nalready establishes the convention of several chip kinds sharing one colour,\ntold apart by glyph and text. Green is left meaning \"approved\" and the accent\nmeaning \"interactive\".\n\nGreen''s remaining uses were checked rather than assumed — approved/paid\namounts, status badges, success toasts, positive confirms — and all are\nsemantic. Only the two chips named here were decorative.\n\n`--soft`, not `--muted`: measured against the 10% tint the chip paints over\nthe --ink-soft card, --soft is 4.76:1 and --muted 2.60:1. At 11px this is\nnormal-size text, so 4.5:1 is the bar and --muted would have looked more\nneutral while failing it.\n\nThe two specs that asserted \"a different colour per variant\" encoded the old\nintent, so they are replaced rather than patched: they now pin one shared\nneutral, plus a new assertion that no chip may claim --grn or --acc at all —\nwhich is the rule this change actually establishes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"861b64ed6f99b11a7c69bdf8acfaa057537c504b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/861b64ed6f99b11a7c69bdf8acfaa057537c504b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/926c7d9a54054412d29698bde8e227f8302a9da3","verification":{"payload":"tree 861b64ed6f99b11a7c69bdf8acfaa057537c504b\nparent c0b6b5b85375f818a48485c9770a0b10e2687caf\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788882156 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788882156 +0200\n\nfix(refund-ui): make the currency and entity chips neutral\n\nGreen was carrying three different jobs on one expense row: the approved\namount, where it encodes a decision, plus the CHF chip and the WellD CH chip,\nwhere it encodes nothing. A reader had to learn which of the three greens\nmeant something. The currency chip additionally spent three more\nmeaning-bearing colours — accent, orange, red — on EUR, USD and GBP, none of\nwhich said anything the ISO code beside them did not.\n\nBoth chips now render in one neutral tone, and every variant of each shares\nit. That is not a loss of signal: the ISO code and the flag-plus-entity-name\nwere always what distinguished the variants, and admin-ui''s ConditionChip\nalready establishes the convention of several chip kinds sharing one colour,\ntold apart by glyph and text. Green is left meaning \"approved\" and the accent\nmeaning \"interactive\".\n\nGreen''s remaining uses were checked rather than assumed — approved/paid\namounts, status badges, success toasts, positive confirms — and all are\nsemantic. Only the two chips named here were decorative.\n\n`--soft`, not `--muted`: measured against the 10% tint the chip paints over\nthe --ink-soft card, --soft is 4.76:1 and --muted 2.60:1. At 11px this is\nnormal-size text, so 4.5:1 is the bar and --muted would have looked more\nneutral while failing it.\n\nThe two specs that asserted \"a different colour per variant\" encoded the old\nintent, so they are replaced rather than patched: they now pin one shared\nneutral, plus a new assertion that no chip may claim --grn or --acc at all —\nwhich is the rule this change actually establishes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLI9UUiPnYRCaOmnrEpdb+FMxkJhdt2TYHVFxvx+880Ea+ktKFCDKKyct5S9koO5pl\ngGk1px+ZI/yfsf2Yak+g4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/926c7d9a54054412d29698bde8e227f8302a9da3","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKDkyNmM3ZDlhNTQwNTQ0MTJkMjk2OThiZGU4ZTIyN2Y4MzAyYTlkYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/c0b6b5b85375f818a48485c9770a0b10e2687caf","sha":"c0b6b5b85375f818a48485c9770a0b10e2687caf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/c0b6b5b85375f818a48485c9770a0b10e2687caf"}],"sha":"926c7d9a54054412d29698bde8e227f8302a9da3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/926c7d9a54054412d29698bde8e227f8302a9da3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/c0b6b5b85375f818a48485c9770a0b10e2687caf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T15:33:40Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T15:33:40Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"fix(refund-ui): render every date as DD.MM.YYYY\n\nOne screen could show two date formats at once: expense-line dates printed the\nraw ISO `2026-08-11`, while the applied mileage rate''s validity went through\n`toLocaleDateString(undefined, …)` and came out as `Jan 31, 2021` on a\nUS-locale browser. Neither reads naturally in Switzerland or Italy, which is\nwhere this product''s users are.\n\nBoth converge on the numeric `DD.MM.YYYY` used natively in both markets, and\ntimestamps on `DD.MM.YYYY, HH:mm` — 24-hour, since AM/PM is exactly the\nambiguity this audience does not use.\n\nThe format is now FIXED rather than derived from the viewer''s locale. These\nare dates on a shared financial record: an employee in Italy and an accountant\nin Switzerland discussing the same expense line should read the same\ncharacters, not two renderings that differ by whoever''s browser drew them.\nPinning it also makes tests and screenshots deterministic — the old specs\nasserted only `toContain(''2026'')`, which was the tell that the output varied\nper machine.\n\nA latent off-by-one is fixed on the way. `new Date(''2026-08-11'')` is UTC\nmidnight, so the old code showed 10.08.2026 to any viewer west of UTC. A\ndate-only value is now formatted from its own characters and never parsed at\nall, making it correct by construction rather than by the office''s longitude.\nThat invariant is tested by making the Date constructor throw, not by\nreassigning process.env.TZ mid-run — Node reads TZ once at startup, so the\nobvious version of that test would have passed on every CH/IT and CI machine\nwhile the bug was live. Verified by mutation.\n\nThe two aria-label specs that asserted a raw ISO date are updated rather than\nworked around: the accessible name must carry the same string a sighted reader\nsees, or the two cannot be matched up.\n\n`todayIsoDate` stays ISO — it feeds an `<input type=\"date\">`, whose value is\ndefined by HTML as yyyy-mm-dd regardless of what the browser displays.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"a576c5e218583bb15a563caf840e6e26d5540272","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/a576c5e218583bb15a563caf840e6e26d5540272"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/c0b6b5b85375f818a48485c9770a0b10e2687caf","verification":{"payload":"tree a576c5e218583bb15a563caf840e6e26d5540272\nparent ea73b725fecabba2365c27b5aa606ab26cf1ba56\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788881620 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788881620 +0200\n\nfix(refund-ui): render every date as DD.MM.YYYY\n\nOne screen could show two date formats at once: expense-line dates printed the\nraw ISO `2026-08-11`, while the applied mileage rate''s validity went through\n`toLocaleDateString(undefined, …)` and came out as `Jan 31, 2021` on a\nUS-locale browser. Neither reads naturally in Switzerland or Italy, which is\nwhere this product''s users are.\n\nBoth converge on the numeric `DD.MM.YYYY` used natively in both markets, and\ntimestamps on `DD.MM.YYYY, HH:mm` — 24-hour, since AM/PM is exactly the\nambiguity this audience does not use.\n\nThe format is now FIXED rather than derived from the viewer''s locale. These\nare dates on a shared financial record: an employee in Italy and an accountant\nin Switzerland discussing the same expense line should read the same\ncharacters, not two renderings that differ by whoever''s browser drew them.\nPinning it also makes tests and screenshots deterministic — the old specs\nasserted only `toContain(''2026'')`, which was the tell that the output varied\nper machine.\n\nA latent off-by-one is fixed on the way. `new Date(''2026-08-11'')` is UTC\nmidnight, so the old code showed 10.08.2026 to any viewer west of UTC. A\ndate-only value is now formatted from its own characters and never parsed at\nall, making it correct by construction rather than by the office''s longitude.\nThat invariant is tested by making the Date constructor throw, not by\nreassigning process.env.TZ mid-run — Node reads TZ once at startup, so the\nobvious version of that test would have passed on every CH/IT and CI machine\nwhile the bug was live. Verified by mutation.\n\nThe two aria-label specs that asserted a raw ISO date are updated rather than\nworked around: the accessible name must carry the same string a sighted reader\nsees, or the two cannot be matched up.\n\n`todayIsoDate` stays ISO — it feeds an `<input type=\"date\">`, whose value is\ndefined by HTML as yyyy-mm-dd regardless of what the browser displays.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIt4LT57McfyceoTFNcVnIc+iAKnEi2MsscvlkbO+1p9Ijp4seiVj3rWtyGPsRnO14\npjPvewNB8EdGBNB/WCkA8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/c0b6b5b85375f818a48485c9770a0b10e2687caf","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKGMwYjZiNWI4NTM3NWY4MThhNDg0ODVjOTc3MGEwYjEwZTI2ODdjYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/ea73b725fecabba2365c27b5aa606ab26cf1ba56","sha":"ea73b725fecabba2365c27b5aa606ab26cf1ba56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/ea73b725fecabba2365c27b5aa606ab26cf1ba56"}],"sha":"c0b6b5b85375f818a48485c9770a0b10e2687caf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/c0b6b5b85375f818a48485c9770a0b10e2687caf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/ea73b725fecabba2365c27b5aa606ab26cf1ba56/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T15:22:24Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T15:22:24Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"fix(refund-ui): move the export control into the request header row\n\n\"Export PDF\" shipped between the totals card and the expense-line list, where\nit read as orphaned — it belonged to neither section. It acts on the whole\nrequest, so it now sits in the header row, right-aligned beside the title, as\na secondary action. Both surfaces move: the employee''s request detail (beside\nthe title and status badge) and accounting''s review detail (beside the title,\nabove the \"Requested by\" line).\n\nVisibility is unchanged — approved only, matching the endpoint''s archivable\ngate, so the control still never appears where it would 409.\n\nPlacement is now tested, not just presence. Nothing asserted WHERE the button\nrendered, so this move changed no test and a drift back would have changed\nnone either. Both page specs now pin the DOM relationship: the control is not\ninside the approved body block, and its nearest common ancestor with the\nheading is the header row. Verified by mutation — moving the control back into\nthe body fails the new assertion rather than passing it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"6c39516deb511234a3c369dbc25adda3ffc5866f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/6c39516deb511234a3c369dbc25adda3ffc5866f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/ea73b725fecabba2365c27b5aa606ab26cf1ba56","verification":{"payload":"tree 6c39516deb511234a3c369dbc25adda3ffc5866f\nparent fb42218d94969d220026c99ffc03a07c631d3102\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788880944 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788880944 +0200\n\nfix(refund-ui): move the export control into the request header row\n\n\"Export PDF\" shipped between the totals card and the expense-line list, where\nit read as orphaned — it belonged to neither section. It acts on the whole\nrequest, so it now sits in the header row, right-aligned beside the title, as\na secondary action. Both surfaces move: the employee''s request detail (beside\nthe title and status badge) and accounting''s review detail (beside the title,\nabove the \"Requested by\" line).\n\nVisibility is unchanged — approved only, matching the endpoint''s archivable\ngate, so the control still never appears where it would 409.\n\nPlacement is now tested, not just presence. Nothing asserted WHERE the button\nrendered, so this move changed no test and a drift back would have changed\nnone either. Both page specs now pin the DOM relationship: the control is not\ninside the approved body block, and its nearest common ancestor with the\nheading is the header row. Verified by mutation — moving the control back into\nthe body fails the new assertion rather than passing it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHy9koOumz743pnOTQdzzy5pzRs5EQMi9rR4jrDu7T1aAd7fuX73JJenalKXUIodJ+\nDipxFYjOREFk92k0Lq7QM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/ea73b725fecabba2365c27b5aa606ab26cf1ba56","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKGVhNzNiNzI1ZmVjYWJiYTIzNjVjMjdiNWFhNjA2YWIyNmNmMWJhNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/fb42218d94969d220026c99ffc03a07c631d3102","sha":"fb42218d94969d220026c99ffc03a07c631d3102","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/fb42218d94969d220026c99ffc03a07c631d3102"}],"sha":"ea73b725fecabba2365c27b5aa606ab26cf1ba56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/ea73b725fecabba2365c27b5aa606ab26cf1ba56"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/fb42218d94969d220026c99ffc03a07c631d3102/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:42:33Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T13:42:33Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"feat(refund): export an approved request as a self-contained archive PDF\n\nAccounting must archive approved expense requests. The archive is one PDF\nholding every expense line — with its mileage-rate provenance, which is part\nof the audited record (ADR-0023/0025) — plus every receipt embedded in full: a\nPDF receipt copied page-for-page, a JPEG/PNG embedded as an image.\n\nThis required reversing a documented decision, so it carries ADR-0043.\nADR-0016 built refund-api never to touch receipt bytes, and storage.ts\nreflected that precisely: mint/head/put/delete, and deliberately no read. A\nPDF that embeds receipts cannot be produced without reading them. Composing\nin the browser was the close call and was rejected: the archive is a financial\nrecord of what was approved, so its figures must be the ones refund-api\ncomputed, and moving money formatting and the approved/requested split into\nthe UI would let them drift from ADR-0025 with nothing failing. Listing\nreceipts as links was rejected outright — presigned links expire in ~60s, and\nan archive of dead links is not an archive.\n\nThe reversal is narrower than it looks and is scoped as such. Proxying a file\na client asked for is still forbidden and mintPresignedGet still serves that;\nwhat is now allowed is reading an object to compose a derived document\nrefund-api authors itself — the category ADR-0019''s batch PDF already occupied\nfor writes. getObject says so at the function, and ADR-0043 commits to\nrevisiting rather than quietly extending if a second caller appears.\n\nMemory is bounded explicitly because nothing else bounds it:\nMAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES caps ONE attachment, and attachments-per-request is\nuncapped, so an unbounded export could pull hundreds of MiB into a small\ncontainer. MAX_EXPORT_RECEIPT_BYTES is enforced from the DB''s sizeBytes column\nBEFORE any object is fetched — an oversized request costs one query and a 413,\nnever a partially-downloaded heap.\n\nA receipt that cannot be embedded fails the WHOLE export (502, naming the\nfile) with no placeholder page. This inverts the suite''s usual fail-soft\nposture on purpose: fail-soft degrades a view, which the user is looking at\nand can re-check. This produces an archive, which nobody re-checks — a\ndocument that looks complete and silently isn''t is worse than a refusal,\nbecause a refusal gets fixed.\n\nApproved and paid only (409 otherwise): a draft''s mileage is recomputed on\nevery read and a submitted request has no approved figures, so archiving\neither would freeze a moving target. No new catalog permission — the existing\nread gate is reused via ADR-0042''s reconstructibility test, and every denial\nis 404 so an export route never becomes the place existence leaks.\n\nThe renderer is pure — it takes already-fetched bytes and does no I/O — which\nconfines the ADR-0016 departure to one call site and lets embedding be tested\nwith real PNG/JPEG/PDF bytes and no storage mock. That split matters here:\nbatches.routes.test.ts already mocks ../lib/storage, and bun''s mock.module is\nprocess-global, so a second storage mock would have been order-dependent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"362a5e84731d0538b9d1beb8e6440e9713249d37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/362a5e84731d0538b9d1beb8e6440e9713249d37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/fb42218d94969d220026c99ffc03a07c631d3102","verification":{"payload":"tree 362a5e84731d0538b9d1beb8e6440e9713249d37\nparent ceb22d1badd0bb3116322ed66726fb5ba3c3c295\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788874953 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788874953 +0200\n\nfeat(refund): export an approved request as a self-contained archive PDF\n\nAccounting must archive approved expense requests. The archive is one PDF\nholding every expense line — with its mileage-rate provenance, which is part\nof the audited record (ADR-0023/0025) — plus every receipt embedded in full: a\nPDF receipt copied page-for-page, a JPEG/PNG embedded as an image.\n\nThis required reversing a documented decision, so it carries ADR-0043.\nADR-0016 built refund-api never to touch receipt bytes, and storage.ts\nreflected that precisely: mint/head/put/delete, and deliberately no read. A\nPDF that embeds receipts cannot be produced without reading them. Composing\nin the browser was the close call and was rejected: the archive is a financial\nrecord of what was approved, so its figures must be the ones refund-api\ncomputed, and moving money formatting and the approved/requested split into\nthe UI would let them drift from ADR-0025 with nothing failing. Listing\nreceipts as links was rejected outright — presigned links expire in ~60s, and\nan archive of dead links is not an archive.\n\nThe reversal is narrower than it looks and is scoped as such. Proxying a file\na client asked for is still forbidden and mintPresignedGet still serves that;\nwhat is now allowed is reading an object to compose a derived document\nrefund-api authors itself — the category ADR-0019''s batch PDF already occupied\nfor writes. getObject says so at the function, and ADR-0043 commits to\nrevisiting rather than quietly extending if a second caller appears.\n\nMemory is bounded explicitly because nothing else bounds it:\nMAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES caps ONE attachment, and attachments-per-request is\nuncapped, so an unbounded export could pull hundreds of MiB into a small\ncontainer. MAX_EXPORT_RECEIPT_BYTES is enforced from the DB''s sizeBytes column\nBEFORE any object is fetched — an oversized request costs one query and a 413,\nnever a partially-downloaded heap.\n\nA receipt that cannot be embedded fails the WHOLE export (502, naming the\nfile) with no placeholder page. This inverts the suite''s usual fail-soft\nposture on purpose: fail-soft degrades a view, which the user is looking at\nand can re-check. This produces an archive, which nobody re-checks — a\ndocument that looks complete and silently isn''t is worse than a refusal,\nbecause a refusal gets fixed.\n\nApproved and paid only (409 otherwise): a draft''s mileage is recomputed on\nevery read and a submitted request has no approved figures, so archiving\neither would freeze a moving target. No new catalog permission — the existing\nread gate is reused via ADR-0042''s reconstructibility test, and every denial\nis 404 so an export route never becomes the place existence leaks.\n\nThe renderer is pure — it takes already-fetched bytes and does no I/O — which\nconfines the ADR-0016 departure to one call site and lets embedding be tested\nwith real PNG/JPEG/PDF bytes and no storage mock. That split matters here:\nbatches.routes.test.ts already mocks ../lib/storage, and bun''s mock.module is\nprocess-global, so a second storage mock would have been order-dependent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEcCJQKBUslBiyzCZRYhEQZpZISiWI9/LRCAom/aW+0l0xIx+kVX15LV6uApl/KxJA\nng7JYJn/u/W4WgDljFGgk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/fb42218d94969d220026c99ffc03a07c631d3102","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKGZiNDIyMThkOTQ5NjlkMjIwMDI2Yzk5ZmZjMDNhMDdjNjMxZDMxMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/ceb22d1badd0bb3116322ed66726fb5ba3c3c295","sha":"ceb22d1badd0bb3116322ed66726fb5ba3c3c295","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/ceb22d1badd0bb3116322ed66726fb5ba3c3c295"}],"sha":"fb42218d94969d220026c99ffc03a07c631d3102","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/fb42218d94969d220026c99ffc03a07c631d3102"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/ceb22d1badd0bb3116322ed66726fb5ba3c3c295/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T12:55:13Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T12:55:13Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"feat(refund): email the employee when their expense request is decided\n\nAn approve/reject decision already pushed an in-app notification (AC-3.6,\nADR-0017). It now also sends an email, so the outcome reaches the employee\nwithout them being signed in.\n\nnotify-api gains two templates rather than one with an `outcome` field:\n`refund_decision_approved` carries money, `refund_decision_rejected` does not,\nand splitting them keeps each `data` shape closed and fixed — the property\nemails.schemas.ts exists to enforce. A rejection therefore cannot carry a\nfigure even by mistake, instead of relying on an optional field being left\nunset. Both are English-only, following the refund family rather than the\nbilingual invitation family: an employee has a User row and a suite locale, so\nrendering two languages at them would contradict the app they are about to\nopen.\n\nThe approved mail states the approved total per currency inline (the user''s\ncall), formatted identically to batches/pdf.ts so the mail and the compiled\nPDF read the same. The rejected mail deliberately omits the rejection\nmotivation: that stays behind sign-in rather than being copied into an inbox\nthat may outlive the employee''s access. Both link into the request rather than\nrestating it, the same posture ADR-0021 set for the batch email.\n\nrefund-api sends it post-commit as a SECOND, independent best-effort channel —\nits own function and its own try/catch, not a branch inside the existing\nnotify helper — so an email outage cannot suppress the in-app push, an in-app\noutage cannot suppress the email, and neither can fail or roll back the\ndecision (ADR-0017 §4). Both independence directions are tested, not just\nasserted in a comment.\n\nThe recipient is the request''s `ownerEmail` snapshot, not a live `auth`\nlookup: this is a delivery target for a decision about a request that person\nfiled, and resolving live would put `auth` on the decision path and break the\nmail for a soft-deleted employee who is still owed money.\n\nNo new env var and no new secret — the existing NOTIFY_INTERNAL_TOKEN and\nREFUND_APP_BASE_URL cover it, so tools/env-doctor''s manifest is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"272efa6d950058b9abb530e006822cc42a583ba0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/272efa6d950058b9abb530e006822cc42a583ba0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/ceb22d1badd0bb3116322ed66726fb5ba3c3c295","verification":{"payload":"tree 272efa6d950058b9abb530e006822cc42a583ba0\nparent 34cce3b022a68b78054a861fd44a9adb876d8857\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788872113 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788872113 +0200\n\nfeat(refund): email the employee when their expense request is decided\n\nAn approve/reject decision already pushed an in-app notification (AC-3.6,\nADR-0017). It now also sends an email, so the outcome reaches the employee\nwithout them being signed in.\n\nnotify-api gains two templates rather than one with an `outcome` field:\n`refund_decision_approved` carries money, `refund_decision_rejected` does not,\nand splitting them keeps each `data` shape closed and fixed — the property\nemails.schemas.ts exists to enforce. A rejection therefore cannot carry a\nfigure even by mistake, instead of relying on an optional field being left\nunset. Both are English-only, following the refund family rather than the\nbilingual invitation family: an employee has a User row and a suite locale, so\nrendering two languages at them would contradict the app they are about to\nopen.\n\nThe approved mail states the approved total per currency inline (the user''s\ncall), formatted identically to batches/pdf.ts so the mail and the compiled\nPDF read the same. The rejected mail deliberately omits the rejection\nmotivation: that stays behind sign-in rather than being copied into an inbox\nthat may outlive the employee''s access. Both link into the request rather than\nrestating it, the same posture ADR-0021 set for the batch email.\n\nrefund-api sends it post-commit as a SECOND, independent best-effort channel —\nits own function and its own try/catch, not a branch inside the existing\nnotify helper — so an email outage cannot suppress the in-app push, an in-app\noutage cannot suppress the email, and neither can fail or roll back the\ndecision (ADR-0017 §4). Both independence directions are tested, not just\nasserted in a comment.\n\nThe recipient is the request''s `ownerEmail` snapshot, not a live `auth`\nlookup: this is a delivery target for a decision about a request that person\nfiled, and resolving live would put `auth` on the decision path and break the\nmail for a soft-deleted employee who is still owed money.\n\nNo new env var and no new secret — the existing NOTIFY_INTERNAL_TOKEN and\nREFUND_APP_BASE_URL cover it, so tools/env-doctor''s manifest is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPpE+YPG7lg+J9SCVxD84DRG1lD/QoQvx2FoH/FIQrljGwa+ciL1Sm/nZu2FMxfu1v\nlGksf/ibWWPeidWdwNlQ4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/ceb22d1badd0bb3116322ed66726fb5ba3c3c295","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKGNlYjIyZDFiYWRkMGJiMzExNjMyMmVkNjY3MjZmYjViYTNjM2MyOTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/34cce3b022a68b78054a861fd44a9adb876d8857","sha":"34cce3b022a68b78054a861fd44a9adb876d8857","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/34cce3b022a68b78054a861fd44a9adb876d8857"}],"sha":"ceb22d1badd0bb3116322ed66726fb5ba3c3c295","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/ceb22d1badd0bb3116322ed66726fb5ba3c3c295"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/34cce3b022a68b78054a861fd44a9adb876d8857/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T09:43:29Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T09:43:29Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"fix(refund-api): order the review queue newest-submitted-first\n\nThe accounting review queue was ordered oldest-first (`submittedAt: \"asc\"`, a\nFIFO worklist), which pushed the most recent submissions to the bottom, below\nevery already-approved request still waiting to be pulled into a monthly\nbatch. Accounting works the queue from the newest end, so the order is\nreversed. AC-5.1 asks only for \"enough summary to prioritize\" and pins no\nordering, so no spec amendment is needed.\n\n`nulls: \"last\"` is stated explicitly because flipping the direction silently\nreverses the database default: `submittedAt` is nullable and Postgres sorts a\nDESC column NULLS FIRST, so a timestamp-less row would move from the bottom of\nthe queue to the top. Such a row never reaches a client either way —\n`mapQueueItem` throws on it rather than serializing a lying timestamp — so\nthis is defence in depth at the query layer, and is pinned by a repo-level\ntest rather than a route-level one that would assert a state the service\nrejects by design.\n\nOrdering had no test at all before this, so nothing would have caught a silent\nflip back. Three are added: the newest-first sequence, that submitted and\napproved-not-yet-batched rows interleave by date rather than forming separate\nblocks, and the null-ordering guard.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"b57ccaa1871470993c0462b046f28a645317733d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/b57ccaa1871470993c0462b046f28a645317733d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/34cce3b022a68b78054a861fd44a9adb876d8857","verification":{"payload":"tree b57ccaa1871470993c0462b046f28a645317733d\nparent d733c7b986072f033a55e4aff177a997c1c9cf97\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788860609 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788860609 +0200\n\nfix(refund-api): order the review queue newest-submitted-first\n\nThe accounting review queue was ordered oldest-first (`submittedAt: \"asc\"`, a\nFIFO worklist), which pushed the most recent submissions to the bottom, below\nevery already-approved request still waiting to be pulled into a monthly\nbatch. Accounting works the queue from the newest end, so the order is\nreversed. AC-5.1 asks only for \"enough summary to prioritize\" and pins no\nordering, so no spec amendment is needed.\n\n`nulls: \"last\"` is stated explicitly because flipping the direction silently\nreverses the database default: `submittedAt` is nullable and Postgres sorts a\nDESC column NULLS FIRST, so a timestamp-less row would move from the bottom of\nthe queue to the top. Such a row never reaches a client either way —\n`mapQueueItem` throws on it rather than serializing a lying timestamp — so\nthis is defence in depth at the query layer, and is pinned by a repo-level\ntest rather than a route-level one that would assert a state the service\nrejects by design.\n\nOrdering had no test at all before this, so nothing would have caught a silent\nflip back. Three are added: the newest-first sequence, that submitted and\napproved-not-yet-batched rows interleave by date rather than forming separate\nblocks, and the null-ordering guard.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNtEJC4loE3zbpCM6DFj9nIb06AevLDnwDqIJkJrkphYYKPXy4FcXoGoELWzEyC6P3\nhQMdVpRV36x2HgbJaDVgE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/34cce3b022a68b78054a861fd44a9adb876d8857","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKDM0Y2NlM2IwMjJhNjhiNzgwNTRhODYxZmQ0NGE5YWRiODc2ZDg4NTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/d733c7b986072f033a55e4aff177a997c1c9cf97","sha":"d733c7b986072f033a55e4aff177a997c1c9cf97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/d733c7b986072f033a55e4aff177a997c1c9cf97"}],"sha":"34cce3b022a68b78054a861fd44a9adb876d8857","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/34cce3b022a68b78054a861fd44a9adb876d8857"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/d733c7b986072f033a55e4aff177a997c1c9cf97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:49:36Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T13:49:36Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"fix(refund-ui): stop the CHF currency chip printing its code twice\n\n`CurrencyBadge` renders a decorative symbol beside the ISO code — `€ EUR`,\n`$ USD`, `£ GBP`. The Swiss franc has no single-character sign in common use\n(Swiss practice writes `Fr.`/`SFr.`, and U+20A3 ₣ is the FRENCH franc sign),\nso its symbol slot had been filled with the literal string `CHF`, rendering\nthe chip as \"CHF CHF\" everywhere it appears: the request page''s per-currency\nsubtotal cards, expense line rows, batch subtotals and the mileage amount\nfield.\n\nThe symbol is now optional (`glyph: string | null`) and CHF renders its code\nonce. No symbol is invented to fill the slot — `Fr.` would be a typographic\nchoice, not a fix. The symbol was already `aria-hidden`, so this was purely\nvisual; screen readers always announced just \"CHF\".\n\nTwo specs had PINNED the duplication rather than caught it —\n`CurrencyBadge.test.tsx` and `MileageAmountField.test.tsx` both asserted\n`textContent === ''CHFCHF''` — which is why it shipped. Both now assert the\nopposite, and two invariants that would have caught it originally are added:\nevery variant shows its ISO code as visible text, and no variant repeats its\ncode.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"145079d2f9f61bd20fbcc8eb0a83d3e5ed46432c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/145079d2f9f61bd20fbcc8eb0a83d3e5ed46432c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/d733c7b986072f033a55e4aff177a997c1c9cf97","verification":{"payload":"tree 145079d2f9f61bd20fbcc8eb0a83d3e5ed46432c\nparent cc1e6788fc29973a0a79ae193fc5779c0462f48a\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788529776 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788529776 +0200\n\nfix(refund-ui): stop the CHF currency chip printing its code twice\n\n`CurrencyBadge` renders a decorative symbol beside the ISO code — `€ EUR`,\n`$ USD`, `£ GBP`. The Swiss franc has no single-character sign in common use\n(Swiss practice writes `Fr.`/`SFr.`, and U+20A3 ₣ is the FRENCH franc sign),\nso its symbol slot had been filled with the literal string `CHF`, rendering\nthe chip as \"CHF CHF\" everywhere it appears: the request page''s per-currency\nsubtotal cards, expense line rows, batch subtotals and the mileage amount\nfield.\n\nThe symbol is now optional (`glyph: string | null`) and CHF renders its code\nonce. No symbol is invented to fill the slot — `Fr.` would be a typographic\nchoice, not a fix. The symbol was already `aria-hidden`, so this was purely\nvisual; screen readers always announced just \"CHF\".\n\nTwo specs had PINNED the duplication rather than caught it —\n`CurrencyBadge.test.tsx` and `MileageAmountField.test.tsx` both asserted\n`textContent === ''CHFCHF''` — which is why it shipped. Both now assert the\nopposite, and two invariants that would have caught it originally are added:\nevery variant shows its ISO code as visible text, and no variant repeats its\ncode.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMrQujrXDdlIsGd52A/qS+tEzRG++jcI0Xp5gIT5SHoTs2uUzEmT9I7nFwwgGe5DSy\nzSwPsnzo9uE8oQlWP+zAE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/d733c7b986072f033a55e4aff177a997c1c9cf97","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKGQ3MzNjN2I5ODYwNzJmMDMzYTU1ZTRhZmYxNzdhOTk3YzFjOWNmOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/cc1e6788fc29973a0a79ae193fc5779c0462f48a","sha":"cc1e6788fc29973a0a79ae193fc5779c0462f48a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/cc1e6788fc29973a0a79ae193fc5779c0462f48a"}],"sha":"d733c7b986072f033a55e4aff177a997c1c9cf97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/d733c7b986072f033a55e4aff177a997c1c9cf97"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/cc1e6788fc29973a0a79ae193fc5779c0462f48a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T15:57:32Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T15:57:32Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"fix(auth): make a refused OAuth sign-in diagnosable instead of a 404\n\nA colleague''s Google sign-in bounced to `/?error=unable_to_create_session`,\nwhich rendered as raw Problem JSON (`GET / does not exist`). Two independent\ngaps turned a deliberate refusal into something indistinguishable from a\nbroken OAuth configuration:\n\n1. Better Auth''s default OAuth error destination is `${baseURL}/error`, whose\n   handler 302s to the origin root. This service registers no `GET /`, so the\n   failure landed on `app.notFound` and the reason survived only in a query\n   string. `onAPIError.errorURL` now routes those failures to the hosted\n   sign-in page (ADR-0002), which already renders `?error=<code>` through an\n   XSS-safe allowlist — it simply was never sent anything.\n   `unable_to_create_session` is spelled out as a deactivated account rather\n   than falling through to a generic \"please try again\", which could never\n   have worked: retrying cannot clear a soft-delete gate.\n\n2. `session.create.before` logged nothing on any deny branch. Since Better\n   Auth collapses every branch into the single client-side code\n   `unable_to_create_session` (`callback.mjs` derives it from\n   `result.error.split(\" \").join(\"_\")` when `createSession` resolves to\n   `null`), reading this source file was the only way to tell the branches\n   apart. It now emits a structured `auth.session_denied` event carrying a\n   distinct reason — the same posture and shape as refund-api''s\n   `refund.self_approval_denied` (ADR-0026 point 5), i.e. a security event,\n   not an `AuditLog` state transition. The user id is logged rather than the\n   email, keeping personal data out of log retention (CLAUDE.md \"Data\n   residency\"); the active-user hot path stays silent.\n\nVerified against the pinned better-auth (1.6.23) by replaying\n`handleOAuthUserInfo`''s exact sequence: a brand-new, never-invited identity\nDOES get a session, so only a soft-deleted row can produce this error. That\nboundary is now a shipped test — if the upstream transaction ordering ever\nchanges, every first sign-in in the suite breaks and the test catches it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM","tree":{"sha":"1c58681873783cccb5bc3e292422d29f5d083840","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/1c58681873783cccb5bc3e292422d29f5d083840"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/cc1e6788fc29973a0a79ae193fc5779c0462f48a","verification":{"payload":"tree 1c58681873783cccb5bc3e292422d29f5d083840\nparent 62db4c3f5edc105ba03ad12c90b02459521953a1\nauthor Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788451052 +0200\ncommitter Matteo Codogno <matteo.codogno@welld.ch> 1788451052 +0200\n\nfix(auth): make a refused OAuth sign-in diagnosable instead of a 404\n\nA colleague''s Google sign-in bounced to `/?error=unable_to_create_session`,\nwhich rendered as raw Problem JSON (`GET / does not exist`). Two independent\ngaps turned a deliberate refusal into something indistinguishable from a\nbroken OAuth configuration:\n\n1. Better Auth''s default OAuth error destination is `${baseURL}/error`, whose\n   handler 302s to the origin root. This service registers no `GET /`, so the\n   failure landed on `app.notFound` and the reason survived only in a query\n   string. `onAPIError.errorURL` now routes those failures to the hosted\n   sign-in page (ADR-0002), which already renders `?error=<code>` through an\n   XSS-safe allowlist — it simply was never sent anything.\n   `unable_to_create_session` is spelled out as a deactivated account rather\n   than falling through to a generic \"please try again\", which could never\n   have worked: retrying cannot clear a soft-delete gate.\n\n2. `session.create.before` logged nothing on any deny branch. Since Better\n   Auth collapses every branch into the single client-side code\n   `unable_to_create_session` (`callback.mjs` derives it from\n   `result.error.split(\" \").join(\"_\")` when `createSession` resolves to\n   `null`), reading this source file was the only way to tell the branches\n   apart. It now emits a structured `auth.session_denied` event carrying a\n   distinct reason — the same posture and shape as refund-api''s\n   `refund.self_approval_denied` (ADR-0026 point 5), i.e. a security event,\n   not an `AuditLog` state transition. The user id is logged rather than the\n   email, keeping personal data out of log retention (CLAUDE.md \"Data\n   residency\"); the active-user hot path stays silent.\n\nVerified against the pinned better-auth (1.6.23) by replaying\n`handleOAuthUserInfo`''s exact sequence: a brand-new, never-invited identity\nDOES get a session, so only a soft-deleted row can produce this error. That\nboundary is now a shipped test — if the upstream transaction ordering ever\nchanges, every first sign-in in the suite breaks and the test catches it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ghcXypMCvEXb6FaQFFXBM\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgw7CRdF428nZkqGOk0rwNcWEJW3\n9HLZzON0d3q8sbF/sAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKaoZ7oyC2y+Y4UyIKpArBWdfz2ltHB/BCidBgND7oPQM6S3Cwuetp+nHo9etbx1Nz\nG1ur0GtbRxzaNkNWNNaQs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers"