e":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T22:14:57Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"test(specs/013): close AC-1.6/AC-3.2/AC-3.3 coverage gaps\n\nQE flagged three WEAK-coverage findings on specs/013-estimate-sharing:\n\n- AC-1.6: the collaborator sub-routes'' stranger-404 tests only asserted\n  status, never that the Problem body is byte-identical to a genuinely\n  absent id (the property plan.md actually claims) — added the same\n  delete-then-reprobe comparison estimates.routes.test.ts already uses\n  for the plain estimate routes, across POST/GET/PATCH/DELETE/`/me`.\n- AC-3.2: the UI editor-mode control-tree assertions never actually\n  mounted with initialAccess=\"editor\", only \"owner\" — a regression\n  narrowing canEdit from `access !== ''viewer''` to `access === ''owner''`\n  would have passed undetected. Parametrised the block over both.\n- AC-3.3: only the editor case was exercised for PATCH/DELETE\n  .../collaborators/{id} refusal; added the missing viewer case.\n\nEach addition was verified to actually catch a regression: temporarily\nbroke the corresponding production behavior, confirmed the new\nassertions fail, then reverted (no production code changes remain).","tree":{"sha":"765061ea429dff1729c3454d1ec668889ad00477","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/765061ea429dff1729c3454d1ec668889ad00477"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/ce7d486e91dd037584664e36c8d2534e6560e858","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/ce7d486e91dd037584664e36c8d2534e6560e858","node_id":"C_kwDORsPN3NoAKGNlN2Q0ODZlOTFkZDAzNzU4NDY2NGUzNmM4ZDI1MzRlNjU2MGU4NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno/operai/commit/cc9e2bf42a9ed0f2778f21b761cdf2a6270e6372","sha":"cc9e2bf42a9ed0f2778f21b761cdf2a6270e6372","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/cc9e2bf42a9ed0f2778f21b761cdf2a6270e6372"}],"sha":"ce7d486e91dd037584664e36c8d2534e6560e858","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/ce7d486e91dd037584664e36c8d2534e6560e858"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/matteocodogno","id":6727995,"login":"matteocodogno","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3Mjc5OTU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/cc9e2bf42a9ed0f2778f21b761cdf2a6270e6372/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T22:03:53Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T22:03:53Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"test(estimai-api): close AC-5.3/AC-9.1 QE coverage gaps (specs/013)\n\nQE verification found two ACs whose plan.md-claimed test coverage did not\nmatch what actually ran:\n\n- AC-9.1: the only existing test proved the DB-level `onDelete: Cascade`\n  fires from a direct `db.estimate.delete()` (collaborator-schema.test.ts).\n  Nothing combined the owner''s REAL HTTP `DELETE /estimates/{id}` with a\n  subsequent collaborator `GET` over real HTTP — the actual user-observable\n  behavior AC-9.1 and plan.md''s test-strategy row describe. Adds an\n  estimates.routes.test.ts case with two real grants (viewer + editor),\n  a real DELETE, and post-delete GET/list checks for both collaborators,\n  plus a byte-identical 404-body comparison between them.\n\n- AC-5.3: no dedicated test existed at all (only doc comments referencing\n  it) — entirely parasitic on AC-5.1/AC-5.2''s next-request tests, with no\n  regression tripwire for the AC''s actual claim (\"no live disconnection\").\n  Adds a static route-scan (no stream/SSE/WebSocket route exists for the\n  estimates domain) plus a runtime check that revoke/downgrade complete as\n  plain DB writes with no live-session side effect, mirroring the existing\n  \"no /system/* route\" mutual-exclusion pattern in the same file.\n\n193/193 pass (190 pre-existing + 3 new), typecheck clean.","tree":{"sha":"08830ab64a1a40