ions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteocodogno","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/commits/d7ccdecb2d4201cc5dcbb29bfbd36eec841334c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T20:11:26Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T20:21:00Z","email":"matteo.codogno@welld.ch","name":"Matteo Codogno"},"message":"feat(estimai-api): notification wiring for collaborator grant/removal (T10, specs/013)\n\nWires src/lib/notify.ts''s already-implemented notifyCollaboratorGranted/\nnotifyCollaboratorRemoved into collaborators.routes.ts''s POST (grant) and\nowner-initiated DELETE {collaboratorId} (removal) handlers, strictly after\neach transaction commits and defended with a try/catch (bestEffortNotify)\nso a notify failure never rolls back the grant/removal or changes the HTTP\nresponse. PATCH (level change) and DELETE /me (self-leave) remain silent\nper AC-7.3. Adds collaborators.repo.ts#findEstimateName (a minimal,\nsingle-field query the notify payloads need) and injectable\nnotifyCollaboratorGranted/Removed deps to CollaboratorRouteDeps for test\nisolation, mirroring checkAppAccess/resolveIdentities. Test coverage:\nAC-7.1/7.2/7.3 wiring assertions plus a mutual-exclusion guard proving the\ncollaborator routes accept only a user JWT (never X-Internal-Token) and\nthat estimai-api exposes no /system/* route (ADR-0040).","tree":{"sha":"43a3cab1e7404e8a31ef0aa8d6274c29ece085d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/trees/43a3cab1e7404e8a31ef0aa8d6274c29ece085d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matteocodogno/operai/git/commits/d7ccdecb2d4201cc5dcbb29bfbd36eec841334c3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6727995?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matteoc