ace (nn.MultiheadAttention bakes batch dim into internal reshapes)\n- Add openWakeWord vs livekit-wakeword comparison to README with\n  side-by-side DET curves and metric explanations\n- Add docs/evaluation.md with full eval documentation\n- Update docs/overview.md with eval in module map and pipeline stages","tree":{"sha":"c6c2570a309a5f19c09b328733fa961510648f55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/git/trees/c6c2570a309a5f19c09b328733fa961510648f55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/git/commits/d5f2d7290ea58b217f2326250867d131625fcb9e","verification":{"payload":"tree c6c2570a309a5f19c09b328733fa961510648f55\nparent ce203336354919b3a6bdd8cc39fc1af0a7e66317\nauthor Binh Pham <60741317+pham-tuan-binh@users.noreply.github.com> 1773335014 +0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773335014 +0800\n\nAdd model evaluation with DET curves, AUT, and FPPH metrics (#40)\n\n- Add eval module (src/livekit/wakeword/eval/) with DET curve computation,\n  AUT scoring, threshold optimization, and DET plot generation\n- Add `livekit-wakeword eval` CLI command with `-m` flag for evaluating\n  any compatible ONNX model\n- Integrate eval as step 6/6 in the `run` pipeline\n- Expose `run_eval` in public API via lazy import\n- Fix ONNX batch size issue: use batch_size=1 in eval to match export\n  trace (nn.MultiheadAttention bakes batch dim into internal reshapes)\n- Add openWakeWord vs livekit-wakeword comparison to README with\n  side-by-side DET curves and metric explanations\n- Add docs/evaluation.md with full eval documentation\n- Update docs/overview.md with eval in module map and pipeline stages","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpsvHmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuLkQABq471moSNs4P56osyQ6g1v/\nGoDgUKGtoUlC2nFObaY8TlTxWYqPbPlT3EOPS3KRhJWj2rzzGYjvIqeii3bjqOMm\nwpbUFs+NNir4lf3qTcukJSw7nk+2lWFxvIZ735ibE7dQEmohVKj+3T50ZI3MpS/O\nJr5Uogl/yjGG7JM9698tSXNmf/0YQFFEupUT/Avz0fK2t2PkdAqxIXrf/