ts{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pham-tuan-binh","id":60741317,"login":"pham-tuan-binh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNzQxMzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/commits/6e0c24b4f5f50368590f587dce79816187e3d033/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-09T09:53:30Z","email":"60741317+pham-tuan-binh@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Binh Pham"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-09T09:53:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Document conv-attention architecture and default model type (#35)\n\n* Document conv-attention architecture and make it the default model type\n\nAdd Architecture section to README explaining the conv-attention classifier\nand its benefits over openWakeWord''s flat DNN head. Change default model_type\nfrom dnn to conv_attention in ModelConfig.\n\n* Fix inaccurate claim about DNN discarding temporal ordering\n\nFlattening preserves positional info in indices; the real limitation is\nthe lack of inductive bias for temporal structure.\n\n* Fix test to expect conv_attention as the default model type","tree":{"sha":"e419fcc5e4abab4d1f542954b19cb4e61cb44b49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/git/trees/e419fcc5e4abab4d1f542954b19cb4e61cb44b49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/git/commits/6e0c24b4f5f50368590f587dce79816187e3d033","verification":{"payload":"tree e419fcc5e4abab4d1f542954b19cb4e61cb44b49\nparent 9d8d9546bb4b31f77102abf6b29064e5e3138fdd\nauthor Binh Pham <60741317+pham-tuan-binh@users.noreply.github.com> 1773050010 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773050010 +0800\n\nDocument conv-attention architecture and default model type (#35)\n\n* Document conv-attention architecture and make it the default model type\n\nAdd Architecture section to README explaining the conv-attention classifier\nand its benefits over openWakeWord''s flat DNN head. Change default model_type\nfrom dnn to conv_attention in ModelConfig.\n\n* Fix inaccurate claim about DNN discarding temporal ordering\n\nFlattening preserves positional info in indices; the real limitation is\nthe lack of inductive bias for temporal structure.\n\n* Fix test to expect conv_attention as the default model type","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJprpiaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKC0QACpyCTFVzgjP0cTLm69qqsgh\nYRnOxGCYZjVu4cyUGcIkfldtPvquyGsXjHO5sQpZ7KrKtQf61tW4nfs4B/XVVeD9\nbyWWc6L3ZyzCICb/Ajh5SyR0mTs58Ncau47p8cQh+2DBHcVApR/6VS+KPMkAfIe6\nODo+Qdd/NTkDGzzbm2YWQLK8607qlCdWiVNHNlaak/2ZdzPzStX4lYWWj0nAAWPr\n8ZYHgBrZPBJClCloTp4196AjivrvCpFfAqFkBJUlKLPrB/qXMcnE5L8TnYdJ9XUn\nw/0X3ZFhLcH84vzfQAPRP44Oqr6sxICIdEFxO/tbV7lucvaIH6zdJwYfu0IP8IgZ\nmdkCzYh83Yu1r43KkgxmOyNl4IW7VmCkgSJbH/4ShFoibEHQRZobcOmFZUHx7rpS\nkDvKx8QM6Y6WaEpoo7jaU6fIZltHGqUN0DLbqeTOXToX7KBllJibDB44Cc69BqSh\nXi6sxt+iUKVqX8nJ2JVy0GogLEyQynPTcJPD760jx3v62XuS5BOfFDOt7kFw7wsi\nAnkrzKuFHOjXvFgxg8nyeXfZDDWz9B+KMEYu56uQfDl6JR7kcJgsiCRgAgINzmqG\nGJBywh7la+ER9BlMWX3Rw/O5Da4pBf9uXV5nu2XYdQfdgcDVNRl3G8JlSdUCLibl\nXzYY6MpiphGQ2y7tg2m0\n=8jR6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-20T16:00:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/commit/6e0c24b4f5f50368590f587dce79816187e3d033","node_id":"C_kwDORsVVN9oAKDZlMGMyNGI0ZjVmNTAzNjg1OTBmNTg3ZGNlNzk4MTYxODdlM2QwMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/commit/9d8d9546bb4b31f77102abf6b29064e5e3138fdd","sha":"9d8d9546bb4b31f77102abf6b29064e5e3138fdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/commits/9d8d9546bb4b31f77102abf6b29064e5e3138fdd"}],"sha":"6e0c24b4f5f50368590f587dce79816187e3d033","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/commits/6e0c24b4f5f50368590f587dce79816187e3d033"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60741317?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pham-tuan-binh","id":60741317,"login":"pham-tuan-binh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNzQxMzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/commits/9d8d9546bb4b31f77102abf6b29064e5e3138fdd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-09T09:29:19Z","email":"60741317+pham-tuan-binh@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Binh Pham"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-09T09:29:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Improve wake word model with conv-attention classifier and training enhancements (#34)\n\n* Add conv_attention classifier head with temporal awareness\n\nThe existing DNN head flattens (16, 96) into a single vector, discarding\ntemporal structure. The new ConvAttentionClassifier uses 1D convolutions\nto capture local phoneme patterns and self-attention to model ordering\nacross the 16 timesteps, while keeping the same ONNX I/O contract.\n\n* Replace BCE + hard example mining with focal loss\n\nFocal loss (gamma=2.0) inherently down-weights well-classified samples\nvia the (1-p_t)^gamma factor, making the manual hard-example mining\nmasks (0.1/0.9 thresholds) unnecessary. This is smoother, has fewer\nhyperparameters, and focuses gradient signal on the decision boundary.\n\n* Switch to AdamW optimizer and add label smoothing\n\nAdamW with weight_decay=0.01 provides proper L2 regularization decoupled\nfrom the adaptive learning rate. Label smoothing (default 0.05) softens\ntargets from hard 0/1 to 0.025/0.975, preventing overconfident sigmoid\noutputs and improving score calibration for threshold-based detection.\n\n* Add embedding-space mixup regularization\n\nInterpolates random pairs of (feature, label) tensors using Beta(0.2, 0.2)\nmixing coefficients during training. This creates virtual training\nexamples in embedding space, improving generalization without requiring\nchanges to the audio augmentation pipeline.\n\n* Add post-training threshold optimization\n\nInstead of always using threshold=0.5, scan 0.01-0.99 on the validation\nset to find the threshold that maximizes recall while keeping FPPH at\nor below the configured target. The optimal threshold is logged to\nmetrics.json so it can be used at inference time.\n\n* Increase SLERP weight diversity for broader speaker variation\n\nUse 5 interpolation points [0.2, 0.35, 0.5, 0.65, 0.8] instead of just\n[0.5]. This generates voices closer to each original speaker (0.2, 0.8)\nas well as the midpoint, producing more diverse synthetic training data\nand reducing overfitting to a narrow range of speaker characteristics.\n\n* Add all config fields to prod.yaml and update docs\n\n- prod.yaml now explicitly lists all config fields: TTS params\n  (noise_scales, noise_scale_ws, length_scales, slerp_weights),\n  weight_decay, label_smoothing, and the new model_type options\n- training.md rewritten for focal loss, AdamW, label smoothing,\n  embedding mixup, threshold optimization, and classifier architectures\n- overview.md updated for ConvAttentionClassifier and focal loss\n- data-generation.md updated for new slerp_weights default\n\n* Switch prod config to conv_attention classifier\n\n* new onnx model based on convattn","tree":{"sha":"c24b02ffb601528dc8028739b839ee5e7701fa8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/git/trees/c24b02ffb601528dc8028739b839ee5e7701fa8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/git/commits/9d8d9546bb4b31f77102abf6b29064e5e3138fdd","verification":{"payload":"tree c24b02ffb601528dc8028739b839ee5e7701fa8d\nparent b5e2f38021b3f0539a44ada5bffa09da0abdfb28\nauthor Binh Pham <60741317+pham-tuan-binh@users.noreply.github.com> 1773048559 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1773048559 +0800\n\nImprove wake word model with conv-attention classifier and training enhancements (#34)\n\n* Add conv_attention classifier head with temporal awareness\n\nThe existing DNN head flattens (16, 96) into a single vector, discarding\ntemporal structure. The new ConvAttentionClassifier uses 1D convolutions\nto capture local phoneme patterns and self-attention to model ordering\nacross the 16 timesteps, while keeping the same ONNX I/O contract.\n\n* Replace BCE + hard example mining with focal loss\n\nFocal loss (gamma=2.0) inherently down-weights well-classified samples\nvia the (1-p_t)^gamma factor, making the manual hard-example mining\nmasks (0.1/0.9 thresholds) unnecessary. This is smoother, has fewer\nhyperparameters, and focuses gradient signal on the decision boundary.\n\n* Switch to AdamW optimizer and add label smoothing\n\nAdamW with weight_decay=0.01 provides proper L2 regularization decoupled\nfrom the adaptive learning rate. Label smoothing (default 0.05) softens\ntargets from hard 0/1 to 0.025/0.975, preventing overconfident sigmoid\noutputs and improving score calibration for threshold-based detection.\n\n* Add embedding-space mixup regularization\n\nInterpolates random pairs of (feature, label) tensors using Beta(0.2, 0.2)\nmixing coefficients during training. This creates virtual training\nexamples in embedding space, improving generalization without requiring\nchanges to the audio augmentation pipeline.\n\n* Add post-training threshold optimization\n\nInstead of always using threshold=0.5, scan 0.01-0.99 on the validation\nset to find the threshold that maximizes recall while keeping FPPH at\nor below the configured target. The optimal threshold is logged to\nmetrics.json so it can be used at inference time.\n\n* Increase SLERP weight diversity for broader speaker variation\n\nUse 5 interpolation points [0.2, 0.35, 0.5, 0.65, 0.8] instead of just\n[0.5]. This generates voices closer to each original speaker (0.2, 0.8)\nas well as the midpoint, producing more diverse synthetic training data\nand reducing overfitting to a narrow range of speaker characteristics.\n\n* Add all config fields to prod.yaml and update docs\n\n- prod.yaml now explicitly lists all config fields: TTS params\n  (noise_scales, noise_scale_ws, length_scales, slerp_weights),\n  weight_decay, label_smoothing, and the new model_type options\n- training.md rewritten for focal loss, AdamW, label smoothing,\n  embedding mixup, threshold optimization, and classifier architectures\n- overview.md updated for ConvAttentionClassifier and focal loss\n- data-generation.md updated for new slerp_weights default\n\n* Switch prod config to conv_attention classifier\n\n* new onnx model based on convattn","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJprpLvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7S4QAAli3vDzWmeyEv3R9kt7Bhgv\nTsALrrkTWFB1ggNLF7msg7pJv8askjk9HT41cMdx7k4BgZxC8ig93EZTj8wm/epT\nsFF1SNn7UAW/xSTPSKwxZXykEXB1Bd8fMhzpY1lcrXO2MNE1i6Agm5+RNtIj5Bfp\nDscirsNgsuEGUYisTKreIIJBm1IR6f5Op0bC62A1jEgZlE8JOACVeIvlGbtYk0+w\nGuXSUHYfh6NGZ5gOSF28Jl6FQ19AXWfgSnJHq5aKECehl0ALXZ+g6fQBhBCag102\nucAHXLxTf3oWjxVjwcH0T9bM8XtQCEZvrgOazxmOKGmWX2Dn2cTu06O0vigHv7GU\nR7CRLzS8SaKitrbNZFb35jMJdcgTqe3w623fgDBRVfBlCGh7Yt2s0I+x4KqcR7NU\nbt/BVx/fwvL7EsFWSCaySWxk9Dod8U7fONm/fe1O90spgeVZEbdyQNwIxR/vHui9\nime4u2LHVDED4dvmE+z8F9fAqdBT/dhIijN1y5OM3lQqxPeK1q0P97yWCpWRraZR\n19ugUQPAv8nuKmjGNT1dtOWw1xSZorgQEim3Y2YwfwKcOmtS29PqbrPGqxg+NfdL\nmsoPDxTXr/+VeTXI6CGQvXRxfuUwiM8v+0tX6Qhu/SEScBpohkTq6agfE4Uq2fHq\nHjIoxVrX2dHufztK7NZo\n=bwJx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-20T16:00:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{