ha":"eb53ece4e27283e967d6644a23860536029b7b90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/commits/eb53ece4e27283e967d6644a23860536029b7b90"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60741317?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pham-tuan-binh","id":60741317,"login":"pham-tuan-binh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNzQxMzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/commits/61bdd281f60d1fad6522c1ef34c04039605c598d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-07T05:37:13Z","email":"60741317+pham-tuan-binh@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Binh Pham"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-07T05:37:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix TTS mispronunciation by expanding unknown words before synthesis (#30)\n\n_expand_unknown_words (e.g. \"livekit\" → \"live kit\") was only applied\nin adversarial phrase generation. Now also applied in synthesize_clips\nso VITS gets proper word boundaries and renders diphthongs correctly.\n\nAlso splits hey_livekit.yaml into prod.yaml and test.yaml configs.","tree":{"sha":"f3c78fb1b80e11f446c7481eaa1899bce0a6366e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/git/trees/f3c78fb1b80e11f446c7481eaa1899bce0a6366e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/git/commits/61bdd281f60d1fad6522c1ef34c04039605c598d","verification":{"payload":"tree f3c78fb1b80e11f446c7481eaa1899bce0a6366e\nparent 55a52a78709781092f51c741b9a5761609a50a45\nauthor Binh Pham <60741317+pham-tuan-binh@users.noreply.github.com> 1772861833 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772861833 +0800\n\nFix TTS mispronunciation by expanding unknown words before synthesis (#30)\n\n_expand_unknown_words (e.g. \"livekit\" → \"live kit\") was only applied\nin adversarial phrase generation. Now also applied in synthesize_clips\nso VITS gets proper word boundaries and renders diphthongs correctly.\n\nAlso splits hey_livekit.yaml into prod.yaml and test.yaml configs.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpq7mJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIiIQABJKJRRNJdi8i5L5pCVrxFLi\nzXBbtQN2gRAuLd+buL3K3lFqhq8vdei1O0pXI7hZRNITXjQsRlQaROQ2IfMzg7uU\naJV7iQChObNAyeOu7de9FYCFgtcPI/o/AoWBFYrbozoV5AC2H3xmyXus9adkCeJI\nZB8a5Gm2fUMJFmrEA0THMor2Ljf1z+b4gGtBK5HKol9JQRFx/z5AMk393/0cj92o\nzLGU5jEcDyudwtMy0NEjP7a8bXZ4xCidDqSH6tbGoYTnBJaZDANg9WEVuv5Stp3H\nBNtCNcAe3NK0QcKn4oq8Cp+ljvvjhk+Dr16QfX+MYavTAWTd6dvIfeG6LJXD0UzM\nKiWHGUpfPgTGh058pWNRVCettYXJcY1pOFFfb8zf38WlgEphdoNFqub17QB85Vdp\nHyJWHgTQrZfTdeJ3IOqLP6iR8u+2uWhk4IJgDDoe9P2JI6B+WAKUJ3xdIGR43foL\nvvcnmuDqJIYhTwf8epFiinmZ8lI6EjaWpOZocrjldNCvv1hZIeHgjAU8ZS26VVhT\nwheSnuo6MS1tIcEsM/foBh/Mk5LcQGFGKSXWK050Etm4HJGUBXwE7aJ3KQ87L9hh\nX4bafCrUuU62SKH4vqSEKTOquA4MSuqvlihOpHI278m0VwrmqNWMc+92rAStNHbu\nqlRFqEQvMhUI/Dv6qygL\n=3CQ6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-20T16:00:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/commit/61bdd281f60d1fad6522c1ef34c04039605c598d","node_id":"C_kwDORsVVN9oAKDYxYmRkMjgxZjYwZDFmYWQ2NTIyYzFlZjM0YzA0MDM5NjA1YzU5OGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/commit/55a52a78709781092f51c741b9a5761609a50a45","sha":"55a52a78709781092f51c741b9a5761609a50a45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/commits/55a52a78709781092f51c741b9a5761609a50a45"}],"sha":"61bdd281f60d1fad6522c1ef34c04039605c598d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/commits/61bdd281f60d1fad6522c1ef34c04039605c598d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60741317?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pham-tuan-binh","id":60741317,"login":"pham-tuan-binh","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNzQxMzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pham-tuan-binh","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/commits/55a52a78709781092f51c741b9a5761609a50a45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-07T05:17:34Z","email":"60741317+pham-tuan-binh@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Binh Pham"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-07T05:17:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix silent audio and 8 pipeline bugs across generation, training, and inference (#29)\n\n* Remove silent audio fallback, fail loudly on generation errors\n\nThe silence fallback in synthesize_clips masked real failures by writing\nall-zeros WAV files when VITS errored or the model was missing. This caused\nentire splits (e.g. negative_test) to be silently filled with empty audio.\n\n- synthesize_clips: raise FileNotFoundError if model missing, no more\n  silence placeholders\n- run_generate: fail early if VITS model doesn''t exist\n- _piper_generate: catch errors per-batch instead of per-pipeline, skip\n  bad batches and continue, raise after 5 consecutive failures or if\n  zero clips generated\n- Update tests to assert FileNotFoundError instead of silence fallback\n\n* Fix three data generation bugs: augment filter, VAD stripping, resume sync\n\nBug 1 (augment.py): The filter to exclude augmented variants (_r1, _r2)\nwas broken — \"_r\" not in \"r1\" is always True. Subsequent augmentation\nrounds processed _rN files, creating compounding double-augmented clips\nthat inflated the training set. Fixed by using the same regex pattern as\n_count_original_clips.\n\nBug 2 (_piper_generate.py): remove_silence could strip all speech frames,\nleaving only 125ms of leading silence. Now falls back to the original\nuntrimmed audio if VAD produces less than 150ms of content beyond the\nmin_start window.\n\nBug 3 (_piper_generate.py): settings_iter was consumed once per sample on\nresume but once per batch during generation, over-advancing by a factor\nof batch_size. Fixed to consume ceil(start_index / batch_size) instead.\n\n* Fix adversarial generation for non-dictionary words + reduce augmentation\n\nAdversarial generation: words not in CMUDict (like \"livekit\") were\ncompletely skipped, so negatives like \"hi livekit\" kept \"livekit\"\nverbatim and sounded nearly identical to the target. Now splits unknown\ncompound words into known subwords (e.g. \"livekit\" → \"live\" + \"kit\"),\nenabling substitutions on both parts to produce diverse adversarials\nlike \"hey love kit\", \"hey live bit\", \"hey life kit\", etc.\n\nAlso filters out exact target phrases from the adversarial list.\n\nAugmentation: reduced aggressive noise/gain that was making clips\nunintelligible:\n- Background noise SNR: -10..15 dB → 0..15 dB (signal no longer\n  quieter than noise)\n- Gain: always-on -18..0 dB → 50% chance of -6..+6 dB (symmetric,\n  not always reducing volume)\n\n* Fix FPPH using hardcoded 11 hours instead of actual validation data size\n\nevaluate_model() defaulted to validation_hours=11.0 (from the external\nACAV100M set). When only generated test clips are present (~2.78h for\n5000 clips), FPPH was ~4x too low, so phase 2/3 negative weight doubling\nnever triggered when it should have. Now computes actual hours from\nneg clip count × clip_duration.\n\n* Reset detection queue on listener reuse to prevent stale detections\n\n__aenter__ reset _frame_buffer, _error, _listening, _done_event but not\n_detection_queue. If a detection was queued but never consumed and the\nsame listener was re-entered, the stale detection would fire immediately\non the next wait_for_detection() call.\n\n* Fix hard example mining thresholds that made it a no-op\n\nOld thresholds (0.001/0.999) were so extreme that virtually every sample\nwas considered \"hard\" — the mining filtered almost nothing. Changed to\n0.1/0.9 so the model stops training on confidently-correct samples and\nfocuses on uncertain or misclassified ones.\n\n* Fix SLERP batch-level fallback that killed speaker diversity\n\nThe .any() check meant one near-parallel speaker pair in a batch forced\nALL pairs to linear interpolation, silently degrading SLERP blending.\nChanged to per-element: each pair independently uses SLERP or linear\ninterp. Also clamps dot product to [-1, 1] to prevent NaN from acos\non float precision overflow.\n\n* Warn when validation samples are truncated during 2D→3D reshape\n\nWhen external validation features have a sample count not divisible by\n16, the remainder was silently dropped. Now logs a warning with the\nexact count so data quality issues are visible.\n\n* Update docs to reflect bug fixes across the pipeline\n\n- data-generation.md: document error-on-missing-model (no more silence\n  fallback), per-batch error handling, compound word splitting for\n  adversarial generation, per-element SLERP fallback, VAD safety net\n- augmentation.md: document SNR range (0-15dB), regex filter excluding\n  augmented variants from subsequent rounds\n- training.md: update hard example mining thresholds (0.1/0.9), FPPH\n  computed from actual data size, validation truncation warning\n- export-and-inference.md: document listener lifecycle and queue reset","tree":{"sha":"843bb12a6da58f6f563fafeba5a6d5960e81d93d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/git/trees/843bb12a6da58f6f563fafeba5a6d5960e81d93d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/livekit/livekit-embedded-wakeword/git/commits/55a52a78709781092f51c741b9a5761609a50a45","verification":{"payload":"tree 843bb12a6da58f6f563fafeba5a6d5960e81d93d\nparent 00652c98b4da9836bd542508b9259112fef4d9c3\nauthor Binh Pham <60741317+pham-tuan-binh@users.noreply.github.com> 1772860654 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772860654 +0800\n\nFix silent audio and 8 pipeline bugs across generation, training, and inference (#29)\n\n* Remove silent audio fallback, fail loudly on generation errors\n\nThe silence fallback in synthesize_clips masked real failures by writing\nall-zeros WAV files when VITS errored or the model was missing. This caused\nentire splits (e.g. negative_test) to be silently filled with empty audio.\n\n- synthesize_clips: raise FileNotFoundError if model missing, no more\n  silence placeholders\n- run_generate: fail early if VITS model doesn''t exist\n- _piper_generate: catch errors per-batch instead of per-pipeline, skip\n  bad batches and continue, raise after 5 consecutive failures or if\n  zero clips generated\n- Update tests to assert FileNotFoundError instead of silence fallback\n\n* Fix three data generation bugs: augment filter, VAD stripping, resume sync\n\nBug 1 (augment.py): The filter to exclude augmented variants (_r1, _r2)\nwas broken — \"_r\" not in \"r1\" is always True. Subsequent augmentation\nrounds processed _rN files, creating compounding double-augmented clips\nthat inflated the training set. Fixed by using the same regex pattern as\n_count_original_clips.\n\nBug 2 (_piper_generate.py): remove_silence could strip all speech frames,\nleaving only 125ms of leading silence. Now falls back to the original\nuntrimmed audio if VAD produces less than 150ms of content beyond the\nmin_start window.\n\nBug 3 (_piper_generate.py): settings_iter was consumed once per sample on\nresume but once per batch during generation, over-advancing by a factor\nof batch_size. Fixed to consume ceil(start_index / batch_size) instead.\n\n* Fix adversarial generation for non-dictionary words + reduce augmentation\n\nAdversarial generation: words not in CMUDict (like \"livekit\") were\ncompletely skipped, so negatives like \"hi livekit\" kept \"livekit\"\nverbatim and sounded nearly identical to the target. Now splits unknown\ncompound words into known subwords (e.g. \"livekit\" → \"live\" + \"kit\"),\nenabling substitutions on both parts to produce diverse adversarials\nlike \"hey love kit\", \"hey live bit\", \"hey life kit\", etc.\n\nAlso filters out exact target phrases from the adversarial list.\n\nAugmentation: reduced aggressive noise/gain that was making clips\nunintelligible:\n- Background noise SNR: -10..15 dB → 0..15 dB (signal no longer\n  quieter than noise)\n- Gain: always-on -18..0 dB → 50% chance of -6..+6 dB (symmetric,\n  not always reducing volume)\n\n* Fix FPPH using hardcoded 11 hours instead of actual validation data size\n\nevaluate_model() defaulted to validation_hours=11.0 (from the external\nACAV100M set). When only generated test clips are present (~2.78h for\n5000 clips), FPPH was ~4x too low, so phase 2/3 negative weight doubling\nnever triggered when it should have. Now computes actual hours from\nneg clip count × clip_duration.\n\n* Reset detection queue on listener reuse to prevent stale detections\n\n__aenter__ reset _frame_buffer, _error, _listening, _done_event but not\n_detection_queue. If a detection was queued but never consumed and the\nsame listener was re-entered, the stale detection would fire immediately\non the next wait_for_detection() call.\n\n* Fix hard example mining thresholds that made it a no-op\n\nOld thresholds (0.001/0.999) were so extreme that virtually every sample\nwas considered \"hard\" — the mining filtered almost nothing. Changed to\n0.1/0.9 so the model stops training on confidently-correct samples and\nfocuses on uncertain or misclassified ones.\n\n* Fix SLERP batch-level fallback that killed speaker diversity\n\nThe .any() check meant one near-parallel speaker pair in a batch forced\nALL pairs to linear interpolation, silently degrading SLERP blending.\nChanged to per-element: each pair independently uses SLERP or linear\ninterp. Also clamps dot product to [-1, 1] to prevent NaN from acos\non float precision overflow.\n\n* Warn when validation samples are truncated during 2D→3D reshape\n\nWhen external validation features have a sample count not divisible by\n16, the remainder was silently dropped. Now logs a warning with the\nexact count so data quality issues are visible.\n\n* Update docs to reflect bug fixes across the pipeline\n\n- data-generation.md: document error-on-missing-model (no more silence\n  fallback), per-batch error handling, compound word splitting for\n  adversarial generation, per-element SLERP fallback, VAD safety net\n- augmentation.md: document SNR range (0-15dB), regex filter excluding\n  augmented variants from subsequent rounds\n- training.md: update hard example mining thresholds (0.1/0.9), FPPH\n  computed from actual data size, validation truncation warning\n- export-and-inference.md: document listener lifecycle and queue reset","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpq7TuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ/sQADeXkff5zvgXe9OglzgOKqke\nz+jE3fRsUT3yAajjghCN/ppjrliIwQWdpC/CPUn2/XzHVndlQmPC0Khw7kbSoVoP\nFu+9GFSIdVh2kpYhNQ7ChrvlJZoqrwM9QK3TddvhOLTu28Om9QIExGTGuRyXIUMQ\nVEcX3Dmr5Ofzv3tMSjO1wdtKtslEojbToSa9Kj6DLG4v4dDgIUNH/AAHrmtIwbkw\n8SNdTIGyKvCOAm5WpdagoWNfZufFUiBGq93z25pym27hq8FEeFW8h6WkoMZ6ud9f\nwA0ThI0z2c5g5ApYd+MqDmnPyMfBPIr+jEE34JktXwN7zFjfdyNAd8/0O9Yei7GD\n5FCvomBtAof7A8xL/ExE0NxnoFFLcgCFJBTmX981yKbAh45F2/eoK/MYk+6pZH/5\nJ/5hf/zIceRf+/dIRPWOzuJuDwH3+xSzN3iMmal60ottfTEBifID+tur82mXoE3Z\nWdLTwx+3aGOgboJ9R1ktrrlaCESTs65YS24/gaD6xbnlzPaB2xX4NbAmMuRJ8ccX\n7Hw0OTBI1jSAM6AKweuot1lRvoSXc5EnIXW6yYOgyeOtNS9MI/3iyUYs2u96CML5\nzFThPfHJGISL+n8ZPpUyIT3b+P0qd/ZC51WRdXwToVcFYlqb5lfi7M417isnSph+\nmfomJeoytRVNf+y4y25X\n=n8pp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-20T16:00:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https:/